(md5('mfd:' || 'around_the_world')::uuid, 'mfd', 'around_the_world', 'Around The World', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying on a bench, you move light dumbbells in a big semicircle from your hips to over your head and back.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding a light dumbbell in each hand at your hips, palms up.','Keep a slight bend in the elbows.']::text[], array['Sweep the dumbbells out to the sides and up in a wide arc until they meet above your head.','Reverse the arc back to your hips.']::text[], array['Use light weights and smooth control','Keep the arms close to the floor plane']::text[], array['Going too heavy','Bending the elbows a lot']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'around_the_worlds')::uuid, 'mfd', 'around_the_worlds', 'Around The Worlds', array['Around The World (Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Around The Worlds is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest. A variation of the around the world: lying on a bench, dumbbells circle from the hips to overhead.', array['Lay down on a flat bench holding a dumbbell in each hand with the palms of the hands facing towards the ceiling. Tip: Your arms should be parallel to the floor and next to your thighs. To avoid injury, make sure that you keep your elbows slightly bent. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Now move the dumbbells by creating a semi-circle as you displace them from the initial position to over the head. All of the movement should happen with the arms parallel to the floor at all times. Breathe in as you perform this portion of the movement.','Reverse the movement to return the weight to the starting position as you exhale.']::text[], array['Use light weights and smooth control','Keep the arms close to the floor plane']::text[], array['Going too heavy','Bending the elbows a lot']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/around_the_worlds/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Around_The_Worlds/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_guillotine_bench_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_guillotine_bench_press', 'Barbell Guillotine Bench Press', array['Bench Press (Guillotine)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Guillotine Bench Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the bench press: bar lowered to the neck with elbows flared. Use light weight and safeties; it stresses the shoulders.', array['Using a medium width grip (a grip that creates a 90-degree angle in the middle of the movement between the forearms and the upper arms), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over your neck with your arms locked. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['As you breathe in, bring the bar down slowly until it is about 1 inch from your neck.','After a second pause, bring the bar back to the starting position as you breathe out and push the bar using your chest muscles. Lock your arms and squeeze your chest in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly again. It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_guillotine_bench_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Guillotine_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_barbell', 'Bench Press (Barbell)', array['flat bench','bench','barbell bench press','bb bench']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'The main horizontal pressing exercise for chest, front shoulders and triceps. Lying on a flat bench, you lower the weight to your chest and press it back up.', array['Lie on the bench with your eyes under the bar (or the handles/weights level with your chest).','Plant your feet flat on the floor, slightly wider than your hips.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down and keep them pinned to the bench; allow a small natural arch in your lower back.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width with wrists stacked straight over your forearms.']::text[], array['Unrack or lift the weight to straight arms over your shoulders.','Lower it under control to your lower chest, elbows about 45–70° from your torso.','Touch the chest lightly without bouncing.','Press back up and slightly toward your face so the weight finishes over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_press_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_cable', 'Bench Press (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'The main horizontal pressing exercise for chest, front shoulders and triceps. Lying on a flat bench, you lower the weight to your chest and press it back up.', array['Place a flat bench between two low cable pulleys.','Lie down holding a handle in each hand at chest level.','Plant your feet and pull your shoulder blades back and down.']::text[], array['Unrack or lift the weight to straight arms over your shoulders.','Lower it under control to your lower chest, elbows about 45–70° from your torso.','Touch the chest lightly without bouncing.','Press back up and slightly toward your face so the weight finishes over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_dumbbell', 'Bench Press (Dumbbell)', array['db bench press','dumbbell press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'The main horizontal pressing exercise for chest, front shoulders and triceps. Lying on a flat bench, you lower the weight to your chest and press it back up.', array['Sit on the end of the bench with the dumbbells on your thighs.','Lie back and use your knees to help bring the dumbbells to your chest.','Plant your feet and pull your shoulder blades back and down.','Hold the dumbbells with palms facing forward or slightly inward.']::text[], array['Unrack or lift the weight to straight arms over your shoulders.','Lower it under control to your lower chest, elbows about 45–70° from your torso.','Touch the chest lightly without bouncing.','Press back up and slightly toward your face so the weight finishes over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders','Press the dumbbells up and slightly together without clanking them']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_press_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_smith', 'Bench Press (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'The main horizontal pressing exercise for chest, front shoulders and triceps. Lying on a flat bench, you lower the weight to your chest and press it back up.', array['Lie on the bench with your eyes under the bar (or the handles/weights level with your chest).','Plant your feet flat on the floor, slightly wider than your hips.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down and keep them pinned to the bench; allow a small natural arch in your lower back.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width with wrists stacked straight over your forearms.']::text[], array['Unrack or lift the weight to straight arms over your shoulders.','Lower it under control to your lower chest, elbows about 45–70° from your torso.','Touch the chest lightly without bouncing.','Press back up and slightly toward your face so the weight finishes over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders','Twist the bar off the hooks and lock it back by rotating your wrists']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_press_smith/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_wide_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_wide_grip', 'Bench Press - Wide Grip (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'The main horizontal pressing exercise for chest, front shoulders and triceps. Lying on a flat bench, you lower the weight to your chest and press it back up.', array['Lie on the bench with your eyes under the bar (or the handles/weights level with your chest).','Plant your feet flat on the floor, slightly wider than your hips.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down and keep them pinned to the bench; allow a small natural arch in your lower back.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width with wrists stacked straight over your forearms.']::text[], array['Unrack or lift the weight to straight arms over your shoulders.','Lower it under control to your lower chest, elbows about 45–70° from your torso.','Touch the chest lightly without bouncing.','Press back up and slightly toward your face so the weight finishes over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_press_wide_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_with_bands', 'Bench Press - With Bands', array['Bench Press (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Bench Press - With Bands is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the bench press: bands instead of a bar, anchored under the bench.', array['Using a flat bench secure a band under the leg of the bench that is nearest to your head.']::text[], array['Once the band is secure, grab it by both handles and lie down on the bench.','Extend your arms so that you are holding the band handles in front of you at shoulder width.','Once at shoulder width, rotate your wrists forward so that the palms of your hands are facing away from you. This will be your starting position.','Bring down the handles slowly until your elbow forms a 90 degree angle. Keep full control at all times.','As you breathe out, bring the handles up using your pectoral muscles. Lock your arms in the contracted position, squeeze your chest, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_press_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bench_Press_-_With_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chain_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chain_press', 'Chain Press', array['Bench Press (Chain Handles)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Chain Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the bench press: chains clipped to handles and pressed like dumbbells.', array['Begin by connecting the chains to the cable handle attachments. Position yourself on the flat bench in the same position as for a dumbbell press. Your wrists should be pronated and arms perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Lower the chains by flexing the elbows, unloading some of the chain onto the floor.','Continue until your elbow forms a 90 degree angle, and then reverse the motion by extending through the elbow to lockout.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chain_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chain_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_bench_press_with_neutral_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_bench_press_with_neutral_grip', 'Dumbbell Bench Press with Neutral Grip', array['Bench Press (Dumbbell, Neutral Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Bench Press with Neutral Grip is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the bench press: palms face each other, which is easier on the shoulders.', array['Take a dumbbell in each hand and lay back onto a flat bench. Your feet should be flat on the floor and your shoulder blades retracted.']::text[], array['Maintaining a neutral grip, palms facing each other, begin with your arms extended directly above you, perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position.','Begin the movement by flexing the elbow, lowering the upper arms to the side. Descend until the dumbbells are to your torso.','Pause, then extend the elbow and return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_bench_press_with_neutral_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Bench_Press_with_Neutral_Grip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_feet_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_feet_up', 'Feet Up Bench Press (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'The main horizontal pressing exercise for chest, front shoulders and triceps. Lying on a flat bench, you lower the weight to your chest and press it back up.', array['Lie on the bench with your eyes under the bar (or the handles/weights level with your chest).','Plant your feet flat on the floor, slightly wider than your hips.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down and keep them pinned to the bench; allow a small natural arch in your lower back.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width with wrists stacked straight over your forearms.']::text[], array['Unrack or lift the weight to straight arms over your shoulders.','Lower it under control to your lower chest, elbows about 45–70° from your torso.','Touch the chest lightly without bouncing.','Press back up and slightly toward your face so the weight finishes over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders','Keep your hips down and core tight']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'neck_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'neck_press', 'Neck Press', array['Bench Press (To Neck)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Neck Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the bench press: bar lowered to the base of the neck with elbows wide. Light weight only; it stresses the shoulders.', array['Lie back on a flat bench. Using a medium-width grip (a grip that creates a 90-degree angle in the middle of the movement between the forearms and the upper arms), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over your neck with your arms locked. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['As you breathe in, come down slowly until you feel the bar on your neck.','After a second pause, bring the bar back to the starting position as you breathe out and push the bar using your chest muscles. Lock your arms and squeeze your chest in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly again. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up).','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/neck_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Neck_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_dumbbell_bench_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_dumbbell_bench_press', 'One Arm Dumbbell Bench Press', array['Bench Press (Single Arm Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One Arm Dumbbell Bench Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the bench press: one dumbbell; the core has to stop the body twisting.', array['Lie down on a flat bench with a dumbbell in one hand on top of your thigh.']::text[], array['By using your thigh to help you get the dumbbell up, clean the dumbbell up so that you can hold it in front of you at shoulder width. Use the hand you are not lifting with to help position the dumbbell over you properly.','Once at shoulder width, rotate your wrist forward so that the palm of your hand is facing away from you. This will be your starting position.','Bring down the weights slowly to your side as you breathe in. Keep full control of the dumbbell at all times. Tip: Use the hand that you are not lifting with to help keep the dumbbell balance as you may struggle a bit at first. Only use your non-lifting hand if it is needed. Otherwise, keep it resting to the side.','As you breathe out, push the dumbbells up using your pectoral muscles. Lock your arms in the contracted position, squeeze your chest, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.','Switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_dumbbell_bench_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Arm_Dumbbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bodyweight_flyes')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bodyweight_flyes', 'Bodyweight Flyes', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bodyweight Flyes is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Position two equally loaded EZ bars on the ground next to each other. Ensure they are able to roll.']::text[], array['Assume a push-up position over the bars, supporting your weight on your toes and hands with your arms extended and body straight.','Place your hands on the bars. This will be your starting position.','Using a slow and controlled motion, move your hands away from the midline of your body, rolling the bars apart. Inhale during this portion of the motion.','After moving the bars as far apart as you can, return to the starting position by pulling them back together. Exhale as you perform this movement.']::text[], array['Push-up position with hands on two rolling bars','Roll the bars apart under control','Squeeze the chest to bring them back']::text[], array['Going too wide','Sagging hips']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bodyweight_flyes/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Flyes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_fly_crossover')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_fly_crossover', 'Cable Fly Crossovers', array['cable crossover','cable flye','high cable fly']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A chest fly on a cable station. The cables keep tension on the chest from the stretch all the way to the squeeze.', array['Set both pulleys to the height for the variation and attach single handles.','Stand in the middle with one foot slightly forward and lean your torso slightly forward.','Start with arms open, a slight bend in the elbows, and a stretch across the chest.']::text[], array['Bring the handles together in a wide arc in front of you.','Squeeze the chest for a moment.','Let the arms open slowly along the same arc.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum','Leaning and rocking the body to move the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_fly_crossover/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Crossover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_iron_cross')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_iron_cross', 'Cable Iron Cross', array['Cable Fly (Iron Cross)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Iron Cross is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest. A variation of the cable fly: high pulleys with the arms sweeping down and together in a wide arc.', array['Begin by moving the pulleys to the high position, select the resistance to be used, and take a handle in each hand.']::text[], array['Stand directly between both pulleys with your arms extended out to your sides. Your head and chest should be up while your arms form a "T". This will be your starting position.','Keeping the elbows extended, pull your arms straight to your sides.','Return your arms back to the starting position after a pause at the peak contraction.','Continue the movement for the prescribed number of repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum','Leaning and rocking the body to move the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_iron_cross/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Iron_Cross/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'flat_bench_cable_flyes')::uuid, 'mfd', 'flat_bench_cable_flyes', 'Flat Bench Cable Flyes', array['Cable Fly (Flat Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Flat Bench Cable Flyes is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest. A variation of the cable fly: lying on a flat bench between low pulleys.', array['Position a flat bench between two low pulleys so that when you are laying on it, your chest will be lined up with the cable pulleys.']::text[], array['Lay flat on the bench and keep your feet on the ground.','Have someone hand you the handles on each hand. You will grab each single handle attachment with a palms up grip.','Extend your arms by your side with a slight bend on your elbows. Tip: You will keep this bend constant through the whole movement. Your arms should be parallel to the floor. This is your starting position.','Now start lifting the arms in a semi-circle motion directly in front of you by pulling the cables together until both hands meet at the top of the movement. Squeeze your chest as you perform this motion and breathe out during this movement. Also, hold the contraction for a second at the top. Tip: When performed correctly, at the top position of this movement, your arms should be perpendicular to your torso and the floor touching above your chest.','Slowly come back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum','Leaning and rocking the body to move the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/flat_bench_cable_flyes/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Flat_Bench_Cable_Flyes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_cable_flye')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_cable_flye', 'Incline Cable Flye', array['Cable Fly (Incline Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Incline Cable Flye is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest. A variation of the cable fly: lying on an incline bench between low pulleys, for the upper chest.', array['To get yourself into the starting position, set the pulleys at the floor level (lowest level possible on the machine that is below your torso).']::text[], array['Place an incline bench (set at 45 degrees) in between the pulleys, select a weight on each one and grab a pulley on each hand.','With a handle on each hand, lie on the incline bench and bring your hands together at arms length in front of your face. This will be your starting position.','With a slight bend of your elbows (in order to prevent stress at the biceps tendon), lower your arms out at both sides in a wide arc until you feel a stretch on your chest. Breathe in as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: Keep in mind that throughout the movement, the arms should remain stationary. The movement should only occur at the shoulder joint.','Return your arms back to the starting position as you squeeze your chest muscles and exhale. Hold the contracted position for a second. Tip: Make sure to use the same arc of motion used to lower the weights.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum','Leaning and rocking the body to move the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_cable_flye/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Cable_Flye/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_fly_low')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_fly_low', 'Low Cable Fly Crossovers', array['low to high cable fly']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A chest fly on a cable station. The cables keep tension on the chest from the stretch all the way to the squeeze.', array['Set both pulleys to the height for the variation and attach single handles.','Stand in the middle with one foot slightly forward and lean your torso slightly forward.','Start with arms open, a slight bend in the elbows, and a stretch across the chest.']::text[], array['Bring the handles together in a wide arc in front of you.','Squeeze the chest for a moment.','Let the arms open slowly along the same arc.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum','Leaning and rocking the body to move the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_fly_low/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Low_Cable_Crossover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_fly_seated')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_fly_seated', 'Seated Chest Flys (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A chest fly on a cable station. The cables keep tension on the chest from the stretch all the way to the squeeze.', array['Place a bench between the pulleys set at chest height.','Sit upright and take a handle in each hand.']::text[], array['Bring the handles together in a wide arc in front of you.','Squeeze the chest for a moment.','Let the arms open slowly along the same arc.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum','Leaning and rocking the body to move the weight']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_fly_single_arm')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_fly_single_arm', 'Single Arm Cable Crossover', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A chest fly on a cable station. The cables keep tension on the chest from the stretch all the way to the squeeze.', array['Set both pulleys to the height for the variation and attach single handles.','Stand in the middle with one foot slightly forward and lean your torso slightly forward.','Start with arms open, a slight bend in the elbows, and a stretch across the chest.']::text[], array['Bring the handles together in a wide arc in front of you.','Squeeze the chest for a moment.','Let the arms open slowly along the same arc.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end','Keep the hips and shoulders square; do not twist']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum','Leaning and rocking the body to move the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_fly_single_arm/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Arm_Cable_Crossover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_dip_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_dip_bodyweight', 'Chest Dip', array['dip','parallel bar dip']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A bodyweight dip with the torso leaning forward to put more of the work on the lower chest.', array['Grip the parallel bars and jump or step up to straight arms.','Lean your torso forward about 30° and let your legs hang slightly in front or bend the knees.']::text[], array['Lower yourself by bending the elbows until your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Keep the elbows pointing back and slightly out.','Push back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Lean forward to bias the chest','Shoulders down, away from the ears']::text[], array['Dropping too deep and straining the shoulders','Shrugging at the bottom','Swinging the legs']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_dip_bodyweight/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dips_-_Chest_Version/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_dip_assisted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_dip_assisted', 'Chest Dip (Assisted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'assisted_bodyweight', 'A bodyweight dip with the torso leaning forward to put more of the work on the lower chest.', array['Grip the parallel bars and jump or step up to straight arms.','Lean your torso forward about 30° and let your legs hang slightly in front or bend the knees.']::text[], array['Lower yourself by bending the elbows until your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Keep the elbows pointing back and slightly out.','Push back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Lean forward to bias the chest','Shoulders down, away from the ears']::text[], array['Dropping too deep and straining the shoulders','Shrugging at the bottom','Swinging the legs']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_dip_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_dip_weighted', 'Chest Dip (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'A bodyweight dip with the torso leaning forward to put more of the work on the lower chest.', array['Grip the parallel bars and jump or step up to straight arms.','Lean your torso forward about 30° and let your legs hang slightly in front or bend the knees.']::text[], array['Lower yourself by bending the elbows until your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Keep the elbows pointing back and slightly out.','Push back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Lean forward to bias the chest','Shoulders down, away from the ears']::text[], array['Dropping too deep and straining the shoulders','Shrugging at the bottom','Swinging the legs']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_dip_weighted/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dips_-_Chest_Version/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_dip_rings')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_dip_rings', 'Ring Dips', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A bodyweight dip with the torso leaning forward to put more of the work on the lower chest.', array['Grip the parallel bars and jump or step up to straight arms.','Lean your torso forward about 30° and let your legs hang slightly in front or bend the knees.']::text[], array['Lower yourself by bending the elbows until your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Keep the elbows pointing back and slightly out.','Push back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Lean forward to bias the chest','Shoulders down, away from the ears']::text[], array['Dropping too deep and straining the shoulders','Shrugging at the bottom','Swinging the legs']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_dip_rings/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Ring_Dips/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_fly_pec_deck')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_fly_pec_deck', 'Butterfly (Pec Deck)', array['pec deck','butterfly']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An isolation exercise for the chest. The arms move in a wide arc while the elbows stay slightly bent.', array['Adjust the seat so your upper arms are level with your shoulders.','Place your forearms or hands on the pads with elbows bent about 90°.']::text[], array['Start with arms extended in front of your chest and a slight bend in the elbows.','Open your arms in a wide arc until you feel a stretch across the chest.','Bring the arms back together along the same arc, as if hugging a large tree.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_fly_pec_deck/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Butterfly/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_fly_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_fly_band', 'Chest Fly (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An isolation exercise for the chest. The arms move in a wide arc while the elbows stay slightly bent.', array['Anchor the band behind you at chest height.','Hold an end in each hand and step forward until the band is taut.']::text[], array['Start with arms extended in front of your chest and a slight bend in the elbows.','Open your arms in a wide arc until you feel a stretch across the chest.','Bring the arms back together along the same arc, as if hugging a large tree.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_fly_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_fly_dumbbell', 'Chest Fly (Dumbbell)', array['fly','flye','pec fly','dumbbell fly','db fly']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An isolation exercise for the chest. The arms move in a wide arc while the elbows stay slightly bent.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding dumbbells above your chest, palms facing each other.','Plant your feet and pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Start with arms extended in front of your chest and a slight bend in the elbows.','Open your arms in a wide arc until you feel a stretch across the chest.','Bring the arms back together along the same arc, as if hugging a large tree.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_fly_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Flyes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_fly_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_fly_machine', 'Chest Fly (Machine)', array['machine fly']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An isolation exercise for the chest. The arms move in a wide arc while the elbows stay slightly bent.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at chest height.','Sit with your back against the pad and grip the handles with a slight elbow bend.']::text[], array['Start with arms extended in front of your chest and a slight bend in the elbows.','Open your arms in a wide arc until you feel a stretch across the chest.','Bring the arms back together along the same arc, as if hugging a large tree.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_fly_suspension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_fly_suspension', 'Chest Fly (Suspension)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'An isolation exercise for the chest. The arms move in a wide arc while the elbows stay slightly bent.', array['Face away from the anchor holding the handles, arms in front of your chest.','Lean forward into a plank-like position; the more you lean, the harder it gets.']::text[], array['Start with arms extended in front of your chest and a slight bend in the elbows.','Open your arms in a wide arc until you feel a stretch across the chest.','Bring the arms back together along the same arc, as if hugging a large tree.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cross_over_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cross_over_with_bands', 'Cross Over - With Bands', array['Chest Fly (Band Crossover)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Cross Over - With Bands is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the biceps. A variation of the chest fly: a band behind the back; hands sweep together in front.', array['Secure an exercise band around a stationary post.']::text[], array['While facing away from the post, grab the handles on both ends of the band and step forward enough to create tension on the band.','Raise your arms to the sides, parallel to the floor, perpendicular to your torso (your torso and the arms should resemble the letter "T") and with the palms facing forward. Have them extended with a slight bend at the elbows. This will be your starting position.','While keeping your arms straight, bring them across your chest in a semicircular motion to the front as you exhale and flex your pecs. Hold the contraction for a second.','Slowly return to the starting position as you inhale.','Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cross_over_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cross_Over_-_With_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_fly_decline_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_fly_decline_dumbbell', 'Decline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An isolation exercise for the chest. The arms move in a wide arc while the elbows stay slightly bent.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding dumbbells above your chest, palms facing each other.','Plant your feet and pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Start with arms extended in front of your chest and a slight bend in the elbows.','Open your arms in a wide arc until you feel a stretch across the chest.','Bring the arms back together along the same arc, as if hugging a large tree.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_fly_decline_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Decline_Dumbbell_Flyes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_fly_incline_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_fly_incline_dumbbell', 'Incline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)', array['incline fly']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An isolation exercise for the chest. The arms move in a wide arc while the elbows stay slightly bent.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding dumbbells above your chest, palms facing each other.','Plant your feet and pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Start with arms extended in front of your chest and a slight bend in the elbows.','Open your arms in a wide arc until you feel a stretch across the chest.','Bring the arms back together along the same arc, as if hugging a large tree.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_fly_incline_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Flyes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_dumbbell_flyes_with_a_twist')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_dumbbell_flyes_with_a_twist', 'Incline Dumbbell Flyes - With A Twist', array['Chest Fly (Incline, With Twist)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Incline Dumbbell Flyes - With A Twist is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest. A variation of the chest fly: palms turn to face you at the top for a harder squeeze.', array['Hold a dumbbell in each hand and lie on an incline bench that is set to an incline angle of no more than 30 degrees.']::text[], array['Extend your arms above you with a slight bend at the elbows.','Now rotate the wrists so that the palms of your hands are facing you. Tip: The pinky fingers should be next to each other. This will be your starting position.','As you breathe in, start to slowly lower the arms to the side while keeping the arms extended and while rotating the wrists until the palms of the hand are facing each other. Tip: At the end of the movement the arms will be by your side with the palms facing the ceiling.','As you exhale start to bring the dumbbells back up to the starting position by reversing the motion and rotating the hands so that the pinky fingers are next to each other again. Tip: Keep in mind that the movement will only happen at the shoulder joint and at the wrist. There is no motion that happens at the elbow joint.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_dumbbell_flyes_with_a_twist/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Flyes_-_With_A_Twist/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_flat_bench_dumbbell_flye')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_flat_bench_dumbbell_flye', 'One-Arm Flat Bench Dumbbell Flye', array['Chest Fly (Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Flat Bench Dumbbell Flye is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest. A variation of the chest fly: one dumbbell; the other hand holds the bench.', array['Lie down on a flat bench with a dumbbell in one hand resting on top of your thigh. The palm of your hand with the dumbbell in it should be at a neutral grip.']::text[], array['By using your thighs to help you get the dumbbell up, clean the dumbbell so that you can hold it in front of you with your lifting arm being fully extended. Remember to maintain a neutral grip with this exercise. Your non lifting hand should be to the side holding the flat bench for better support. This will be your starting position.','Your arm with the weight should have a slight bend on your elbow in order to prevent stress at the biceps tendon. Begin by lowering your arm with the weight in it out in a wide arc until you feel a stretch on your chest. Breathe in as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: Keep in mind that throughout the movement, your lifting arm should remain stationary; the movement should only occur at the shoulder joint.','Return your lifting arm back to the starting position as you squeeze your chest muscles and breathe out. Tip: Make sure to use the same arc of motion used to lower the weights.','Hold for a second at the contracted position and repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the exercise.']::text[], array['Keep the same small elbow bend throughout','Think of moving the upper arms, not the hands','Squeeze the chest at the end']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows, which turns it into a press','Lowering too far and straining the front of the shoulder','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_flat_bench_dumbbell_flye/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Flat_Bench_Dumbbell_Flye/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_chest_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_chest_press', 'Cable Chest Press', array['Chest Press (Cable)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Chest Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the chest press: seated or standing, pressing two cable handles forward.', array['Adjust the weight to an appropriate amount and be seated, grasping the handles. Your upper arms should be about 45 degrees to the body, with your head and chest up. The elbows should be bent to about 90 degrees. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by extending through the elbow, pressing the handles together straight in front of you. Keep your shoulder blades retracted as you execute the movement.','After pausing at full extension, return to th starting position, keeping tension on the cables.','You can also execute this movement with your back off the pad, at an incline or decline, or alternate hands.']::text[], array['Chest up, shoulders down','Do not let the shoulders roll forward at the end']::text[], array['Locking the elbows hard','Leaning into the press','Rushing the return']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_chest_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Chest_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_press_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_press_band', 'Chest Press (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated or standing press that works the chest, front shoulders and triceps with a guided path.', array['Anchor the band behind you at chest height, or wrap it around your upper back.','Hold one end in each hand at chest level and step forward to take up the slack.']::text[], array['Press the handles forward until your arms are almost straight.','Pause briefly.','Return slowly until you feel a stretch across the chest.']::text[], array['Chest up, shoulders down','Do not let the shoulders roll forward at the end']::text[], array['Locking the elbows hard','Seat too high or too low','Rushing the return']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_press_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_press_machine', 'Chest Press (Machine)', array['seated chest press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated or standing press that works the chest, front shoulders and triceps with a guided path.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at mid-chest height.','Sit tall with your back against the pad and feet flat.','Pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Press the handles forward until your arms are almost straight.','Pause briefly.','Return slowly until you feel a stretch across the chest.']::text[], array['Chest up, shoulders down','Do not let the shoulders roll forward at the end']::text[], array['Locking the elbows hard','Seat too high or too low','Rushing the return']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_press_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Machine_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_cable_chest_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_cable_chest_press', 'Incline Cable Chest Press', array['Chest Press (Cable, Incline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Incline Cable Chest Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the chest press: on an incline bench between low cables, for the upper chest.', array['Adjust the weight to an appropriate amount and be seated, grasping the handles. Your upper arms should be about 45 degrees to the body, with your head and chest up. The elbows should be bent to about 90 degrees. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by extending through the elbow, pressing the handles together straight in front of you. Keep your shoulder blades retracted as you execute the movement.','After pausing at full extension, return to the starting position, keeping tension on the cables.']::text[], array['Chest up, shoulders down','Do not let the shoulders roll forward at the end']::text[], array['Locking the elbows hard','Bench angle too steep','Rushing the return']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_cable_chest_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Cable_Chest_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_press_iso_lateral')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_press_iso_lateral', 'Iso-Lateral Chest Press (Machine)', array['hammer strength chest press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated or standing press that works the chest, front shoulders and triceps with a guided path.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at mid-chest height.','Sit tall with your back against the pad and feet flat.','Pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Press the handles forward until your arms are almost straight.','Pause briefly.','Return slowly until you feel a stretch across the chest.']::text[], array['Chest up, shoulders down','Do not let the shoulders roll forward at the end']::text[], array['Locking the elbows hard','Seat too high or too low','Rushing the return']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_press_iso_lateral/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_Chest_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_cable_chest_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_cable_chest_press', 'Standing Cable Chest Press', array['Chest Press (Cable, Standing)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Cable Chest Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the chest press: standing in a split stance between two cables.', array['Position dual pulleys to chest height and select an appropriate weight. Stand a foot or two in front of the cables, holding one in each hand. You can stagger your stance for better stability.']::text[], array['Position the upper arm at a 90 degree angle with the shoulder blades together. This will be your starting position.','Keeping the rest of the body stationary, extend through the elbows to press the handles forward, drawing them together in front of you.','Pause at the top of the motion, and return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Chest up, shoulders down','Do not let the shoulders roll forward at the end']::text[], array['Locking the elbows hard','Leaning into the press','Rushing the return']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_cable_chest_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Cable_Chest_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'behind_head_chest_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'behind_head_chest_stretch', 'Behind Head Chest Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Behind Head Chest Stretch is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the chest.', array['Sit upright on the floor with your partner behind you.']::text[], array['Place your hands behind your hand, and push your elbows back as far as you can. Your partner should hold your elbows. This will be your starting position.','Gently attempt to pull your elbows forward with your hands still behind your head for 10 or more seconds. Your partner should prevent your elbows from moving.','Now, relax your muscles and have your partner gently pull the elbows back as far as it comfortable for you. Be sure to let your partner know when the stretch is adequate to prevent overstretching or injury.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/behind_head_chest_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Behind_Head_Chest_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_and_front_of_shoulder_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_and_front_of_shoulder_stretch', 'Chest And Front Of Shoulder Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Chest And Front Of Shoulder Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the chest.', array['Start off by standing with your legs together, holding a bodybar or a broomstick.']::text[], array['Take a slightly wider than shoulder width grip on the pole and hold it in front of you with your palms facing down.','Carefully lift the pole up and behind your head.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_and_front_of_shoulder_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chest_And_Front_Of_Shoulder_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_stretch_on_stability_ball')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_stretch_on_stability_ball', 'Chest Stretch on Stability Ball', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Chest Stretch on Stability Ball is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the chest.', array['Get on your hands and knees next to an exercise ball.']::text[], array['Place your elbows on top of the ball, keeping your arm out to your side. This will be your starting position.','Lower your torso towards the floor, keeping your elbow on top of the ball. Hold the stretch for 20-30 seconds, and repeat with the other arm.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_stretch_on_stability_ball/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chest_Stretch_on_Stability_Ball/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'elbows_back')::uuid, 'mfd', 'elbows_back', 'Elbows Back', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Elbows Back is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the chest.', array['Stand up straight.']::text[], array['Place both hands on your lower back, fingers pointing downward and elbows out.','Then gently pull your elbows back aiming to touch them together.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/elbows_back/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Elbows_Back/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'decline_bench_press_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'decline_bench_press_barbell', 'Decline Bench Press (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press with your head lower than your hips. It shortens the range of motion and emphasises the lower part of the chest.', array['Set a decline bench to about 15–30° and lock your legs under the pads.','Lie back with your shoulder blades pulled together.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Start with arms straight above your lower chest.','Lower the weight to your lower chest.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Control the descent']::text[], array['Lowering toward the neck','Bouncing off the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/decline_bench_press_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Decline_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'decline_bench_press_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'decline_bench_press_dumbbell', 'Decline Bench Press (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press with your head lower than your hips. It shortens the range of motion and emphasises the lower part of the chest.', array['Set a decline bench to about 15–30° and lock your legs under the pads.','Lie back with your shoulder blades pulled together.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Start with arms straight above your lower chest.','Lower the weight to your lower chest.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Control the descent']::text[], array['Lowering toward the neck','Bouncing off the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/decline_bench_press_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Decline_Dumbbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'decline_bench_press_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'decline_bench_press_machine', 'Decline Bench Press (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press with your head lower than your hips. It shortens the range of motion and emphasises the lower part of the chest.', array['Set a decline bench to about 15–30° and lock your legs under the pads.','Lie back with your shoulder blades pulled together.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Start with arms straight above your lower chest.','Lower the weight to your lower chest.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Control the descent']::text[], array['Lowering toward the neck','Bouncing off the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/decline_bench_press_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_Decline_Chest_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'decline_bench_press_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'decline_bench_press_smith', 'Decline Bench Press (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press with your head lower than your hips. It shortens the range of motion and emphasises the lower part of the chest.', array['Set a decline bench to about 15–30° and lock your legs under the pads.','Lie back with your shoulder blades pulled together.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Start with arms straight above your lower chest.','Lower the weight to your lower chest.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Control the descent']::text[], array['Lowering toward the neck','Bouncing off the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/decline_bench_press_smith/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Decline_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wide_grip_decline_barbell_bench_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wide_grip_decline_barbell_bench_press', 'Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Bench Press', array['Decline Bench Press (Wide Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Bench Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the decline bench press: a wider grip puts more load on the chest.', array['Lie back on a decline bench with the feet securely locked at the front of the bench. Using a wide, pronated (palms forward) grip that is around 3 inches away from shoulder width (for each hand), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms locked. The bar will be perpendicular to the torso and the floor. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['As you breathe in, come down slowly until you feel the bar on your lower chest.','After a second pause, bring the bar back to the starting position as you breathe out and push the bar using your chest muscles. Lock your arms and squeeze your chest in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly again. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Control the descent']::text[], array['Lowering toward the neck','Bouncing off the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wide_grip_decline_barbell_bench_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Decline_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squeeze_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squeeze_press', 'Dumbbell Squeeze Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A dumbbell press where you squeeze the dumbbells together the whole time, which keeps the chest working hard.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding two dumbbells together above your chest, palms facing each other.','Pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Squeeze the dumbbells together firmly.','Lower them to your chest while keeping them pressed together.','Press back up, still squeezing.']::text[], array['Squeeze as if crushing something between the dumbbells','Elbows close to your sides']::text[], array['Letting the dumbbells drift apart','Using weight too heavy to keep the squeeze']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squeeze_press_hex')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squeeze_press_hex', 'Hex Press (Dumbbell)', array['hex press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A dumbbell press where you squeeze the dumbbells together the whole time, which keeps the chest working hard.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding two dumbbells together above your chest, palms facing each other.','Pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Squeeze the dumbbells together firmly.','Lower them to your chest while keeping them pressed together.','Press back up, still squeezing.']::text[], array['Squeeze as if crushing something between the dumbbells','Elbows close to your sides']::text[], array['Letting the dumbbells drift apart','Using weight too heavy to keep the squeeze']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dynamic_chest_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dynamic_chest_stretch', 'Dynamic Chest Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Dynamic Chest Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the chest, with help from the upper back.', '{}'::text[], array['Stand with your hands together, arms extended directly in front of you. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your arms straight, quickly move your arms back as far as possible and back in again, similar to an exaggerated clapping motion. Repeat 5-10 times, increasing speed as you do so.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dynamic_chest_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dynamic_Chest_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternating_floor_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternating_floor_press', 'Alternating Floor Press', array['Floor Press (Kettlebell, Alternating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating Floor Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps. A variation of the floor press: two kettlebells pressed one at a time.', array['Lie on the floor with two kettlebells next to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Position one in place on your chest and then the other, gripping the kettlebells on the handle with the palms facing forward.','Extend both arms, so that the kettlebells are being held above your chest. Lower one kettlebell, bringing it to your chest and turn the wrist in the direction of the locked out kettlebell.','Raise the kettlebell and repeat on the opposite side.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternating_floor_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternating_Floor_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'extended_range_one_arm_kettlebell_floor_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'extended_range_one_arm_kettlebell_floor_press', 'Extended Range One-Arm Kettlebell Floor Press', array['Floor Press (Kettlebell, Extended Range)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Extended Range One-Arm Kettlebell Floor Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the floor press: single kettlebell; reach past the shoulder at the top.', '{}'::text[], array['Lie on the floor and position a kettlebell for one arm to press. The kettlebell should be held by the handle. The leg on the same side that you are pressing should be bent, with the knee crossing over the midline of the body.','Press the kettlebell by extending the elbow and adducting the arm, pressing it above your body. Return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/extended_range_one_arm_kettlebell_floor_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Extended_Range_One-Arm_Kettlebell_Floor_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'floor_press_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'floor_press_barbell', 'Floor Press (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A press lying on the floor. The floor stops your elbows partway, so it trains the top half of the press and is easy on the shoulders.', array['Lie on your back on the floor, knees bent or legs straight.','Position the weight over your chest with arms straight.','Pull your shoulder blades together.']::text[], array['Lower the weight until the backs of your upper arms gently touch the floor.','Pause briefly without relaxing.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/floor_press_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Floor_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'floor_press_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'floor_press_dumbbell', 'Floor Press (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A press lying on the floor. The floor stops your elbows partway, so it trains the top half of the press and is easy on the shoulders.', array['Lie on your back on the floor, knees bent or legs straight.','Position the weight over your chest with arms straight.','Pull your shoulder blades together.']::text[], array['Lower the weight until the backs of your upper arms gently touch the floor.','Pause briefly without relaxing.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/floor_press_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Floor_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_over_floor_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_over_floor_press', 'Leg-Over Floor Press', array['Floor Press (Kettlebell, Leg Over)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Leg-Over Floor Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the floor press: leg on the working side crossed over for a stable base.', array['Lie on the floor with one kettlebell in place on your chest, holding it by the handle. Extend leg on working side over leg on non-working side. Your free arm can be extended out to your side for support.']::text[], array['Press the kettlebll into a locked out position.','Lower the weight until the elbow touches the ground, keeping the kettlebell above the elbow. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_over_floor_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leg-Over_Floor_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_floor_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_floor_press', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Floor Press', array['Floor Press (Single Arm Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Floor Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the floor press: one kettlebell from the floor.', array['Lie on the floor holding a kettlebell with one hand, with your upper arm supported by the floor. The palm should be facing in.']::text[], array['Press the kettlebell straight up toward the ceiling, rotating your wrist.','Lower the kettlebell back to the starting position and repeat.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_floor_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Floor_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hammer_grip_incline_db_bench_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hammer_grip_incline_db_bench_press', 'Hammer Grip Incline DB Bench Press', array['Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell, Neutral Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Hammer Grip Incline DB Bench Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the incline bench press: palms face each other.', array['Lie back on an incline bench with a dumbbell on each hand on top of your thighs. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.']::text[], array['By using your thighs to help you get the dumbbells up, clean the dumbbells one arm at a time so that you can hold them at shoulder width.','Once at shoulder width, keep the palms of your hands with a neutral grip (palms facing each other). Keep your elbows flared out with the upper arms in line with the shoulders (perpendicular to the torso) and the elbows bent creating a 90-degree angle between the upper arm and the forearm. This will be your starting position.','Now bring down the weights slowly to your side as you breathe in. Keep full control of the dumbbells at all times.','As you breathe out, push the dumbbells up using your pectoral muscles. Lock your arms in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','When you are done, place the dumbbells back in your thighs and then on the floor. This is the safest manner to dispose of the dumbbells.']::text[], array['Elbows slightly tucked, not flared','Chest stays up toward the weight','Wrists stacked over elbows']::text[], array['Setting the bench too steep','Lowering to the lower chest or stomach','Arching so much the incline is lost']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hammer_grip_incline_db_bench_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hammer_Grip_Incline_DB_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_bench_press_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_bench_press_barbell', 'Incline Bench Press (Barbell)', array['incline press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press on a bench set to about 30°. The incline puts more emphasis on the upper chest and front shoulders.', array['Set the bench to about 30° (15–45° works; steeper turns it into a shoulder press).','Sit with your back flat against the pad and feet planted.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Start with arms straight above your upper chest.','Lower the weight to your upper chest, just below the collarbones.','Press back up until your arms are straight above your shoulders.']::text[], array['Elbows slightly tucked, not flared','Chest stays up toward the weight','Wrists stacked over elbows']::text[], array['Setting the bench too steep','Lowering to the lower chest or stomach','Arching so much the incline is lost']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_bench_press_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Incline_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_bench_press_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_bench_press_dumbbell', 'Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)', array['incline db press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press on a bench set to about 30°. The incline puts more emphasis on the upper chest and front shoulders.', array['Set the bench to about 30° (15–45° works; steeper turns it into a shoulder press).','Sit with your back flat against the pad and feet planted.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Start with arms straight above your upper chest.','Lower the weight to your upper chest, just below the collarbones.','Press back up until your arms are straight above your shoulders.']::text[], array['Elbows slightly tucked, not flared','Chest stays up toward the weight','Wrists stacked over elbows']::text[], array['Setting the bench too steep','Lowering to the lower chest or stomach','Arching so much the incline is lost']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_bench_press_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_bench_press_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_bench_press_smith', 'Incline Bench Press (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press on a bench set to about 30°. The incline puts more emphasis on the upper chest and front shoulders.', array['Set the bench to about 30° (15–45° works; steeper turns it into a shoulder press).','Sit with your back flat against the pad and feet planted.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Start with arms straight above your upper chest.','Lower the weight to your upper chest, just below the collarbones.','Press back up until your arms are straight above your shoulders.']::text[], array['Elbows slightly tucked, not flared','Chest stays up toward the weight','Wrists stacked over elbows']::text[], array['Setting the bench too steep','Lowering to the lower chest or stomach','Arching so much the incline is lost']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_bench_press_smith/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Incline_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_dumbbell_bench_with_palms_facing_in')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_dumbbell_bench_with_palms_facing_in', 'Incline Dumbbell Bench With Palms Facing In', array['Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell, Palms In)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Incline Dumbbell Bench With Palms Facing In is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the incline bench press: palms face each other throughout.', array['Lie back on an incline bench with a dumbbell on each hand on top of your thighs. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.']::text[], array['By using your thighs to help you get the dumbbells up, clean the dumbbells one arm at a time so that you can hold them at shoulder width.','Once at shoulder width, keep the palms of your hands with a neutral grip (palms facing each other). Keep your elbows flared out with the upper arms in line with the shoulders (perpendicular to the torso) and the elbows bent creating a 90-degree angle between the upper arm and the forearm. This will be your starting position.','Now bring down the weights slowly to your side as you breathe in. Keep full control of the dumbbells at all times.','As you breathe out, push the dumbbells up using your pectoral muscles. Lock your arms in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','When you are done, place the dumbbells back in your thighs and then on the floor. This is the safest manner to dispose of the dumbbells.']::text[], array['Elbows slightly tucked, not flared','Chest stays up toward the weight','Wrists stacked over elbows']::text[], array['Setting the bench too steep','Lowering to the lower chest or stomach','Arching so much the incline is lost']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_dumbbell_bench_with_palms_facing_in/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Dumbbell_Bench_With_Palms_Facing_In/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_chest_press_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_chest_press_machine', 'Incline Chest Press (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A machine version of the incline press. The fixed path makes it easy to learn and safe to push close to failure.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles line up with your upper chest.','Sit with your back against the pad and feet flat.','Pull your shoulder blades back.']::text[], array['Press the handles forward and up until your arms are almost straight.','Return slowly until you feel a stretch in the chest.']::text[], array['Keep your back on the pad','Control the way back']::text[], array['Seat too low, which turns it into a shoulder press','Letting the weight stack crash']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_chest_press_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_Incline_Chest_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'isometric_chest_squeezes')::uuid, 'mfd', 'isometric_chest_squeezes', 'Isometric Chest Squeezes', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'time', 'Isometric Chest Squeezes is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps.', array['While either seating or standing, bend your arms at a 90-degree angle and place the palms of your hands together in front of your chest. Tip: Your hands should be open with the palms together and fingers facing forward (perpendicular to your torso).']::text[], array['Push both hands against each other as you contract your chest. Start with slow tension and increase slowly. Keep breathing normally as you execute this contraction.','Hold for the recommended number of seconds.','Now release the tension slowly.','Rest for the recommended amount of time and repeat.']::text[], array['Press the palms together in front of the chest','Squeeze hard for 5–10 seconds','Keep the shoulders down']::text[], array['Shrugging','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/isometric_chest_squeezes/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Isometric_Chest_Squeezes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'isometric_wipers')::uuid, 'mfd', 'isometric_wipers', 'Isometric Wipers', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Isometric Wipers is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Assume a push-up position, supporting your weight on your hands and toes while keeping your body straight. Your hands should be just outside of shoulder width. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by shifting your body weight as far to one side as possible, allowing the elbow on that side to flex as you lower your body.','Reverse the motion by extending the flexed arm, pushing yourself up and then dropping to the other side.','Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.']::text[], array['Push-up position with a wide base','Shift the weight to one arm, then the other','Body stays in a straight line']::text[], array['Hips sagging','Moving too fast']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/isometric_wipers/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Isometric_Wipers/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_push_multiple_response')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_push_multiple_response', 'Chest Push (multiple response)', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Chest Push (multiple response) is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Begin in a kneeling position facing a wall or utilize a partner. Hold the ball with both hands tight into the chest.']::text[], array['Execute the pass by exploding forward and outward with the hips while pushing the ball as hard as possible.','Follow through by falling forward, catching yourself with your hands.','Immediately return to an upright position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_push_multiple_response/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chest_Push_multiple_response/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_push_single_response')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_push_single_response', 'Chest Push (single response)', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Chest Push (single response) is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Begin in a kneeling position holding the medicine ball with both hands tightly into the chest.']::text[], array['Execute the pass by exploding forward and outward with the hips while pushing the ball as far as possible.','Follow through by falling forward, catching yourself with your hands.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_push_single_response/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chest_Push_single_response/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_push_from_3_point_stance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_push_from_3_point_stance', 'Chest Push from 3 point stance', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Chest Push from 3 point stance is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Begin in a three point stance, squatted down with your back flat and one hand on the ground. Place the medicine ball directly in front of you.']::text[], array['To begin, take your first step as you pull the ball to your chest, positioning both hands to prepare for the throw.','As you execute the second step, explosively release the ball forward as hard as possible.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_push_from_3_point_stance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chest_Push_from_3_point_stance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_push_with_run_release')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_push_with_run_release', 'Chest Push with Run Release', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Chest Push with Run Release is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Begin in an athletic stance with the knees bent, hips back, and back flat. Hold the medicine ball near your legs. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['While taking your first step draw the medicine ball into your chest.','As you take the second step, explosively push the ball forward, immediately sprinting for 10 yards after the release. If you are really fast, you can catch your own pass!']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_push_with_run_release/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chest_Push_with_Run_Release/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'heavy_bag_thrust')::uuid, 'mfd', 'heavy_bag_thrust', 'Heavy Bag Thrust', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Heavy Bag Thrust is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Utilize a heavy bag for this exercise. Assume an upright stance next to the bag, with your feet staggered, fairly wide apart. Place your hand on the bag at about chest height. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by twisting at the waist, pushing the bag forward as hard as possible. Perform this move quickly, pushing the bag away from your body.','Receive the bag as it swings back by reversing these steps.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/heavy_bag_thrust/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Heavy_Bag_Thrust/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'medicine_ball_chest_pass')::uuid, 'mfd', 'medicine_ball_chest_pass', 'Medicine Ball Chest Pass', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Medicine Ball Chest Pass is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps.', array['You will need a partner for this exercise. Lacking one, this movement can be performed against a wall.']::text[], array['Begin facing your partner holding the medicine ball at your torso with both hands.','Pull the ball to your chest, and reverse the motion by extending through the elbows. For sports applications, you can take a step as you throw.','Your partner should catch the ball, and throw it back to you.','Receive the throw with both hands at chest height.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/medicine_ball_chest_pass/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Medicine_Ball_Chest_Pass/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'plate_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'plate_press', 'Plate Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing press with a weight plate held between the palms, pushed straight out from the chest.', array['Stand tall holding a plate at chest height between your flat palms.','Squeeze the plate hard.']::text[], array['Press the plate straight out until your arms are straight.','Bring it back to your chest under control.']::text[], array['Keep squeezing the plate the whole time','Ribs down, do not lean back']::text[], array['Letting the plate drop below chest height','Shrugging the shoulders']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'plate_press_svend')::uuid, 'mfd', 'plate_press_svend', 'Plate Squeeze (Svend Press)', array['svend press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing press with a weight plate held between the palms, pushed straight out from the chest.', array['Stand tall holding a plate at chest height between your flat palms.','Squeeze the plate hard.']::text[], array['Press the plate straight out until your arms are straight.','Bring it back to your chest under control.']::text[], array['Keep squeezing the plate the whole time','Ribs down, do not lean back']::text[], array['Letting the plate drop below chest height','Shrugging the shoulders']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/plate_press_svend/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Svend_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_raise_and_pullover')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_raise_and_pullover', 'Front Raise And Pullover', array['Pullover (Front Raise and Pullover)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Front Raise And Pullover is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the lats and triceps. A variation of the pullover: barbell raised from the thighs to overhead while lying on a bench.', array['Lie on a flat bench while holding a barbell using a palms down grip that is about 15 inches apart.']::text[], array['Place the bar on your upper thighs, extend your arms and lock them while keeping a slight bend on the elbows. This will be your starting position.','Now raise the weight using a semicircular motion and keeping your arms straight as you inhale. Continue the same movement until the bar is on the other side above your head . (Tip: the bar will travel approximately 180-degrees). At this point your arms should be parallel to the floor with the palms of your hands facing the ceiling.','Now return the barbell to the starting position by reversing the motion as you exhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Ribs down; do not arch to get more range','Elbows stay slightly bent']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows','Going deeper than your shoulders allow']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_raise_and_pullover/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Raise_And_Pullover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wide_grip_decline_barbell_pullover')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wide_grip_decline_barbell_pullover', 'Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Pullover', array['Pullover (Barbell, Decline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Pullover is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the pullover: decline bench, wide grip.', array['Lie down on a decline bench with both legs securely locked in position. Reach for the barbell behind the head using a pronated grip (palms facing out). Make sure to grab the barbell wider than shoulder width apart for this exercise. Slowly lift the barbell up from the floor by using your arms.']::text[], array['When positioned properly, your arms should be fully extended and perpendicular to the floor. This is the starting position.','Begin by moving the barbell back down in a semicircular motion as if you were going to place it on the floor, but instead, stop when the arms are parallel to the floor. Tip: Keep the arms fully extended at all times. The movement should only happen at the shoulder joint. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Now bring the barbell up while exhaling until you are back at the starting position. Remember to keep full control of the barbell at all times.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.','When finished with your set, slowly lower the barbell back down until it is level with your head and release it.']::text[], array['Ribs down; do not arch to get more range','Elbows stay slightly bent']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows','Going deeper than your shoulders allow']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wide_grip_decline_barbell_pullover/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Decline_Barbell_Pullover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_clap')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_clap', 'Clap Push Ups', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_clap/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Plyo_Push-up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clock_push_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clock_push_up', 'Clock Push-Up', array['Push Up (Clock)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Clock Push-Up is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the push up: hands walk around in a circle between reps.', array['Move into a prone position on the floor, supporting your weight on your hands and toes.']::text[], array['Your arms should be fully extended with the hands around shoulder width. Keep your body straight throughout the movement. This will be your starting position.','Descend by flexing at the elbow, lowering your chest toward the ground.','At the bottom, reverse the motion by pushing yourself up through elbow extension as quickly as possible until you are air borne. Aim to "jump" 12-18 inches to one side.','As you accelerate up, move your outside foot away from your direction of travel. Leaving the ground, shift your body about 30 degrees for the next repetition.','Return to the starting position and repeat the exercise, working all the way around until you are back where you started.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clock_push_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clock_Push-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_decline')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_decline', 'Decline Push Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_decline/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Decline_Push-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'drop_push')::uuid, 'mfd', 'drop_push', 'Drop Push', array['Push Up (Drop Push)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Drop Push is an intermediate-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the push up: drop from raised platforms to the floor and push back up explosively.', array['Position low boxes or other platforms 2-3 feet apart.']::text[], array['Move to a pushup position between them, supporting yourself by placing your hands on the boxes.','With good posture, drop from the platforms by pressing up and moving your hands to shoulder width, cushioning your landing by absorbing the impact through the arm.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/drop_push/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Drop_Push/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_incline')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_incline', 'Incline Push Ups', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_incline/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_push_up_depth_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_push_up_depth_jump', 'Incline Push-Up Depth Jump', array['Push Up (Incline Depth Jump)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Incline Push-Up Depth Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the push up: explosive incline push-up, landing on the floor and pushing back up to the bench.', array['For this drill you will need a box about 12 inches high, and two thick mats or aerobics steps.']::text[], array['Place the steps just outside of your shoulders, and place your feet on top of the box so that you are in an incline pushup position, your hands just inside the steps. This will be your starting position.','Begin by bending at the elbows to lower your body, quickly reversing position to push your body off of the ground. As you leave the ground, move your hands onto the steps, bending your elbows to absorb the impact.','Repeat the motion to return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_push_up_depth_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Depth_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_push_up_medium')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_push_up_medium', 'Incline Push-Up Medium', array['Push Up (Incline, Medium Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Incline Push-Up Medium is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps. A variation of the push up: hands on a raised surface, shoulder width.', array['Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.']::text[], array['Place your hands on the bar, with your hands about shoulder width apart.','Position your feet back from the bar with arms and body straight. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your body straight, lower your chest to the bar by bending the arms.','Return to the starting position by extending the elbows, pressing yourself back up.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_push_up_medium/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Medium/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_push_up_reverse_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_push_up_reverse_grip', 'Incline Push-Up Reverse Grip', array['Push Up (Incline, Reverse Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Incline Push-Up Reverse Grip is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps. A variation of the push up: hands on a bar, palms facing you.', array['Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.']::text[], array['Place your hands on the bar palms up, with your hands about shoulder width apart.','Position your feet back from the bar with arms and body straight. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your body straight, lower your chest to the bar by bending the arms.','Return to the starting position by extending the elbows, pressing yourself back up.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_push_up_reverse_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Reverse_Grip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_push_up_wide')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_push_up_wide', 'Incline Push-Up Wide', array['Push Up (Incline, Wide)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Incline Push-Up Wide is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps. A variation of the push up: hands on a raised surface, wider than the shoulders.', array['Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.']::text[], array['Place your hands on the bar, with your hands wider than shoulder width.','Position your feet back from the bar with arms and body straight. Your arms should be perpendicular to the body. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your body straight, lower your chest to the bar by bending the arms.','Return to the starting position by extending the elbows, pressing yourself back up.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_push_up_wide/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Wide/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_kneeling')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_kneeling', 'Kneeling Push Up', array['knee push up']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_one_arm')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_one_arm', 'One Arm Push Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_one_arm/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Arm_Push-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_plank')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_plank', 'Plank Pushup', array['plank up','up down plank']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Moving between a forearm plank and a high plank, one arm at a time.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Start in a forearm plank.','Place one hand under your shoulder and push up, then the other, to reach a high plank.','Lower back down to your forearms one arm at a time.','Alternate the leading arm each rep.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top','Keep your hips level; avoid rocking side to side']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'plyo_kettlebell_pushups')::uuid, 'mfd', 'plyo_kettlebell_pushups', 'Plyo Kettlebell Pushups', array['Push Up (Plyometric Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Plyo Kettlebell Pushups is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the push up: push up explosively, moving the hands between the floor and a kettlebell.', array['Place a kettlebell on the floor. Place yourself in a pushup position, on your toes with one hand on the ground and one hand holding the kettlebell, with your elbows extended. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by lowering yourself as low as you can, keeping your back straight.','Quickly and forcefully reverse direction, pushing yourself up to the other side of the kettlebell, switching hands as you do so. Continue the movement by descending and repeating the movement back and forth.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/plyo_kettlebell_pushups/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Plyo_Kettlebell_Pushups/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_standard')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_standard', 'Push Up', array['pushup','press up']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_standard/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Pushups/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_weighted', 'Push Up (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_close_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_close_grip', 'Push Up - Close Grip', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_close_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Push-Ups_-_Close_Triceps_Position/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_wide')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_wide', 'Push-Up Wide', array['Push Up (Wide)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Push-Up Wide is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps. A variation of the push up: hands wider than the shoulders puts more on the chest.', array['With your hands wide apart, support your body on your toes and hands in a plank position. Your elbows should be extended and your body straight. Do not allow your hips to sag. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['To begin, allow the elbows to flex, lowering your chest to the floor as you inhale.','Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the starting position by extending the elbows. Exhale as you perform this step.','After pausing at the contracted position, repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_wide/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Push-Up_Wide/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_ups_with_feet_on_an_exercise_ball')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_ups_with_feet_on_an_exercise_ball', 'Push-Ups With Feet On An Exercise Ball', array['Push Up (Feet on Ball)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Push-Ups With Feet On An Exercise Ball is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the push up: feet on a ball; harder for the core.', array['Lie on the floor face down and place your hands about 36 inches apart from each other holding your torso up at arms length.']::text[], array['Place your toes on top of an exercise ball. This will allow your body to be elevated.','Lower yourself until your chest almost touches the floor as you inhale.','Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the starting position and squeeze your chest. Breathe out as you perform this step.','After a second pause at the contracted position, repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_ups_with_feet_on_an_exercise_ball/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Push-Ups_With_Feet_On_An_Exercise_Ball/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pushups_close_and_wide_hand_positions')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pushups_close_and_wide_hand_positions', 'Pushups (Close and Wide Hand Positions)', array['Push Up (Close and Wide)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Pushups (Close and Wide Hand Positions) is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the push up: alternate close and wide hand positions.', array['Lie on the floor face down and body straight with your toes on the floor and the hands wider than shoulder width for a wide hand position and closer than shoulder width for a close hand position. Make sure you are holding your torso up at arms length.']::text[], array['Lower yourself until your chest almost touches the floor as you inhale.','Using your pectoral muscles, press your upper body back up to the starting position and squeeze your chest. Breathe out as you perform this step.','After a second pause at the contracted position, repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pushups_close_and_wide_hand_positions/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Pushups_Close_and_Wide_Hand_Positions/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_rings')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_rings', 'Ring Push Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'suspended_push_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'suspended_push_up', 'Suspended Push-Up', array['Push Up (Suspension)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Suspended Push-Up is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the triceps. A variation of the push up: hands in suspension straps; the instability works the chest and shoulders harder.', array['Anchor your suspension straps securely to the top of a rack or other object.']::text[], array['Leaning into the straps, take a handle in each hand and move into a push-up plank position. You should be as close to parallel to the ground as you can manage with your arms fully extended, maintaining good posture.','Maintaining a straight, rigid torso, descend slowly by allowing the elbows to flex.','Continue until your elbows break 90 degrees, pausing before you extend to return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/suspended_push_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Suspended_Push-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_to_side_plank')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_to_side_plank', 'Push Up to Side Plank', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Push Up to Side Plank is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the abs & core and triceps.', array['Get into pushup position on the toes with your hands just outside of shoulder width.']::text[], array['Perform a pushup by allowing the elbows to flex. As you descend, keep your body straight.','Do one pushup and as you come up, shift your weight on the left side of the body, twist to the side while bringing the right arm up towards the ceiling in a side plank.','Lower the arm back to the floor for another pushup and then twist to the other side.','Repeat the series, alternating each side, for 10 or more reps.']::text[], array['Do a full push-up','Rotate onto one hand into a side plank','Return and alternate sides']::text[], array['Hips sagging in the side plank','Rushing the rotation']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_up_to_side_plank/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Push_Up_to_Side_Plank/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'forward_drag_with_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'forward_drag_with_press', 'Forward Drag with Press', array['Sled Pull (Forward Drag and Press)']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Forward Drag with Press is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the chest, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings, quadriceps and triceps. A variation of the sled pull: walking forward, pressing the straps out in front on each step.', '{}'::text[], array['Attach a dual handled chain or rope attachment to the sled. You should be facing away from the sled, holding a handle in each hand.','Begin the movement by moving forward for one step. Leaning forward, extend through the legs and hips to move, pausing with each step to extend through the elbows, pressing your hands forward. Step forward until you return to the start position prepared to press.']::text[], array['Stay low and drive through the legs']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/forward_drag_with_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Forward_Drag_with_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kneeling_forearm_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kneeling_forearm_stretch', 'Kneeling Forearm Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Kneeling Forearm Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the forearms.', '{}'::text[], array['Start by kneeling on a mat with your palms flat and your fingers pointing back toward your knees.','Slowly lean back keeping your palms flat on the floor until you feel a stretch in your wrists and forearms. Hold for 20-30 seconds.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulder relaxed and down','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Pulling hard on the joint','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kneeling_forearm_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kneeling_Forearm_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'concentration_curl_reverse_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'concentration_curl_reverse_grip', 'Reverse Grip Concentration Curl', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated one-arm curl with the elbow braced against the inner thigh, which removes any swinging.', array['Sit on a bench with legs apart.','Hold a dumbbell and rest the back of that upper arm against your inner thigh.']::text[], array['Curl the dumbbell toward your shoulder.','Squeeze at the top.','Lower until the arm is straight.']::text[], array['Upper arm stays pressed into the thigh','Turn the little finger up at the top']::text[], array['Lifting the elbow off the thigh','Using the shoulder']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dead_hang')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dead_hang', 'Dead Hang', array['bar hang']::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Simply hanging from a bar for time. It builds grip strength and decompresses the shoulders.', array['Grip a pull-up bar overhand, about shoulder-width apart.']::text[], array['Lift your feet and hang with straight arms.','Keep a light tension in the shoulders rather than fully collapsing.','Hold for the target time, then step down.']::text[], array['Relax the legs','Breathe steadily']::text[], array['Swinging','Holding your breath']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_circles')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_circles', 'Wrist Circles', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Wrist Circles is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the forearms.', array['Start by standing straight with your feet being shoulder width apart from each other. Elevate your arms to the side of you until they are fully extended and parallel to the floor at a height that is evenly aligned with your shoulders. Tip: Your torso and arms should form the letter "T: Your palms should be facing down. This is the starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping your entire body stationary except for the wrists, begin to rotate both wrists forward in a circular motion. Tip: Pretend that you are trying to draw circles by using your hands as the brush. Breathe normally as you perform this exercise.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_circles/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wrist_Circles/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'farmers_walk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'farmers_walk', 'Farmers Walk', array['farmer carry','farmer''s walk']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Walking while holding heavy weights at your sides. Builds grip, traps and a strong core.', array['Stand between two heavy dumbbells, kettlebells or farmer handles.','Squat or hinge down with a flat back and pick them up.']::text[], array['Stand tall with shoulders back and down.','Walk with short, quick steps for the set distance.','Set the weights down with a flat back.']::text[], array['Tall posture; do not lean','Squeeze the handles hard']::text[], array['Rounding the shoulders forward','Leaning to one side']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/farmers_walk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Farmers_Walk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_lying_pronation')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_lying_pronation', 'Dumbbell Lying Pronation', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Lying Pronation is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms.', array['Lie on a flat bench face down with one arm holding a dumbbell and the other hand on top of the bench folded so that you can rest your head on it.']::text[], array['Bend the elbows of the arm holding the dumbbell so that it creates a 90-degree angle between the upper arm and the forearm.','Now raise the upper arm so that the forearm is perpendicular to the floor and the upper arm is perpendicular to your torso. Tip: The upper arm should be parallel to the floor and also creating a 90-degree angle with your torso. This will be your starting position.','As you breathe out, externally rotate your forearm so that the dumbbell is lifted forward as you maintain the 90 degree angle bend between the upper arms and the forearm. You will continue this external rotation until the forearm is parallel to the floor. At this point you will hold the contraction for a second.','As you breathe in, slowly go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Forearm supported, elbow still','Rotate slowly through the full range','Hold the dumbbell off-centre to make it harder']::text[], array['Moving the elbow or shoulder','Going too heavy and losing control']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_lying_pronation/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_Pronation/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_lying_supination')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_lying_supination', 'Dumbbell Lying Supination', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Lying Supination is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms.', array['Lie sideways on a flat bench with one arm holding a dumbbell and the other hand on top of the bench folded so that you can rest your head on it.']::text[], array['Bend the elbows of the arm holding the dumbbell so that it creates a 90-degree angle between the upper arm and the forearm.','Now raise the upper arm so that the forearm is parallel to the floor and perpendicular to your torso (Tip: So the forearm will be directly in front of you). The upper arm will be stationary by your torso and should be parallel to the floor (aligned with your torso at all times). This will be your starting position.','As you breathe out, externally rotate your forearm so that the dumbbell is lifted up in a semicircle motion as you maintain the 90 degree angle bend between the upper arms and the forearm. You will continue this external rotation until the forearm is perpendicular to the floor and the torso pointing towards the ceiling. At this point you will hold the contraction for a second.','As you breathe in, slowly go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and then switch to the other arm.']::text[], array['Forearm supported, elbow still','Rotate slowly through the full range','Hold the dumbbell off-centre to make it harder']::text[], array['Moving the elbow or shoulder','Going too heavy and losing control']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_lying_supination/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_Supination/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_rotations_with_straight_bar')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_rotations_with_straight_bar', 'Wrist Rotations with Straight Bar', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Wrist Rotations with Straight Bar is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms.', array['Hold a barbell with both hands and your palms facing down; hands spaced about shoulder width. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Alternating between each of your hands, perform the movement by extending the wrist as though you were rolling up a newspaper. Continue alternating back and forth until failure.','Reverse the motion by flexing the wrist, rolling the opposite direction. Continue the alternating motion until failure.']::text[], array['Forearm supported, elbow still','Rotate slowly through the full range','Hold the dumbbell off-centre to make it harder']::text[], array['Moving the elbow or shoulder','Going too heavy and losing control']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_rotations_with_straight_bar/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wrist_Rotations_with_Straight_Bar/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'plate_pinch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'plate_pinch', 'Plate Pinch', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Plate Pinch is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms.', array['Grab two wide-rimmed plates and put them together with the smooth sides facing outward']::text[], array['Use your fingers to grip the outside part of the plate and your thumb for the other side thus holding both plates together. This is the starting position.','Squeeze the plate with your fingers and thumb. Hold this position for as long as you can.','Repeat for the recommended amount of sets prescribed in your program.','Switch arms and repeat the movements.']::text[], array['Squeeze as hard as possible for the whole set','Smooth plates and a thumb-against-fingers pinch','Time each hold']::text[], array['Letting the plates slide','Bending the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/plate_pinch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Plate_Pinch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_olympic_plate_hand_squeeze')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_olympic_plate_hand_squeeze', 'Standing Olympic Plate Hand Squeeze', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Olympic Plate Hand Squeeze is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms, with help from the biceps.', array['To begin, stand straight while holding a weight plate by the ridge at arm''s length in each hand using a neutral grip (palms facing in). You feet should be shoulder width apart from each other. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Lower the plates until the fingers are nearly extended but can still hold weights. Inhale as you lower the plates.','Now raise the plates back to the starting position as you exhale by closing your hands.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions prescribed in your program.']::text[], array['Squeeze as hard as possible for the whole set','Smooth plates and a thumb-against-fingers pinch','Time each hold']::text[], array['Letting the plates slide','Bending the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_olympic_plate_hand_squeeze/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Olympic_Plate_Hand_Squeeze/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bottoms_up_clean_from_the_hang_position')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bottoms_up_clean_from_the_hang_position', 'Bottoms-Up Clean From The Hang Position', array['Kettlebell Clean (Bottoms Up)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bottoms-Up Clean From The Hang Position is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms, with help from the biceps. A variation of the kettlebell clean: caught upside down, which demands a strong grip.', '{}'::text[], array['Initiate the exercise by standing upright with a kettlebell in one hand.','Swing the kettlebell back forcefully and then reverse the motion forcefully. Crush the kettlebell handle as hard as possible and raise the kettlebell to your shoulder.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bottoms_up_clean_from_the_hang_position/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bottoms-Up_Clean_From_The_Hang_Position/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_curl_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_curl_barbell', 'Reverse Curl (Barbell)', array['overhand curl']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A curl with an overhand (palms down) grip. It focuses on the forearms and brachialis.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with an overhand grip, arms straight.']::text[], array['Curl the weight up keeping the palms facing down.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Wrists stay straight','Elbows pinned']::text[], array['Letting the wrists bend back','Swinging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_curl_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Barbell_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_curl_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_curl_cable', 'Reverse Curl (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A curl with an overhand (palms down) grip. It focuses on the forearms and brachialis.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with an overhand grip, arms straight.']::text[], array['Curl the weight up keeping the palms facing down.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Wrists stay straight','Elbows pinned']::text[], array['Letting the wrists bend back','Swinging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_curl_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Cable_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_curl_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_curl_dumbbell', 'Reverse Curl (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A curl with an overhand (palms down) grip. It focuses on the forearms and brachialis.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with an overhand grip, arms straight.']::text[], array['Curl the weight up keeping the palms facing down.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Wrists stay straight','Elbows pinned']::text[], array['Letting the wrists bend back','Swinging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_curl_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Reverse_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rickshaw_carry')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rickshaw_carry', 'Rickshaw Carry', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Rickshaw Carry is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the forearms, with help from the abs & core, calves, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, quadriceps and traps.', '{}'::text[], array['Position the frame at the starting point, and load with the appropriate weight. Standing in the center of the frame, begin by gripping the handles and driving through your heels to lift the frame. Ensure your chest and head are up and your back is straight.','Immediately begin walking briskly with quick, controlled steps. Keep your chest up and head forward, and make sure you continue breathing. Bring the frame to the ground after you have reached the end point.']::text[], array['Brace before you lift and stay tall','Short, quick steps','Eyes ahead']::text[], array['Long strides that make the load swing','Leaning forward','Holding the breath for the whole distance']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rickshaw_carry/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rickshaw_Carry/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_curl_behind_back')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_curl_behind_back', 'Behind the Back Wrist Curl (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Curling the wrists up with palms facing up to train the forearm flexors and grip.', array['Stand holding a barbell behind your thighs with palms facing back.']::text[], array['Let the weight roll down toward your fingertips.','Curl your wrists up as high as possible.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_curl_behind_back/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Palms-Up_Barbell_Behind_The_Back_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_curl_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_curl_cable', 'Cable Wrist Curl', array['cable wrist curls','cabel wrist curls']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Curling the wrists up with palms facing up to train the forearm flexors and grip.', array['Attach a straight bar to a low pulley.','Kneel or sit facing the stack with forearms on a bench, palms up.']::text[], array['Let the weight roll down toward your fingertips.','Curl your wrists up as high as possible.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_curl_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'finger_curls')::uuid, 'mfd', 'finger_curls', 'Finger Curls', array['Wrist Curl (Finger Curls)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Finger Curls is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist curl: let the bar roll down to the fingertips, then curl it back into the palm.', array['Hold a barbell with both hands and your palms facing up; hands spaced about shoulder width.']::text[], array['Place your feet flat on the floor, at a distance that is slightly wider than shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.','Lower the bar as far as possible by extending the fingers. Allowing the bar to roll down the hands, catch the bar with the final joint in the fingers.','Now curl bar up as high as possible by closing your hands while exhaling. Hold the contraction at the top.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/finger_curls/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Finger_Curls/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'palms_up_barbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'palms_up_barbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench', 'Palms-Up Barbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench', array['Wrist Curl (Barbell, Over Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Palms-Up Barbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist curl: kneeling, forearms on a bench.', array['Start out by placing a barbell on one side of a flat bench.']::text[], array['Kneel down on both of your knees so that your body is facing the flat bench.','Use your arms to grab the barbell with a supinated grip (palms up) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat bench. Your wrists should be hanging over the edge.','Start out by curling your wrist upwards and exhaling.','Slowly lower your wrists back down to the starting position while inhaling.','Your forearms should be stationary as your wrist is the only movement needed to perform this exercise.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/palms_up_barbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Palms-Up_Barbell_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'palms_up_dumbbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'palms_up_dumbbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench', 'Palms-Up Dumbbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench', array['Wrist Curl (Dumbbell, Over Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Palms-Up Dumbbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist curl: kneeling, forearms on a bench.', array['Start out by placing two dumbbells on one side of a flat bench.']::text[], array['Kneel down on both of your knees so that your body is facing the flat bench.','Use your arms to grab both of the dumbbells with a supinated grip (palms up) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat bench. Your wrists should be hanging over the edge.','Start out by curling your wrist upwards and exhaling.','Slowly lower your wrists back down to the starting position while inhaling. Make sure to inhale during this part of the exercise.','Your forearms should be stationary as your wrist is the only movement needed to perform this exercise.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/palms_up_dumbbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Palms-Up_Dumbbell_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_one_arm_dumbbell_palms_up_wrist_curl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_one_arm_dumbbell_palms_up_wrist_curl', 'Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Up Wrist Curl', array['Wrist Curl (Single Arm Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Up Wrist Curl is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist curl: one arm, forearm on the thigh.', array['Sit on a flat bench with a dumbbell in your right hand.']::text[], array['Place your feet flat on the floor, at a distance that is slightly wider than shoulder width apart.','Lean forward and place your right forearm on top of your upper right thigh with your palm up. Tip: Make sure that the front of the wrist lies on top of your knees. This will be your starting position.','Lower the dumbbell as far as possible as you keep a tight grip on the dumbbell. Inhale as you perform this movement.','Now curl the dumbbell as high as possible as you contract the forearms and as you exhale. Keep the contraction for a second before you lower again. Tip: The only movement should happen at the wrist.','Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions, switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_one_arm_dumbbell_palms_up_wrist_curl/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Palms-Up_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_curl_seated_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_curl_seated_dumbbell', 'Seated Palms Up Wrist Curl', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Curling the wrists up with palms facing up to train the forearm flexors and grip.', array['Sit with your forearms resting on your thighs or a bench, palms up, wrists just past the edge.']::text[], array['Let the weight roll down toward your fingertips.','Curl your wrists up as high as possible.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_curl_seated_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Palms-Up_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_two_arm_palms_up_low_pulley_wrist_curl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_two_arm_palms_up_low_pulley_wrist_curl', 'Seated Two-Arm Palms-Up Low-Pulley Wrist Curl', array['Wrist Curl (Cable, Two Arms)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated Two-Arm Palms-Up Low-Pulley Wrist Curl is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist curl: low pulley with a bar.', array['Put a bench in front of a low pulley machine that has a barbell or EZ Curl attachment on it.']::text[], array['Move the bench far enough away so that when you bring the handle to the top of your thighs tension is created on the cable due to the weight stack being moved up.','Now hold the handle with both hands, palms up, using a shoulder-width grip.','Step back and sit on the bench with your feet about shoulder width apart, firmly on the floor.','Lean forward and place the forearms on your thighs with the back of your wrists over your knees. This will be your starting position.','Lower the bar as far as possible, while inhaling and keeping a tight grip.','Now curl the bar up as high as possible while contracting the forearms. Tip: Only the wrist should move; not the forearms.','After a second contraction at the top go back to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_two_arm_palms_up_low_pulley_wrist_curl/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Two-Arm_Palms-Up_Low-Pulley_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_curl_seated_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_curl_seated_barbell', 'Seated Wrist Curl (Barbell)', array['forearm curl']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Curling the wrists up with palms facing up to train the forearm flexors and grip.', array['Sit with your forearms resting on your thighs or a bench, palms up, wrists just past the edge.']::text[], array['Let the weight roll down toward your fingertips.','Curl your wrists up as high as possible.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Full range: fingers to wrist curl']::text[], array['Lifting the forearms','Bouncing the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_curl_seated_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Palm-Up_Barbell_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'palms_down_dumbbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'palms_down_dumbbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench', 'Palms-Down Dumbbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench', array['Wrist Extension (Dumbbell, Over Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Palms-Down Dumbbell Wrist Curl Over A Bench is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist extension: kneeling, forearms on a bench.', array['Start out by placing two dumbbells on one side of a flat bench.']::text[], array['Kneel down on both of your knees so that your body is facing the flat bench.','Use your arms to grab both of the dumbbells with a pronated grip (palms facing down) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat bench. Your wrists should be hanging over the edge.','Start out by curling your wrist upwards and exhaling.','Slowly lower your wrists back down to the starting position while inhaling.','Your forearms should be stationary as your wrist is the only movement needed to perform this exercise.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Small, controlled movement']::text[], array['Going too heavy','Moving the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/palms_down_dumbbell_wrist_curl_over_a_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Palms-Down_Dumbbell_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'palms_down_wrist_curl_over_a_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'palms_down_wrist_curl_over_a_bench', 'Palms-Down Wrist Curl Over A Bench', array['Wrist Extension (Barbell, Over Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Palms-Down Wrist Curl Over A Bench is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist extension: kneeling, forearms on a bench.', array['Start out by placing a barbell on one side of a flat bench.']::text[], array['Kneel down on both of your knees so that your body is facing the flat bench.','Use your arms to grab the barbell with a pronated grip (palms down) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the flat bench. Your wrists should be hanging over the edge.','Start out by curling your wrist upwards and exhaling.','Slowly lower your wrists back down to the starting position while inhaling.','Your forearms should be stationary as your wrist is the only movement needed to perform this exercise.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Small, controlled movement']::text[], array['Going too heavy','Moving the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/palms_down_wrist_curl_over_a_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl_Over_A_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_extension_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_extension_dumbbell', 'Reverse Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the back of the hands up with palms facing down to train the forearm extensors.', array['Sit with forearms on your thighs or a bench, palms down, wrists just past the edge.']::text[], array['Lift the back of your hands up as high as possible.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Small, controlled movement']::text[], array['Going too heavy','Moving the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_extension_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_one_arm_dumbbell_palms_down_wrist_curl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_one_arm_dumbbell_palms_down_wrist_curl', 'Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Down Wrist Curl', array['Wrist Extension (Single Arm Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Down Wrist Curl is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the forearms. A variation of the wrist extension: one arm, forearm on the thigh.', array['Sit on a flat bench with a dumbbell in your right hand.']::text[], array['Place your feet flat on the floor, at a distance that is slightly wider than shoulder width apart.','Lean forward and place your right forearm on top of your upper right thigh with your palm down. Tip: Make sure that the back of the wrist lies on top of your knees. This will be your starting position.','Lower the dumbbell as far as possible as you keep a tight grip on the dumbbell. Inhale as you perform this movement.','Now curl the dumbbell as high as possible as you contract the forearms and as you exhale. Keep the contraction for a second before you lower again. Tip: The only movement should happen at the wrist.','Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions, switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Small, controlled movement']::text[], array['Going too heavy','Moving the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_one_arm_dumbbell_palms_down_wrist_curl/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_extension_seated_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_extension_seated_barbell', 'Seated Wrist Extension (Barbell)', array['reverse wrist curl']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the back of the hands up with palms facing down to train the forearm extensors.', array['Sit with forearms on your thighs or a bench, palms down, wrists just past the edge.']::text[], array['Lift the back of your hands up as high as possible.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Forearms stay still','Small, controlled movement']::text[], array['Going too heavy','Moving the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_extension_seated_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Palms-Down_Barbell_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wrist_roller')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wrist_roller', 'Wrist Roller', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Rolling a weight up and down on a rope wound around a handle, using only your wrists.', array['Hold the roller with both hands, arms straight in front at shoulder height, palms down.']::text[], array['Roll the handle one hand at a time to wind the rope up until the weight reaches the handle.','Unwind it slowly back down.']::text[], array['Arms stay straight and level','Control the way down']::text[], array['Letting the arms drop','Letting the weight drop fast']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wrist_roller/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wrist_Roller/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_pull_through')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_pull_through', 'Cable Pull Through', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Facing away from a low cable, you hinge forward and pull a rope through your legs by driving the hips forward.', array['Attach a rope to a low pulley and face away from it.','Hold the rope between your legs and step forward, feet wider than hips.']::text[], array['Hinge back, letting the rope pull your hands between your legs.','Drive your hips forward to stand up, squeezing the glutes.']::text[], array['It is a hinge, not a squat','Arms just hold the rope']::text[], array['Pulling with the arms','Leaning back at the top']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_pull_through/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Pull_Through/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean', 'Clean', array['squat clean']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the barbell from the floor to the front of the shoulders in one explosive movement, catching it in a squat.', array['Stand with the bar over mid-foot, feet hip-width.','Grip just outside the legs, hook grip if you know it.','Hips higher than knees, back flat, shoulders over the bar, arms straight.']::text[], array['Push the floor away to lift the bar to mid-thigh, keeping the back angle.','Jump explosively: extend hips, knees and ankles and shrug.','Pull yourself under the bar and turn the elbows fast to catch it on your shoulders in a front squat.','Stand up to finish.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Patient off the floor, explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_hang')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_hang', 'Hang Clean', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'A clean that starts standing with the bar at the hips, lowered to just above the knees, instead of from the floor.', array['Stand holding the bar at the hips with a clean grip.','Hinge slightly so the bar slides to just above the knees.']::text[], array['From the hang position just above the knees, jump explosively: extend hips, knees and ankles and shrug.','Pull yourself under the bar and turn the elbows fast to catch it on your shoulders.','Stand up to finish.','Lower the bar back to the hips for the next rep.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_hang/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hang_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_power')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_power', 'Power Clean', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the barbell from the floor to the front of the shoulders in one explosive movement, catching it in a squat.', array['Stand with the bar over mid-foot, feet hip-width.','Grip just outside the legs, hook grip if you know it.','Hips higher than knees, back flat, shoulders over the bar, arms straight.']::text[], array['Push the floor away to lift the bar to mid-thigh, keeping the back angle.','Jump explosively: extend hips, knees and ankles and shrug.','Pull yourself under the bar and turn the elbows fast to catch it on your shoulders in a front squat.','Stand up to finish.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Patient off the floor, explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_power/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Power_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_pull')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_pull', 'Clean Pull', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'The pulling part of the clean without the catch: an explosive pull from the floor finishing with full extension and a shrug.', array['Set up exactly as for the clean.']::text[], array['Lift the bar to mid-thigh with the same back angle.','Drive explosively through the legs and hips and shrug hard.','Let the bar come back down under control.']::text[], array['Full extension of hips, knees and ankles','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Bending the arms early','Leaning back excessively']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_pull/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clean_Pull/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_and_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_and_jerk', 'Clean and Jerk', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'The full Olympic lift: a clean to the shoulders followed by a jerk to straight arms overhead.', array['Set up as for the clean.']::text[], array['Clean the bar to your shoulders and stand up.','Reset your feet and breathe.','Dip and drive the bar up, then drop under it into a split or squat with arms locked.','Recover to standing with feet together.']::text[], array['Treat the clean and the jerk as two separate efforts','Vertical dip and drive']::text[], array['Pressing the bar out instead of dropping under it']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_and_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clean_and_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_and_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_and_press', 'Clean and Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cleaning the bar to your shoulders and then strictly pressing it overhead.', array['Set up as for the clean.']::text[], array['Clean the bar to the front of your shoulders.','Brace and press it overhead to straight arms.','Lower it to the shoulders, then back to the floor.']::text[], array['Brace again before the press']::text[], array['Leaning back to press']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_and_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clean_and_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'curtsy_lunge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'curtsy_lunge', 'Curtsy Lunge (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A lunge where the back leg crosses diagonally behind the front leg, like a curtsy. Targets the glutes, including the sides.', array['Stand tall holding dumbbells at your sides.']::text[], array['Step one leg back and across behind the other.','Lower until the front thigh is about parallel.','Return and alternate.']::text[], array['Hips stay facing forward','Front knee over the toes']::text[], array['Twisting the hips','Crossing too far']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deadlift_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deadlift_band', 'Deadlift (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting a weight from the floor to standing by driving with the legs and hips. Trains nearly the whole back of the body.', array['Stand on the middle of the band with feet hip-width.','Hinge down and hold the band with straight arms.']::text[], array['Brace, then push the floor away with your legs.','Keep the weight close to your legs as it rises.','Once the weight passes your knees, drive the hips forward to stand tall.','Lower by pushing the hips back first, then bending the knees once the weight passes them.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deadlift_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deadlift_barbell', 'Deadlift (Barbell)', array['conventional deadlift','bb deadlift']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting a weight from the floor to standing by driving with the legs and hips. Trains nearly the whole back of the body.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart, the bar over the middle of your feet (about 3 cm from your shins).','Hinge down and grip the bar just outside your legs.','Bend the knees until your shins touch the bar, then lift your chest so your back is flat.','Pull the slack out of the bar: arms straight, lats tight, shoulders just in front of the bar.']::text[], array['Brace, then push the floor away with your legs.','Keep the weight close to your legs as it rises.','Once the weight passes your knees, drive the hips forward to stand tall.','Lower by pushing the hips back first, then bending the knees once the weight passes them.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/deadlift_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deadlift_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deadlift_dumbbell', 'Deadlift (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting a weight from the floor to standing by driving with the legs and hips. Trains nearly the whole back of the body.', array['Stand with dumbbells on the floor beside your feet or in front of your shins.','Hinge and bend the knees to grip them with a flat back.']::text[], array['Brace, then push the floor away with your legs.','Keep the weight close to your legs as it rises.','Once the weight passes your knees, drive the hips forward to stand tall.','Lower by pushing the hips back first, then bending the knees once the weight passes them.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deadlift_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deadlift_smith', 'Deadlift (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting a weight from the floor to standing by driving with the legs and hips. Trains nearly the whole back of the body.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart, the bar over the middle of your feet (about 3 cm from your shins).','Hinge down and grip the bar just outside your legs.','Bend the knees until your shins touch the bar, then lift your chest so your back is flat.','Pull the slack out of the bar: arms straight, lats tight, shoulders just in front of the bar.']::text[], array['Brace, then push the floor away with your legs.','Keep the weight close to your legs as it rises.','Once the weight passes your knees, drive the hips forward to stand tall.','Lower by pushing the hips back first, then bending the knees once the weight passes them.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'downward_facing_balance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'downward_facing_balance', 'Downward Facing Balance', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Downward Facing Balance is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the abs & core and hamstrings.', '{}'::text[], array['Lie facedown on top of an exercise ball.','While resting on your stomach on the ball, walk your hands forward along the floor and lift your legs, extending your elbows and knees.']::text[], array['Walk the hands out until only the legs are on the ball','Hold a straight line from head to heels','Breathe and hold']::text[], array['Sagging hips','Locked elbows with shrugged shoulders']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/downward_facing_balance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Downward_Facing_Balance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_snatch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_snatch', 'Dumbbell Snatch', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting a dumbbell from the floor to overhead in one explosive movement with one arm.', array['Stand with the dumbbell between your feet.','Squat down and grip it with one hand, back flat.']::text[], array['Drive explosively through the legs and hips.','Pull the dumbbell up close to your body and punch it overhead.','Lower it to the shoulder, then the floor.']::text[], array['Hips drive it, the arm guides it']::text[], array['Curling or pressing the dumbbell up']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'flutter_kicks_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'flutter_kicks_bodyweight', 'Flutter Kicks', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Flutter Kicks is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the hamstrings.', array['On a flat bench lie facedown with the hips on the edge of the bench, the legs straight with toes high off the floor and with the arms on top of the bench holding on to the front edge.']::text[], array['Squeeze your glutes and hamstrings and straighten the legs until they are level with the hips. This will be your starting position.','Start the movement by lifting the left leg higher than the right leg.','Then lower the left leg as you lift the right leg.','Continue alternating in this manner (as though you are doing a flutter kick in water) until you have done the recommended amount of repetitions for each leg. Make sure that you keep a controlled movement at all times. Tip: You will breathe normally as you perform this movement.']::text[], array['Hips on the edge of the bench, legs level with the hips','Kick the legs up and down in small fast movements','Squeeze the glutes']::text[], array['Arching the lower back','Big, swinging kicks']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/flutter_kicks_bodyweight/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Flutter_Kicks/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'piriformis_smr')::uuid, 'mfd', 'piriformis_smr', 'Piriformis-SMR', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Piriformis-SMR is an intermediate-level self-massage (foam rolling) exercise that mainly targets the glutes.', '{}'::text[], array['Sit with your buttocks on top of a foam roll. Bend your knees, and then cross one leg so that the ankle is over the knee. This will be your starting position.','Shift your weight to the side of the crossed leg, rolling over the buttocks until you feel tension in your upper glute. You may assist the stretch by using one hand to pull the bent knee towards your chest. Hold this position for 10-30 seconds, and then switch sides.']::text[], array['Roll slowly, about 2–3 cm per second','Pause 20–30 seconds on tender spots','Support your weight with hands and feet to control the pressure','30–90 seconds per area']::text[], array['Rolling fast back and forth','Rolling directly over joints or bones','Pressing so hard you tense up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/piriformis_smr/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Piriformis-SMR/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'frog_pump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'frog_pump', 'Frog Pumps (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A glute bridge with the soles of the feet pressed together and knees open, done for high reps.', array['Lie on your back with the soles of your feet together and knees falling out.','Rest a dumbbell on your hips.']::text[], array['Drive your hips up by squeezing the glutes.','Lower and repeat quickly but controlled.']::text[], array['Squeeze hard at the top']::text[], array['Arching the lower back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_bridge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Lying on your back and lifting your hips. A simple glute exercise and a good warm-up.', array['Lie on your back with knees bent and feet flat, hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Drive through your heels to lift your hips until your body forms a line from knees to shoulders.','Squeeze the glutes.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Push through the heels','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/glute_bridge/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Butt_Lift_Bridge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_bridge_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_bridge_barbell', 'Glute Bridge (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying on your back and lifting your hips. A simple glute exercise and a good warm-up.', array['Lie on your back with knees bent and feet flat, hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Drive through your heels to lift your hips until your body forms a line from knees to shoulders.','Squeeze the glutes.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Push through the heels','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/glute_bridge_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Glute_Bridge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hip_lift_with_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hip_lift_with_band', 'Hip Lift with Band', array['Glute Bridge (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Hip Lift with Band is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the calves and hamstrings. A variation of the glute bridge: a band across the hips, anchored on each side, adds resistance at the top.', array['After choosing a suitable band, lay down in the middle of the rack, after securing the band on either side of you. If your rack doesn''t have pegs, the band can be secured using heavy dumbbells or similar objects, just ensure they won''t move.']::text[], array['Adjust your position so that the band is directly over your hips. Bend your knees and place your feet flat on the floor. Your hands can be on the floor or holding the band in position.','Keeping your shoulders on the ground, drive through your heels to raise your hips, pushing into the band as high as you can.','Pause at the top of the motion, and return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Push through the heels','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hip_lift_with_band/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hip_Lift_with_Band/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_bridge_partial_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_bridge_partial_barbell', 'Partial Glute Bridge (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying on your back and lifting your hips. A simple glute exercise and a good warm-up.', array['Lie on your back with knees bent and feet flat, hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Drive through your heels to lift your hips until your body forms a line from knees to shoulders.','Squeeze the glutes.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Push through the heels','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Arching the lower back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'physioball_hip_bridge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'physioball_hip_bridge', 'Physioball Hip Bridge', array['Glute Bridge (Stability Ball)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Physioball Hip Bridge is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the hamstrings. A variation of the glute bridge: upper back on a ball; the hips lower and lift.', array['Lay on a ball so that your upper back is on the ball with your hips unsupported. Both feet should be flat on the floor, hip width apart or wider. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by extending the hips using your glutes and hamstrings, raising your hips upward as you bridge.','Pause at the top of the motion and return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Push through the heels','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/physioball_hip_bridge/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Physioball_Hip_Bridge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_bridge_single_leg')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_bridge_single_leg', 'Single Leg Glute Bridge', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Lying on your back and lifting your hips. A simple glute exercise and a good warm-up.', array['Lie on your back with knees bent and feet flat, hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Drive through your heels to lift your hips until your body forms a line from knees to shoulders.','Squeeze the glutes.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Push through the heels','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/glute_bridge_single_leg/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single_Leg_Glute_Bridge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_kickback_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_kickback_machine', 'Glute Kickback (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kicking one leg straight back to squeeze the glute.', array['Set the machine so the pad sits behind your working foot or knee.','Hold the handles and brace on the chest pad or support.']::text[], array['Kick the working leg straight back by squeezing the glute.','Pause, then return slowly.']::text[], array['Move from the hip, not the lower back','Hips stay square']::text[], array['Arching the back to kick higher','Swinging']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_kickback_floor')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_kickback_floor', 'Glute Kickback on Floor', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Kicking one leg straight back to squeeze the glute.', array['Start on hands and knees.']::text[], array['Kick the working leg straight back by squeezing the glute.','Pause, then return slowly.']::text[], array['Move from the hip, not the lower back','Hips stay square']::text[], array['Arching the back to kick higher','Swinging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/glute_kickback_floor/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Glute_Kickback/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hip_extension_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hip_extension_with_bands', 'Hip Extension with Bands', array['Glute Kickback (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Hip Extension with Bands is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the hamstrings. A variation of the glute kickback: standing, a band at the ankle; drive the leg straight back.', array['Secure one end of the band to the lower portion of a post and attach the other to one ankle.']::text[], array['Facing the attachment point of the band, hold on to the column to stabilize yourself.','Keeping your head and your chest up, move the resisted leg back as far as you can while keeping the knee straight.','Return the leg to the starting position.']::text[], array['Move from the hip, not the lower back','Hips stay square']::text[], array['Arching the back to kick higher','Swinging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hip_extension_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hip_Extension_with_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_lift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_lift', 'Leg Lift', array['Glute Kickback (Standing)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Leg Lift is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the hamstrings. A variation of the glute kickback: standing, holding a support; lift one leg back, optionally with an ankle weight.', array['While standing up straight with both feet next to each other at around shoulder width, grab a sturdy surface such as the sides of a squat rack or the top of a chair to brace yourself and keep balance.']::text[], array['With or without an ankle weight, lift one leg behind you as if performing a leg curl but standing up while keeping the other leg straight. Breathe out as you perform this movement.','Slowly bring the raised leg back to the floor as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','Repeat the movement with the opposite leg.']::text[], array['Move from the hip, not the lower back','Hips stay square']::text[], array['Arching the back to kick higher','Swinging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_lift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leg_Lift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_kickback_rear_kick_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_kickback_rear_kick_machine', 'Rear Kick (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kicking one leg straight back to squeeze the glute.', array['Set the machine so the pad sits behind your working foot or knee.','Hold the handles and brace on the chest pad or support.']::text[], array['Kick the working leg straight back by squeezing the glute.','Pause, then return slowly.']::text[], array['Move from the hip, not the lower back','Hips stay square']::text[], array['Arching the back to kick higher','Swinging']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_kickback_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_kickback_cable', 'Standing Cable Glute Kickbacks', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kicking one leg straight back to squeeze the glute.', array['Attach an ankle strap to a low pulley.','Face the machine and hold on for support.']::text[], array['Kick the working leg straight back by squeezing the glute.','Pause, then return slowly.']::text[], array['Move from the hip, not the lower back','Hips stay square']::text[], array['Arching the back to kick higher','Swinging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/glute_kickback_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Legged_Cable_Kickback/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'ankle_on_the_knee')::uuid, 'mfd', 'ankle_on_the_knee', 'Ankle On The Knee', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Ankle On The Knee is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the glutes.', array['From a lying position, bend your knees and keep your feet on the floor.']::text[], array['Place your ankle of one foot on your opposite knee.','Grasp the thigh or knee of the bottom leg and pull both of your legs into the chest. Relax your neck and shoulders. Hold for 10-20 seconds and then switch sides.']::text[], array['Keep the hips square and the lower back flat on the floor where lying','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Twisting the pelvis to fake the range','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/ankle_on_the_knee/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Ankle_On_The_Knee/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'knee_across_the_body')::uuid, 'mfd', 'knee_across_the_body', 'Knee Across The Body', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Knee Across The Body is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the abductors and lower back.', '{}'::text[], array['Lie down on the floor with your right leg straight. Bend your left leg and lower it across your body, holding the knee down toward the floor with your right hand. (The knee doesn''t need to touch the floor if you''re tight.)','Place your left arm comfortably beside you and turn your head to the left. Imagine you have a weight tied to your tailbone. let your tailbone fall back toward the floor as your chest reaches in the opposite direction to stretch your lower back. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Keep the hips square and the lower back flat on the floor where lying','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Twisting the pelvis to fake the range','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/knee_across_the_body/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Knee_Across_The_Body/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_glute')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_glute', 'Lying Glute', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Lying Glute is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the abductors.', array['Lie on your back with your partner kneeling beside you.']::text[], array['Flex the hip of one leg, raising it off of the floor. Rotate the leg so the foot is over the opposite hip, the lower leg perpendicular to your body. Your partner should hold the knee and ankle in place. This will be your starting position.','Attempt to push your leg towards your partner, who should be preventing any actual movement of the leg.','After 10-20 seconds, completely relax as your partner gently pushes the ankle and knee towards your chest. Be sure to inform your helper when the stretch is adequate to prevent injury or overstretching.']::text[], array['Keep the hips square and the lower back flat on the floor where lying','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Twisting the pelvis to fake the range','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_glute/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Glute/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_knee_to_chest')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_knee_to_chest', 'One Knee To Chest', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'One Knee To Chest is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the hamstrings and lower back.', array['Start off by lying on the floor.']::text[], array['Extend one leg straight and pull the other knee to your chest. Hold under the knee joint to protect the kneecap.','Gently tug that knee toward your nose.','Switch sides. This stretches the buttocks and lower back of the bent leg and the hip flexor of the straight leg.']::text[], array['Keep the hips square and the lower back flat on the floor where lying','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Twisting the pelvis to fake the range','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_knee_to_chest/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Knee_To_Chest/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_glute')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_glute', 'Seated Glute', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Seated Glute is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the adductors.', array['In a seated position with your knees bent, cross one ankle over the opposite knee. Your partner will stand behind you. Now, lean forward as your partner braces your shoulders with their hands. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Attempt to push your torso back for 10-20 seconds, as your partner prevents any actual movement of your torso.','Now relax your muscles as your partner increases the stretch by gently pushing your torso forward for 10-20 seconds.']::text[], array['Keep the hips square and the lower back flat on the floor where lying','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Twisting the pelvis to fake the range','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_glute/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Glute/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hip_thrust_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hip_thrust_bodyweight', 'Hip Thrust', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Driving the hips up with your upper back on a bench. One of the most direct glute exercises.', array['Sit on the floor with your upper back (just below the shoulder blades) against a bench.','Feet flat, hip-width apart, close enough that your shins are vertical at the top.']::text[], array['Tuck your chin slightly and drive through your heels to lift the hips.','Lock out with hips fully extended and ribs down.','Squeeze the glutes for a second.','Lower with control.']::text[], array['Shins vertical at the top','Ribs down; finish with the glutes, not the lower back','Eyes forward, chin tucked']::text[], array['Arching the lower back to finish','Feet too far forward (hamstrings take over)','Feet too close (quads take over)']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hip_thrust_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hip_thrust_barbell', 'Hip Thrust (Barbell)', array['barbell hip thrust','glute thrust']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Driving the hips up with your upper back on a bench. One of the most direct glute exercises.', array['Sit on the floor with your upper back (just below the shoulder blades) against a bench.','Place the weight across your hips: roll a padded barbell over them or hold a dumbbell in place.','Feet flat, hip-width apart, close enough that your shins are vertical at the top.']::text[], array['Tuck your chin slightly and drive through your heels to lift the hips.','Lock out with hips fully extended and ribs down.','Squeeze the glutes for a second.','Lower with control.']::text[], array['Shins vertical at the top','Ribs down; finish with the glutes, not the lower back','Eyes forward, chin tucked']::text[], array['Arching the lower back to finish','Feet too far forward (hamstrings take over)','Feet too close (quads take over)']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hip_thrust_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Hip_Thrust/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
