(md5('mfd:' || 'kneeling_jump_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kneeling_jump_squat', 'Kneeling Jump Squat', array['Jump Squat (Kneeling Barbell)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Kneeling Jump Squat is an advanced-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the calves, hamstrings and quadriceps. A variation of the jump squat: from kneeling, jump to the feet with a bar on the back.', array['Begin kneeling on the floor with a barbell racked across the back of your shoulders, or you can use your body weight for this exercise. This can be done inside of a power rack to make unracking easier.']::text[], array['Sit back with your hips until your glutes touch your feet, keeping your head and chest up.','Explode up with your hips, generating enough power to land with your feet flat on the floor.','Continue with the squat by driving through your heels and extending the knees to come to a standing position.']::text[], array['Soft landings']::text[], array['Landing with straight legs','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kneeling_jump_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kneeling_Jump_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_clean', 'Kettlebell Clean', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Swinging the kettlebell up into the rack position on the front of the shoulder in one movement.', array['Set up as for a single-arm swing.']::text[], array['Hike the bell back.','Drive the hips forward and guide the bell close to your body.','Rotate your hand around the handle to catch the bell softly in the rack.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_snatch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_snatch', 'Kettlebell Snatch', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Swinging the kettlebell from between the legs to locked out overhead in one movement.', array['Set up as for a single-arm swing.']::text[], array['Hike the bell back and drive the hips.','Keep it close as it rises and punch your hand through at the top.','Lock out overhead, then let it drop back into the next swing.']::text[], array['Punch through so the bell does not crash on the forearm']::text[], array['Letting the bell flip over']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_snatch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_swing')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_swing', 'Kettlebell Swing', array['russian swing','kb swing']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An explosive hip hinge that swings a kettlebell to chest height. Builds power in the glutes and hamstrings.', array['Stand with feet slightly wider than hips, kettlebell on the floor about 30 cm in front.','Hinge and grip the handle with both hands.']::text[], array['Hike the bell back between your legs.','Snap your hips forward to stand tall, letting the bell float to chest height.','Let it fall back and hinge to receive it between your legs.']::text[], array['It is a hinge, not a squat','Snap the hips; arms just hold on','Stand tall and squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Squatting the bell up','Lifting with the arms','Leaning back at the top']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kneeling_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kneeling_squat', 'Kneeling Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kneeling Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the abs & core, hamstrings and lower back.', array['Set the bar to the proper height in a power rack. Kneel behind the bar; it may be beneficial to put a mat down to pad your knees. Slide under the bar, racking it across the back of your shoulders. Your shoulder blades should be retracted and the bar tight across your back. Unrack the weight.']::text[], array['With your head looking forward, sit back with your butt until you touch your calves.','Reverse the motion, returning the torso to an upright position.']::text[], array['Kneel behind the bar on a mat','Sit back onto the heels','Drive the hips forward to kneel tall']::text[], array['Arching the lower back','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kneeling_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kneeling_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_hyperextension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_hyperextension', 'Reverse Hyperextension', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying face down with your legs hanging off the end of a bench or machine, lifting the legs up behind you.', array['Lie face down on the reverse hyper (or a high bench) with hips at the edge.','Hold the handles; legs hang down.']::text[], array['Lift your legs up behind you until they are in line with your body.','Lower with control.']::text[], array['Squeeze the glutes to lift','Do not swing']::text[], array['Over-arching the lower back','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_hyperextension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Hyperextension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_plank')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_plank', 'Reverse Plank', '{}'::text[], 'core', 'time', 'Holding a straight body facing up, supported on your hands (or forearms) and heels.', array['Sit with legs straight and hands on the floor behind your hips, fingers toward your feet.']::text[], array['Lift your hips until your body forms a straight line from shoulders to heels.','Hold.']::text[], array['Squeeze the glutes','Chest open']::text[], array['Hips dropping']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch_hang')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch_hang', 'Hang Snatch', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the bar from the floor to locked arms overhead in one movement, catching it in an overhead squat.', array['Take a wide (snatch) grip so the bar sits in your hip crease when standing.','Set up with the bar over mid-foot, back flat, hips lower than for a deadlift.']::text[], array['Start standing with the bar at your hips, then lower it to just above the knees.','Extend explosively and pull yourself under the bar.','Catch it with locked arms in an overhead squat.','Stand up.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch_hang/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hang_Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch_power')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch_power', 'Power Snatch', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the bar from the floor to locked arms overhead in one movement, catching it in an overhead squat.', array['Take a wide (snatch) grip so the bar sits in your hip crease when standing.','Set up with the bar over mid-foot, back flat, hips lower than for a deadlift.']::text[], array['Lift the bar to the hips keeping it close.','Extend explosively and pull yourself under the bar.','Catch it with locked arms in an overhead squat.','Stand up.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch_power/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Power_Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch', 'Snatch', array['squat snatch']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the bar from the floor to locked arms overhead in one movement, catching it in an overhead squat.', array['Take a wide (snatch) grip so the bar sits in your hip crease when standing.','Set up with the bar over mid-foot, back flat, hips lower than for a deadlift.']::text[], array['Lift the bar to the hips keeping it close.','Extend explosively and pull yourself under the bar.','Catch it with locked arms in an overhead squat.','Stand up.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'step_up_with_knee_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'step_up_with_knee_raise', 'Step-up with Knee Raise', array['Step Up (With Knee Raise)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Step-up with Knee Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the glutes, with help from the hamstrings and quadriceps. A variation of the step up: drive the other knee up at the top.', array['Stand facing a box or bench of an appropriate height with your feet together. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the movement by stepping up, putting your left foot on the top of the bench. Extend through the hip and knee of your front leg to stand up on the box. As you stand on the box with your left leg, flex your right knee and hip, bringing your knee as high as you can.','Reverse this motion to step down off the box, and then repeat the sequence on the opposite leg.']::text[], array['Push through the top leg, not the bottom foot','Stand fully tall on top']::text[], array['Pushing off the floor leg','Knee caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/step_up_with_knee_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Step-up_with_Knee_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sumo_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sumo_deadlift', 'Sumo Deadlift', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A deadlift with a very wide stance and hands inside the legs. The torso stays more upright and the hips and inner thighs work harder.', array['Stand with feet well wider than shoulders, toes turned out, shins close to the bar.','Grip the bar inside your legs, arms hanging straight down.','Push your knees out and lift your chest.']::text[], array['Brace and push the floor apart with your feet.','Keep the bar close as you stand up.','Lock out by squeezing the glutes.','Lower with control.']::text[], array['Knees out over the toes','Chest up, hips close to the bar']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Hips rising first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sumo_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'box_jump_multiple_response')::uuid, 'mfd', 'box_jump_multiple_response', 'Box Jump (Multiple Response)', array['Box Jump (Repeated)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Box Jump (Multiple Response) is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and quadriceps. A variation of the box jump: several jumps in a row without resetting.', array['Assume a relaxed stance facing the box or platform approximately an arm''s length away. Arms should be down at the sides and legs slightly bent.']::text[], array['Using the arms to aid in the initial burst, jump upward and forward, landing with feet simultaneously on top of the box or platform.','Immediately drop or jump back down to the original starting place; then repeat the sequence.']::text[], array['Land quietly','Knees in line with the toes']::text[], array['Choosing a box so high that you land in a deep squat','Jumping back down']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/box_jump_multiple_response/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Box_Jump_Multiple_Response/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'box_skip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'box_skip', 'Box Skip', array['Box Jump (Skip)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Box Skip is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and quadriceps. A variation of the box jump: skipping onto a box, alternating legs.', array['You will need several boxes lined up about 8 feet apart.']::text[], array['Begin facing the first box with one leg slightly behind the other.','Drive off the back leg, attempting to gain as much height with the hips as possible.','Immediately upon landing on the box, drive the other leg forward and upward to gain height and distance, leaping from the box. Land between the first two boxes with the same leg that landed on the first box.','Then, step to the next box and repeat.']::text[], array['Land quietly','Knees in line with the toes']::text[], array['Choosing a box so high that you land in a deep squat','Jumping back down']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/box_skip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Box_Skip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'band_good_morning_pull_through')::uuid, 'mfd', 'band_good_morning_pull_through', 'Band Good Morning (Pull Through)', array['Cable Pull Through (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Band Good Morning (Pull Through) is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes and lower back. A variation of the cable pull through: a band anchored low behind you replaces the cable.', array['Loop the band around a post. Standing a little ways away, loop the opposite end around the neck. Your hands can help hold the band in position.']::text[], array['Begin by bending at the hips, getting your butt back as far as possible. Keep your back flat and bend forward to about 90 degrees. Your knees should be only slightly bent.','Return to the starting position be driving through with the hips to come back to a standing position.']::text[], array['It is a hinge, not a squat','Arms just hold the band']::text[], array['Pulling with the arms','Leaning back at the top']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/band_good_morning_pull_through/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Band_Good_Morning_Pull_Through/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_clean', 'Dumbbell Clean', array['Clean (Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Clean is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, forearms, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the clean: two dumbbells pulled and caught at the shoulders.', array['Begin standing with a dumbbell in each hand with your feet shoulder width apart.']::text[], array['Lower the weights to the floor by flexing at the hips and knees, pushing your hips back until the dumbbells reach the floor. This will be your starting position.','To initiate the movement, violently jump upward by extending the hips, knees, and ankles to acclerate the weights upward. Maintaining a neutral grip on the dumbbells, keep the arms straight until full extension is reached.','After full extension, rebend the hips and knees to receive the weight in a squat position. Allow the arms to bend, guiding the dumbbells to your shoulders.','Upon receiving the weight in the squat position, extend the hips and knees to finish in a standing position with the weights on your shoulders.']::text[], array['Dumbbells stay close to the body','Explosive hip drive, then pull yourself under','Catch on the shoulders with the elbows forward']::text[], array['Curling the dumbbells up with the arms','Dumbbells swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'power_clean_from_blocks')::uuid, 'mfd', 'power_clean_from_blocks', 'Power Clean from Blocks', array['Clean (Power, From Blocks)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Power Clean from Blocks is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the quadriceps. A variation of the clean: bar starts on blocks; caught above parallel.', array['With a barbell on boxes of the desired height, take a grip just outside the legs. Lower your hips with the weight focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, chest up, with your shoulders just in front of the bar. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your knees. Your back angle should stay the same, and your arms should remain straight. As the bar approaches the mid-thigh position, begin extending through the hips.','In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hips, knees, and ankles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the weight. At the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended.','As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the elbows up and out. At peak extension, pull yourself under the bar far enough that it can be racked onto the shoulders, rotating your elbows under the bar as you do so. The bar should be racked onto the protracted shoulders, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed.','Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torso upright and elbows up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position, and complete the repetition by returning the weight to the boxes.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Patient off the floor, explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/power_clean_from_blocks/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Power_Clean_from_Blocks/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_hang_power_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_hang_power_clean', 'Smith Machine Hang Power Clean', array['Clean (Smith, Hang Power)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine Hang Power Clean is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the clean: smith machine; teaches the bar path.', array['Position the bar at knee height and load it to an appropriate weight.']::text[], array['Take a pronated grip on the bar outside of shoulder width and unhook the bar from the machine. Your arms should be fully extended with your head and chest up. Your elbows should be pointed out with your shoulders back and down. Your hips should be back, loading the tension into the hamstrings. This will be your starting position.','Initate the movement by forcefully extending the hips and knees, accelerating into the bar. Ensure that you keep your arms straight during this part of the motion.','Upon full extension, rebend the hips and knees to lower your receiving position.','Allow the arms to flex at this point, rotating the elbows around the bar to receive it on your shoulders.','Extend through the hips and knees to come to a standing position with the bar racked on your shoulders to complete the movement.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Patient off the floor, explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_hang_power_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Hang_Power_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_deadlift', 'Clean Deadlift', array['Clean Pull (Clean Deadlift)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Clean Deadlift is a beginner-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the forearms, glutes, lower back, upper back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the clean pull: lift to standing with clean positions, no jump.', array['Begin standing with a barbell close to your shins. Your feet should be directly under your hips with your feet turned out slightly. Grip the bar with a double overhand grip or hook grip, about shoulder width apart. Squat down to the bar. Your spine should be in full extension, with a back angle that places your shoulders in front of the bar and your back as vertical as possible.']::text[], array['Begin by driving through the floor through the front of your heels. As the bar travels upward, maintain a constant back angle. Flare your knees out to the side to help keep them out of the bar''s path.','After the bar crosses the knees, complete the lift by driving the hips into the bar until your hips and knees are extended.']::text[], array['Full extension of hips, knees and ankles','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Bending the arms early','Leaning back excessively']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clean_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch_deadlift', 'Snatch Deadlift', array['Clean Pull (Snatch Grip Deadlift)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Snatch Deadlift is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the forearms, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the clean pull: wide snatch grip, lift to standing.', array['The snatch deadlift strengthens the first pull of the snatch. Begin with a wide snatch grip with the barbell placed on the platform. The feet should be directly under the hips, with the feet turned out. Squat down to the bar, keeping the back in absolute extension with the head facing forward.']::text[], array['Initiate the movement by driving through the heels, raising the hips. The back angle should remain the same until the bar passes the knees.','At that point, drive your hips through the bar as you lay back. Return the bar to the platform by reversing the motion.']::text[], array['Full extension of hips, knees and ankles','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Bending the arms early','Leaning back excessively']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Snatch_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch_pull')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch_pull', 'Snatch Pull', array['Clean Pull (Snatch Pull)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Snatch Pull is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the clean pull: wide snatch grip, full extension and shrug.', array['With a barbell on the floor close to the shins, take a wide snatch grip. Lower your hips with the weight focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, chest up, with your shoulders just in front of the bar. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your knees. Your back angle should stay the same, and your arms should remain straight. Move the weight with control as you continue to above the knees.','Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the pull. As the bar approaches the mid-thigh position, begin extending through the hips. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hips, knees, and ankles, using speed to move the bar upward.','There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the weight; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back. Full extension should be violent and abrupt, and ensure that you do not prolong the extension for longer than necessary.']::text[], array['Full extension of hips, knees and ankles','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Bending the arms early','Leaning back excessively']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch_pull/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Snatch_Pull/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'downward_dog')::uuid, 'mfd', 'downward_dog', 'Downward Dog', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'reps', 'A yoga pose forming an upside-down V, stretching the hamstrings, calves and shoulders.', '{}'::text[], array['From hands and knees, lift your hips up and back.','Straighten your legs as far as comfortable and press your heels toward the floor.','Hold, then lower your knees.']::text[], array['Long spine; bend the knees if needed','Push the floor away']::text[], array['Rounding the back to straighten the legs']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_leg_raises')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_leg_raises', 'Front Leg Raises', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Front Leg Raises is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings.', '{}'::text[], array['Stand next to a chair or other support, holding on with one hand.','Swing your leg forward, keeping the leg straight. Continue with a downward swing, bringing the leg as far back as your flexibility allows. Repeat 5-10 times, and then switch legs.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_leg_raises/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Leg_Raises/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'inchworm')::uuid, 'mfd', 'inchworm', 'Inchworm', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Inchworm is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings.', array['Stand with your feet close together. Keeping your legs straight, stretch down and put your hands on the floor directly in front of you. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by walking your hands forward slowly, alternating your left and your right. As you do so, bend only at the hip, keeping your legs straight.','Keep going until your body is parallel to the ground in a pushup position.','Now, keep your hands in place and slowly take short steps with your feet, moving only a few inches at a time.','Continue walking until your feet are by hour hands, keeping your legs straight as you do so.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/inchworm/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Inchworm/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'worlds_greatest_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'worlds_greatest_stretch', 'World''s Greatest Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'World''s Greatest Stretch is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, glutes and quadriceps.', array['This is a three-part stretch. Begin by lunging forward, with your front foot flat on the ground and on the toes of your back foot. With your knees bent, squat down until your knee is almost touching the ground. Keep your torso erect, and hold this position for 10-20 seconds.']::text[], array['Now, place the arm on the same side as your front leg on the ground, with the elbow next to the foot. Your other hand should be placed on the ground, parallel to your lead leg, to help support you during this portion of the stretch.','After 10-20 seconds, place your hands on either side of your front foot. Raise the toes of the front foot off of the ground, and straighten your leg. You may need to reposition your rear leg to do so. Hold for 10-20 seconds, and then repeat the entire sequence for the other side.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/worlds_greatest_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Worlds_Greatest_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hamstring_smr')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hamstring_smr', 'Hamstring-SMR', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Hamstring-SMR is a beginner-level self-massage (foam rolling) exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings.', array['In a seated position, extend your legs over a foam roll so that it is position on the back of the upper legs. Place your hands to the side or behind you to help support your weight. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Using your hands, lift your hips off of the floor and shift your weight on the foam roll to one leg. Relax the hamstrings of the leg you are stretching.','Roll over the foam from below the hip to above the back of the knee, pausing at points of tension for 10-30 seconds. Repeat for the other leg.']::text[], array['Roll slowly, about 2–3 cm per second','Pause 20–30 seconds on tender spots','Support your weight with hands and feet to control the pressure','30–90 seconds per area']::text[], array['Rolling fast back and forth','Rolling directly over joints or bones','Pressing so hard you tense up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hamstring_smr/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hamstring-SMR/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'glute_ham_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'glute_ham_raise', 'Glute Ham Raise', array['ghr']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'On a glute-ham developer, you lower your torso and pull yourself back up using the hamstrings and glutes.', array['Lock your feet in the foot plate with knees just behind the pad.']::text[], array['Start upright, then lower your torso forward until it is parallel to the floor.','Pull yourself back up by curling your heels into the plate.']::text[], array['Hips stay straight','Pull with the hamstrings']::text[], array['Bending at the hips','Using momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/glute_ham_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Glute_Ham_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'band_good_morning')::uuid, 'mfd', 'band_good_morning', 'Band Good Morning', array['Good Morning (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Band Good Morning is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes and lower back. A variation of the good morning: standing on a band looped behind the neck.', array['Using a 41 inch band, stand on one end, spreading your feet a small amount. Bend at the hips to loop the end of the band behind your neck. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping your legs straight, extend through the hips to come to a near vertical position.','Ensure that you do not round your back as you go down back to the starting position.']::text[], array['Flat back throughout','Hips back, not down']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/band_good_morning/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Band_Good_Morning/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'good_morning')::uuid, 'mfd', 'good_morning', 'Good Morning (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'With a bar on your upper back, you hinge forward at the hips and stand back up. Trains the hamstrings and lower back.', array['Rest a light barbell on your upper back as for a squat.','Feet hip-width apart, knees soft.']::text[], array['Push your hips back and lower your torso until it is near parallel or you feel a strong hamstring stretch.','Drive the hips forward to stand up.']::text[], array['Flat back throughout','Hips back, not down']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/good_morning/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Good_Morning/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'good_morning_off_pins')::uuid, 'mfd', 'good_morning_off_pins', 'Good Morning off Pins', array['Good Morning (Off Pins)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Good Morning off Pins is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abs & core, glutes and lower back. A variation of the good morning: starts from the bottom with the bar on safety pins.', '{}'::text[], array['Begin with a bar on a rack at about the same height as your stomach. Bend over underneath the bar and rack the bar across the rear of your shoulders as you would a power squat, not on top of your shoulders. At the proper height, you should be near parallel to the floor when bent over. Keep your back tight, shoulder blades pinched together, and your knees slightly bent. Keep your back arched and your cervical spine in proper alignment.','Begin the motion by extending through the hips with your glutes and hamstrings, and you are standing with the weight. Slowly lower the weight back to the pins returning to the starting position.']::text[], array['Flat back throughout','Hips back, not down']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/good_morning_off_pins/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Good_Morning_off_Pins/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hanging_bar_good_morning')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hanging_bar_good_morning', 'Hanging Bar Good Morning', array['Good Morning (Hanging Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Hanging Bar Good Morning is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abs & core, glutes and lower back. A variation of the good morning: bar hangs from chains or bands at the bottom position.', array['Begin with a bar on a rack at about the same height as your stomach. Suspend the bar using chains or suspension straps.']::text[], array['Bend over underneath the bar and rack the bar across the rear of your shoulders as you would a power squat, not on top of your traps. At the proper height, you should be near parallel to the floor when bent over. Keep your back tight, shoulder blades pinched together, and your knees slightly bent. Keep your back arched and your cervical spine in proper alignment.','Begin the motion by extending through the hips with your glutes and hamstrings, and you are standing with the weight.','Slowly lower the weight back to the starting position, where it is supported by the chains.']::text[], array['Flat back throughout','Hips back, not down']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hanging_bar_good_morning/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hanging_Bar_Good_Morning/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'intermediate_groin_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'intermediate_groin_stretch', 'Intermediate Groin Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Intermediate Groin Stretch is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings.', '{}'::text[], array['Lie on your back with your legs extended. Loop a belt, rope, or band around one of your feet, and swing that leg as far to the side as you can. This will be your starting position.','Pull gently on the belt to create tension in your groin and hamstring muscles. Hold for 10-20 seconds, and repeat on the other side.']::text[], array['Let the knees fall out under their own weight before pressing gently','Sit tall with a long spine','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Pushing hard on the knees','Rounding the back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/intermediate_groin_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Intermediate_Groin_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'the_straddle')::uuid, 'mfd', 'the_straddle', 'The Straddle', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'The Straddle is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the adductors and calves.', '{}'::text[], array['Begin in a seated, upright position. Start by extending your legs in front of you in a V.','With your hands on the floor, lean forward as far as possible. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.']::text[], array['Let the knees fall out under their own weight before pressing gently','Sit tall with a long spine','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Pushing hard on the knees','Rounding the back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/the_straddle/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/The_Straddle/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || '90_90_hamstring')::uuid, 'mfd', '90_90_hamstring', '90/90 Hamstring', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', '90/90 Hamstring is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves.', array['Lie on your back, with one leg extended straight out.']::text[], array['With the other leg, bend the hip and knee to 90 degrees. You may brace your leg with your hands if necessary. This will be your starting position.','Extend your leg straight into the air, pausing briefly at the top. Return the leg to the starting position.','Repeat for 10-20 repetitions, and then switch to the other leg.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/90_90_hamstring/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/90_90_Hamstring/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chair_leg_extended_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chair_leg_extended_stretch', 'Chair Leg Extended Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Chair Leg Extended Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the adductors.', array['Sit upright in a chair and grip the seat on the sides.']::text[], array['Raise one leg, extending the knee, flexing the ankle as you do so.','Slowly move that leg outward as far as you can, and then back to the center and down.','Repeat for your other leg.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chair_leg_extended_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chair_Leg_Extended_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hamstring_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hamstring_stretch', 'Hamstring Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Hamstring Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings.', array['Lie on your back with one leg extended above you, with the hip at ninety degrees. Keep the other leg flat on the floor.']::text[], array['Loop a belt, band, or rope over the ball of your foot. This will be your starting position.','Pull on the belt to create tension in the calves and hamstrings. Hold this stretch for 10-30 seconds, and repeat with the other leg.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hamstring_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hamstring_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_up_hamstring_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_up_hamstring_stretch', 'Leg-Up Hamstring Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Leg-Up Hamstring Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings.', array['Lie flat on your back, bend one knee, and put that foot flat on the floor to stabilize your spine.']::text[], array['Extend the other leg in the air. If you''re tight, you wont be able to straighten it. That''s okay. Extend the knee so that the sole of the lifted foot faces the ceiling (or as close as you can get it).','Slowly straighten the legs as much as possible and then pull the leg toward your nose. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_up_hamstring_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leg-Up_Hamstring_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_hamstring')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_hamstring', 'Lying Hamstring', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Lying Hamstring is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves.', array['Lie on your back with your legs extended. Your partner should be kneeling beside you. Raise one leg up towards the ceiling and have your partner hold the ankle. Your partner can use their shoulder to brace your leg if necessary. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['With your partner holding your leg in place, attempt to flex the knee, contracting the hamstrings for 10-20 seconds.','Then relax your leg, allowing your partner to gently push the leg towards your head. Be sure to inform your helper when the stretch is adequate to prevent injury or overstretching. Switch sides once complete.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_hamstring/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Hamstring/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'runners_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'runners_stretch', 'Runner''s Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Runner''s Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves.', array['It''s easiest to get into this stretch if you start standing up, put one leg behind you, and slowly lower your torso down to the floor.']::text[], array['Keep the front heel on the floor (if it lifts up, scoot your other leg further back).','Place your hands on either side of your front leg. To get more out of this stretch, push your butt up toward the ceiling, and then gradually lower it back toward the floor. You''ll Stretch the hip flexor of the back leg and the hamstring and buttocks of the front.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/runners_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Runners_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_floor_hamstring_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_floor_hamstring_stretch', 'Seated Floor Hamstring Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Seated Floor Hamstring Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves.', '{}'::text[], array['Sit on a mat with your right leg extended in front of you and your left leg bent with your foot against your right inner thigh.','Lean forward from your hips and reach for your ankle until you feel a stretch in your hamstring. Hold for 15 seconds, then repeat for your other side.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_floor_hamstring_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Floor_Hamstring_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_hamstring')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_hamstring', 'Seated Hamstring', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Seated Hamstring is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves.', array['In a seated position with your legs extended, have your partner stand behind you. Now, lean forward as your partner braces your shoulders with their hands. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Attempt to push your torso back for 10-20 seconds, as your partner prevents any actual movement of your torso.','Now relax your muscles as your partner increases the stretch by gently pushing your torso forward for 10-20 seconds.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_hamstring/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Hamstring/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_hamstring_and_calf_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_hamstring_and_calf_stretch', 'Seated Hamstring and Calf Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Seated Hamstring and Calf Stretch is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves.', '{}'::text[], array['Loop a belt, rope, or band around one foot. Sit down with both legs extended . This will be your starting position.','Leaning forward slightly, pull on the belt to draw the toes of your foot back. Hold this position for 10-20 seconds and then repeat with the other leg.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_hamstring_and_calf_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Hamstring_and_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_hamstring_and_calf_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_hamstring_and_calf_stretch', 'Standing Hamstring and Calf Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Standing Hamstring and Calf Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings.', array['Being by looping a belt, band, or rope around one foot. While standing, place that foot forward.']::text[], array['Bend your back leg, while keeping the front one straight. Now raise the toes of your front foot off of the ground and lean forward.','Using the belt, pull on the top of the foot to increase the stretch in the calf. Hold for 10-20 seconds and repeat with the other foot.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_hamstring_and_calf_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Hamstring_and_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_toe_touches')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_toe_touches', 'Standing Toe Touches', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Standing Toe Touches is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves.', '{}'::text[], array['Stand with some space in front and behind you.','Bend at the waist, keeping your legs straight, until you can relax and let your upper body hang down in front of you. Let your arms and hands hang down naturally. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_toe_touches/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Toe_Touches/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'upper_back_leg_grab')::uuid, 'mfd', 'upper_back_leg_grab', 'Upper Back-Leg Grab', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Upper Back-Leg Grab is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the lower back and upper back.', '{}'::text[], array['While seated, bend forward to hug your thighs from underneath with both arms.','Keep your knees together and your legs extended out as you bring your chest down to your knees. You can also stretch your middle back by pulling your back away from your knees as your hugging them.']::text[], array['Hinge from the hips with a long back instead of rounding to reach','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed','A slight knee bend is fine']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back to reach further','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/upper_back_leg_grab/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Upper_Back-Leg_Grab/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hurdle_hops')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hurdle_hops', 'Hurdle Hops', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Hurdle Hops is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves and glutes.', array['Set up a row of hurdles or other small barriers, placing them a few feet apart.']::text[], array['Stand in front of the first hurdle with your feet shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.','Begin by jumping with both feet over the first hurdle, swinging both arms as you jump.','Absorb the impact of landing by bending the knees, rebounding out of the first leap by jumping over the next hurdle. Continue until you have jumped over all of the hurdles.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hurdle_hops/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hurdle_Hops/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'knee_tuck_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'knee_tuck_jump', 'Knee Tuck Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Knee Tuck Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and quadriceps.', array['Begin in a comfortable standing position with your knees slightly bent. Hold your hands in front of you, palms down with your fingertips together at chest height. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Rapidly dip down into a quarter squat and immediately explode upward. Drive the knees towards the chest, attempting to touch them to the palms of the hands.','Jump as high as you can, raising your knees up, and then ensure a good land be re-extending your legs, absorbing impact through be allowing the knees to rebend.']::text[], array['Jump straight up and land where you started','Land softly with bent knees','Keep the chest up']::text[], array['Landing stiff-legged','Hunching over in the air','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/knee_tuck_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Knee_Tuck_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternating_hang_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternating_hang_clean', 'Alternating Hang Clean', array['Kettlebell Clean (Alternating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating Hang Clean is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the biceps, calves, forearms, glutes, lower back and traps. A variation of the kettlebell clean: two kettlebells, cleaned one at a time.', array['Place two kettlebells between your feet. To get in the starting position, push your butt back and look straight ahead.']::text[], array['Clean one kettlebell to your shoulder and hold on to the other kettlebell in a hanging position. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrist as you do so.','Lower the cleaned kettlebell to a hanging position and clean the alternate kettlebell. Repeat.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternating_hang_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternating_Hang_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'double_kettlebell_alternating_hang_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'double_kettlebell_alternating_hang_clean', 'Double Kettlebell Alternating Hang Clean', array['Kettlebell Clean (Double, Alternating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Double Kettlebell Alternating Hang Clean is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the biceps, calves, forearms, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the kettlebell clean: two kettlebells, alternating sides from the hang.', array['Place two kettlebells between your feet. To get in the starting position, push your butt back and look straight ahead.']::text[], array['Clean one kettlebell to your shoulder and hold on to the other kettlebell.','With a fluid motion, lower the top kettlebell while driving the bottom kettlebell up.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/double_kettlebell_alternating_hang_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Alternating_Hang_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_dead_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_dead_clean', 'Kettlebell Dead Clean', array['Kettlebell Clean (Dead Clean)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Dead Clean is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the kettlebell clean: each rep starts from the floor.', array['Place kettlebell between your feet. To get in the starting position, push your butt back and look straight ahead.']::text[], array['Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulders by extending through the legs and hips as you raise the kettlebell towards your shoulder. The wrist should rotate as you do so.','Lower the kettlebell, keeping the hamstrings loaded by keeping your back straight and your butt out.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_dead_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Dead_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_open_palm_kettlebell_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_open_palm_kettlebell_clean', 'One-Arm Open Palm Kettlebell Clean', array['Kettlebell Clean (Open Palm, Single)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Open Palm Kettlebell Clean is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the forearms, glutes, lower back and quadriceps. A variation of the kettlebell clean: released and caught with an open hand.', array['Place one kettlebell between your feet.']::text[], array['Grab the handle with one hand and raise the kettlebell rapidly, let it flip so that the ball of the kettlebell lands in the palm of your hand.','Throw the kettlebell out in front of you and catch the handle with one hand.','Take the kettlebell to the floor and repeat. Make sure to work both arms.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_open_palm_kettlebell_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Open_Palm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'open_palm_kettlebell_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'open_palm_kettlebell_clean', 'Open Palm Kettlebell Clean', array['Kettlebell Clean (Open Palm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Open Palm Kettlebell Clean is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes, lower back and quadriceps. A variation of the kettlebell clean: released and caught with an open hand.', array['Place one kettlebell between your feet. Clean the kettlebell by extending through the legs and hips as you raise the kettlebell towards your shoulders.']::text[], array['Release the kettlebell as it comes up, and let it flip so that the ball of the kettlebell lands in the palms of your hands.','Release the kettlebell out in front of you and catch the handle with both hands. Lower the kettlebell to the starting position and repeat.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/open_palm_kettlebell_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Open_Palm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_swings')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_swings', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Swings', array['Kettlebell Swing (Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Swings is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, glutes and lower back. A variation of the kettlebell swing: one hand; the core resists twisting.', array['Stand with feet a little wider than shoulder width and a kettlebell on the floor just in front of you. Hinge at the hips and grip the handle with one hand.']::text[], array['Hike the kettlebell back between your legs, keeping the back flat and the free arm out to the side for balance.','Drive the hips forward forcefully to stand tall, letting the momentum swing the kettlebell up to about chest height. The arm guides the bell; the hips lift it.','Let the bell fall back down, hinge at the hips as it passes between your legs, and go straight into the next swing.','Complete the set, then switch hands.']::text[], array['It is a hinge, not a squat','Snap the hips; arms just hold on','Stand tall and squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Squatting the bell up','Lifting with the arms','Leaning back at the top']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_swings/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Swings/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'vertical_swing')::uuid, 'mfd', 'vertical_swing', 'Vertical Swing', array['Kettlebell Swing (Dumbbell)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Vertical Swing is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes and quadriceps. A variation of the kettlebell swing: one dumbbell held by the end with both hands, swung up overhead.', array['Allow the dumbbell to hang at arms length between your legs, holding it with both hands. Keep your back straight and your head up.']::text[], array['Swing the dumbbell between your legs, flexing at the hips and bending the knees slightly.','Powerfully reverse the motion by extending at the hips, knees, and ankles to propel yourself upward, swinging the dumbell over your head.','As you land, absorb the impact through your legs and draw the dumbbell to your torso before the next repetition.']::text[], array['It is a hinge, not a squat','Snap the hips; arms just hold on','Stand tall and squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Squatting the bell up','Lifting with the arms','Leaning back at the top']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/vertical_swing/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Vertical_Swing/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'ball_leg_curl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'ball_leg_curl', 'Ball Leg Curl', array['Leg Curl (Stability Ball)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Ball Leg Curl is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves and glutes. A variation of the leg curl: lying on the back, heels on a ball, hips lifted; curl the ball in.', array['Begin on the floor laying on your back with your feet on top of the ball.']::text[], array['Position the ball so that when your legs are extended your ankles are on top of the ball. This will be your starting position.','Raise your hips off of the ground, keeping your weight on the shoulder blades and your feet.','Flex the knees, pulling the ball as close to you as you can, contracting the hamstrings.','After a brief pause, return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Hips stay down','Control the return']::text[], array['Lifting the hips to cheat','Partial range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/ball_leg_curl/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Ball_Leg_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_curl_lying')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_curl_lying', 'Lying Leg Curl (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending the knees against a pad to isolate the hamstrings.', array['Lie face down with your knees just past the bench edge.','Place the pad just above your heels.']::text[], array['Curl your heels toward your glutes.','Squeeze the hamstrings.','Return slowly to straight legs.']::text[], array['Hips stay down','Control the return']::text[], array['Lifting the hips to cheat','Partial range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_curl_lying/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Leg_Curls/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'platform_hamstring_slides')::uuid, 'mfd', 'platform_hamstring_slides', 'Platform Hamstring Slides', array['Leg Curl (Slider)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Platform Hamstring Slides is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes. A variation of the leg curl: heels on sliders or a towel with the hips lifted; slide the heels in.', array['For this movement a wooden floor or similar is needed. Lay on your back with your legs extended. Place a gym towel or a light weight underneath your heel. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the movement by flexing the knee, keeping your other leg straight.','Continue bringing the heel closer to you, sliding it on the floor.','At full knee flexion, reverse the movement to return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Hips stay down','Control the return']::text[], array['Lifting the hips to cheat','Partial range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/platform_hamstring_slides/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Platform_Hamstring_Slides/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'prone_manual_hamstring')::uuid, 'mfd', 'prone_manual_hamstring', 'Prone Manual Hamstring', array['Leg Curl (Partner)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Prone Manual Hamstring is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings. A variation of the leg curl: lying face down; a partner resists the curl by hand.', array['You will need a partner for this exercise. Lay face down with your legs straight. Your assistant will place their hand on your heel.']::text[], array['To begin, flex the knee to curl your leg up. Your partner should provide resistance, starting light and increasing the pressure as the movement is completed. Communicate with your partner to monitor appropriate resistance levels.','Pause at the top, returning the leg to the starting position as your partner provides resistance going the other direction.']::text[], array['Hips stay down','Control the return']::text[], array['Lifting the hips to cheat','Partial range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/prone_manual_hamstring/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Prone_Manual_Hamstring/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_band_hamstring_curl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_band_hamstring_curl', 'Seated Band Hamstring Curl', array['Leg Curl (Band, Seated)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Seated Band Hamstring Curl is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings. A variation of the leg curl: seated, a band anchored in front of you.', array['Secure a band close to the ground and place a bench a couple feet away from it.']::text[], array['Seat yourself on the bench and secure the band behind your ankles, beginning with your legs straight. This will be your starting position.','Flex the knees, bringing your feet towards the bench. You may need to lean back slightly to keep your feet from striking the floor.','Pause at the completion of the movement, and then slowly return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Hips stay down','Control the return']::text[], array['Lifting the hips to cheat','Partial range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_band_hamstring_curl/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Band_Hamstring_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_curl_seated')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_curl_seated', 'Seated Leg Curl (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending the knees against a pad to isolate the hamstrings.', array['Sit with the back of your knees at the edge of the seat and lock the thigh pad down.','Place the lower pad behind your ankles.']::text[], array['Curl your heels toward your glutes.','Squeeze the hamstrings.','Return slowly to straight legs.']::text[], array['Hips stay down','Control the return']::text[], array['Lifting the hips to cheat','Partial range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_curl_seated/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Leg_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_curl_standing')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_curl_standing', 'Standing Leg Curls', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending the knees against a pad to isolate the hamstrings.', array['Adjust the machine so your knees line up with the pivot.','Place the pad just above your heels.']::text[], array['Curl your heels toward your glutes.','Squeeze the hamstrings.','Return slowly to straight legs.']::text[], array['Hips stay down','Control the return']::text[], array['Lifting the hips to cheat','Partial range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_curl_standing/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Leg_Curl/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lunge_pass_through')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lunge_pass_through', 'Lunge Pass Through', array['Lunge (Kettlebell Pass-Through)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lunge Pass Through is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, glutes and quadriceps. A variation of the lunge: pass a kettlebell under the front leg on each lunge.', array['Stand with your torso upright holding a kettlebell in your right hand. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Step forward with your left foot and lower your upper body down by flexing the hip and the knee, keeping the torso upright. Lower your back knee until it nearly touches the ground.','As you lunge, pass the kettlebell under your front leg to your opposite hand.','Pressing through the heel of your foot, return to the starting position.','Repeat the movement for the recommended amount of repetitions, alternating legs.']::text[], array['Torso upright','Front knee in line with the toes','Push through the front heel']::text[], array['Front knee caving in','Step too short so the heel lifts','Leaning forward']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lunge_pass_through/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lunge_Pass_Through/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'floor_glute_ham_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'floor_glute_ham_raise', 'Floor Glute-Ham Raise', array['Nordic Hamstring Curl (Floor)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Floor Glute-Ham Raise is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves and glutes. A variation of the nordic hamstring curl: kneeling with the ankles held down by a partner or bar.', array['You can use a partner for this exercise or brace your feet under something stable.']::text[], array['Begin on your knees with your upper legs and torso upright. If using a partner, they will firmly hold your feet to keep you in position. This will be your starting position.','Lower yourself by extending at the knee, taking care to NOT flex the hips as you go forward.','Place your hands in front of you as you reach the floor. This movement is very difficult and you may be unable to do it unaided. Use your arms to lightly push off the floor to aid your return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Straight line from knees to head','Fight the fall']::text[], array['Bending at the hips']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/floor_glute_ham_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Floor_Glute-Ham_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'nordic_hamstring_curl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'nordic_hamstring_curl', 'Nordic Hamstrings Curls', array['nordic curl']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Kneeling with your ankles anchored, you lower your body forward as slowly as possible using the hamstrings.', array['Kneel on a pad with your ankles secured under something solid or held by a partner.']::text[], array['Keeping hips straight, lean forward and lower your body as slowly as you can.','Catch yourself with your hands.','Push off lightly and pull back up with the hamstrings.']::text[], array['Straight line from knees to head','Fight the fall']::text[], array['Bending at the hips']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/nordic_hamstring_curl/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Natural_Glute_Ham_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pilates')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pilates', 'Pilates', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Low-impact exercise focused on core control, posture and flexibility.', '{}'::text[], array['Follow a mat or reformer session suited to your level.']::text[], array['Move slowly and with control','Keep the core engaged']::text[], array['Rushing the movements']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'split_squats')::uuid, 'mfd', 'split_squats', 'Split Squats', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Split Squats is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, glutes and quadriceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Being in a standing position. Jump into a split leg position, with one leg forward and one leg back, flexing the knees and lowering your hips slightly as you do so.','As you descend, immediately reverse direction, standing back up and jumping, reversing the position of your legs. Repeat 5-10 times on each leg.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/split_squats/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Split_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'romanian_deadlift_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'romanian_deadlift_barbell', 'Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)', array['rdl','barbell rdl']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A deadlift that starts standing and lowers only until the hamstrings are stretched, with soft knees. One of the best hamstring exercises.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs, feet hip-width apart.','Unlock your knees slightly.']::text[], array['Push your hips back and let the weight slide down the front of your legs.','Keep your back flat and knees soft (they barely move).','Stop when you feel a strong stretch in the hamstrings, usually just below the knee.','Drive the hips forward to stand up.']::text[], array['Hips go back, not down','Weight stays close to the legs','Flat back from head to hips']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach lower','Bending the knees into a squat','Letting the weight drift forward']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/romanian_deadlift_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Romanian_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'romanian_deadlift_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'romanian_deadlift_dumbbell', 'Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)', array['db rdl']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A deadlift that starts standing and lowers only until the hamstrings are stretched, with soft knees. One of the best hamstring exercises.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs, feet hip-width apart.','Unlock your knees slightly.']::text[], array['Push your hips back and let the weight slide down the front of your legs.','Keep your back flat and knees soft (they barely move).','Stop when you feel a strong stretch in the hamstrings, usually just below the knee.','Drive the hips forward to stand up.']::text[], array['Hips go back, not down','Weight stays close to the legs','Flat back from head to hips']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach lower','Bending the knees into a squat','Letting the weight drift forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'romanian_deadlift_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'romanian_deadlift_smith', 'Romanian Deadlift (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A deadlift that starts standing and lowers only until the hamstrings are stretched, with soft knees. One of the best hamstring exercises.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs, feet hip-width apart.','Unlock your knees slightly.']::text[], array['Push your hips back and let the weight slide down the front of your legs.','Keep your back flat and knees soft (they barely move).','Stop when you feel a strong stretch in the hamstrings, usually just below the knee.','Drive the hips forward to stand up.']::text[], array['Hips go back, not down','Weight stays close to the legs','Flat back from head to hips']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach lower','Bending the knees into a squat','Letting the weight drift forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'romanian_deadlift_from_deficit')::uuid, 'mfd', 'romanian_deadlift_from_deficit', 'Romanian Deadlift from Deficit', array['Romanian Deadlift (Deficit)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Romanian Deadlift from Deficit is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the forearms, glutes, lower back and traps. A variation of the romanian deadlift: standing on a platform for a longer stretch at the bottom.', array['Begin standing while holding a bar at arm''s length in front of you. You can stand on a raised platform to increase the range of motion.']::text[], array['Begin by flexing the knees slightly, and then flex at the hip, moving your butt back as far as possible, lowering the torso as far as flexibility allows. The back should remain in absolute extension at all times, and the bar should remain in contact with the legs. If done properly, there should be heavy tension felt in the hamstrings.','Reverse the motion to return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Hips go back, not down','Weight stays close to the legs','Flat back from head to hips']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach lower','Bending the knees into a squat','Letting the weight drift forward']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/romanian_deadlift_from_deficit/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Romanian_Deadlift_from_Deficit/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_one_legged_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_one_legged_deadlift', 'Kettlebell One-Legged Deadlift', array['Single Leg Romanian Deadlift (Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell One-Legged Deadlift is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes and lower back. A variation of the single leg romanian deadlift: kettlebell held in the hand opposite the standing leg.', array['Hold a kettlebell by the handle in one hand. Stand on one leg, on the same side that you hold the kettlebell.']::text[], array['Keeping that knee slightly bent, perform a stiff legged deadlift by bending at the hip, extending your free leg behind you for balance.','Continue lowering the kettlebell until you are parallel to the ground, and then return to the upright position.']::text[], array['Hips stay square to the floor','Body moves like a seesaw']::text[], array['Opening the hip toward the ceiling','Rounding the back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_one_legged_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_One-Legged_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_romanian_deadlift_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_romanian_deadlift_barbell', 'Single Leg Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A Romanian deadlift on one leg with the other leg extending behind you. Builds hamstrings, glutes and balance.', array['Stand on one leg holding the weight, standing knee slightly bent.']::text[], array['Hinge forward at the hip while the free leg extends straight back.','Lower until your torso is close to parallel or you feel the stretch.','Return to standing by driving the hip forward.']::text[], array['Hips stay square to the floor','Body moves like a seesaw']::text[], array['Opening the hip toward the ceiling','Rounding the back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_romanian_deadlift_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_romanian_deadlift_dumbbell', 'Single Leg Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)', array['single leg rdl','sl rdl']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A Romanian deadlift on one leg with the other leg extending behind you. Builds hamstrings, glutes and balance.', array['Stand on one leg holding the weight, standing knee slightly bent.']::text[], array['Hinge forward at the hip while the free leg extends straight back.','Lower until your torso is close to parallel or you feel the stretch.','Return to standing by driving the hip forward.']::text[], array['Hips stay square to the floor','Body moves like a seesaw']::text[], array['Opening the hip toward the ceiling','Rounding the back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'prowler_sprint')::uuid, 'mfd', 'prowler_sprint', 'Prowler Sprint', array['Sled Push (Sprint)']::text[], 'cardio', 'distance_time', 'Prowler Sprint is a beginner-level cardio exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the cardio, calves, chest, glutes and quadriceps. A variation of the sled push: light sled, sprinting.', array['Place your sled on an appropriate surface, loaded to a suitable weight. The sled should provide enough resistance to require effort, but not so heavy that you are significantly slowed down.']::text[], array['You may use the upright or the low handles for this exercise. Place your hands on the handles with your arms extended, leaning into the implement.','With good posture, drive through the ground with alternating, short steps. Move as fast as you can for a short distance.']::text[], array['Low body angle','Drive the knees forward']::text[], array['Standing too upright','Long, slow strides']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/prowler_sprint/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Prowler_Sprint/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hang_snatch_below_knees')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hang_snatch_below_knees', 'Hang Snatch - Below Knees', array['Snatch (Hang, Below Knees)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Hang Snatch - Below Knees is an advanced-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abs & core, calves, forearms, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the snatch: starts from the hang just below the knees.', array['Begin with a wide grip on the bar, with an overhand or hook grip. The feet should be directly below the hips with the feet turned out. Your knees should be slightly bent, and the torso inclined forward. The spine should be fully extended and the head facing forward. The bar should be just below the knees. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Aggressively extend through the legs and hips. At peak extension, shrug the shoulders and allow the elbows to flex to the side.','As you move your feet into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. Receive the bar with your body as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead.','Return to a standing position with the weight overhead, and then return the weight to the floor under control.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hang_snatch_below_knees/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hang_Snatch_-_Below_Knees/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'muscle_snatch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'muscle_snatch', 'Muscle Snatch', array['Snatch (Muscle)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Muscle Snatch is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes, lower back, quadriceps and triceps. A variation of the snatch: no re-bend of the knees; the arms finish the lift.', array['Begin with a loaded barbell held at the mid thigh position with a wide grip. The feet should be directly below the hips, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hips, with the chest up and the head looking forward. The shoulders should be just in front of the bar. This will be the starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hips knees and ankles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body.','Continue raising the bar to the overhead position, without rebending the knees.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/muscle_snatch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Muscle_Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'split_snatch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'split_snatch', 'Split Snatch', array['Snatch (Split)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Split Snatch is an advanced-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, forearms, glutes, lower back, quadriceps, traps and triceps. A variation of the snatch: caught in a split stance.', array['Begin with a loaded barbell on the floor. The bar should be close to or touching the shins, and a wide grip should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hips, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hips, with the chest up and the head looking forward. The shoulders should be just in front of the bar. This will be the starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the ground. The back angle should stay the same until the bar passes the knees.','Transition into the second pull by extending through the hips knees and ankles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the shoulders and allow the elbows to flex to the side.','As you move your feet into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move forcefully to a split position, one foot forward one foot back. Receive the bar with your body as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead.','Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, your head and chest up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position, bringing your feet together.','Carefully return the weight to floor.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/split_snatch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Split_Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'linear_3_part_start_technique')::uuid, 'mfd', 'linear_3_part_start_technique', 'Linear 3-Part Start Technique', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Linear 3-Part Start Technique is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves and quadriceps.', array['This drill helps you accelerate as quickly as possible into a sprint from a dead stop. It helps to use a line to start from. Begin with two feet on the line. Place your left foot with the toe next to your right ankle. Place your right foot 4-6 inches behind the left.']::text[], array['Place your right hand onto the line, and thing bring your nose close to your left knee.','Squat down as you lean foward, your head being lower than your hips and your weight loaded onto the left leg. This will be your starting position.','Take your left hand up so that it is parallel to the ground, pointing behind you, and explode out when ready.']::text[], array['Drive the knee up and the foot down under the hips','Arms swing from the shoulder, elbows about 90 degrees','Stay tall with a slight forward lean']::text[], array['Reaching out with the foot in front of the body','Arms crossing the body','Running the drill tired; quality comes first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/linear_3_part_start_technique/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Linear_3-Part_Start_Technique/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'linear_acceleration_wall_drill')::uuid, 'mfd', 'linear_acceleration_wall_drill', 'Linear Acceleration Wall Drill', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Linear Acceleration Wall Drill is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves, glutes and quadriceps.', array['Lean at around 45 degrees against a wall. Your feet should be together, glutes contracted.']::text[], array['Begin by lifting your right knee quickly, pausing, and then driving it straight down into the ground.','Switch legs, raising the opposite knee, and then attacking the ground straight down.','Repeat once more with your right leg, and as soon as the right foot strikes the ground hammer them out rapidly, alternating left and right as fast as you can.']::text[], array['Drive the knee up and the foot down under the hips','Arms swing from the shoulder, elbows about 90 degrees','Stay tall with a slight forward lean']::text[], array['Reaching out with the foot in front of the body','Arms crossing the body','Running the drill tired; quality comes first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/linear_acceleration_wall_drill/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Linear_Acceleration_Wall_Drill/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'moving_claw_series')::uuid, 'mfd', 'moving_claw_series', 'Moving Claw Series', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Moving Claw Series is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the calves and quadriceps.', array['This move helps prepare your running form to help you excel at sprinting. As you run, be sure to flex the knee, aiming to kick your glutes as the hip extends.']::text[], array['Reload the quad as the leg moves back forward, attacking the ground on the next step.','Ensure that as you run, you block with the arms, punching through in a rapid 1-2 motion.']::text[], array['Drive the knee up and the foot down under the hips','Arms swing from the shoulder, elbows about 90 degrees','Stay tall with a slight forward lean']::text[], array['Reaching out with the foot in front of the body','Arms crossing the body','Running the drill tired; quality comes first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/moving_claw_series/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Moving_Claw_Series/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_stiff_legged_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_stiff_legged_deadlift', 'Smith Machine Stiff-Legged Deadlift', array['Straight Leg Deadlift (Smith)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine Stiff-Legged Deadlift is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes and lower back. A variation of the straight leg deadlift: smith machine bar.', array['To begin, set the bar on the smith machine to a height that is around the middle of your thighs. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, grasp the bar using a pronated (palms forward) grip that is shoulder width apart. You may need some wrist wraps if using a significant amount of weight.']::text[], array['Lift the bar up by fully extending your arms while keeping your back straight. Stand with your torso straight and your legs spaced using a shoulder width or narrower stance. The knees should be slightly bent. This is your starting position.','Keeping the knees stationary, lower the barbell to over the top of your feet by bending at the waist while keeping your back straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from the floor until you feel a stretch on the hamstrings. Exhale as you perform this movement','Start bringing your torso up straight again as soon as you feel the hamstrings stretch by extending your hips and waist until you are back at the starting position. Inhale as you perform this movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Flat back is more important than depth','Bar close to the legs']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_stiff_legged_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Stiff-Legged_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'stiff_legged_dumbbell_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'stiff_legged_dumbbell_deadlift', 'Stiff-Legged Dumbbell Deadlift', array['Straight Leg Deadlift (Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Stiff-Legged Dumbbell Deadlift is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the glutes and lower back. A variation of the straight leg deadlift: dumbbells.', array['Grasp a couple of dumbbells holding them by your side at arm''s length.']::text[], array['Stand with your torso straight and your legs spaced using a shoulder width or narrower stance. The knees should be slightly bent. This is your starting position.','Keeping the knees stationary, lower the dumbbells to over the top of your feet by bending at the waist while keeping your back straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from the floor until you feel a stretch on the hamstrings. Exhale as you perform this movement','Start bringing your torso up straight again by extending your hips and waist until you are back at the starting position. Inhale as you perform this movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Flat back is more important than depth','Dumbbells close to the legs']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/stiff_legged_dumbbell_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Stiff-Legged_Dumbbell_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'straight_leg_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'straight_leg_deadlift', 'Straight Leg Deadlift', array['stiff leg deadlift','sldl']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A deadlift with nearly straight legs, starting from the floor each rep. Places a large stretch on the hamstrings.', array['Stand with the bar over mid-foot, knees only slightly bent.','Hinge to grip the bar with a flat back.']::text[], array['Lift the bar by driving the hips forward, keeping the legs nearly straight.','Lower by pushing the hips back until the bar reaches the floor or your flexibility limit.']::text[], array['Flat back is more important than depth','Bar close to the legs']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/straight_leg_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Stiff-Legged_Barbell_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wide_stance_stiff_legs')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wide_stance_stiff_legs', 'Wide Stance Stiff Legs', array['Straight Leg Deadlift (Wide Stance)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Wide Stance Stiff Legs is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the adductors, glutes and lower back. A variation of the straight leg deadlift: a wide stance adds the inner thighs.', '{}'::text[], array['Begin with a barbell loaded on the floor. Adopt a wide stance, and then bend at the hips to grab the bar. Your hips should be as far back as possible, and your legs nearly straight. Keep your back straight, and your head and chest up. This will be your starting position.','Begin the movement be engaging the hips, driving them forward as you allow the arms to hang straight. Continue until you are standing straight up, and then slowly return the weight to the starting position. For successive reps, the weight need not touch the floor.']::text[], array['Flat back is more important than depth','Bar close to the legs']::text[], array['Rounding the back to reach the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wide_stance_stiff_legs/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide_Stance_Stiff_Legs/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'stretching')::uuid, 'mfd', 'stretching', 'Stretching', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Static or dynamic stretching to improve flexibility and recovery.', '{}'::text[], array['Warm up the muscles first.','Hold each static stretch for 20–60 seconds without bouncing.']::text[], array['Mild tension, never pain','Relax into the stretch']::text[], array['Bouncing','Stretching cold muscles hard']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'power_stairs')::uuid, 'mfd', 'power_stairs', 'Power Stairs', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Power Stairs is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the adductors, calves, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps.', array['In the power stairs, implements are moved up a staircase. For training purposes, these can be performed with a tire or box.']::text[], array['Begin by taking the implement with both hands. Set your feet wide, with your head and chest up. Drive through the ground with your heels, extending your knees and hips to raise the weight from the ground.','As you lean back, attempt to swing the weight onto the stairs, which are usually around 16-18" high. You can use your legs to help push the weight onto the stair.','Repeat for 3-5 repetitions, and continue with a heavier weight, moving as fast as possible.']::text[], array['Straddle the implement and wrap it tight to the body','Lap it first if needed, then drive the hips forward to load','Keep it close the whole way']::text[], array['Pulling with the arms','Letting it drift away from the body','Rounding with no brace']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/power_stairs/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Power_Stairs/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_band_sumo_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_band_sumo_deadlift', 'Reverse Band Sumo Deadlift', array['Sumo Deadlift (Reverse Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Band Sumo Deadlift is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, forearms, glutes, lower back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the sumo deadlift: bands from above help off the floor.', array['Begin with a bar loaded on the floor inside of a power rack. Attach bands to the top of the rack, using either pegs or the frame itself. Attach the other end to the barbell.']::text[], array['Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hips to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the shoulders, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the shoulders, which in effect lengthens your arms.','Take a breath, and then lower your hips, looking forward with your head with your chest up. Drive through the floor, spreading your feet apart, with your weight on the back half of your feet. Extend through the hips and knees.','As the bar passes through the knees, lean back and drive the hips into the bar, pulling your shoulder blades together.','Return the weight to the ground by bending at the hips and controlling the weight on the way down.']::text[], array['Knees out over the toes','Chest up, hips close to the bar']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Hips rising first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_band_sumo_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Sumo_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sumo_deadlift_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sumo_deadlift_with_bands', 'Sumo Deadlift with Bands', array['Sumo Deadlift (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Sumo Deadlift with Bands is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the adductors, forearms, glutes, lower back, upper back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the sumo deadlift: bands add load toward lockout.', array['To deadlift with short bands, simply loop them over the bar before you start, and step into them to set up. Ensure that they under the back half of your foot, directly where you are driving into the floor.']::text[], array['Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hips to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the shoulders, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip.','Take a breath, and then lower your hips, looking forward with your head with your chest up. Drive through the floor, spreading your feet apart, with your weight on the back half of your feet. Extend through the hips and knees.','As the bar passes through the knees, lean back and drive the hips into the bar, pulling your shoulder blades together.','Return the weight to the ground by bending at the hips and controlling the weight on the way down.']::text[], array['Knees out over the toes','Chest up, hips close to the bar']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Hips rising first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sumo_deadlift_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift_with_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sumo_deadlift_with_chains')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sumo_deadlift_with_chains', 'Sumo Deadlift with Chains', array['Sumo Deadlift (Chains)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Sumo Deadlift with Chains is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the hamstrings, with help from the abductors, adductors, forearms, glutes, lower back, upper back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the sumo deadlift: chains add load toward lockout.', array['You can attach the chains to the sleeves of the bar, or just drape the middle over the bar so there is a greater weight increase as you lift. Attempt to keep the ends of the chains away from the plates so you don''t hit them when you lower the weight.']::text[], array['Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hips to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the shoulders, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the shoulders, which in effect lengthens your arms.','Take a breath, and then lower your hips, looking forward with your head with your chest up. Drive through the floor, spreading your feet apart, with your weight on the back half of your feet. Extend through the hips and knees.','As the bar passes through the knees, lean back and drive the hips into the bar, pulling your shoulder blades together.','Return the weight to the ground by bending at the hips and controlling the weight on the way down.']::text[], array['Knees out over the toes','Chest up, hips close to the bar']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Hips rising first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sumo_deadlift_with_chains/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift_with_Chains/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'yoga')::uuid, 'mfd', 'yoga', 'Yoga', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'A practice of postures, breathing and movement for flexibility, strength and relaxation.', '{}'::text[], array['Follow a class or sequence suited to your level.','Move into each pose only as far as is comfortable.']::text[], array['Breathe slowly through the nose','Never force a stretch']::text[], array['Forcing range of motion','Holding the breath']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chair_lower_back_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chair_lower_back_stretch', 'Chair Lower Back Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Chair Lower Back Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lats, with help from the lower back.', array['Sit upright on a chair.']::text[], array['Bend to one side with your arm over your head. You can hold onto the chair with your free hand.','Hold for 10 seconds, and repeat for your other side.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chair_lower_back_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chair_Lower_Back_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'ball_slam')::uuid, 'mfd', 'ball_slam', 'Ball Slams', array['medicine ball slam']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting a slam ball overhead and throwing it into the floor as hard as you can.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width holding a slam ball (one that does not bounce).']::text[], array['Lift the ball overhead, rising onto your toes.','Slam it down hard in front of your feet, hinging with it.','Pick it up and repeat.']::text[], array['Use the whole body','Hinge to pick it up']::text[], array['Rounding the back to pick up the ball']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/ball_slam/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Overhead_Slam/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_row_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_row_band', 'Bent Over Row (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A standing row with the torso hinged forward. It builds the whole upper back and lats and trains you to hold a strong hip hinge.', array['Stand on the middle of the band with feet hip-width apart.','Hinge forward with a flat back and hold the band ends with arms straight.']::text[], array['Pull the weight toward your lower ribs or upper stomach.','Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the top.','Lower under control until your arms are straight again, keeping the torso still.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_row_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_row_barbell', 'Bent Over Row (Barbell)', array['row','barbell row','bb row']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A standing row with the torso hinged forward. It builds the whole upper back and lats and trains you to hold a strong hip hinge.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart, holding the weight with an overhand grip just wider than your knees.','Push your hips back and bend the knees slightly until your torso is at about 30–45° above horizontal.','Let your arms hang straight down, back flat, neck in line with the spine.']::text[], array['Pull the weight toward your lower ribs or upper stomach.','Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the top.','Lower under control until your arms are straight again, keeping the torso still.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_row_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Barbell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_row_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_row_dumbbell', 'Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)', array['db row bent over']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A standing row with the torso hinged forward. It builds the whole upper back and lats and trains you to hold a strong hip hinge.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart, holding the weight with an overhand grip just wider than your knees.','Push your hips back and bend the knees slightly until your torso is at about 30–45° above horizontal.','Let your arms hang straight down, back flat, neck in line with the spine.']::text[], array['Pull the weight toward your lower ribs or upper stomach.','Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the top.','Lower under control until your arms are straight again, keeping the torso still.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_row_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Two-Dumbbell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_row_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_row_smith', 'Bent Over Row (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A standing row with the torso hinged forward. It builds the whole upper back and lats and trains you to hold a strong hip hinge.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart, holding the weight with an overhand grip just wider than your knees.','Push your hips back and bend the knees slightly until your torso is at about 30–45° above horizontal.','Let your arms hang straight down, back flat, neck in line with the spine.']::text[], array['Pull the weight toward your lower ribs or upper stomach.','Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the top.','Lower under control until your arms are straight again, keeping the torso still.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_row_smith/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Bent_Over_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_against_wall')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_against_wall', 'One Arm Against Wall', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'One Arm Against Wall is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lats.', '{}'::text[], array['From a standing position, place a bent arm against a wall or doorway.','Slowly lean toward your arm until you feel a stretch in your lats.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_against_wall/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Arm_Against_Wall/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_lat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_lat', 'Overhead Lat', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Overhead Lat is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the lats, with help from the triceps.', array['Sit upright on the floor with your partner behind you. Raise one arm straight up, and flex the elbow, attempting to touch your hand to your back. Your parner should hold your tricep and wrist. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Attempt to pull your upper arm to your side as your partner prevents you from doing actually doing so.','After 10-20 seconds, relax the arm and allow your partner to further stretch the lat by applying gentle pressure to the tricep. Hold for 10-20 seconds, and then switch sides.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_lat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Overhead_Lat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_lying_floor_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_lying_floor_stretch', 'Side-Lying Floor Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Side-Lying Floor Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lats.', '{}'::text[], array['First lie on your left side, bending your left knee in front of you to stabilize your torso (use your abdominal muscles as well to hold you upright).','Straighten your right leg and rest the right foot on the floor behind your left. Straighten your right arm over your head and gently pull on your right wrist to stretch the entire right side of the body. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_lying_floor_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side-Lying_Floor_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chin_up_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chin_up_bodyweight', 'Chin Up', array['chinup','chin-up']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A pull up with an underhand, shoulder-width grip. It uses more biceps and is usually a little easier than a pull up.', array['Grip the bar underhand with hands about shoulder-width apart.','Hang with straight arms and a tight core.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down to start.','Pull until your chin is over the bar.','Lower slowly to a full hang.']::text[], array['Chest to the bar','Elbows close in front of the body','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Swinging','Stopping short of a full hang']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chin_up_bodyweight/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chin-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chin_up_assisted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chin_up_assisted', 'Chin Up (Assisted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'assisted_bodyweight', 'A pull up with an underhand, shoulder-width grip. It uses more biceps and is usually a little easier than a pull up.', array['Grip the bar underhand with hands about shoulder-width apart.','Hang with straight arms and a tight core.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down to start.','Pull until your chin is over the bar.','Lower slowly to a full hang.']::text[], array['Chest to the bar','Elbows close in front of the body','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Swinging','Stopping short of a full hang']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chin_up_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chin_up_weighted', 'Chin Up (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'A pull up with an underhand, shoulder-width grip. It uses more biceps and is usually a little easier than a pull up.', array['Grip the bar underhand with hands about shoulder-width apart.','Hang with straight arms and a tight core.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down to start.','Pull until your chin is over the bar.','Lower slowly to a full hang.']::text[], array['Chest to the bar','Elbows close in front of the body','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Swinging','Stopping short of a full hang']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chin_up_weighted/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chin-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'climbing')::uuid, 'mfd', 'climbing', 'Climbing', '{}'::text[], 'activity', 'time', 'Indoor or outdoor rock climbing or bouldering.', '{}'::text[], array['Warm up on easy routes.','Climb with straight arms where possible and push with the legs.']::text[], array['Push with the legs','Keep hips close to the wall']::text[], array['Over-gripping','Climbing hard without a warm-up']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_handed_hang')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_handed_hang', 'One Handed Hang', array['Dead Hang (Single Arm)']::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'One Handed Hang is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps. A variation of the dead hang: hang from one hand.', '{}'::text[], array['Grab onto a chinup bar with one hand, using a pronated grip. Keep your feet on the floor or a step. Allow the majority of your weight to hang from that hand, while keeping your feet on the ground. Hold for 10-20 seconds and switch sides.']::text[], array['Relax the legs','Breathe steadily']::text[], array['Swinging','Holding your breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_handed_hang/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Handed_Hang/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_row', 'Dumbbell Row', array['one arm dumbbell row','single arm db row']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A one-arm row with your other hand and knee on a bench for support. A very effective lat exercise that is easy on the lower back.', array['Place one knee and the same-side hand on a flat bench.','Put the other foot on the floor, back flat and roughly parallel to the floor.','Hold the dumbbell with the free arm hanging straight down.']::text[], array['Pull the dumbbell toward your hip, keeping the elbow close to your body.','Pause when the elbow is just past your torso.','Lower slowly until the arm is straight and you feel a stretch in the lat.']::text[], array['Pull toward the hip, not the shoulder','Keep the shoulders square to the floor']::text[], array['Twisting the torso to lift the weight','Shrugging the shoulder up to the ear','Cutting the stretch short']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Dumbbell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dynamic_back_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dynamic_back_stretch', 'Dynamic Back Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Dynamic Back Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lats.', '{}'::text[], array['Stand with your feet shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your arms straight, swing them straight up in front of you 5-10 times, increasing the range of motion each time until your arms are above your head.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dynamic_back_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dynamic_Back_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'latissimus_dorsi_smr')::uuid, 'mfd', 'latissimus_dorsi_smr', 'Latissimus Dorsi-SMR', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Latissimus Dorsi-SMR is a beginner-level self-massage (foam rolling) exercise that mainly targets the lats.', '{}'::text[], array['While lying on the floor, place a foam roll under your back and to one side, just behind your arm pit. This will be your starting position.','Keep the arm of the side being stretched behind and to the side of you as you shift your weight onto your lats, keeping your upper body off of the ground. Hold for 10-30 seconds, and switch sides.']::text[], array['Roll slowly, about 2–3 cm per second','Pause 20–30 seconds on tender spots','Support your weight with hands and feet to control the pressure','30–90 seconds per area']::text[], array['Rolling fast back and forth','Rolling directly over joints or bones','Pressing so hard you tense up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/latissimus_dorsi_smr/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Latissimus_Dorsi-SMR/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_lever_hold')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_lever_hold', 'Front Lever Hold', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'A gymnastic hold where you hang from a bar with your body horizontal and face up.', array['Hang from a bar with an overhand grip and straight arms.']::text[], array['Pull the bar down with straight arms while lifting your body to horizontal.','Hold the straight position.']::text[], array['Straight arms, push the bar toward your hips','Body rigid']::text[], array['Bending the arms','Piking at the hips']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_lever_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_lever_raise', 'Front Lever Raise', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A gymnastic hold where you hang from a bar with your body horizontal and face up.', array['Hang from a bar with an overhand grip and straight arms.']::text[], array['From a hang, raise your straight body up to the front lever (or higher) with straight arms.','Lower slowly back to the hang.']::text[], array['Straight arms, push the bar toward your hips','Body rigid']::text[], array['Bending the arms','Piking at the hips']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'gorilla_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'gorilla_row', 'Gorilla Row (Kettlebell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating kettlebell rows from a wide, deep hinge position with the kettlebells on the floor between your feet.', array['Stand with feet wider than shoulders and two kettlebells between your feet.','Hinge forward with a flat back and grip both handles.']::text[], array['Row one kettlebell to your hip while pushing the other into the floor.','Lower it back down and row the other side.','Keep alternating.']::text[], array['Push the down kettlebell into the floor','Hips stay level']::text[], array['Rotating the torso','Rounding the back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'inverted_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'inverted_row', 'Inverted Row', array['australian pull up','body row']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A bodyweight row hanging under a bar with your heels on the floor. Great for building up to pull ups.', array['Set a bar at about hip height in a rack or Smith machine.','Lie under it and grip it slightly wider than shoulder width.','Straighten your body so it forms a line from head to heels.']::text[], array['Pull your chest up to the bar.','Pause, then lower until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays a straight plank','Lead with the chest']::text[], array['Hips sagging','Reaching with the chin instead of the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/inverted_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Inverted_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'landmine_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'landmine_row', 'Landmine Row', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A row using a barbell anchored in a landmine, pulled with both hands close together or one hand at a time.', array['Stand beside or over the loaded end of the landmine bar.','Hinge forward with a flat back and grip the bar near the plates.']::text[], array['Row the bar toward your torso.','Pause, then lower until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Flat back, fixed torso angle','Elbows drive back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Using the legs to heave the bar']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'full_range_of_motion_lat_pulldown')::uuid, 'mfd', 'full_range_of_motion_lat_pulldown', 'Full Range-Of-Motion Lat Pulldown', array['Lat Pulldown (Full Range)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Full Range-Of-Motion Lat Pulldown is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the lat pulldown: leaning back slightly with a full stretch at the top.', '{}'::text[], array['Either standing or seated on a high bench, grasp two stirrup cables that are attached to the high pulleys. Grab with the opposing hand so your arms are crisscrossed about you and your palms are facing forward.','Keeping your chest up and maintaining a slight arch in your lower back, pull the handles down as if you were doing a regular pulldown. The range of motion will be more of an arc. During the movement, rotate your hands so that in the bottom position your palms face each other rather than forward. Return slowly to the starting position and repeat.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/full_range_of_motion_lat_pulldown/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Full_Range-Of-Motion_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kneeling_high_pulley_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kneeling_high_pulley_row', 'Kneeling High Pulley Row', array['Lat Pulldown (Kneeling Row)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kneeling High Pulley Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the lat pulldown: kneeling at a high pulley, pulling to the chest.', array['Select the appropriate weight using a pulley that is above your head. Attach a rope to the cable and kneel a couple of feet away, holding the rope out in front of you with both arms extended. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Initiate the movement by flexing the elbows and fully retracting your shoulders, pulling the rope toward your upper chest with your elbows out.','After pausing briefly, slowly return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kneeling_high_pulley_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kneeling_High_Pulley_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_kneeling_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_kneeling_band', 'Kneeling Pulldown (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A pulldown done kneeling, pulling a band anchored overhead. Good for training at home or warming up.', array['Anchor the band high above you and kneel facing it.','Hold the band with arms straight overhead.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull your hands down beside your shoulders.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the band pull your arms back up slowly until they are straight.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back','Shrugging the shoulders up','Letting the band snap the arms back up']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kneeling_single_arm_high_pulley_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kneeling_single_arm_high_pulley_row', 'Kneeling Single-Arm High Pulley Row', array['Lat Pulldown (Kneeling, Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kneeling Single-Arm High Pulley Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the lat pulldown: kneeling at a high pulley, one arm at a time.', array['Attach a single handle to a high pulley and make your weight selection.']::text[], array['Kneel in front of the cable tower, taking the cable with one hand with your arm extended. This will be your starting position.','Starting with your palm facing forward, pull the weight down to your torso by flexing the elbow and retract the shoulder blade. As you do so, rotate the wrist so that at the completion of the movement, your palm is now facing you.','After a brief pause, return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kneeling_single_arm_high_pulley_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kneeling_Single-Arm_High_Pulley_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_band', 'Lat Pulldown (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A pulldown with a resistance band anchored overhead, done sitting or kneeling.', array['Anchor the band high above you.','Kneel or sit facing the anchor, holding the band with straight arms.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull your hands down beside your shoulders.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the band pull your arms back up slowly until they are straight.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back','Shrugging the shoulders up','Letting the band snap the arms back up']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_cable', 'Lat Pulldown (Cable)', array['pulldown','lat pull down']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated vertical pull that trains the lats. It works like a pull up but lets you choose the load.', array['Adjust the thigh pad so your legs are locked in.','Grip the bar slightly wider than shoulder width with an overhand grip.','Sit down with arms straight and lean back slightly.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull the bar to your upper chest.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight and the lats are stretched.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lat_pulldown_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_machine', 'Lat Pulldown (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated vertical pull that trains the lats. It works like a pull up but lets you choose the load.', array['Adjust the thigh pad so your legs are locked in.','Grip the bar slightly wider than shoulder width with an overhand grip.','Sit down with arms straight and lean back slightly.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull the bar to your upper chest.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight and the lats are stretched.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_close_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_close_grip', 'Lat Pulldown - Close Grip (Cable)', array['close grip pulldown','v bar pulldown']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated vertical pull that trains the lats. It works like a pull up but lets you choose the load.', array['Adjust the thigh pad so your legs are locked in.','Grip the bar slightly wider than shoulder width with an overhand grip.','Sit down with arms straight and lean back slightly.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull the bar to your upper chest.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight and the lats are stretched.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lat_pulldown_close_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Front_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_reverse_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_reverse_grip', 'Reverse Grip Lat Pulldown (Cable)', array['underhand pulldown','supinated pulldown']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated vertical pull that trains the lats. It works like a pull up but lets you choose the load.', array['Adjust the thigh pad so your legs are locked in.','Grip the bar slightly wider than shoulder width with an overhand grip.','Sit down with arms straight and lean back slightly.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull the bar to your upper chest.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight and the lats are stretched.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lat_pulldown_reverse_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Underhand_Cable_Pulldowns/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_single_arm')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_single_arm', 'Single Arm Lat Pulldown', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated vertical pull that trains the lats. It works like a pull up but lets you choose the load.', array['Adjust the thigh pad so your legs are locked in.','Grip the bar slightly wider than shoulder width with an overhand grip.','Sit down with arms straight and lean back slightly.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull the bar to your upper chest.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight and the lats are stretched.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lat_pulldown_single_arm/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Arm_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lat_pulldown_vertical_traction')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lat_pulldown_vertical_traction', 'Vertical Traction (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated vertical pull that trains the lats. It works like a pull up but lets you choose the load.', array['Adjust the thigh pad so your legs are locked in.','Grip the bar slightly wider than shoulder width with an overhand grip.','Sit down with arms straight and lean back slightly.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down first, then pull the bar to your upper chest.','Keep your chest up and elbows pointing down.','Let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight and the lats are stretched.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wide_grip_pulldown_behind_the_neck')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wide_grip_pulldown_behind_the_neck', 'Wide-Grip Pulldown Behind The Neck', array['Lat Pulldown (Behind the Neck)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Wide-Grip Pulldown Behind The Neck is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the lat pulldown: bar pulled behind the head. Needs good shoulder mobility; most people should pull to the chest.', array['Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Make sure that you adjust the knee pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent your body from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar.']::text[], array['Grab the bar with the palms facing forward using the prescribed grip. Note on grips: For a wide grip, your hands need to be spaced out at a distance wider than your shoulder width. For a medium grip, your hands need to be spaced out at a distance equal to your shoulder width and for a close grip at a distance smaller than your shoulder width.','As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torso and head forward. Think of an imaginary line from the center of the bar down to the back of your neck. This is your starting position.','As you breathe out, bring the bar down until it touches the back of your neck by drawing the shoulders and the upper arms down and back. Tip: Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torso should remain stationary and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work except for holding the bar; therefore do not try to pull down the bar using the forearms.','After a second on the contracted position squeezing your shoulder blades together, slowly raise the bar back to the starting position when your arms are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. Inhale during this portion of the movement.','Repeat this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Drive the elbows down toward your back pockets','Chest up to meet the bar','Full stretch at the top']::text[], array['Leaning far back and rowing the weight','Pulling the bar behind the neck','Using momentum from the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wide_grip_pulldown_behind_the_neck/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Pulldown_Behind_The_Neck/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'london_bridges')::uuid, 'mfd', 'london_bridges', 'London Bridges', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'London Bridges is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps, forearms and upper back.', array['Attach a climbing rope to a high beam or cross member. Below it, ensure that the smith machine bar is locked in place with the safeties and cannot move. Alternatively, a secure box could also be utilized.']::text[], array['Stand on the bar, using the rope to balance yourself. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your body straight, lean back and lower your body by slowly going hand over hand with the rope. Continue until you are perpendicular to the ground.','Keeping your body straight, reverse the motion, going hand over hand back to the starting position.']::text[], array['Lean back with a straight body','Pull hand over hand up the rope','Lower with control']::text[], array['Bending at the hips','Dropping fast']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/london_bridges/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/London_Bridges/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'suspension_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'suspension_row', 'Low Row (Suspension)', array['trx row']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A bodyweight row on suspension straps. Walking your feet closer to the anchor makes it harder.', array['Face the anchor holding both handles with arms straight.','Lean back with your body straight, heels on the floor.']::text[], array['Pull your chest toward the handles, elbows close to your sides.','Lower back to straight arms with control.']::text[], array['Body stays rigid','Squeeze the shoulder blades at the top']::text[], array['Hips dropping','Letting the shoulders shrug']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/suspension_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Inverted_Row_with_Straps/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'meadows_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'meadows_row', 'Meadows Rows (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A one-arm landmine row done side-on to the bar, gripping the end of the bar with an overhand grip.', array['Stand side-on to the end of a landmine bar in a staggered stance.','Rest your free forearm on your front knee and hinge forward.','Grip the thick end of the bar overhand.']::text[], array['Row the bar up and back toward your hip.','Lower under control until the arm is straight.']::text[], array['Elbow travels high and back','Keep the hips square']::text[], array['Twisting the torso','Shortening the range']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'catch_and_overhead_throw')::uuid, 'mfd', 'catch_and_overhead_throw', 'Catch and Overhead Throw', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Catch and Overhead Throw is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the abs & core and chest.', array['Begin standing while facing a wall or a partner.']::text[], array['Using both hands, position the ball behind your head, stretching as much as possible, and forcefully throw the ball forward.','Ensure that you follow your throw through, being prepared to receive your rebound from your throw. If you are throwing against the wall, make sure that you stand close enough to the wall to receive the rebound, and aim a little higher than you would with a partner.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/catch_and_overhead_throw/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Catch_and_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kipping_muscle_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kipping_muscle_up', 'Kipping Muscle Up', array['Muscle Up (Kipping)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Kipping Muscle Up is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the abs & core, biceps, forearms, upper back, traps and triceps. A variation of the muscle up: a hip swing helps the pull. Learn the strict version first.', array['Grip the rings using a false grip, with the base of your palms on top of the rings.']::text[], array['Begin with a movement swinging your legs backward slightly.','Counter that movement by swinging your legs forward and up, jerking your chin and chest back, pulling yourself up with both arms as you do so. As you reach the top position of the pull-up, pull the rings to your armpits as you roll your shoulders forward, allowing your elbows to move straight back behind you. This puts you into the proper position to continue into the dip portion of the movement.','Maintaining control and stability, extend through the elbow to complete the motion.','Use care when lowering yourself to the ground.']::text[], array['Pull high and close to the bar','Fast transition']::text[], array['Pulling straight up instead of toward the hips','One arm crossing over before the other ("chicken wing")']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kipping_muscle_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kipping_Muscle_Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'muscle_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'muscle_up', 'Muscle Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A gymnastic skill that combines an explosive pull up with a transition over the bar into a dip.', array['Hang from the bar (or rings) with a false grip or a firm overhand grip.','Engage your shoulders and core.']::text[], array['Pull explosively toward your lower chest, pulling the bar toward your hips.','As the bar reaches your chest, lean forward and rotate your wrists over the bar.','Press up to straight arms above the bar.','Lower back down under control.']::text[], array['Pull high and close to the bar','Fast transition']::text[], array['Pulling straight up instead of toward the hips','One arm crossing over before the other ("chicken wing")']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/muscle_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Muscle_Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pendlay_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pendlay_row', 'Pendlay Row (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A strict, explosive barbell row where each rep starts from a dead stop on the floor with the torso near horizontal.', array['Set up like a deadlift with the bar over mid-foot.','Hinge until your torso is almost parallel to the floor, back flat.','Grip the bar slightly wider than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Pull the bar explosively from the floor to your lower chest.','Lower it back to the floor and let it settle for a moment.','Reset your brace before the next rep.']::text[], array['Torso stays parallel; only the arms move','Explode up, control down']::text[], array['Lifting the torso to help the bar up','Bouncing the bar off the floor']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_kipping')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_kipping', 'Kipping Pull Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the pull.','Pull until your chin clears the bar, leading with the chest.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_negative')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_negative', 'Negative Pull Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Step or jump up so your chin is over the bar.','Lower yourself as slowly as you can, ideally 3–5 seconds, to a full hang.','Step back up and repeat.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_bodyweight', 'Pull Up', array['pullup','pull-up']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the pull.','Pull until your chin clears the bar, leading with the chest.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pull_up_bodyweight/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Pullups/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_assisted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_assisted', 'Pull Up (Assisted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'assisted_bodyweight', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the pull.','Pull until your chin clears the bar, leading with the chest.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_band', 'Pull Up (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'assisted_bodyweight', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the pull.','Pull until your chin clears the bar, leading with the chest.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pull_up_band/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Band_Assisted_Pull-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_weighted', 'Pull Up (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the pull.','Pull until your chin clears the bar, leading with the chest.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pull_up_weighted/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Weighted_Pull_Ups/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_rings')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_rings', 'Ring Pull Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A pull up on gymnastic rings. The rings move freely, which lets the wrists and shoulders find a natural path.', array['Set the rings high enough to hang with straight arms.','Grip the rings with palms facing forward or each other.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down to start.','Pull until your chin is above your hands, letting the palms turn in.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Letting the rings drift wide']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rocky_pull_ups_pulldowns')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rocky_pull_ups_pulldowns', 'Rocky Pull-Ups/Pulldowns', array['Pull Up (Front and Back)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Rocky Pull-Ups/Pulldowns is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the pull up: alternates pulling to the front and behind the neck.', array['Grab the pull-up bar with the palms facing forward using a wide grip.']::text[], array['As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torso back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your chest out. This is your starting position.','Pull your torso up until the bar touches your upper chest by drawing the shoulders and the upper arms down and back. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torso should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.','After a second on the contracted position, start to inhale and slowly lower your torso back to the starting position when your arms are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.','Now repeat the same movements as described above except this time your torso will remain straight as you go up and the bar will touch the back of the neck instead of the upper chest. Tip: Use the head to lean forward slightly as it will help you properly execute this portion of the exercise.','Once you have lowered yourself back down to the starting position, repeat the exercise for the prescribed amount of repetitions in your program.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rocky_pull_ups_pulldowns/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rocky_Pull-Ups_Pulldowns/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_to_side_chins')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_to_side_chins', 'Side To Side Chins', array['Pull Up (Side to Side)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Side To Side Chins is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps, forearms and upper back. A variation of the pull up: pull up toward one hand, then the other.', array['Grab the pull-up bar with the palms facing forward using a wide grip.']::text[], array['As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at a wide grip, bring your torso back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your chest out. This is your starting position.','Pull your torso up while leaning to the left hand side until the bar almost touches your upper chest by drawing the shoulders and the upper arms down and back. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torso should remain stationary as it moves through space (no swinging) and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.','After a second of contraction, inhale as you go back to the starting position.','Now, pull your torso up while leaning to the right hand side until the bar almost touches your upper chest by drawing the shoulders and the upper arms down and back. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torso should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.','After a second of contraction, inhale as you go back to the starting position.','Repeat steps 3-6 until you have performed the prescribed amount of repetitions for each side.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_to_side_chins/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_To_Side_Chins/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_sternum')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_sternum', 'Sternum Pull up (Gironda)', array['gironda pull up']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the pull.','Pull until your chin clears the bar, leading with the chest.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pull_up_sternum/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Gironda_Sternum_Chins/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'v_bar_pullup')::uuid, 'mfd', 'v_bar_pullup', 'V-Bar Pullup', array['Pull Up (V-Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'V-Bar Pullup is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the pull up: a V handle over the bar; close neutral grip.', array['Start by placing the middle of the V-bar in the middle of the pull-up bar (assuming that the pull-up station you are using does not have neutral grip handles). The V-Bar handles will be facing down so that you can hang from the pull-up bar through the use of the handles.']::text[], array['Once you securely place the V-bar, take a hold of the bar from each side and hang from it. Stick your chest out and lean yourself back slightly in order to better engage the lats. This will be your starting position.','Using your lats, pull your torso up while leaning your head back slightly so that you do not hit yourself with the chin-up bar. Continue until your chest nearly touches the V-bar. Exhale as you execute this motion.','After a second hold on the contracted position, slowly lower your body back to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/v_bar_pullup/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/V-Bar_Pullup/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pull_up_wide')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pull_up_wide', 'Wide Pull Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Pulling your body up to a bar with an overhand grip. One of the best exercises for back and arm strength.', array['Grip the bar overhand, slightly wider than shoulder width.','Hang with straight arms and legs together, core tight.']::text[], array['Pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the pull.','Pull until your chin clears the bar, leading with the chest.','Lower under control to a full hang.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wide_grip_rear_pull_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wide_grip_rear_pull_up', 'Wide-Grip Rear Pull-Up', array['Pull Up (Behind the Neck)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Wide-Grip Rear Pull-Up is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the pull up: wide grip, head forward of the bar. Needs good shoulder mobility.', array['Grab the pull-up bar with the palms facing forward using a wide grip.']::text[], array['As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar, bring your torso forward and head so that there is an imaginary line from the pull-up bar to the back of your neck. This is your starting position.','Pull your torso up until the bar is near the back of your neck. To do this, draw the shoulders and upper arms down and back while slightly leaning your head forward. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torso should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.','After a second on the contracted position, start to inhale and slowly lower your torso back to the starting position when your arms are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.','Repeat this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wide_grip_rear_pull_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Rear_Pull-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_arm_barbell_pullover')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_arm_barbell_pullover', 'Bent-Arm Barbell Pullover', array['Pullover (Barbell, Bent Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent-Arm Barbell Pullover is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the chest and triceps. A variation of the pullover: barbell with bent elbows, lying across or along a bench.', array['Lie on a flat bench with a barbell using a shoulder grip width.']::text[], array['Hold the bar straight over your chest with a bend in your arms. This will be your starting position.','While keeping your arms in the bent arm position, lower the weight slowly in an arc behind your head while breathing in until you feel a stretch on the chest.','At that point, bring the barbell back to the starting position using the arc through which the weight was lowered and exhale as you perform this movement.','Hold the weight on the initial position for a second and repeat the motion for the prescribed number of repetitions.']::text[], array['Ribs down; do not arch to get more range','Elbows stay slightly bent']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows','Going deeper than your shoulders allow']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_arm_barbell_pullover/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent-Arm_Barbell_Pullover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pullover_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pullover_dumbbell', 'Pullover (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An arcing movement from over the chest to behind the head and back, stretching and working the lats and chest.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding one dumbbell with both hands above your chest.','Keep a slight bend in the elbows.']::text[], array['Lower the dumbbell in an arc behind your head until you feel a stretch in the lats and chest.','Pull it back over your chest along the same arc.']::text[], array['Ribs down; do not arch to get more range','Elbows stay slightly bent']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows','Going deeper than your shoulders allow']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pullover_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Straight-Arm_Dumbbell_Pullover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pullover_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pullover_machine', 'Pullover (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An arcing movement from over the chest to behind the head and back, stretching and working the lats and chest.', array['Adjust the seat so your shoulders line up with the machine pivot.','Place your elbows or forearms on the pads.']::text[], array['Pull the pads down and forward in an arc until your arms reach your sides.','Return slowly until you feel a stretch in the lats.']::text[], array['Ribs down; do not arch to get more range','Elbows stay slightly bent']::text[], array['Bending and straightening the elbows','Going deeper than your shoulders allow']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'renegade_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'renegade_row', 'Renegade Row (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A row from a high plank on two dumbbells. It trains the back and challenges the core to resist rotation.', array['Get into a high plank with hands on two dumbbells under your shoulders.','Set your feet wider than hip width for balance.']::text[], array['Row one dumbbell to your hip while pushing the other into the floor.','Lower it under control.','Repeat on the other side.']::text[], array['Hips stay square to the floor','Brace like a plank']::text[], array['Twisting the hips up as you row','Sagging the hips']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rope_climb')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rope_climb', 'Rope Climb', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Rope Climb is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps, forearms and upper back.', array['Grab the rope with both hands above your head. Pull down on the rope as you take a small jump.']::text[], array['Wrap the rope around one leg, using your feet to pinch the rope. Reach up as high as possible with your arms, gripping the rope tightly.','Release the rope from your feet as you pull yourself up with your arms, bringing your knees towards your chest.','Resecure your feet on the rope, and then stand up to take another high hold on the rope. Continue until you reach the top of the rope.','To lower yourself, loosen the grip of your feet on the rope as you slide down using a hand over hand motion.']::text[], array['Pull with the arms and lock the rope with the feet','Stand up on the feet, then reach higher','Climb down hand over hand']::text[], array['Climbing with arms only','Sliding down the rope']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rope_climb/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rope_Climb/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'elevated_cable_rows')::uuid, 'mfd', 'elevated_cable_rows', 'Elevated Cable Rows', array['Seated Cable Row (Elevated)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Elevated Cable Rows is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the upper back and traps. A variation of the seated cable row: seated on a box for a lower angle of pull.', array['Get a platform of some sort (it can be an aerobics or calf raise platform) that is around 4-6 inches in height.']::text[], array['Place it on the seat of the cable row machine.','Sit down on the machine and place your feet on the front platform or crossbar provided making sure that your knees are slightly bent and not locked.','Lean over as you keep the natural alignment of your back and grab the V-bar handles.','With your arms extended pull back until your torso is at a 90-degree angle from your legs. Your back should be slightly arched and your chest should be sticking out. You should be feeling a nice stretch on your lats as you hold the bar in front of you. This is the starting position of the exercise.','Keeping the torso stationary, pull the handles back towards your torso while keeping the arms close to it until you touch the abdominals. Breathe out as you perform that movement. At that point you should be squeezing your back muscles hard. Hold that contraction for a second and slowly go back to the original position while breathing in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Sit tall; small forward lean at the stretch is fine','Elbows drive back past the body','Shoulders down, not shrugged']::text[], array['Rocking the torso back and forth','Rounding the back at the front','Pulling with the arms only']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/elevated_cable_rows/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Elevated_Cable_Rows/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_cable_row_bar')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_cable_row_bar', 'Seated Cable Row - Bar Grip', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated row on a low cable station. A controlled way to train the mid back and lats with constant tension.', array['Sit on the bench with feet on the footplate and knees slightly bent.','Grab the handle and sit upright with your arms straight in front of you.']::text[], array['Pull the handle toward your lower ribs while keeping your torso upright.','Squeeze the shoulder blades together.','Let the arms extend forward slowly until you feel a stretch between the shoulder blades.']::text[], array['Sit tall; small forward lean at the stretch is fine','Elbows drive back past the body','Shoulders down, not shrugged']::text[], array['Rocking the torso back and forth','Rounding the back at the front','Pulling with the arms only']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_cable_row_v_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_cable_row_v_grip', 'Seated Cable Row - V Grip (Cable)', array['cable row','low row','close grip cable row','v bar row']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated row on a low cable station. A controlled way to train the mid back and lats with constant tension.', array['Sit on the bench with feet on the footplate and knees slightly bent.','Grab the handle and sit upright with your arms straight in front of you.']::text[], array['Pull the handle toward your lower ribs while keeping your torso upright.','Squeeze the shoulder blades together.','Let the arms extend forward slowly until you feel a stretch between the shoulder blades.']::text[], array['Sit tall; small forward lean at the stretch is fine','Elbows drive back past the body','Shoulders down, not shrugged']::text[], array['Rocking the torso back and forth','Rounding the back at the front','Pulling with the arms only']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_cable_row_v_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Cable_Rows/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shotgun_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shotgun_row', 'Shotgun Row', array['Seated Cable Row (Single Arm, Rotating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Shotgun Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the seated cable row: one arm, with the palm turning up as you pull.', array['Attach a single handle to a low cable.']::text[], array['After selecting the correct weight, stand a couple feet back with a wide-split stance. Your arm should be extended and your shoulder forward. This will be your starting position.','Perform the movement by retracting the shoulder and flexing the elbow. As you pull, supinate the wrist, turning the palm upward as you go.','After a brief pause, return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Sit tall; small forward lean at the stretch is fine','Elbows drive back past the body','Shoulders down, not shrugged']::text[], array['Rocking the torso back and forth','Rounding the back at the front','Pulling with the arms only']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shotgun_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Shotgun_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_cable_row_single_arm')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_cable_row_single_arm', 'Single Arm Cable Row', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated row on a low cable station. A controlled way to train the mid back and lats with constant tension.', array['Sit on the bench with feet on the footplate and knees slightly bent.','Grab the handle and sit upright with your arms straight in front of you.']::text[], array['Pull the handle toward your lower ribs while keeping your torso upright.','Squeeze the shoulder blades together.','Let the arms extend forward slowly until you feel a stretch between the shoulder blades.']::text[], array['Sit tall; small forward lean at the stretch is fine','Elbows drive back past the body','Shoulders down, not shrugged','Do not twist to finish the rep']::text[], array['Rocking the torso back and forth','Rounding the back at the front','Pulling with the arms only']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_cable_row_single_arm/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_One-arm_Cable_Pulley_Rows/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_row_machine_iso_lateral_high')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_row_machine_iso_lateral_high', 'Iso-Lateral High Row (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A plate-loaded or selectorised row machine, usually with a chest pad, for training the back without loading the spine.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at about chest height.','Sit with your chest against the pad and grab the handles with straight arms.']::text[], array['Pull the handles back until your elbows pass your torso.','Squeeze the shoulder blades.','Return slowly.']::text[], array['Chest stays on the pad','Pull with the elbows']::text[], array['Leaning back off the pad','Letting the stack slam between reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_row_machine_iso_lateral_high/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_High_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_row_machine_iso_lateral_low')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_row_machine_iso_lateral_low', 'Iso-Lateral Low Row', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A plate-loaded or selectorised row machine, usually with a chest pad, for training the back without loading the spine.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at about chest height.','Sit with your chest against the pad and grab the handles with straight arms.']::text[], array['Pull the handles back until your elbows pass your torso.','Squeeze the shoulder blades.','Return slowly.']::text[], array['Chest stays on the pad','Pull with the elbows']::text[], array['Leaning back off the pad','Letting the stack slam between reps']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_row_machine_iso_lateral')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_row_machine_iso_lateral', 'Iso-Lateral Row (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A plate-loaded or selectorised row machine, usually with a chest pad, for training the back without loading the spine.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at about chest height.','Sit with your chest against the pad and grab the handles with straight arms.']::text[], array['Pull the handles back until your elbows pass your torso.','Squeeze the shoulder blades.','Return slowly.']::text[], array['Chest stays on the pad','Pull with the elbows']::text[], array['Leaning back off the pad','Letting the stack slam between reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_row_machine_iso_lateral/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_Iso_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_row_machine_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_row_machine_machine', 'Seated Row (Machine)', array['machine row']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A plate-loaded or selectorised row machine, usually with a chest pad, for training the back without loading the spine.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at about chest height.','Sit with your chest against the pad and grab the handles with straight arms.']::text[], array['Pull the handles back until your elbows pass your torso.','Squeeze the shoulder blades.','Return slowly.']::text[], array['Chest stays on the pad','Pull with the elbows']::text[], array['Leaning back off the pad','Letting the stack slam between reps']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_incline_pushdown')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_incline_pushdown', 'Cable Incline Pushdown', array['Straight Arm Pulldown (Incline Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Incline Pushdown is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lats. A variation of the straight arm pulldown: lying back on an incline bench below a high pulley.', array['Lie on incline an bench facing away from a high pulley machine that has a straight bar attachment on it.']::text[], array['Grasp the straight bar attachment overhead with a pronated (overhand; palms down) shoulder width grip and extend your arms in front of you. The bar should be around 2 inches away from your upper thighs. This will be your starting position.','Keeping the upper arms stationary, lift your arms back in a semi circle until the bar is straight over your head. Breathe in during this portion of the movement.','Slowly go back to the starting position using your lats and hold the contraction once you reach the starting position. Breathe out during the execution of this movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Arms stay long with soft elbows','Move only at the shoulders']::text[], array['Bending the elbows into a pushdown','Leaning and dropping the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_incline_pushdown/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Incline_Pushdown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'straight_arm_pulldown_rope')::uuid, 'mfd', 'straight_arm_pulldown_rope', 'Rope Straight Arm Pulldown', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A lat isolation exercise. Standing at a high cable, you sweep a bar or rope down to your thighs with straight arms.', array['Attach a straight bar or rope to a high pulley.','Step back, hinge forward slightly and hold it with straight arms at about head height.']::text[], array['Keeping the arms straight, sweep the handle down in an arc to your thighs.','Squeeze the lats at the bottom.','Let the arms rise slowly back to the start.']::text[], array['Arms stay long with soft elbows','Move only at the shoulders']::text[], array['Bending the elbows into a pushdown','Leaning and dropping the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/straight_arm_pulldown_rope/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rope_Straight-Arm_Pulldown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'straight_arm_pulldown_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'straight_arm_pulldown_cable', 'Straight Arm Lat Pulldown (Cable)', array['straight arm lat pulldown','lat prayer']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A lat isolation exercise. Standing at a high cable, you sweep a bar or rope down to your thighs with straight arms.', array['Attach a straight bar or rope to a high pulley.','Step back, hinge forward slightly and hold it with straight arms at about head height.']::text[], array['Keeping the arms straight, sweep the handle down in an arc to your thighs.','Squeeze the lats at the bottom.','Let the arms rise slowly back to the start.']::text[], array['Arms stay long with soft elbows','Move only at the shoulders']::text[], array['Bending the elbows into a pushdown','Leaning and dropping the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/straight_arm_pulldown_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Straight-Arm_Pulldown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 't_bar_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 't_bar_row', 'T Bar Row', array['t-bar row']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A row with one end of a barbell anchored to the floor and a handle under the loaded end. It allows heavy loading of the mid back.', array['Straddle the bar facing the loaded end and attach a close-grip handle under the plates.','Hinge forward with a flat back and knees slightly bent.']::text[], array['Pull the handle toward your chest.','Squeeze your shoulder blades together.','Lower until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Keep the chest up and back flat','Drive the elbows back past the body']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Standing up taller each rep']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/t_bar_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/T-Bar_Row_with_Handle/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'back_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'back_extension', 'Back Extension (Hyperextension)', array['hyperextension','45 degree back extension']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Bending forward over a hip pad and lifting your torso back up. Trains the lower back, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Set the pad so the top sits just below your hip bones.','Lock your heels under the foot pads.','Cross your arms over your chest or hold a weight.']::text[], array['Lower your torso by hinging at the hips until you feel a stretch in the hamstrings.','Raise your torso back until your body forms a straight line.']::text[], array['Stop at a straight line; do not over-arch','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Hyperextending the lower back at the top','Swinging up with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/back_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hyperextensions_Back_Extensions/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'back_extension_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'back_extension_machine', 'Back Extension (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending forward over a hip pad and lifting your torso back up. Trains the lower back, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Sit in the machine with the back pad across your upper back and feet on the platform.']::text[], array['Push back against the pad by extending your spine and hips.','Return slowly to the start.']::text[], array['Stop at a straight line; do not over-arch','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Hyperextending the lower back at the top','Swinging up with momentum']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'back_extension_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'back_extension_weighted', 'Back Extension (Weighted Hyperextension)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'Bending forward over a hip pad and lifting your torso back up. Trains the lower back, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Set the pad so the top sits just below your hip bones.','Lock your heels under the foot pads.','Cross your arms over your chest or hold a weight.']::text[], array['Lower your torso by hinging at the hips until you feel a stretch in the hamstrings.','Raise your torso back until your body forms a straight line.']::text[], array['Stop at a straight line; do not over-arch','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Hyperextending the lower back at the top','Swinging up with momentum']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hyperextensions_with_no_hyperextension_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hyperextensions_with_no_hyperextension_bench', 'Hyperextensions With No Hyperextension Bench', array['Back Extension (Partner or Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Hyperextensions With No Hyperextension Bench is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the back extension: a partner holds the legs on a flat bench.', array['With someone holding down your legs, slide yourself down to the edge a flat bench until your hips hang off the end of the bench. Tip: Your entire upper body should be hanging down towards the floor. Also, you will be in the same position as if you were on a hyperextension bench but the range of motion will be shorter due to the height of the flat bench vs. that of the hyperextension bench.']::text[], array['With your body straight, cross your arms in front of you (my preference) or behind your head. This will be your starting position. Tip: You can also hold a weight plate for extra resistance in front of you under your crossed arms.','Start bending forward slowly at the waist as far as you can while keeping your back flat. Inhale as you perform this movement. Keep moving forward until you almost touch the floor or you feel a nice stretch on the hamstrings (whichever comes first). Tip: Never round the back as you perform this exercise.','Slowly raise your torso back to the initial position as you exhale. Tip: Avoid the temptation to arch your back past a straight line. Also, do not swing the torso at any time in order to protect the back from injury.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Stop at a straight line; do not over-arch','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Hyperextending the lower back at the top','Swinging up with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hyperextensions_with_no_hyperextension_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hyperextensions_With_No_Hyperextension_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'weighted_ball_hyperextension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'weighted_ball_hyperextension', 'Weighted Ball Hyperextension', array['Back Extension (Stability Ball)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Weighted Ball Hyperextension is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the glutes, hamstrings and upper back. A variation of the back extension: lying face down over a ball, holding a weight.', array['To begin, lie down on an exercise ball with your torso pressing against the ball and parallel to the floor. The ball of your feet should be pressed against the floor to help keep you balanced. Place a weighted plate under your chin or behind your neck. This is the starting position.']::text[], array['Slowly raise your torso up by bending at the waist and lower back. Remember to exhale during this movement.','Hold the contraction on your lower back for a second and lower your torso back down to the starting position while inhaling.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions prescribed in your program.']::text[], array['Stop at a straight line; do not over-arch','Squeeze the glutes at the top']::text[], array['Hyperextending the lower back at the top','Swinging up with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/weighted_ball_hyperextension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Weighted_Ball_Hyperextension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cat_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cat_stretch', 'Cat Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Cat Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the upper back and traps.', array['Position yourself on the floor on your hands and knees.']::text[], array['Pull your belly in and round your spine, lower back, shoulders, and neck, letting your head drop.','Hold for 15 seconds.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cat_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cat_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'childs_pose')::uuid, 'mfd', 'childs_pose', 'Child''s Pose', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Child''s Pose is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the glutes and upper back.', array['Get on your hands and knees, walk your hands in front of you.']::text[], array['Lower your buttocks down to sit on your heels. Let your arms drag along the floor as you sit back to stretch your entire spine.','Once you settle onto your heels, bring your hands next to your feet and relax. "breathe" into your back. Rest your forehead on the floor. Avoid this position if you have knee problems.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/childs_pose/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Childs_Pose/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dancers_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dancers_stretch', 'Dancer''s Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Dancer''s Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the abductors and glutes.', array['Sit up on the floor.']::text[], array['Cross your right leg over your left, keeping the knee bent. Your left leg is straight and down on the floor.','Place your left arm on your right leg and your right hand on the floor.','Rotate your upper body to the right, and hold for 10-20 seconds. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dancers_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dancers_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hug_a_ball')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hug_a_ball', 'Hug A Ball', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Hug A Ball is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the calves and glutes.', array['Seat yourself on the floor.']::text[], array['Straddle an exercise ball between both legs and lower your hips down toward the floor.','Hug your arms around the ball to support your body. Adjust your legs so that your feet are flat on the floor and your knees line up over your ankles. Keep a good grip on the ball so it doesn''t roll away from you and send you back onto your buttocks.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hug_a_ball/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hug_A_Ball/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hug_knees_to_chest')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hug_knees_to_chest', 'Hug Knees To Chest', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Hug Knees To Chest is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the glutes.', array['Lie down on your back and pull both knees up to your chest.']::text[], array['Hold your arms under the knees, not over (that would put to much pressure on your knee joints).','Slowly pull the knees toward your shoulders. This also stretches your buttocks muscles.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hug_knees_to_chest/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hug_Knees_To_Chest/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pelvic_tilt_into_bridge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pelvic_tilt_into_bridge', 'Pelvic Tilt Into Bridge', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Pelvic Tilt Into Bridge is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back.', array['Lie down with your feet on the floor, heels directly under your knees.']::text[], array['Lift only your tailbone to the ceiling to stretch your lower back. (Don''t lift the entire spine yet.) Pull in your stomach.','To go into a bridge, lift the entire spine except the neck.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pelvic_tilt_into_bridge/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Pelvic_Tilt_Into_Bridge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pyramid')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pyramid', 'Pyramid', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Pyramid is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back.', '{}'::text[], array['Start off by rolling your torso forward onto the ball so your hips rest on top of the ball and become the highest point of your body.','Rest your hands and feet on the floor. Your arms and legs can be slightly bent or straight, depending on the size of the ball, your flexibility, and the length of your limbs. This also helps develop stabilizing strength in your torso and shoulders.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pyramid/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Pyramid/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_pelvic_tilt')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_pelvic_tilt', 'Standing Pelvic Tilt', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Standing Pelvic Tilt is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the glutes.', array['Start off with your feet hip-distance apart.']::text[], array['Bend your knees slightly to keep them soft and springy.','You may want to move your pelvis forward and backward and back few times before holding the tailbone forward in this stretch.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_pelvic_tilt/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Pelvic_Tilt/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bird_dog')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bird_dog', 'Bird Dog', '{}'::text[], 'core', 'reps', 'On hands and knees, extending the opposite arm and leg while keeping the back still.', array['Start on hands and knees, hands under shoulders, knees under hips, back flat.']::text[], array['Extend one arm forward and the opposite leg back until both are level with your body.','Pause, return, and switch sides.']::text[], array['Hips stay level','Reach long, not high']::text[], array['Arching the lower back','Rotating the hips']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'axle_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'axle_deadlift', 'Axle Deadlift', array['Deadlift (Axle)']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Axle Deadlift is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, upper back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the deadlift: a thick, non-rotating bar that is much harder to grip.', array['Approach the bar so that it is centered over your feet. You feet should be about hip width apart. Bend at the hip to grip the bar at shoulder width, allowing your shoulder blades to protract. Typically, you would use an over/under grip.']::text[], array['With your feet and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hips and flex the knees until your shins contact the bar. Look forward with your head, keep your chest up and your back arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the weight upward.','After the bar passes the knees, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your shoulder blades together as you drive your hips forward into the bar.','Lower the bar by bending at the hips and guiding it to the floor.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/axle_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Axle_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deadlift_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deadlift_with_bands', 'Deadlift with Bands', array['Deadlift (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Deadlift with Bands is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, upper back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the deadlift: bands over the bar add load toward lockout.', array['To deadlift with short bands, simply loop them over the bar before you start, and step into them to set up. For long bands, they will need to be anchored to a secure base, such as heavy dumbbells or a rack.']::text[], array['With your feet, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hips and bend the knees until your shins contact the bar. Look forward with your head, keep your chest up and your back arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the weight upward. After the bar passes the knees, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your shoulder blades together as you drive your hips forward into the bar.','Lower the bar by bending at the hips and guiding it to the floor.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/deadlift_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Deadlift_with_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deadlift_with_chains')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deadlift_with_chains', 'Deadlift with Chains', array['Deadlift (Chains)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Deadlift with Chains is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, upper back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the deadlift: chains add load toward lockout.', array['You can attach the chains to the sleeves of the bar, or just drape the middle over the bar so there is a greater weight increase as you lift.']::text[], array['Approach the bar so that it is centered over your feet. You feet should be about hip width apart. Bend at the hip to grip the bar at shoulder width, allowing your shoulder blades to protract. Typically, you would use an overhand grip or an over/under grip on heavier sets. With your feet, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hips and bend the knees until your shins contact the bar.','Look forward with your head, keep your chest up and your back arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the weight upward. After the bar passes the knees, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your shoulder blades together as you drive your hips forward into the bar.','Lower the bar by bending at the hips and guiding it to the floor.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/deadlift_with_chains/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Deadlift_with_Chains/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deficit_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deficit_deadlift', 'Deficit Deadlift', array['Deadlift (Deficit)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Deficit Deadlift is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, upper back, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the deadlift: standing on a plate or platform, which lengthens the pull from the floor.', array['Begin by having a platform or weight plates that you can stand on, usually 1-3 inches in height. Approach the bar so that it is centered over your feet. You feet should be about hip width apart. Bend at the hip to grip the bar at shoulder width, allowing your shoulder blades to protract. Typically, you would use an overhand grip or an over/under grip on heavier sets.']::text[], array['With your feet, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hips and bend the knees until your shins contact the bar. Look forward with your head, keep your chest up and your back arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the weight upward. After the bar passes the knees, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your shoulder blades together as you drive your hips forward into the bar.','Lower the bar by bending at the hips and guiding it to the floor.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/deficit_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Deficit_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_band_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_band_deadlift', 'Reverse Band Deadlift', array['Deadlift (Reverse Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Band Deadlift is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes, hamstrings and quadriceps. A variation of the deadlift: bands from above help off the floor, so the lockout is heaviest.', array['Set the bar up in a power rack. Attach bands to the top of the rack, using either bands pegs or the frame itself. Attach the other end of the bands to the bar.']::text[], array['Approach the bar so that it is centered over your feet. You feet should be about hip width apart. Bend at the hip to grip the bar at shoulder width, allowing your shoulder blades to protract. Typically, you would use an overhand grip or an over/under grip on heavier sets.','With your feet, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hips and bend the knees until your shins contact the bar. Look forward with your head, keep your chest up and your back arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the weight upward.','After the bar passes the knees, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your shoulder blades together as you drive your hips forward into the bar.','Lower the bar by bending at the hips and guiding it to the floor.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_band_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'crossover_reverse_lunge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'crossover_reverse_lunge', 'Crossover Reverse Lunge', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Crossover Reverse Lunge is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the abs & core, abductors, glutes, hamstrings and quadriceps.', array['Stand with your feet shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Perform a rear lunge by stepping back with one foot and flexing the hips and front knee. As you do so, rotate your torso across the front leg.','After a brief pause, return to the starting position and repeat on the other side, continuing in an alternating fashion.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/crossover_reverse_lunge/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Crossover_Reverse_Lunge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lower_back_smr')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lower_back_smr', 'Lower Back-SMR', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Lower Back-SMR is a beginner-level self-massage (foam rolling) exercise that mainly targets the lower back.', '{}'::text[], array['In a seated position, place a foam roll under your lower back. Cross your arms in front of you and protract your shoulders. This will be your starting position.','Raise your hips off of the floor and lean back, keeping your weight on your lower back. Now shift your weight slightly to one side, keeping your weight off of the spine and on the muscles to the side of it. Roll over your lower back, holding points of tension for 10-30 seconds. Repeat on the other side.']::text[], array['Roll slowly, about 2–3 cm per second','Pause 20–30 seconds on tender spots','Support your weight with hands and feet to control the pressure','30–90 seconds per area']::text[], array['Rolling fast back and forth','Rolling directly over joints or bones','Pressing so hard you tense up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lower_back_smr/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lower_Back-SMR/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_good_mornings')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_good_mornings', 'Seated Good Mornings', array['Good Morning (Seated)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated Good Mornings is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the glutes. A variation of the good morning: seated on a bench; hinge forward from the hips.', array['Set up a box in a power rack. The pins should be set at an appropriate height. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the shoulders, not on top of your traps. Squeeze your shoulder blades together and rotate your elbows forward, attempting to bend the bar across your shoulders.']::text[], array['Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back. Keep your head facing forward. With your back, shoulders, and core tight, push your knees and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips until you are seated on the box. This will be your starting position.','Keeping the bar tight, bend forward at the hips as much as possible. If you set the pins to what would be parallel, you not only have a safety if you fail, but know when to stop.','Pause just above the pins and reverse the motion until your torso it upright.']::text[], array['Flat back throughout','Hips back, not down']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_good_mornings/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Good_Mornings/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'stiff_leg_barbell_good_morning')::uuid, 'mfd', 'stiff_leg_barbell_good_morning', 'Stiff Leg Barbell Good Morning', array['Good Morning (Straight Leg)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Stiff Leg Barbell Good Morning is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the good morning: knees nearly straight, for more hamstring stretch.', array['This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.']::text[], array['Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Step away from the rack and position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your legs stationary, move your torso forward by bending at the hips while inhaling. Lower your torso until it is parallel with the floor.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by elevating your torso back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Flat back throughout','Hips back, not down']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/stiff_leg_barbell_good_morning/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Stiff_Leg_Barbell_Good_Morning/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rack_pull')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rack_pull', 'Rack Pull', array['block pull']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A partial deadlift from pins set around knee height. It overloads the top of the lift and the upper back.', array['Set the safety pins so the bar sits just below or at the knees.','Set up as for a deadlift with a flat back.']::text[], array['Drive the hips forward to stand up with the bar.','Lock out tall with shoulders back.','Lower back to the pins with control.']::text[], array['Flat back','Squeeze the glutes to lock out']::text[], array['Leaning back excessively at the top','Slamming the bar onto the pins']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rack_pull/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rack_Pulls/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rack_pull_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rack_pull_with_bands', 'Rack Pull with Bands', array['Rack Pull (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Rack Pull with Bands is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, quadriceps and traps. A variation of the rack pull: bands add load toward lockout.', array['Set up in a power rack with the bar on the pins. The pins should be set to the desired point; just below the knees, just above, or in the mid thigh position. Attach bands to the base of the rack, or secure them with dumbbells. Attach the other end to the bar. You may need to choke the bands to provide tension.']::text[], array['Position yourself against the bar in proper deadlifting position. Your feet should be under your hips, your grip shoulder width, back arched, and hips back to engage the hamstrings. Since the weight is typically heavy, you may use a mixed grip, a hook grip, or use straps to aid in holding the weight.','With your head looking forward, extend through the hips and knees, pulling the weight up and back until lockout. Be sure to pull your shoulders back as you complete the movement. Return the weight to the pins and repeat.']::text[], array['Flat back','Squeeze the glutes to lock out']::text[], array['Leaning back excessively at the top','Slamming the bar onto the pins']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rack_pull_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rack_Pull_with_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'atlas_stone_trainer')::uuid, 'mfd', 'atlas_stone_trainer', 'Atlas Stone Trainer', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Atlas Stone Trainer is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the biceps, forearms, glutes, hamstrings and quadriceps.', array['This trainer is effective for developing Atlas Stone strength for those who don''t have access to stones, and are typically made from bar ends or heavy pipe.']::text[], array['Begin by loading the desired weight onto the bar. Straddle the weight, wrapping your arms around the implement, bending at the hips.','Begin by pulling the weight up past the knees, extending through the hips. As the weight clears the knees, it can be lapped by resting it on your thighs and sitting back, hugging it tightly to your chest.','Finish the movement by extending through your hips and knees to raise the weight as high as possible. The weight can be returned to the lap or to the ground for successive repetitions.']::text[], array['Straddle the implement and wrap it tight to the body','Lap it first if needed, then drive the hips forward to load','Keep it close the whole way']::text[], array['Pulling with the arms','Letting it drift away from the body','Rounding with no brace']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/atlas_stone_trainer/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Atlas_Stone_Trainer/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'atlas_stones')::uuid, 'mfd', 'atlas_stones', 'Atlas Stones', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Atlas Stones is an advanced-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the abs & core, adductors, biceps, calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, upper back, quadriceps and traps.', array['Begin with the atlas stone between your feet. Bend at the hips to wrap your arms vertically around the Atlas Stone, attempting to get your fingers underneath the stone. Many stones will have a small flat portion on the bottom, which will make the stone easier to hold.']::text[], array['Pulling the stone into your torso, drive through the back half of your feet to pull the stone from the ground.','As the stone passes the knees, lap it by sitting backward, pulling the stone on top of your thighs.','Sit low, getting the stone high onto your chest as you change your grip to reach over the stone. Stand, driving through with your hips. Close distance to the loading platform, and lean back, extending the hips to get the stone as high as possible.']::text[], array['Straddle the implement and wrap it tight to the body','Lap it first if needed, then drive the hips forward to load','Keep it close the whole way']::text[], array['Pulling with the arms','Letting it drift away from the body','Rounding with no brace']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/atlas_stones/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Atlas_Stones/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'keg_load')::uuid, 'mfd', 'keg_load', 'Keg Load', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Keg Load is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the lower back, with help from the abs & core, biceps, calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, upper back, quadriceps and traps.', array['To load kegs, place the desired number a distance from the loading platform, typically 30-50 feet.']::text[], array['Begin by grabbing the close handle of the first keg, tilting it onto its side to grab the opposite edge of the bottom of the keg. Lift the keg up to your chest.','The higher you can place the keg, the faster you should be able to move to the platform. Shouldering is usually not allowed. Be sure to keep a firm hold on the keg. Move as quickly as possible to the platform, and load it, extending through your hips, knees, and ankles to get it as high as possible.','Return to the starting position to retrieve the next keg, and repeat until the event is completed.']::text[], array['Straddle the implement and wrap it tight to the body','Lap it first if needed, then drive the hips forward to load','Keep it close the whole way']::text[], array['Pulling with the arms','Letting it drift away from the body','Rounding with no brace']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/keg_load/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Keg_Load/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'superman')::uuid, 'mfd', 'superman', 'Superman', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Lying face down and lifting your arms and legs off the floor to strengthen the back of the body.', array['Lie face down with arms extended overhead and legs straight.']::text[], array['Lift your arms, chest and legs a few centimetres off the floor at the same time.','Hold for 1–2 seconds.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Look at the floor to keep the neck neutral','Lift long, not high']::text[], array['Cranking the head up','Jerking the limbs up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/superman/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Superman/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'neck_smr')::uuid, 'mfd', 'neck_smr', 'Neck-SMR', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Neck-SMR is an intermediate-level self-massage (foam rolling) exercise that mainly targets the neck.', '{}'::text[], array['Using a muscle roller or a rolling pin, place the roller behind your head and against your neck. Make sure that you do not place the roller directly against the spine, but turned slightly so that the roller is pressed against the muscles to either side of the spine. This will be your starting position.','Starting at the top of your neck, slowly roll down the muscles of your neck, pausing at points of tension for 10-30 seconds.']::text[], array['Roll slowly, about 2–3 cm per second','Pause 20–30 seconds on tender spots','Support your weight with hands and feet to control the pressure','30–90 seconds per area']::text[], array['Rolling fast back and forth','Rolling directly over joints or bones','Pressing so hard you tense up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/neck_smr/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Neck-SMR/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_face_up_plate_neck_resistance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_face_up_plate_neck_resistance', 'Lying Face Up Plate Neck Resistance', array['Lying Neck Curls (Plate)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying Face Up Plate Neck Resistance is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the neck. A variation of the lying neck curls: lying face up on a bench, a plate on the forehead.', array['Lie face up with your whole body straight on a flat bench while holding a weight plate on top of your forehead. Tip: You will need to position yourself so that your shoulders are slightly above the end of a flat bench in order for the traps, neck and head to be off the bench. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['While keeping the plate secure on your forehead slowly lower your head back in a semi-circular motion as you breathe in.','Raise your head back up to the starting position in a semi-circular motion as you breathe out. Hold the contraction for a second.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Slow and controlled','Small range is fine']::text[], array['Jerking the head']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_face_up_plate_neck_resistance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Face_Up_Plate_Neck_Resistance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'neck_curl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'neck_curl', 'Lying Neck Curls', array['neck flexion']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Lying on your back with your head off the end of a bench, lifting the chin toward the chest.', array['Lie face up on a bench with your head and neck past the edge.']::text[], array['Let your head lower gently backward.','Curl your chin toward your chest.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Slow and controlled','Small range is fine']::text[], array['Jerking the head']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'neck_curl_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'neck_curl_weighted', 'Lying Neck Curls (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying on your back with your head off the end of a bench, lifting the chin toward the chest.', array['Lie face up on a bench with your head and neck past the edge.']::text[], array['Let your head lower gently backward.','Curl your chin toward your chest.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Slow and controlled','Small range is fine']::text[], array['Jerking the head']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_face_down_plate_neck_resistance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_face_down_plate_neck_resistance', 'Lying Face Down Plate Neck Resistance', array['Lying Neck Extension (Plate)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying Face Down Plate Neck Resistance is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the neck. A variation of the lying neck extension: lying face down on a bench, a plate on the back of the head.', array['Lie face down with your whole body straight on a flat bench while holding a weight plate behind your head. Tip: You will need to position yourself so that your shoulders are slightly above the end of a flat bench in order for the upper chest, neck and face to be off the bench. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['While keeping the plate secure on the back of your head slowly lower your head (as in saying "yes") as you breathe in.','Raise your head back up to the starting position in a semi-circular motion as you breathe out. Hold the contraction for a second.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Slow and controlled']::text[], array['Cranking the head far back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_face_down_plate_neck_resistance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Face_Down_Plate_Neck_Resistance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'neck_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'neck_extension', 'Lying Neck Extension', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Lying face down with your head off the end of a bench, lifting your head up and back.', array['Lie face down on a bench with your head and neck past the edge.']::text[], array['Let your head lower toward the floor.','Lift it up until it is level with your body or slightly higher.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Slow and controlled']::text[], array['Cranking the head far back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'neck_extension_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'neck_extension_weighted', 'Lying Neck Extension (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying face down with your head off the end of a bench, lifting your head up and back.', array['Lie face down on a bench with your head and neck past the edge.']::text[], array['Let your head lower toward the floor.','Lift it up until it is level with your body or slightly higher.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Slow and controlled']::text[], array['Cranking the head far back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_head_harness_neck_resistance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_head_harness_neck_resistance', 'Seated Head Harness Neck Resistance', array['Lying Neck Extension (Head Harness)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Seated Head Harness Neck Resistance is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the neck. A variation of the lying neck extension: seated, bent forward, a weight hanging from a head harness.', array['Place a neck strap on the floor at the end of a flat bench. Once you have selected the weights, sit at the end of the flat bench with your feet wider than shoulder width apart from each other. Your toes should be pointed out.']::text[], array['Slowly move your torso forward until it is almost parallel with the floor. Using both hands, securely position the neck strap around your head. Tip: Make sure the weights are still lying on the floor to prevent any strain on the neck. Now grab the weight with both hands while elevating your torso back until it is almost perpendicular to the floor. Note: Your head and torso needs to be slightly tilted forward to perform this exercise.','Now place both hands on top of your knees. This is the starting position.','Slowly lower your neck down until your chin touches the upper part of your chest while breathing in.','While exhaling, bring your neck back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Slow and controlled']::text[], array['Cranking the head far back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_head_harness_neck_resistance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Head_Harness_Neck_Resistance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'isometric_neck_exercise_front_and_back')::uuid, 'mfd', 'isometric_neck_exercise_front_and_back', 'Isometric Neck Exercise - Front And Back', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Isometric Neck Exercise - Front And Back is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the neck.', array['With your head and neck in a neutral position (normal position with head erect facing forward), place both of your hands on the front side of your head.']::text[], array['Now gently push forward as you contract the neck muscles but resisting any movement of your head. Start with slow tension and increase slowly. Keep breathing normally as you execute this contraction.','Hold for the recommended number of seconds.','Now release the tension slowly.','Rest for the recommended amount of time and repeat with your hands placed on the back side of your head.']::text[], array['Press the hand against the head while the head does not move','Build up to a moderate effort over 2 seconds','Hold 5–10 seconds']::text[], array['Jerking into the hand','Using maximal force']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/isometric_neck_exercise_front_and_back/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Isometric_Neck_Exercise_-_Front_And_Back/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'isometric_neck_exercise_sides')::uuid, 'mfd', 'isometric_neck_exercise_sides', 'Isometric Neck Exercise - Sides', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Isometric Neck Exercise - Sides is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the neck.', array['With your head and neck in a neutral position (normal position with head erect facing forward), place your left hand on the left side of your head.']::text[], array['Now gently push towards the left as you contract the left neck muscles but resisting any movement of your head. Start with slow tension and increase slowly. Keep breathing normally as you execute this contraction.','Hold for the recommended number of seconds.','Now release the tension slowly.','Rest for the recommended amount of time and repeat with your right hand placed on the right side of your head.']::text[], array['Press the hand against the head while the head does not move','Build up to a moderate effort over 2 seconds','Hold 5–10 seconds']::text[], array['Jerking into the hand','Using maximal force']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/isometric_neck_exercise_sides/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Isometric_Neck_Exercise_-_Sides/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chin_to_chest_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chin_to_chest_stretch', 'Chin To Chest Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Chin To Chest Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the neck, with help from the traps.', '{}'::text[], array['Get into a seated position on the floor.','Place both hands at the rear of your head, fingers interlocked, thumbs pointing down and elbows pointing straight ahead. Slowly pull your head down to your chest. Hold for 20-30 seconds.']::text[], array['Move the head slowly and gently','Keep the shoulders down and relaxed','Hold 15–30 seconds']::text[], array['Pulling hard on the head','Rolling the neck quickly','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chin_to_chest_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chin_To_Chest_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_neck_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_neck_stretch', 'Side Neck Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Side Neck Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the neck.', '{}'::text[], array['Start with your shoulders relaxed, gently tilt your head towards your shoulder.','Assist stretch with a gentle pull on the side of the head.']::text[], array['Move the head slowly and gently','Keep the shoulders down and relaxed','Hold 15–30 seconds']::text[], array['Pulling hard on the head','Rolling the neck quickly','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_neck_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_Neck_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'belt_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'belt_squat', 'Belt Squat (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A squat with the load hanging from a belt around your hips, so nothing loads the spine.', array['Attach the belt around your hips and stand on the platform.','Hold the handles lightly for balance.']::text[], array['Squat down as deep as you can with good form.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Sit straight down','Knees out']::text[], array['Pulling on the handles to help']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'weighted_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'weighted_squat', 'Weighted Squat', array['Belt Squat (Hip Belt)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Weighted Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the belt squat: a dipping belt holds the weight at the hips.', array['Start by positioning two flat benches shoulder width apart from each other. Stand on top of them and wrap the weighted belt around your waist with the amount of weight you feel comfortable with. Make sure your toes are facing out.']::text[], array['Once you are standing straight up with the weight hanging in between your legs, position your arms so that they are fully extended to the side of your body. This is the starting position.','Begin by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knees should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that are perpendicular to the front. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to move the body back up by pushing the floor of the flat bench with the ball of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position. Exhale as you perform this portion of the exercise.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Sit straight down','Knees out']::text[], array['Pulling on the handles to help']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/weighted_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Weighted_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternate_leg_diagonal_bound')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternate_leg_diagonal_bound', 'Alternate Leg Diagonal Bound', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Alternate Leg Diagonal Bound is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Assume a comfortable stance with one foot slightly in front of the other.']::text[], array['Begin by pushing off with the front leg, driving the opposite knee forward and as high as possible before landing. Attempt to cover as much distance to each side with each bound.','It may help to use a line on the ground to guage distance from side to side.','Repeat the sequence with the other leg.']::text[], array['Load the hips and swing the arms back before each jump','Drive through the whole foot and extend the hips fully','Stick the landing with bent knees before the next rep']::text[], array['Landing with straight knees','Knees caving in on landing','Not using the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternate_leg_diagonal_bound/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternate_Leg_Diagonal_Bound/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_standing_long_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_standing_long_jump', 'Side Standing Long Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Side Standing Long Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Begin standing with your feet hip width apart in an athletic stance. Your head and chest should be up, knees and hips slightly bent. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Leaning to your right, extend through your hips, knees, and ankles to jump into the air. Block with the arms to lead the movement, jumping as far to your right as you can.','Land facing the same direction with your feet hip width apart, absorbing the impact through your lower body.']::text[], array['Load the hips and swing the arms back before each jump','Drive through the whole foot and extend the hips fully','Stick the landing with bent knees before the next rep']::text[], array['Landing with straight knees','Knees caving in on landing','Not using the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_standing_long_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_Standing_Long_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_push_off')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_push_off', 'Single Leg Push-off', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Single Leg Push-off is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves and hamstrings.', array['Stand on the ground with one foot resting on the box, heel close to the edge.']::text[], array['Push off with your foot on top of the box, trying to gain as much height as possible by extending through the hip and knee.','Land with the same foot on top of the box, returning your other foot back to the start position.']::text[], array['Load the hips and swing the arms back before each jump','Drive through the whole foot and extend the hips fully','Stick the landing with bent knees before the next rep']::text[], array['Landing with straight knees','Knees caving in on landing','Not using the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_leg_push_off/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single_Leg_Push-off/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_stride_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_stride_jump', 'Single-Leg Stride Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Single-Leg Stride Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves and hamstrings.', array['Stand to the side of a box with your inside foot on top of it, close to the edge.']::text[], array['Begin by swinging the arms upward as you push through the top leg, jumping upward as high as possible. Attempt to drive the opposite knee upward.','Land in the same position that you started, using your inside leg to decelerate the impact.']::text[], array['Load the hips and swing the arms back before each jump','Drive through the whole foot and extend the hips fully','Stick the landing with bent knees before the next rep']::text[], array['Landing with straight knees','Knees caving in on landing','Not using the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_leg_stride_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Stride_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_long_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_long_jump', 'Standing Long Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Standing Long Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['This drill is best done in sand or other soft landing surface. Ensure that you are able to measure distance. Stand in a partial squat stance with feet shoulder width apart.']::text[], array['Utilizing a big arm swing and a countermovement of the legs, jump forward as far as you can.','Attempt to land with your feet out in front you, reaching as far as possible with your legs.','Measure the distance from your landing point to the starting point and track results.']::text[], array['Load the hips and swing the arms back before each jump','Drive through the whole foot and extend the hips fully','Stick the landing with bent knees before the next rep']::text[], array['Landing with straight knees','Knees caving in on landing','Not using the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_long_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Long_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'stride_jump_crossover')::uuid, 'mfd', 'stride_jump_crossover', 'Stride Jump Crossover', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Stride Jump Crossover is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves and hamstrings.', array['Stand to the side of a box with your inside foot on top of it, close to the edge.']::text[], array['Begin by swinging the arms upward as you push through the top leg, jumping upward as high as possible. Attempt to drive the opposite knee upward.','Land in the opposite position that you started, on the opposite side of the box. The foot that was initially on the box will now be on the ground, with the opposite foot now on the box.','Repeat the movement, crossing back over to the other side.']::text[], array['Load the hips and swing the arms back before each jump','Drive through the whole foot and extend the hips fully','Stick the landing with bent knees before the next rep']::text[], array['Landing with straight knees','Knees caving in on landing','Not using the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/stride_jump_crossover/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Stride_Jump_Crossover/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'box_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'box_jump', 'Box Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Jumping from the floor onto a box and landing softly. Builds explosive leg power.', array['Stand about a foot-length from a sturdy box, feet hip-width.']::text[], array['Swing your arms back and dip into a quarter squat.','Jump explosively onto the box.','Land softly with both feet in a half squat.','Stand up, then step down (do not jump down).']::text[], array['Land quietly','Knees in line with the toes']::text[], array['Choosing a box so high that you land in a deep squat','Jumping back down']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/box_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Box_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_seated_box_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_seated_box_jump', 'Dumbbell Seated Box Jump', array['Box Jump (Seated, Dumbbell)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Seated Box Jump is an intermediate-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the box jump: jump from a seated start, holding light dumbbells.', array['Position a box a couple feet to the side of a bench. Hold a dumbbell to your chest with both hands and seat yourself on the bench facing the box. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Plant your feet firmly on the ground as you lean forward, extending through the hips and knees to jump up and forward.','Land on the box with both feet, absorbing the impact by allowing the hips and knees to bend.','Step down and return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Land quietly','Knees in line with the toes']::text[], array['Choosing a box so high that you land in a deep squat','Jumping back down']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_seated_box_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Seated_Box_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'box_jump_lateral')::uuid, 'mfd', 'box_jump_lateral', 'Lateral Box Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Jumping from the floor onto a box and landing softly. Builds explosive leg power.', array['Stand about a foot-length from a sturdy box, feet hip-width.']::text[], array['Swing your arms back and dip into a quarter squat.','Jump explosively onto the box.','Land softly with both feet in a half squat.','Stand up, then step down (do not jump down).']::text[], array['Land quietly','Knees in line with the toes']::text[], array['Choosing a box so high that you land in a deep squat','Jumping back down']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/box_jump_lateral/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lateral_Box_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bulgarian_split_squat_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bulgarian_split_squat_barbell', 'Bulgarian Split Squat (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A split squat with the back foot raised on a bench. A very effective single-leg exercise for quads and glutes.', array['Stand about a long stride in front of a bench.','Place the top of your back foot on the bench.']::text[], array['Lower until the front thigh is about parallel and the back knee is near the floor.','Drive up through the front foot.','Finish all reps, then switch legs.']::text[], array['Front foot far enough forward that the heel stays down','Lean slightly forward for more glutes, stay upright for more quads']::text[], array['Front foot too close to the bench','Bouncing off the back leg']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bulgarian_split_squat_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bulgarian_split_squat_dumbbell', 'Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)', array['rear foot elevated split squat','bss']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A split squat with the back foot raised on a bench. A very effective single-leg exercise for quads and glutes.', array['Stand about a long stride in front of a bench.','Place the top of your back foot on the bench.']::text[], array['Lower until the front thigh is about parallel and the back knee is near the floor.','Drive up through the front foot.','Finish all reps, then switch legs.']::text[], array['Front foot far enough forward that the heel stays down','Lean slightly forward for more glutes, stay upright for more quads']::text[], array['Front foot too close to the bench','Bouncing off the back leg']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_leg_barbell_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_leg_barbell_squat', 'One Leg Barbell Squat', array['Bulgarian Split Squat (Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One Leg Barbell Squat is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the bulgarian split squat: rear foot on a bench, bar on the back.', array['Start by standing about 2 to 3 feet in front of a flat bench with your back facing the bench. Have a barbell in front of you on the floor. Tip: Your feet should be shoulder width apart from each other.']::text[], array['Bend the knees and use a pronated grip with your hands being wider than shoulder width apart from each other to lift the barbell up until you can rest it on your chest.','Then lift the barbell over your head and rest it on the base of your neck. Move one foot back so that your toe is resting on the flat bench. Your other foot should be stationary in front of you. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. Tip: Make sure your back is straight and chest is out while performing this exercise.','As you inhale, slowly lower your leg until your thigh is parallel to the floor. At this point, your knee should be over your toes. Your chest should be directly above the middle of your thigh.','Leading with the chest and hips and contracting the quadriceps, elevate your leg back to the starting position as you exhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','Switch legs and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Front foot far enough forward that the heel stays down','Lean slightly forward for more glutes, stay upright for more quads']::text[], array['Front foot too close to the bench','Bouncing off the back leg']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_leg_barbell_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Leg_Barbell_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'suspended_split_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'suspended_split_squat', 'Suspended Split Squat', array['Bulgarian Split Squat (Suspension)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Suspended Split Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the bulgarian split squat: rear foot in a suspension strap.', array['Suspend your straps so the handles are 18-30 inches from the floor.']::text[], array['Facing away from the setup, place your rear foot into the handle behind you. Keep your head looking forward and your chest up, with your knee slightly bent. This will be your starting position.','Descend by flexing the knee and hips, lowering yourself to the ground. Keep your weight on the heel of your foot and maintain your posture throughout the exercise.','At the bottom of the movement, reverse the motion, extending through the hip and knee to return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Front foot far enough forward that the heel stays down','Lean slightly forward for more glutes, stay upright for more quads']::text[], array['Front foot too close to the anchor','Bouncing off the back leg']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/suspended_split_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Suspended_Split_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'burpee')::uuid, 'mfd', 'burpee', 'Burpee', '{}'::text[], 'cardio', 'reps', 'A squat, a jump back to a plank, a push up, a jump forward and a jump up, all in one flowing movement.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width apart.']::text[], array['Squat down and place your hands on the floor.','Jump your feet back to a plank and lower your chest to the floor.','Push up, jump your feet back toward your hands.','Jump up and clap overhead.']::text[], array['Keep a steady rhythm','Land softly']::text[], array['Hips sagging in the plank','Rushing so form breaks down']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'burpee_broad_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'burpee_broad_jump', 'Burpee Broad Jumps', '{}'::text[], 'cardio', 'distance_time', 'A squat, a jump back to a plank, a push up, a jump forward and a jump up, all in one flowing movement.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width apart.']::text[], array['Squat down and place your hands on the floor.','Jump your feet back to a plank and lower your chest to the floor.','Push up, jump your feet back toward your hands.','Jump up and clap overhead.']::text[], array['Keep a steady rhythm','Land softly']::text[], array['Hips sagging in the plank','Rushing so form breaks down']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'burpee_over_the_bar')::uuid, 'mfd', 'burpee_over_the_bar', 'Burpee Over the Bar', '{}'::text[], 'cardio', 'reps', 'A squat, a jump back to a plank, a push up, a jump forward and a jump up, all in one flowing movement.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width apart.']::text[], array['Squat down and place your hands on the floor.','Jump your feet back to a plank and lower your chest to the floor.','Push up, jump your feet back toward your hands.','Jump up and clap overhead.']::text[], array['Keep a steady rhythm','Land softly']::text[], array['Hips sagging in the plank','Rushing so form breaks down']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_from_blocks')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_from_blocks', 'Clean from Blocks', array['Clean (From Blocks)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Clean from Blocks is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and traps. A variation of the clean: bar starts on blocks at knee height.', array['With a barbell on boxes or stands of the desired height, take an overhand or hook grip just outside the legs. Lower your hips with the weight focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, chest up, with your shoulders just in front of the bar. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your knees. Your back angle should stay the same, and your arms should remain straight with the elbows pointed out.','As full extension is achieved, transition into the receiving position by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the elbows up and out. Aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your elbows under the bar as you do so. Receive the bar in a front squat position, the depth of which is dependent upon the height of the bar at the end of the third pull. The bar should be racked onto the protracted shoulders, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom squat position, which will help in the recovery.','Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torso upright and elbows up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position. Return the weight to the boxes for the next rep.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Patient off the floor, explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_from_blocks/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clean_from_Blocks/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hang_clean_below_the_knees')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hang_clean_below_the_knees', 'Hang Clean - Below the Knees', array['Clean (Hang, Below Knees)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Hang Clean - Below the Knees is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back and traps. A variation of the clean: starts from the hang just below the knees.', array['Begin with a shoulder width, double overhand or hook grip, with the bar hanging just below the knees. Your back should be straight and inclined slightly forward.']::text[], array['Begin by aggressively extending through the hips, knees and ankles, driving the weight upward. As you do so, shrug your shoulders towards your ears. As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the elbows up and out.','At peak extension, aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your elbows under the bar as you do so. Receive the bar in a front squat position, the depth of which is dependent upon the height of the bar at the end of the third pull. The bar should be racked onto the protracted shoulders, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom squat position, which will help in the recovery.','Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torso upright and elbows up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Patient off the floor, explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hang_clean_below_the_knees/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hang_Clean_-_Below_the_Knees/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'split_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'split_clean', 'Split Clean', array['Clean (Split)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Split Clean is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back and traps. A variation of the clean: caught in a split stance instead of a squat.', array['With a barbell on the floor close to the shins, take an overhand grip just outside the legs. Lower your hips with the weight focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, chest up, with your shoulders just in front of the bar. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your knees. Your back angle should stay the same, and your arms should remain straight. Move the weight with control as you continue to above the knees.','Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the clean. As the bar approaches the mid-thigh position, begin extending through the hips. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hips, knees, and ankles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the weight; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended.','As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the elbows up and out. At peak extension, aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your elbows under the bar as you do so.','Receive the bar with the feet split, aggressively moving one foot forward and one foot back. The bar should be racked onto the protracted shoulders, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom position, which will help in the recovery.','Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torso upright and elbows up. Bring the feet together as you stand up.']::text[], array['Bar stays close to the body','Patient off the floor, explosive at the hips','Fast elbows in the catch']::text[], array['Pulling early with the arms','Bar swinging away from the body','Catching with low elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/split_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Split_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'conans_wheel')::uuid, 'mfd', 'conans_wheel', 'Conan''s Wheel', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Conan''s Wheel is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, biceps, calves, forearms, lower back and traps.', '{}'::text[], array['With the weight loaded, take a zurcher hold on the end of the implement. Place the bar in the crook of the elbow and hold onto your wrist. Try to keep the weight off of the forearms.','Begin by lifting the weight from the ground. Keep a tight, upright posture as you being to walk, taking short, fast steps. Look up and away as you turn in a circle. Do not hold your breath during the event. Continue walking until you complete one or more complete turns.']::text[], array['Bar held in the crook of the elbows','Brace and walk in a circle','Short steps']::text[], array['Rounding forward','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/conans_wheel/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Conans_Wheel/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_deadlifts')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_deadlifts', 'Cable Deadlifts', array['Deadlift (Cable)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Deadlifts is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the deadlift: low pulley with a bar, facing the stack.', array['Move the cables to the bottom of the towers and select an appropriate weight. Stand directly in between the uprights.']::text[], array['To begin, squat down be flexing your hips and knees until you can reach the handles.','After grasping them, begin your ascent. Driving through your heels extend your hips and knees keeping your hands hanging at your side. Keep your head and chest up throughout the movement.','After reaching a full standing position, Return to the starting position and repeat.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_deadlifts/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Deadlifts/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'car_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'car_deadlift', 'Car Deadlift', array['Deadlift (Car Deadlift (Strongman))']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Car Deadlift is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back and traps. A variation of the deadlift: strongman frame or handles beside the body.', array['This event apparatus typically has neutral grip handles, however some have a straight bar that you can approach like a normal deadlift. The apparatus can be loaded with a vehicle or other heavy objects such as tractor tires or kegs.']::text[], array['Center yourself between the handles if you are a strong squatter, or back a couple inches if you are a strong deadlifter. You feet should be about hip width apart. Bend at the hip to grip the handles. With your feet and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hips and flex the knees.','Look forward with your head, keep your chest up and your back arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the weight upward. As the weight comes up, pull your shoulder blades together as you drive your hips forward.','Lower the weight by bending at the hips and guiding it to the floor.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/car_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Car_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'deadlift_trap_bar')::uuid, 'mfd', 'deadlift_trap_bar', 'Deadlift (Trap Bar)', array['hex bar deadlift']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting a weight from the floor to standing by driving with the legs and hips. Trains nearly the whole back of the body.', array['Stand in the centre of the trap bar.','Hinge and bend the knees to grip the handles at your sides.','Flat back, chest up.']::text[], array['Brace, then push the floor away with your legs.','Keep the weight close to your legs as it rises.','Once the weight passes your knees, drive the hips forward to stand tall.','Lower by pushing the hips back first, then bending the knees once the weight passes them.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/deadlift_trap_bar/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Trap_Bar_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leverage_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leverage_deadlift', 'Leverage Deadlift', array['Deadlift (Machine)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Leverage Deadlift is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the deadlift: a plate-loaded lever deadlift machine.', '{}'::text[], array['Load the pins to an appropriate weight. Position yourself directly between the handles. Grasp the bottom handles with a comfortable grip, and then lower your hips as you take a breath. Look forward with your head and keep your chest up. This will be your starting position.','Return the weight to the starting position.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leverage_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_side_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_side_deadlift', 'One-Arm Side Deadlift', array['Deadlift (Single Arm (Suitcase))']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Side Deadlift is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, calves, glutes, hamstrings, lower back and traps. A variation of the deadlift: one hand in the middle of the bar beside you; the core stops you leaning.', array['Stand to the side of a barbell next to its center. Bend your knees and lower your body until you are able to reach the barbell.']::text[], array['Grasp the bar as if you were grabbing a briefcase (palms facing you since the bar is sideways). You may need a wrist wrap if you are using a significant amount of weight. This is your starting position.','Use your legs to help lift the barbell up while exhaling. Your arms should extend fully as bring the barbell up until you are in a standing position.','Slowly bring the barbell back down while inhaling. Tip: Make sure to bend your knees while lowering the weight to avoid any injury from occurring.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_side_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Side_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rickshaw_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rickshaw_deadlift', 'Rickshaw Deadlift', array['Deadlift (Rickshaw (Strongman))']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Rickshaw Deadlift is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back and traps. A variation of the deadlift: handles of a rickshaw frame beside the body.', array['Load the frame with the desired weight. Center yourself between the handles. You feet should be about hip width apart. Bend at the hips to grip the handles, allowing your shoulder blades to protract.']::text[], array['With your feet and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hips and flex the knees. Look forward with your head, keep your chest up and your back arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the weight upward. As the weight comes up, pull your shoulder blades together as you drive your hips forward.','Lower the weight by bending at the hips and guiding it to the ground.']::text[], array['Weight stays close to the legs','Push the floor away','Hips and shoulders rise together','Stand tall at the top; do not lean back']::text[], array['Rounding the lower back','Weight drifting away from the body','Hips shooting up first so it becomes a stiff-leg pull','Jerking the weight off the floor']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rickshaw_deadlift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rickshaw_Deadlift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'depth_jump_leap')::uuid, 'mfd', 'depth_jump_leap', 'Depth Jump Leap', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Depth Jump Leap is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['For this drill you will need two boxes or benches, one 12 to 16 inches high and the other 22 to 26 inches high.']::text[], array['Stand on one of the two boxes with arms at the sides; feet should be together and slightly off the edge as in the depth jump. Place the other box approximately two or three feet in front of and facing the performer.','Begin by dropping off the initial box, landing and simultaneously taking off with both feet.','Rebound by driving upward and outward as intensely as possible, using the arms and full extension of the body to jump onto the higher box. Again, allow the legs to absorb the impact.']::text[], array['Step off the box; do not jump off it','Land on both feet and leave the ground again as fast as possible','Knees track over the toes on landing','Start with a low box (30 cm)']::text[], array['A box that is too high, causing a slow, deep landing','Knees caving in on landing','Pausing on the ground']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/depth_jump_leap/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Depth_Jump_Leap/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'linear_depth_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'linear_depth_jump', 'Linear Depth Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Linear Depth Jump is an intermediate-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['You will need two boxes or benches spaced a few feet away from each other. Begin by standing on one box facing towards the other platform.']::text[], array['To initiate the movement, gently drop down to the ground between your platforms, allowing the knees and hips to flex.','Reverse the motion by exploding, extending through the hips, knees, and ankles to jump onto the other platform.','Land softly, asborbing the impact through the legs.']::text[], array['Step off the box; do not jump off it','Land on both feet and leave the ground again as fast as possible','Knees track over the toes on landing','Start with a low box (30 cm)']::text[], array['A box that is too high, causing a slow, deep landing','Knees caving in on landing','Pausing on the ground']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/linear_depth_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Linear_Depth_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'frog_hops')::uuid, 'mfd', 'frog_hops', 'Frog Hops', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Frog Hops is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', '{}'::text[], array['Stand with your hands behind your head, and squat down keeping your torso upright and your head up. This will be your starting position.','Jump forward several feet, avoiding jumping unnecessarily high. As your feet contact the ground, absorb the impact through your legs, and jump again. Repeat this action 5-10 times.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/frog_hops/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Frog_Hops/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'iron_crosses_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'iron_crosses_stretch', 'Iron Crosses (stretch)', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Iron Crosses (stretch) is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', array['Lie face down on the floor, with your arms extended out to your side, palms pressed to the floor. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['To begin, flex one knee and bring that leg across the back of your body, attempting to touch it to the ground near the opposite hand.','Promptly return the leg to the starting postion, and quickly repeat with the other leg. Continue alternating for 10-20 repetitions.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/iron_crosses_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Iron_Crosses_stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rear_leg_raises')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rear_leg_raises', 'Rear Leg Raises', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Rear Leg Raises is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Place yourself on your hands knees on an exercise mat. Your head should be looking forward and the bend of the knees should create a 90-degree angle between the hamstrings and the calves. This will be your starting position.','Extend one leg up and behind you. The knee and hip should both extend. Repeat for 5-10 repetitions, and then switch sides.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rear_leg_raises/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rear_Leg_Raises/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'quadriceps_smr')::uuid, 'mfd', 'quadriceps_smr', 'Quadriceps-SMR', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Quadriceps-SMR is an intermediate-level self-massage (foam rolling) exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Lay facedown on the floor with your weight supported by your hands or forearms. Place a foam roll underneath one leg on the quadriceps, and keep the foot off of the ground. Make sure to relax the leg as much as possible. This will be your starting position.','Shifting as much weight onto the leg to be stretched as is tolerable, roll over the foam from above the knee to below the hip, holding points of tension for 10-30 seconds. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Roll slowly, about 2–3 cm per second','Pause 20–30 seconds on tender spots','Support your weight with hands and feet to control the pressure','30–90 seconds per area']::text[], array['Rolling fast back and forth','Rolling directly over joints or bones','Pressing so hard you tense up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/quadriceps_smr/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Quadriceps-SMR/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'frog_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'frog_jump', 'Frog Jumps', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Jumping forward from a deep, wide squat and landing back in the same squat.', array['Stand with feet wide, toes turned out.','Squat down and touch the floor between your feet.']::text[], array['Jump forward explosively.','Land softly back into the deep squat.','Repeat.']::text[], array['Land soft and deep']::text[], array['Landing on straight legs']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'frankenstein_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'frankenstein_squat', 'Frankenstein Squat', array['Front Squat (Frankenstein)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Frankenstein Squat is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the front squat: arms straight out in front with the bar balanced on the shoulders, to teach an upright torso.', array['This drill teaches you the proper positioning of both the bar and your body during the clean and front squat.']::text[], array['Place the barbell on the front of the shoulders, releasing your grip and extending your arms out in front of you. The shoulders should be pushed forward to create a shelf, and the bar should be in contact with the throat. Ensure that you only move your shoulder blades forward; don''t round the thoracic spine.','Squat by flexing the knees and hips, sitting in between your legs. Keep the torso upright, the arms up, and the shoulders forward, and the bar should stay in place. Go to the bottom of the squat, until your hamstrings contact your calves.','Return to the upright position by driving through the front of the heel and extending the knees and hips.']::text[], array['Elbows up the whole time','Torso tall','Knees forward and out']::text[], array['Elbows dropping so the bar rolls forward','Rounding the upper back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/frankenstein_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Frankenstein_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_barbell_squat_to_a_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_barbell_squat_to_a_bench', 'Front Barbell Squat To A Bench', array['Front Squat (To Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Front Barbell Squat To A Bench is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the front squat: front squat until you lightly touch a bench.', array['This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set a flat bench behind you and set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, bring your arms up under the bar while keeping the elbows high and the upper arm slightly above parallel to the floor. Rest the bar on top of the deltoids and cross your arms while grasping the bar for total control.']::text[], array['Lift the bar off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Step away from the rack and position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances described in the foot positioning section).','Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until you touch the bench with your glutes. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knees should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor mainly with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows up the whole time','Torso tall','Knees forward and out']::text[], array['Elbows dropping so the bar rolls forward','Rounding the upper back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_barbell_squat_to_a_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Barbell_Squat_To_A_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_squat', 'Front Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A squat with the bar held on the front of the shoulders. It keeps the torso more upright and works the quads and upper back harder.', array['Set the bar in a rack at upper-chest height.','Step under it so it rests on the front of your shoulders, close to your throat.','Hold it with fingertips under the bar and elbows high (or arms crossed).']::text[], array['Brace and squat straight down, keeping the elbows high.','Go as deep as you can with an upright torso.','Drive up, leading with the elbows.']::text[], array['Elbows up the whole time','Torso tall','Knees forward and out']::text[], array['Elbows dropping so the bar rolls forward','Rounding the upper back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Barbell_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_squats_with_two_kettlebells')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_squats_with_two_kettlebells', 'Front Squats With Two Kettlebells', array['Front Squat (Double Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Front Squats With Two Kettlebells is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves and glutes. A variation of the front squat: two kettlebells held in the rack position.', array['Clean two kettlebells to your shoulders. Clean the kettlebells to your shoulders by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebells towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrists as you do so.']::text[], array['Looking straight ahead at all times, squat as low as you can and pause at the bottom. As you squat down, push your knees out. You should squat between your legs, keeping an upright torso, with your head and chest up.','Rise back up by driving through your heels and repeat.']::text[], array['Elbows up the whole time','Torso tall','Knees forward and out']::text[], array['Elbows dropping so the kettlebells pull you forward','Rounding the upper back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_squats_with_two_kettlebells/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Squats_With_Two_Kettlebells/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sit_squats')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sit_squats', 'Sit Squats', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Sit Squats is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Stand with your feet shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the movement by flexing your knees and hips, sitting back with your hips.','Continue until you have squatted a portion of the way down, but are above parallel, and quickly reverse the motion until you return to the starting position. Repeat for 5-10 repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep the hips square and the lower back flat on the floor where lying','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Twisting the pelvis to fake the range','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sit_squats/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sit_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'goblet_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A squat holding one weight against your chest. The front load makes good squat form easy to learn.', array['Hold one dumbbell vertically by the top end (or a kettlebell by the horns) against your chest.','Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out.']::text[], array['Squat down between your heels, elbows travelling inside your knees.','Go as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Stand up tall.']::text[], array['Weight stays against your chest','Elbows push the knees out at the bottom']::text[], array['Letting the weight drift away from the body','Heels lifting']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'goblet_squat_kettlebell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'goblet_squat_kettlebell', 'Kettlebell Goblet Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A squat holding one weight against your chest. The front load makes good squat form easy to learn.', array['Hold a kettlebell by the horns (the sides of the handle) against your chest.','Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out.']::text[], array['Squat down between your heels, elbows travelling inside your knees.','Go as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Stand up tall.']::text[], array['Weight stays against your chest','Elbows push the knees out at the bottom']::text[], array['Letting the weight drift away from the body','Heels lifting']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/goblet_squat_kettlebell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Goblet_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hack_squat_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hack_squat_barbell', 'Hack Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A barbell lift where you stand up holding the bar behind your legs. It works the quads hard with an upright torso.', array['Stand in front of a barbell on the floor and grip it behind your legs.']::text[], array['Stand up holding the bar behind your thighs, like a deadlift behind the body.','Lower it back down by bending at the knees.']::text[], array['Back stays against the pad','Knees track over the toes']::text[], array['Hips lifting off the pad','Shallow reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hack_squat_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Hack_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hack_squat_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hack_squat_machine', 'Hack Squat (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A squat on an angled sled machine with your back against a pad. It lets you train the quads hard with little stress on the back.', array['Stand on the platform with your back and shoulders against the pads.','Feet shoulder-width, in the middle of the platform.']::text[], array['Release the safety handles.','Lower until your thighs are at least parallel to the platform.','Push back up through the whole foot.']::text[], array['Back stays against the pad','Knees track over the toes']::text[], array['Hips lifting off the pad','Shallow reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hack_squat_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hack_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_machine_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_machine_squat', 'Lying Machine Squat', array['Hack Squat (Lying Machine)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying Machine Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the hack squat: a lying squat machine, back on the pad.', array['Adjust the leg machine to a height that will allow you to get inside it with your knees bent and the thighs slightly below parallel.']::text[], array['Once you select the weight, position yourself inside the machine face up with the knees bent and thighs slightly below parallel to the platform. Make sure that the knees do not go past the toes. The angle created between the hamstrings and the calves should be one that is slightly less than 90 degrees (since your starting position requires you to start slightly below parallel). Your back and your head should be resting on the machine while your shoulders are pressed under the shoulder pads.','Place your hands by the handles and position your feet slightly pointing out at a shoulder width position. This will be your starting position.','While pressing with the balls of the feet as you breathe out, make your whole body erect as you squeeze the quads. Hold the contracted position for a second. Tip: Since you are starting below parallel, you can opt to use your hands to help you up by pressing on your thighs only on the first repetition.','Slowly squat down as you inhale but instead of going all the way down to the starting position, just stop once your thighs are parallel to the platform. The angle between your hamstrings and calves should be a 90-degree angle.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Back stays against the pad','Knees track over the toes']::text[], array['Hips lifting off the pad','Shallow reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_machine_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Machine_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'narrow_stance_hack_squats')::uuid, 'mfd', 'narrow_stance_hack_squats', 'Narrow Stance Hack Squats', array['Hack Squat (Narrow Stance)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Narrow Stance Hack Squats is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the hack squat: feet close together, more quads.', array['Place the back of your torso against the back pad of the machine and hook your shoulders under the shoulder pads provided.']::text[], array['Position your legs in the platform using a less than shoulder width narrow stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Your feet should be around 3 inches or less apart. Tip: Keep your head up at all times and also maintain the back on the pad at all times.','Place your arms on the side handles of the machine and disengage the safety bars (which on most designs is done by moving the side handles from a facing front position to a diagonal position).','Now straighten your legs without locking the knees. This will be your starting position.','Begin to slowly lower the unit by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up (back on the pad at all times). Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Begin to raise the unit as you exhale by pushing the floor with mainly with the heels of your feet as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Back stays against the pad','Knees track over the toes']::text[], array['Hips lifting off the pad','Shallow reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/narrow_stance_hack_squats/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Narrow_Stance_Hack_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'fast_skipping')::uuid, 'mfd', 'fast_skipping', 'Fast Skipping', array['High Knees (Fast Skipping)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Fast Skipping is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the high knees: quick, low skips.', array['Start in a relaxed position with one leg slightly forward. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Skip by executing a step-hop pattern of right-right-step to left-left-step, and so on, alternating back and forth.','Perform fast skips by maintaining close contact with the ground and reduce air time, moving as quickly as possible.']::text[], array['Stay on the balls of the feet','Tall posture']::text[], array['Leaning back','Knees not reaching hip height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/fast_skipping/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Fast_Skipping/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'trail_running_walking')::uuid, 'mfd', 'trail_running_walking', 'Trail Running/Walking', array['Hiking (Trail Run or Walk)']::text[], 'cardio', 'distance_time', 'Trail Running/Walking is a beginner-level cardio exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the cardio, calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the hiking: on trails.', '{}'::text[], array['Running or hiking on trails will get the blood pumping and heart beating almost immediately. Make sure you have good shoes. While you use the muscles in your calves and buttocks to pull yourself up a hill, the knees, joints and ankles absorb the bulk of the pounding coming back down. Take smaller steps as you walk downhill, keep your knees bent to reduce the impact and slow down to avoid falling.','A 150 lb person can burn over 200 calories for 30 minutes walking uphill, compared to 175 on a flat surface. If running the trail, a 150 lb person can burn well over 500 calories in 30 minutes.']::text[], array['Short steps uphill','Soft knees downhill']::text[], array['Starting too fast']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/trail_running_walking/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Trail_Running_Walking/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'hip_flexion_with_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'hip_flexion_with_band', 'Hip Flexion with Band', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Hip Flexion with Band is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps.', array['Secure one end of the band to the lower portion of a post and attach the other to one ankle.']::text[], array['Face away from the attachment point of the band.','Keeping your head and your chest up, raise your knee up to 90 degrees and pause.','Return the leg to the starting position.']::text[], array['Stand tall facing away from the anchor','Drive the knee up to hip height','Lower slowly']::text[], array['Leaning back','Swinging the leg']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/hip_flexion_with_band/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Hip_Flexion_with_Band/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_jump', 'Bench Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Bench Jump is an intermediate-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Begin with a box or bench 1-2 feet in front of you. Stand with your feet shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Perform a short squat in preparation for the jump; swing your arms behind you.','Rebound out of this position, extending through the hips, knees, and ankles to jump as high as possible. Swing your arms forward and up.','Jump over the bench, landing with the knees bent, absorbing the impact through the legs.','Turn around and face the opposite direction, then jump back over the bench.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bench_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_cone_hops_or_hurdle_hops')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_cone_hops_or_hurdle_hops', 'Front Cone Hops (or hurdle hops)', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Front Cone Hops (or hurdle hops) is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Set up a row of cones or other small barriers, placing them a few feet apart.']::text[], array['Stand in front of the first cone with your feet shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.','Begin by jumping with both feet over the first cone, swinging both arms as you jump.','Absorb the impact of landing by bending the knees, rebounding out of the first leap by jumping over the next cone.','Continue until you have jumped over all of the cones.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_cone_hops_or_hurdle_hops/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Cone_Hops_or_hurdle_hops/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'quick_leap')::uuid, 'mfd', 'quick_leap', 'Quick Leap', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Quick Leap is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves and hamstrings.', array['You will need a box for this exerise.']::text[], array['Begin facing the box standing 1-2 feet from its edge.','By utilizing your hips, hop onto the box, landing on both legs. Ensure that you land with your legs bent and your feet flat.','Immediately upon landing, fully extend through the entire body and swing your arms overhead to explode off of the box. Use your legs to absorb the impact of landing.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/quick_leap/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Quick_Leap/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_hop_sprint')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_hop_sprint', 'Side Hop-Sprint', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'distance_time', 'Side Hop-Sprint is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves and hamstrings.', array['Stand to the side of a cone or hurdle.']::text[], array['Begin this drill by hopping sideways over the obstacle, rebounding out of your landing to hop back to where you started.','Hop for a prescribed number or repetitions as quickly as possible, and finish this drill by sprinting a short distance upon landing the last hop.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_hop_sprint/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_Hop-Sprint/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_to_side_box_shuffle')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_to_side_box_shuffle', 'Side to Side Box Shuffle', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Side to Side Box Shuffle is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves and hamstrings.', array['Stand to one side of the box with your left foot resting on the middle of it.']::text[], array['To begin, jump up and over to the other side of the box, landing with your right foot on top of the box and your left foot on the floor. Swing your arms to aid your movement.','Continue shuffling back and forth across the box.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_to_side_box_shuffle/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_to_Side_Box_Shuffle/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_hop_progression')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_hop_progression', 'Single-Leg Hop Progression', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Single-Leg Hop Progression is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves and hamstrings.', array['Arrange a line of cones in front of you. Assume a relaxed standing position, balanced on one leg. Raise the knee of your opposite leg. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Hop forward, jumping and landing with the same leg over the cone.','Use a countermovement jump to hop from cone to cone.','At the end, turn around and go back on the other leg.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_leg_hop_progression/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Hop_Progression/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_lateral_hop')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_lateral_hop', 'Single-Leg Lateral Hop', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Single-Leg Lateral Hop is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves and hamstrings.', array['Stand to the side of a cone or hurdle. To get into the start position, stand on one leg with your knee slightly bent.']::text[], array['To begin, execute a counterjump to hop sideways over the cone.','Land on your jumping leg, and immediately rebound out of it by jumping back to the start position.','Continue hopping back and forth.']::text[], array['Land softly on the balls of the feet','Spend as little time on the ground as possible','Knees track over the toes','Arms drive each jump']::text[], array['Landing on the heels or stiff-legged','Knees caving in','Doing too many reps when tired']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_leg_lateral_hop/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Lateral_Hop/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'jefferson_squats')::uuid, 'mfd', 'jefferson_squats', 'Jefferson Squats', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Jefferson Squats is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings, lower back and traps.', array['Place a barbell on the floor.']::text[], array['Stand in the middle of the bar length wise.','Bend down by bending at the knees and keeping your back straight and grasp the front of the bar with your right hand. Your palm should be in (neutral grip) facing the left side.','Grasp the rear of the bar with your left hand. The palm of your hand should be in neutral grip alignment (palms facing the right side). Tip: Ensure that your grip is even on the bar. Your torso should be positioned right in the middle of the bar and the distance between your torso and your right hand (which should be at the front) should be the same as the distance between your torso and your left hand (which should be to your back).','Now stand straight up with the weight. Tip: Your feet should be shoulder width apart and your toes slightly pointed out.','Squat down by bending at the knees and keeping your back straight until your upper thighs are parallel with the floor. Tip: Keep your back as vertical as possible with the floor and your head up. Also remember to not let your knees go past your toes. Inhale during this portion of the movement.','Now drive yourself back up to the starting position by pushing with the feet . Tip: Keep the bar hanging at arm''s length and your elbows locked with a slight bend. The arms only serve as hooks. Avoid doing any lifting with them. Do the lifting with your thighs; not your arms.']::text[], array['Straddle the bar, one hand in front and one behind','Squat down with an upright torso','Alternate the leg in front each set']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Twisting the hips']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/jefferson_squats/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Jefferson_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'jump_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'jump_squat', 'Jump Squat', array['squat jump']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'A bodyweight squat finished with an explosive jump.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width apart.']::text[], array['Squat down to about parallel.','Jump as high as you can.','Land softly and go straight into the next squat.']::text[], array['Soft landings']::text[], array['Landing with straight legs','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/jump_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Freehand_Jump_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'weighted_jump_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'weighted_jump_squat', 'Weighted Jump Squat', array['Jump Squat (Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Weighted Jump Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the jump squat: light bar on the back.', array['Position a lightly loaded barbell across the back of your shoulders. You could also use a weighted vest, sandbag, or other type of resistance for this exercise.']::text[], array['The weight should be light enough that it doesn''t slow you down significantly. Your feet should be just outside of shoulder width with your head and chest up. This will be your starting position.','Using a countermovement, squat partially down and immediately reverse your direction to explode off of the ground, extending through your hips, knees, and ankles. Maintain good posture throughout the jump.','As you return to the ground, absorb the impact through your legs.']::text[], array['Soft landings']::text[], array['Landing with straight legs','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/weighted_jump_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Weighted_Jump_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'jumping_lunge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'jumping_lunge', 'Jumping Lunge', array['split jump']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Jumping from one lunge position and switching legs in the air to land in the opposite lunge.', array['Start in a lunge with one foot forward.']::text[], array['Jump up explosively.','Switch legs in the air.','Land softly in a lunge with the other foot forward.']::text[], array['Land softly and balanced']::text[], array['Front knee caving in on landing']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/jumping_lunge/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Split_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'scissors_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'scissors_jump', 'Scissors Jump', array['Jumping Lunge (Scissors)']::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Scissors Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the jumping lunge: switch legs in the air from a lunge.', array['Assume a lunge stance position with one foot forward with the knee bent, and the rear knee nearly touching the ground.']::text[], array['Ensure that the front knee is over the midline of the foot. Extending through both legs, jump as high as possible, swinging your arms to gain lift.','As you jump as high as you can, switch the position of your legs, moving your front leg to the back and the rear leg to the front.','As you land, absorb the impact through the legs by adopting the lunge position, and repeat.']::text[], array['Land softly and balanced']::text[], array['Front knee caving in on landing']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/scissors_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Scissors_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'double_leg_butt_kick')::uuid, 'mfd', 'double_leg_butt_kick', 'Double Leg Butt Kick', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Double Leg Butt Kick is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Begin standing with your knees slightly bent.']::text[], array['Quickly squat a short distance, flexing the hips and knees, and immediately extend to jump for maximum vertical height.','As you go up, tuck your heels by flexing the knees, attempting to touch the buttocks.','Finish the motion by landing with the knees only partially bent, using your legs to absorb the impact.']::text[], array['Jump straight up and land where you started','Land softly with bent knees','Keep the chest up']::text[], array['Landing stiff-legged','Hunching over in the air','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/double_leg_butt_kick/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Double_Leg_Butt_Kick/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rocket_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rocket_jump', 'Rocket Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Rocket Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves and hamstrings.', array['Begin in a relaxed stance with your feet shoulder width apart and hold your arms close to the body.']::text[], array['To initiate the move, squat down halfway and explode back up as high as possible.','Fully extend your entire body, reaching overhead as far as possible. As you land, absorb your impact through the legs.']::text[], array['Jump straight up and land where you started','Land softly with bent knees','Keep the chest up']::text[], array['Landing stiff-legged','Hunching over in the air','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rocket_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rocket_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_butt_kick')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_butt_kick', 'Single Leg Butt Kick', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Single Leg Butt Kick is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves and hamstrings.', array['Begin by standing on one leg, with the bent knee raised. This will be your start position.']::text[], array['Using a countermovement jump, take off upward by extending the hip, knee, and ankle of the grounded leg.','Immediately flex the knee and attempt to touch your butt with the heel of your jumping leg.','Return the leg to a partially bent position underneath the hips and land. Your opposite leg should stay in relatively the same position throughout the drill.']::text[], array['Jump straight up and land where you started','Land softly with bent knees','Keep the chest up']::text[], array['Landing stiff-legged','Hunching over in the air','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_leg_butt_kick/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single_Leg_Butt_Kick/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'star_jump')::uuid, 'mfd', 'star_jump', 'Star Jump', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Star Jump is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Begin in a relaxed stance with your feet shoulder width apart and hold your arms close to the body.']::text[], array['To initiate the move, squat down halfway and explode back up as high as possible. Fully extend your entire body, spreading your legs and arms away from the body.','As you land, bring your limbs back in and absorb your impact through the legs.']::text[], array['Jump straight up and land where you started','Land softly with bent knees','Keep the chest up']::text[], array['Landing stiff-legged','Hunching over in the air','Knees caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/star_jump/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Star_Jump/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'landmine_squat_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'landmine_squat_press', 'Landmine Squat and Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Holding the end of a landmine bar at your chest, squatting and then pressing it up and forward.', array['Hold the end of the landmine bar at your chest with both hands, feet shoulder-width.']::text[], array['Squat down keeping the bar at your chest.','Stand up and press the bar up and forward.','Bring it back to your chest.']::text[], array['Drive from the legs into the press']::text[], array['Leaning back to press']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_side_split_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_side_split_squat', 'Barbell Side Split Squat', array['Lateral Lunge (Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Side Split Squat is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the lateral lunge: bar on the back.', array['Stand up straight while holding a barbell placed on the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck). Your feet should be placed wide apart with the foot of the lead leg angled out to the side. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Lower your body towards the side of your angled foot by bending the knee and hip of your lead leg and while keeping the opposite leg only slightly bent. Breathe in as you lower your body.','Return to the starting position by extending the hip and knee of the lead leg. Breathe out as you perform this movement.','After performing the recommended amount of reps, repeat the movement with the opposite leg.']::text[], array['Sit back into the hip','Toes point forward']::text[], array['Knee caving in','Rounding the back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_side_split_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Side_Split_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_lunge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_lunge', 'Lateral Lunge', array['side lunge']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Stepping out to the side and bending that knee while the other leg stays straight.', array['Stand tall with feet together.']::text[], array['Take a wide step to the side.','Bend the stepping knee and sit back, keeping the other leg straight.','Push back to the start and alternate.']::text[], array['Sit back into the hip','Toes point forward']::text[], array['Knee caving in','Rounding the back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_squat', 'Lateral Squat', array['side squat','cossack squat']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Shifting into a deep squat on one leg while the other leg stays straight out to the side.', array['Stand with feet very wide, toes forward or slightly out.']::text[], array['Shift your weight to one side and squat down on that leg, keeping the other leg straight.','Push back to the middle and repeat on the other side.']::text[], array['Bent-leg heel stays down','Chest up']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Knee caving in']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_extension_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_extension_machine', 'Leg Extension (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straightening the knees against a pad while seated. Isolates the quadriceps.', array['Adjust the back pad so your knees line up with the machine pivot.','Place the ankle pad just above your ankles.']::text[], array['Straighten your legs until they are almost fully extended.','Squeeze the quads for a moment.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Hold the handles and keep hips down','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the weight up','Lifting the hips off the seat']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_extension_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leg_Extensions/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_extension_single_leg')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_extension_single_leg', 'Single Leg Extensions', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straightening the knees against a pad while seated. Isolates the quadriceps.', array['Adjust the back pad so your knees line up with the machine pivot.','Place the ankle pad just above your ankles.']::text[], array['Straighten your legs until they are almost fully extended.','Squeeze the quads for a moment.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Hold the handles and keep hips down','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the weight up','Lifting the hips off the seat']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_extension_single_leg/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Leg_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_press_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_press_machine', 'Leg Press (Machine)', array['45 degree leg press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a weighted platform away with your legs while seated. Lets you load the legs heavily with back support.', array['Sit with your back and hips flat against the pad.','Place your feet shoulder-width apart in the middle of the platform.']::text[], array['Release the safety and lower the platform until your knees are bent about 90° or more.','Keep your lower back and hips on the pad.','Push the platform back up without locking the knees hard.']::text[], array['Hips stay down on the seat','Knees in line with the toes','Push through the whole foot']::text[], array['Lowering so deep the hips curl off the pad','Snapping the knees straight','Placing hands on the knees']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/leg_press_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leg_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_press_horizontal')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_press_horizontal', 'Leg Press Horizontal (Machine)', array['seated leg press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a weighted platform away with your legs while seated. Lets you load the legs heavily with back support.', array['Sit with your back and hips flat against the pad.','Place your feet shoulder-width apart in the middle of the platform.']::text[], array['Release the safety and lower the platform until your knees are bent about 90° or more.','Keep your lower back and hips on the pad.','Push the platform back up without locking the knees hard.']::text[], array['Hips stay down on the seat','Knees in line with the toes','Push through the whole foot']::text[], array['Lowering so deep the hips curl off the pad','Snapping the knees straight','Placing hands on the knees']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'narrow_stance_leg_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'narrow_stance_leg_press', 'Narrow Stance Leg Press', array['Leg Press (Narrow Stance)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Narrow Stance Leg Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the leg press: feet close together, more quads.', array['Using a leg press machine, sit down on the machine and place your legs on the platform directly in front of you at a less-than-shoulder-width narrow stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Your feet should be around 3 inches or less apart. Tip: Keep your head up at all times and also maintain the back on the pad at all times.']::text[], array['Lower the safety bars holding the weighted platform in place and press the platform all the way up until your legs are fully extended in front of you. Tip: Make sure that you do not lock your knees. Your torso and the legs should make a perfect 90-degree angle. This will be your starting position.','As you inhale, slowly lower the platform until your upper and lower legs make a 90-degree angle.','Pushing mainly with the heels of your feet and using the quadriceps go back to the starting position as you exhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and ensure to lock the safety pins properly once you are done. You do not want that platform falling on you fully loaded.']::text[], array['Hips stay down on the seat','Knees in line with the toes','Push through the whole foot']::text[], array['Lowering so deep the hips curl off the pad','Snapping the knees straight','Placing hands on the knees']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/narrow_stance_leg_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Narrow_Stance_Leg_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'leg_press_single_leg')::uuid, 'mfd', 'leg_press_single_leg', 'Single Leg Press (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a weighted platform away with your legs while seated. Lets you load the legs heavily with back support.', array['Sit with your back and hips flat against the pad.','Place your feet shoulder-width apart in the middle of the platform.']::text[], array['Release the safety and lower the platform until your knees are bent about 90° or more.','Keep your lower back and hips on the pad.','Push the platform back up without locking the knees hard.']::text[], array['Hips stay down on the seat','Knees in line with the toes','Push through the whole foot']::text[], array['Lowering so deep the hips curl off the pad','Snapping the knees straight','Placing hands on the knees']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_leg_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_leg_press', 'Smith Machine Leg Press', array['Leg Press (Smith)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine Leg Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the leg press: lying under a Smith bar, pressing it with the feet.', array['Position a Smith machine bar a couple feet off of the ground. Ensure that it is resting on the safeties. After loading the bar to an appropriate weight, lie underneath the bar. Place the middle of your feet on the bar, tucking your knees to your chest. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the movement by driving through your feet to move the bar upward, extending the hips and knees. Do not lock out your knees.','At the top of the motion, pause briefly before returning to the starting position.']::text[], array['Lower back stays flat on the floor or bench','Knees in line with the toes','Push through the whole foot']::text[], array['Lowering so deep the hips curl up','Snapping the knees straight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_leg_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Leg_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lunge_bosu')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lunge_bosu', 'Dynamic Lunges on Bosu Ball', array['dynamic lunges on bosu ball','bosu lunge']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Stepping forward into a split stance and lowering until both knees are bent about 90°.', array['Stand tall with feet hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Take a long step forward.','Lower until your back knee nearly touches the floor and the front thigh is about parallel.','Push through the front foot to return to standing.','Alternate legs.']::text[], array['Torso upright','Front knee in line with the toes','Push through the front heel']::text[], array['Front knee caving in','Step too short so the heel lifts','Leaning forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lunge_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lunge_bodyweight', 'Lunge', array['forward lunge']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Stepping forward into a split stance and lowering until both knees are bent about 90°.', array['Stand tall with feet hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Take a long step forward.','Lower until your back knee nearly touches the floor and the front thigh is about parallel.','Push through the front foot to return to standing.','Alternate legs.']::text[], array['Torso upright','Front knee in line with the toes','Push through the front heel']::text[], array['Front knee caving in','Step too short so the heel lifts','Leaning forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lunge_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lunge_barbell', 'Lunge (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Stepping forward into a split stance and lowering until both knees are bent about 90°.', array['Stand tall with feet hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Take a long step forward.','Lower until your back knee nearly touches the floor and the front thigh is about parallel.','Push through the front foot to return to standing.','Alternate legs.']::text[], array['Torso upright','Front knee in line with the toes','Push through the front heel']::text[], array['Front knee caving in','Step too short so the heel lifts','Leaning forward']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lunge_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Lunge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lunge_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lunge_dumbbell', 'Lunge (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Stepping forward into a split stance and lowering until both knees are bent about 90°.', array['Stand tall with feet hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Take a long step forward.','Lower until your back knee nearly touches the floor and the front thigh is about parallel.','Push through the front foot to return to standing.','Alternate legs.']::text[], array['Torso upright','Front knee in line with the toes','Push through the front heel']::text[], array['Front knee caving in','Step too short so the heel lifts','Leaning forward']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lunge_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lunges/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_lunge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_lunge', 'Overhead Dumbbell Lunge', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A lunge while holding dumbbells locked out overhead, challenging leg strength and shoulder stability.', array['Press the dumbbells overhead and lock your arms.']::text[], array['Lunge forward while keeping the weights overhead.','Push back up and alternate legs.']::text[], array['Arms locked, biceps by your ears','Ribs down']::text[], array['Weights drifting forward','Arching the back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_overhead_kettlebell_squats')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_overhead_kettlebell_squats', 'One-Arm Overhead Kettlebell Squats', array['Overhead Squat (Single Arm Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Overhead Kettlebell Squats is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the overhead squat: one kettlebell locked out overhead.', array['Clean and press a kettlebell with one arm. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulder. Rotate your wrist as you do so. Press the weight overhead by extending through the elbow. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Looking straight ahead and keeping a kettlebell locked out above you, flex the knees and hips and lower your torso between your legs, keeping your head and chest up.','Pause at the bottom position for a second before rising back to the top, driving through the heels of your feet.']::text[], array['Lock the arm and push the kettlebell to the ceiling','Kettlebell stays over the mid-foot','Watch the kettlebell or look straight ahead']::text[], array['Kettlebell drifting forward','Elbow bending']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_overhead_kettlebell_squats/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Overhead_Kettlebell_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_squat', 'Overhead Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A squat with the bar locked out overhead in a wide grip. It demands mobility, balance and stability through the whole body.', array['Hold the bar overhead with a wide (snatch) grip, arms locked.','Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out.']::text[], array['Keep pushing the bar up as you squat down.','Keep the bar over the middle of your feet.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Push the bar to the ceiling','Bar over mid-foot']::text[], array['Bar drifting forward','Elbows bending']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Overhead_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pendulum_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pendulum_squat', 'Pendulum Squat (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A machine squat where you move in an arc, which keeps tension on the quads and allows very deep knee bend.', array['Stand on the platform with your shoulders under the pads and back against the pad.']::text[], array['Lower into a deep squat as the machine swings.','Push back up through the whole foot.']::text[], array['Go deep','Heels stay down']::text[], array['Bouncing at the bottom']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pistol_squat_assisted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pistol_squat_assisted', 'Assisted Pistol Squats', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A full squat on one leg with the other leg held straight out in front.', array['Stand on one leg with the other leg raised in front, arms forward for balance.']::text[], array['Squat down on the standing leg as low as you can.','Keep the heel down and the knee in line with the toes.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Arms forward to counterbalance','Heel stays down']::text[], array['Knee caving in','Rounding the back to reach depth']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_pistol_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_pistol_squat', 'Kettlebell Pistol Squat', array['Pistol Squat (Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Pistol Squat is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the pistol squat: a kettlebell held in front as a counterweight.', array['Pick up a kettlebell with two hands and hold it by the horns. Hold one leg off of the floor and squat down on the other.']::text[], array['Squat down by flexing the knee and sitting back with the hips, holding the kettlebell up in front of you.','Hold the bottom position for a second and then reverse the motion, driving through the heel and keeping your head and chest up.','Lower yourself again and repeat.']::text[], array['Arms forward to counterbalance','Heel stays down']::text[], array['Knee caving in','Rounding the back to reach depth']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_pistol_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Pistol_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pistol_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pistol_squat', 'Pistol Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A full squat on one leg with the other leg held straight out in front.', array['Stand on one leg with the other leg raised in front, arms forward for balance.']::text[], array['Squat down on the standing leg as low as you can.','Keep the heel down and the knee in line with the toes.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Arms forward to counterbalance','Heel stays down']::text[], array['Knee caving in','Rounding the back to reach depth']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_leg_high_box_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_leg_high_box_squat', 'Single-Leg High Box Squat', array['Pistol Squat (To High Box)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Single-Leg High Box Squat is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the pistol squat: sit down onto a high box on one leg.', array['Position a box in a rack. Secure a band or rope in place above the box.']::text[], array['Standing in front of it, step onto the box to a full standing position, letting your other leg remain unsupported. Hold onto the band for balance','. Continue stepping up and down on the same leg before switching to the opposite side.']::text[], array['Arms forward to counterbalance','Heel stays down']::text[], array['Knee caving in','Rounding the back to reach depth']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_leg_high_box_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Leg_High_Box_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_pistol_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_pistol_squat', 'Smith Machine Pistol Squat', array['Pistol Squat (Smith)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine Pistol Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the pistol squat: smith bar on the back for balance.', array['To begin, first set the bar to a position that best matches your height. Step under it and position the bar across the back of your shoulders.']::text[], array['Take the bar with your hands facing forward, unlock it and lift it off the rack by extending your legs. 3','Move one foot forward about 12 inches in front of the bar. Extend the other leg out in front of you, holding it off the ground. Look forward at all times and maintain a neutral or slightly arched spine. This will be your starting position.','Maintaining good posture, lower yourself by flexing the knee and hip, going down as far as flexibility allows.','Pause briefly at the bottom and then return to the starting position by driving through the heel of your foot, extending the knee and hip.']::text[], array['Arms forward to counterbalance','Heel stays down']::text[], array['Knee caving in','Rounding the back to reach depth']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_pistol_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Pistol_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'all_fours_quad_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'all_fours_quad_stretch', 'All Fours Quad Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'All Fours Quad Stretch is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', array['Start off on your hands and knees, then lift your leg off the floor and hold the foot with your hand.']::text[], array['Use your hand to hold the foot or ankle, keeping the knee fully flexed, stretching the quadriceps and hip flexors.','Focus on extending your hips, thrusting them towards the floor. Hold for 10-20 seconds and then switch sides.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/all_fours_quad_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/All_Fours_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'looking_at_ceiling')::uuid, 'mfd', 'looking_at_ceiling', 'Looking At Ceiling', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Looking At Ceiling is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Kneel on the floor, holding your heels with both hands.','Lift your buttocks up and forward while bringing your head back to look up at the ceiling, to give an arch in your back.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/looking_at_ceiling/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Looking_At_Ceiling/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_prone_quadriceps')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_prone_quadriceps', 'Lying Prone Quadriceps', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Lying Prone Quadriceps is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', array['Lay face down on the floor with your partner kneeling beside you. Flex one knee and raise that leg off the ground, attempting to touch your glutes with your foot. Your partner should hold the knee and ankle. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Attempt to extend your knee while your partner prevents any actual movement.','After 10-20 seconds, relax your muscles as your partner gently pushes the foot towards your glutes, further stretching the quadriceps and hip flexors.','After 10-20 seconds, switch sides.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_prone_quadriceps/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Prone_Quadriceps/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'on_your_side_quad_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'on_your_side_quad_stretch', 'On Your Side Quad Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'On Your Side Quad Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Start off by lying on your right side, with your right knee bent at a 90-degree angle resting on the floor in front of you (this stabilizes the torso).','Bend your left knee behind you and hold your left foot with your left hand. To stretch your hip flexor, press your left hip forward as you push your left foot back into your hand. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/on_your_side_quad_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/On_Your_Side_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'on_your_back_quad_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'on_your_back_quad_stretch', 'On-Your-Back Quad Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'On-Your-Back Quad Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', array['Lie on a flat bench or step, and hang one leg and arm over the side.']::text[], array['Bend the knee and hold the top of the foot. As you do this, be careful not to arch your lower back.','Pull the belly button to the spine to stay in neutral. Press your foot down and into your hand. To add the hip stretch, lift the hip of the leg you''re holding up toward the ceiling.','Switch sides.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/on_your_back_quad_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/On-Your-Back_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_half_locust')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_half_locust', 'One Half Locust', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'One Half Locust is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, biceps and chest.', array['Lie facedown on the floor.']::text[], array['Put your left hand under your left hipbone to pad your hip and pubic bone.','Bend your right knee so you can hold the foot in your right hand.','Lift the foot in the air and simultaneously lift your shoulders off the floor. This also stretches the right hip flexor and the chest and shoulders. Switch sides. If it doesn''t bother your back, you can try it with both arms and legs at the same time.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_half_locust/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Half_Locust/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'quad_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'quad_stretch', 'Quad Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Quad Stretch is an intermediate-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Lay on your side. Loop a belt, rope, or band around your top foot. Flex the knee and extend your hip, attempting to touch your glutes with your foot, and holding the belt with your hands. This will be your starting position.','With the belt being held over the shoulder or overhead, gently pull to increase the stretch in the quadriceps. Hold for 10-20 seconds, and then switch sides.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/quad_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Quad_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_elevated_quad_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_elevated_quad_stretch', 'Standing Elevated Quad Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Standing Elevated Quad Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the quadriceps.', array['Start by standing with your back about two to three feet away from a bench or step.']::text[], array['Lift one leg behind you and rest your foot on the step,either on your instep or the ball of your foot, whichever you find most comfortable.','Keep your supporting knee slightly bent and avoid letting that knee extend out beyond your toes. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Tuck the pelvis under and squeeze the glute on the stretching side','Keep the knees close together for the quad stretch','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Arching the lower back instead of tucking the pelvis','Pulling the knee out to the side','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_elevated_quad_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Elevated_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'elevated_back_lunge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'elevated_back_lunge', 'Elevated Back Lunge', array['Reverse Lunge (Deficit)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Elevated Back Lunge is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the reverse lunge: standing on a platform for a deeper lunge.', array['Position a bar onto a rack at shoulder height loaded to an appropriate weight. Place a short, raised platform behind you.']::text[], array['Rack the bar onto your upper back, keeping your back arched and tight. Step onto your raised platform with both feet. This will be your starting position.','Begin by stepping backwards with one leg. Descend by flexing your hips and knees until your knee touches the floor.','Pause, and extend through the hips and knees to rise up, returning all the way to the starting position before alternating.']::text[], array['Most weight on the front leg','Torso upright']::text[], array['Stepping back too narrow (like a tightrope)','Pushing off the back foot']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/elevated_back_lunge/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Elevated_Back_Lunge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_lunge_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_lunge_bodyweight', 'Reverse Lunge', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Stepping backward into a lunge. Usually easier on the knees than a forward lunge.', array['Stand tall with feet hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Step one foot back and lower until the back knee nearly touches the floor.','Push through the front foot to stand back up.','Alternate legs.']::text[], array['Most weight on the front leg','Torso upright']::text[], array['Stepping back too narrow (like a tightrope)','Pushing off the back foot']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_lunge_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_lunge_barbell', 'Reverse Lunge (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Stepping backward into a lunge. Usually easier on the knees than a forward lunge.', array['Stand tall with feet hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Step one foot back and lower until the back knee nearly touches the floor.','Push through the front foot to stand back up.','Alternate legs.']::text[], array['Most weight on the front leg','Torso upright']::text[], array['Stepping back too narrow (like a tightrope)','Pushing off the back foot']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_lunge_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_lunge_dumbbell', 'Reverse Lunge (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Stepping backward into a lunge. Usually easier on the knees than a forward lunge.', array['Stand tall with feet hip-width apart.']::text[], array['Step one foot back and lower until the back knee nearly touches the floor.','Push through the front foot to stand back up.','Alternate legs.']::text[], array['Most weight on the front leg','Torso upright']::text[], array['Stepping back too narrow (like a tightrope)','Pushing off the back foot']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_lunge_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Rear_Lunge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sissy_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sissy_squat', 'Sissy Squat (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Leaning back while bending the knees forward so the quads take nearly all the work.', array['Stand holding something for balance (or use a sissy squat bench), weight held to the chest if loaded.']::text[], array['Rise onto the balls of your feet and push your knees forward while leaning back, keeping hips straight.','Lower until your knees are well bent.','Return to standing using the quads.']::text[], array['Straight line from knees to shoulders','Go only as low as you control']::text[], array['Bending at the hips','Dropping fast into the bottom']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'weighted_sissy_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'weighted_sissy_squat', 'Weighted Sissy Squat', array['Sissy Squat (Weighted)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Weighted Sissy Squat is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the sissy squat: holding a plate at the chest.', array['Standing upright, with feet at shoulder width and toes raised, use one hand to hold onto the beams of a squat rack and the opposite arm to hold a plate on top of your chest. This is your starting position.']::text[], array['As you use one arm to hold yourself, bend at the knees and slowly lower your torso toward the ground by bringing your pelvis and knees forward. Inhale as you go down and stop when your upper and lower legs almost create a 90-degree angle. Hold the stretch position for a second.','After your one second hold, use your thigh muscles to bring your torso back up to the starting position. Exhale as you move up.','Repeat for the recommended amount of times.']::text[], array['Straight line from knees to shoulders','Go only as low as you control']::text[], array['Bending at the hips','Dropping fast into the bottom']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/weighted_sissy_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Weighted_Sissy_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'backward_drag')::uuid, 'mfd', 'backward_drag', 'Backward Drag', array['Sled Pull (Backward Drag)']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Backward Drag is a beginner-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the sled pull: walking backward, pulling the sled with straps or handles.', '{}'::text[], array['Load a sled with the desired weight, attaching a rope or straps to the sled that you can hold onto.','Begin the exercise by moving backwards for a given distance. Leaning back, extend through the legs for short steps to move as quickly as possible.']::text[], array['Stay low and drive through the legs']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/backward_drag/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Backward_Drag/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bear_crawl_sled_drags')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bear_crawl_sled_drags', 'Bear Crawl Sled Drags', array['Sled Pull (Bear Crawl)']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Bear Crawl Sled Drags is a beginner-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the sled pull: crawling on hands and feet with the sled attached to a belt.', '{}'::text[], array['Wearing either a harness or a loose weight belt, attach the chain to the back so that you will be facing away from the sled. Bend down so that your hands are on the ground. Your back should be flat and knees bent. This is your starting position.','Begin by driving with legs, alternating left and right. Use your hands to maintain balance and to help pull. Try to keep your back flat as you move over a given distance.']::text[], array['Stay low and drive through the legs']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bear_crawl_sled_drags/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bear_Crawl_Sled_Drags/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sled_drag_harness')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sled_drag_harness', 'Sled Drag - Harness', array['Sled Pull (Harness)']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Sled Drag - Harness is a beginner-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the sled pull: harness on the shoulders, walking or running forward.', '{}'::text[], array['To begin, load the sled with the desired weight and attach the pulling strap. You can pull with handles, use a harness, or attach the pulling strap to a weight belt.','Whether pulling forwards or backwards, lean in the direction of travel and progress by extending through the hips and knees.']::text[], array['Stay low and drive through the legs']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sled_drag_harness/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sled_Drag_-_Harness/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sled_pull')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sled_pull', 'Sled Pull', array['sled drag']::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Dragging a weighted sled with a rope or harness, walking backward or forward.', array['Attach a rope or harness to the sled.','Face the sled holding the rope (or face away wearing the harness).']::text[], array['Walk backward hand over hand pulling the rope, or walk forward leaning into the harness.','Continue for the set distance.']::text[], array['Stay low and drive through the legs']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sled_push')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sled_push', 'Sled Push', array['prowler push']::text[], 'strongman', 'distance_time', 'Pushing a weighted sled across the floor. Builds leg drive and conditioning with little stress on the joints.', array['Grip the sled poles with arms extended or bent, body leaning forward at about 45°.']::text[], array['Drive through the balls of your feet with short, powerful steps.','Keep pushing for the set distance.']::text[], array['Low body angle','Drive the knees forward']::text[], array['Standing too upright','Long, slow strides']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sled_push/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sled_Push/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'power_snatch_from_blocks')::uuid, 'mfd', 'power_snatch_from_blocks', 'Power Snatch from Blocks', array['Snatch (Power, From Blocks)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Power Snatch from Blocks is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, traps and triceps. A variation of the snatch: bar starts on blocks; caught above parallel.', array['Begin with a loaded barbell on boxes or stands of the desired height. A wide grip should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hips, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hips, with the chest up and the head looking forward. The shoulders should be just in front of the bar, with the elbows pointed out. This will be the starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the boxes.','Transition into the second pull by extending through the hips knees and ankles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the shoulders and allow the elbows to flex to the side.','As you move your feet into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move to just outside the hips, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar above a full squat and with the arms fully extended overhead.','Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, your head and chest up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the weight to the boxes.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/power_snatch_from_blocks/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Power_Snatch_from_Blocks/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch_from_blocks')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch_from_blocks', 'Snatch from Blocks', array['Snatch (From Blocks)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Snatch from Blocks is an advanced-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, traps and triceps. A variation of the snatch: bar starts on blocks.', array['Begin with a loaded barbell on boxes or stands of the desired height. A wide grip should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hips, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hips, with the chest up and the head looking forward. The shoulders should be just in front of the bar, with the elbows pointed out. This will be the starting position.']::text[], array['Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the boxes.','Transition into the second pull by extending through the hips knees and ankles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the shoulders and allow the elbows to flex to the side.','As you move your feet into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move to just outside the hips, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar with your body as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead.','Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, your head and chest up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the weight to the boxes.']::text[], array['Bar close to the body','Punch the arms up to lock out']::text[], array['Bar swinging forward','Catching with bent elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch_from_blocks/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Snatch_from_Blocks/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'heaving_snatch_balance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'heaving_snatch_balance', 'Heaving Snatch Balance', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'time', 'Heaving Snatch Balance is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, forearms, glutes, hamstrings and triceps.', array['This drill helps you learn the snatch. Begin by holding a light weight across the back of the shoulders. Your feet should be slightly wider than hip width apart with the feet turned out, the same position that you would perform a squat with.']::text[], array['Begin by dipping with the knees slightly, and popping back up to briefly unload the bar. Drive yourself underneath the bar, elevating it overhead as you descend into a full squat.','Return to a standing position.']::text[], array['Bar on the back with a snatch grip','Drive yourself down under the bar, not the bar up','Catch in a full overhead squat with locked arms']::text[], array['Pressing the bar out slowly','Soft elbows in the catch','Catching high and riding down']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/heaving_snatch_balance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Heaving_Snatch_Balance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch_balance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch_balance', 'Snatch Balance', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'time', 'Snatch Balance is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and triceps.', array['Begin with the feet in the pulling position, the bar racked across the back of the shoulders, and the hands placed in a wide snatch grip.']::text[], array['Pop the bar with an abrupt dip and drive of the knees, and aggressively drive under the bar, transitioning the feet into the receiving position.','Receive the bar locked out overhead near the bottom of the squat. The torso should remain vertical, lowering the hips between the legs.','Continue to descend to full depth, and return to a standing position. Carefully lower the weight.']::text[], array['Bar on the back with a snatch grip','Drive yourself down under the bar, not the bar up','Catch in a full overhead squat with locked arms']::text[], array['Pressing the bar out slowly','Soft elbows in the catch','Catching high and riding down']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch_balance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Snatch_Balance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'jerk_dip_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'jerk_dip_squat', 'Jerk Dip Squat', array['Split Jerk (Jerk Dip (Drill))']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Jerk Dip Squat is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core and calves. A variation of the split jerk: drill: the dip and drive only, bar in the front rack.', '{}'::text[], array['This movement strengthens the dip portion of the jerk. Begin with the bar racked in the jerk position, with the shoulders forward to create a shelf and the bar lightly contacting the throat. The feet should be directly under the hips, with the feet turned out as is comfortable.','Keeping the torso vertical, dip by flexing the knees, allowing them to travel forward and without moving the hips to the rear. The dip should not be excessive. Return the weight to the starting position by driving forcefully though the feet.']::text[], array['Vertical dip','Punch under the bar']::text[], array['Dipping forward','Soft elbows in the catch']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/jerk_dip_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Jerk_Dip_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'power_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'power_jerk', 'Power Jerk', array['Split Jerk (Power Jerk)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Power Jerk is an advanced-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, calves, glutes, hamstrings and triceps. A variation of the split jerk: feet land in a quarter squat instead of a split.', array['Standing with the weight racked on the front of the shoulders, begin with the dip. With your feet directly under your hips, flex the knees without moving the hips backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible.']::text[], array['Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move your head out of the way as the bar leaves the shoulders.','At this moment as the feet leave the floor, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athletes effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should be moved to a slightly wider stance, with the knees partially bent.','Receive the bar with the arms locked out overhead.','Return to a standing position.']::text[], array['Vertical dip','Punch under the bar']::text[], array['Dipping forward','Soft elbows in the catch']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/power_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Power_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_jerk', 'Squat Jerk', array['Split Jerk (Squat Jerk)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Squat Jerk is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and triceps. A variation of the split jerk: caught in a full overhead squat.', array['Standing with the weight racked on the front of the shoulders, begin with the dip. With your feet directly under your hips, flex the knees without moving the hips backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move your head out of the way as the bar leaves the shoulders.']::text[], array['At this moment as the feet leave the floor, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athlete''s effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should move forcefully to just outside the hips, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar with your body in a full squat and the arms fully extended overhead.','Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, your head and chest up, drive throught heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the weight to floor.']::text[], array['Vertical dip','Punch under the bar']::text[], array['Dipping forward','Soft elbows in the catch']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Squat_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lunge_sprint')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lunge_sprint', 'Lunge Sprint', array['Split Squat (Smith, Explosive)']::text[], 'strength', 'distance_time', 'Lunge Sprint is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the split squat: smith machine split squat, driving up as fast as possible.', array['Adjust a bar in a Smith machine to an appropriate height. Position yourself under the bar, racking it across the back of your shoulders. Unrack the bar, and then split your feet, moving one foot forward and one foot back. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Lower your back knee nearly to the ground, flexing the knees and lowering your hips as you do so.','At the bottom of the descent, immediately reverse direction. Explosively drive through the heel of your front foot with light pressure from your back foot. Jump up and reverse the position of your legs.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Straight down, straight up','Front heel stays planted']::text[], array['Stance too short','Leaning forward over the front knee']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lunge_sprint/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lunge_Sprint/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_single_leg_split_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_single_leg_split_squat', 'Smith Single-Leg Split Squat', array['Split Squat (Smith)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Single-Leg Split Squat is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the split squat: smith machine bar.', array['To begin, place a flat bench 2-3 feet behind the smith machine. Then, set the bar on the height that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.']::text[], array['Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side (palms facing forward), unlock it and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Position your legs by placing one foot slightly forward under the bar and extending your other leg back and place the top of your foot on the bench. This will be your starting position','Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knee as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calf becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knee should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your knee is past that imaginary line (if it is past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten your leg again and go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','Switch legs and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Straight down, straight up','Front heel stays planted']::text[], array['Stance too short','Leaning forward over the front knee']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_single_leg_split_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Single-Leg_Split_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'split_squat_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'split_squat_dumbbell', 'Split Squat (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A lunge without stepping: you stay in a split stance and lower straight down and up.', array['Stand in a long split stance, holding dumbbells at your sides.','Back heel lifted.']::text[], array['Lower straight down until the back knee nearly touches the floor.','Push up through the front foot.','Finish all reps, then switch legs.']::text[], array['Straight down, straight up','Front heel stays planted']::text[], array['Stance too short','Leaning forward over the front knee']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/split_squat_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Split_Squat_with_Dumbbells/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_sprint')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_sprint', 'Bench Sprint', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'distance_time', 'Bench Sprint is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['Stand on the ground with one foot resting on a bench or box with your heel close to the edge.']::text[], array['Push off with your foot on top of the bench, extending through the hip and knee.','Land with the opposite foot on top of the box, returning your other foot back to the start position.','Continue alternating from one foot to another to complete the set.']::text[], array['Drive the knee up and the foot down under the hips','Arms swing from the shoulder, elbows about 90 degrees','Stay tall with a slight forward lean']::text[], array['Reaching out with the foot in front of the body','Arms crossing the body','Running the drill tired; quality comes first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_sprint/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bench_Sprint/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_cone_sprint_drill')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_cone_sprint_drill', 'Single-Cone Sprint Drill', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'distance_time', 'Single-Cone Sprint Drill is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings.', array['This drill teaches quick foot action. You need a single cone. Begin standing next to the cone with one arm back and one arm forward.']::text[], array['Chop the feet as quickly as possible, blocking with the arms. Circle the cone, keep your knees up, with violent foot action.','Rest after three trips around the cone.']::text[], array['Drive the knee up and the foot down under the hips','Arms swing from the shoulder, elbows about 90 degrees','Stay tall with a slight forward lean']::text[], array['Reaching out with the foot in front of the body','Arms crossing the body','Running the drill tired; quality comes first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_cone_sprint_drill/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Cone_Sprint_Drill/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_squat_to_a_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_squat_to_a_bench', 'Barbell Squat To A Bench', array['Squat (To Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Squat To A Bench is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: squat until you lightly touch a bench, then stand.', array['This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first place a flat bench or a box behind you. The flat bench is used to teach you to set your hips back and to hit depth.']::text[], array['Then, set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.','Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Step away from the rack and position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).','Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees and sitting your hips back as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until you slightly touch the bench behind you. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knees should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs and extend the hips to go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_squat_to_a_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Squat_To_A_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_box')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_box', 'Box Squat (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Set the bar in a rack at about upper-chest height.','Step under it and rest it on your upper back (on the traps, not the neck), hands just outside your shoulders.','Stand up to lift it off, take two or three steps back, feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out slightly.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control','Touch the box lightly; do not drop onto it']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_box/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Box_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'box_squat_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'box_squat_with_bands', 'Box Squat with Bands', array['Squat (Box, Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Box Squat with Bands is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: box squat with bands adding load near the top.', array['Begin in a power rack with a box at the appropriate height behind you. Set up the bands on the sleeves, secured to either band pegs, the rack, or dumbbells so that there is appropriate tension. If dumbbells are used, secure them so that they don''t move. Also, ensure that the dumbbells you are using are heavy enough for the bands that you are using. Additional plates can be used to hold the dumbbells down. If more tension is needed, you can either widen the base on the floor or choke the bands. Typically, you would aim for a box height that brings you to a parallel squat, but you can train higher or lower if desired.']::text[], array['Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the shoulders. Squeeze your shoulder blades together and rotate your elbows forward, attempting to bend the bar across your shoulders. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place your feet wider for more emphasis on the back, glutes, adductors, and hamstrings, or closer together for more quad development. Keep your head facing forward.','With your back, shoulders, and core tight, push your knees and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips until you are seated on the box. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Pause when you reach the box, and relax the hip flexors. Never bounce off of a box.','Keeping the weight on your heels and pushing your feet and knees out, drive upward off of the box as you lead the movement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe. Use care to return the barbell to the rack.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/box_squat_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Box_Squat_with_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'box_squat_with_chains')::uuid, 'mfd', 'box_squat_with_chains', 'Box Squat with Chains', array['Squat (Box, Chains)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Box Squat with Chains is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: box squat with chains adding load near the top.', array['Begin in a power rack with a box at the appropriate height behind you. Typically, you would aim for a box height that brings you to a parallel squat, but you can train higher or lower if desired.']::text[], array['To set up the chains, begin by looping the leader chain over the sleeves of the bar. The heavy chain should be attached using a snap hook. Adjust the length of the lead chain so that a few links are still on the floor at the top of the movement.','Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the shoulders. Squeeze your shoulder blades together and rotate your elbows forward, attempting to bend the bar across your shoulders. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place your feet wider for more emphasis on the back, glutes, adductors, and hamstrings, or closer together for more quad development. Keep your head facing forward.','With your back, shoulders, and core tight, push your knees and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips until you are seated on the box. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Pause when you reach the box, and relax the hip flexors. Never bounce off of a box.','Keeping the weight on your heels and pushing your feet and knees out, drive upward off of the box as you lead the movement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/box_squat_with_chains/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Box_Squat_with_Chains/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chair_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chair_squat', 'Chair Squat', array['Squat (Chair Squat)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Chair Squat is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the squat: feet well forward of the bar, sitting straight back.', array['To begin, first set the bar to a position that best matches your height. Once the bar is loaded, step under it and position it across the back of your shoulders.']::text[], array['Take the bar with your hands facing forward, unlock it and lift it off the rack by extending your legs.','Move your feet forward about 18 inches in front of the bar. Position your legs using a shoulder width stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Look forward at all times and maintain a neutral or slightly arched spine. This will be your starting position.','Slowly lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper and lower leg breaks 90 degrees.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heels of your feet, extending the knees and returning to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chair_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chair_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_squat_to_a_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_squat_to_a_bench', 'Dumbbell Squat To A Bench', array['Squat (Dumbbell to Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Squat To A Bench is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: dumbbells at the sides; squat until you lightly touch a bench.', array['Stand up straight with a flat bench behind you while holding a dumbbell on each hand (palms facing the side of your legs).']::text[], array['Position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position. Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section.','Begin to slowly lower your torso by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until you slightly touch the bench behind you. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knees should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_squat_to_a_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Squat_To_A_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_full')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_full', 'Full Squat', array['atg squat','deep squat']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Set the bar in a rack at about upper-chest height.','Step under it and rest it on your upper back (on the traps, not the neck), hands just outside your shoulders.','Stand up to lift it off, take two or three steps back, feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out slightly.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_full/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Full_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'narrow_stance_squats')::uuid, 'mfd', 'narrow_stance_squats', 'Narrow Stance Squats', array['Squat (Narrow Stance)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Narrow Stance Squats is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: feet closer, more knee travel and quads.', array['This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.']::text[], array['Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Step away from the rack and position your legs using a less-than-shoulder-width narrow stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Feet should be around 3-6 inches apart. Keep your head up at all times (looking down will get you off balance) and maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).','Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knees should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/narrow_stance_squats/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Narrow_Stance_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'olympic_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'olympic_squat', 'Olympic Squat', array['Squat (Olympic (High Bar))']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Olympic Squat is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the squat: high bar, upright torso, full depth.', array['Begin with a barbell supported on top of the traps. The chest should be up, and the head facing forward. Adopt a hip width stance with the feet turned out as needed.']::text[], array['Descend by flexing the knees, refraining from moving the hips back as much as possible. This requires that the knees travel forward; ensure that they stay aligned with the feet. The goal is to keep the torso as upright as possible. Continue all the way down, keeping the weight on the front of the heel.','At the moment the upper legs contact the lower, reverse the motion, driving the weight upward.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/olympic_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Olympic_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_pause')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_pause', 'Pause Squat (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Set the bar in a rack at about upper-chest height.','Step under it and rest it on your upper back (on the traps, not the neck), hands just outside your shoulders.','Stand up to lift it off, take two or three steps back, feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out slightly.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control','Stay tight during the pause; do not relax at the bottom']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_band_box_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_band_box_squat', 'Reverse Band Box Squat', array['Squat (Box, Reverse Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Band Box Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: bands from above help at the bottom.', array['Begin in a power rack with a box at the appropriate height behind you. Set up the bands either on band pegs or attached to the top of the rack, ensuring they will be directly above the bar during the squat. Attach the other end to the bar.']::text[], array['Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the shoulders. Squeeze your shoulder blades together and rotate your elbows forward, attempting to bend the bar across your shoulders. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place your feet wider for more emphasis on the back, glutes, adductors, and hamstrings, or closer together for more quad development. Keep your head facing forward.','With your back, shoulders, and core tight, push your knees and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips until you are seated on the box. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Pause when you reach the box, and relax the hip flexors. Never bounce off of a box.','Keeping the weight on your heels and pushing your feet and knees out, drive upward off of the box as you lead the movement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe. Use care to return the barbell to the rack.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_band_box_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Box_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_band_power_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_band_power_squat', 'Reverse Band Power Squat', array['Squat (Reverse Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Band Power Squat is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the adductors, calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: bands from above help at the bottom.', array['Begin in a power rack with the pins and bar set at the appropriate height. After loading the bar, attach bands to the top of the rack, using either pegs or the frame itself. Attach the other end of the bands to the bar.']::text[], array['Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the shoulders. Squeeze your shoulder blades together and rotate your elbows forward, attempting to bend the bar across your shoulders. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place your feet wide for more emphasis on the back, glutes, adductors, and hamstrings.','Keep your head facing forward. With your back, shoulders, and core tight, push your knees and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torso lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hip being in line with the top of the knee.','Keeping the weight on your heels and pushing your feet and knees out, drive upward as you lead the movement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the starting position.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_band_power_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Power_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'speed_box_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'speed_box_squat', 'Speed Box Squat', array['Squat (Box, Speed)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Speed Box Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the squat: light weight, as fast as possible off the box.', array['Attach bands to the bar that are securely anchored near the ground. You may need to choke the bands to get adequate tension.']::text[], array['Use a box of an appropriate height for this exercise. Load the bar to a weight that still requires effort, but isn''t so heavy that speed is compromised. Typically, that will be between 50-70% of your one rep max.','Position the bar on your upper back, shoulder blades retracted, back arched and everything tight head to toe. This will be the starting position.','Unrack the bar and position yourself in front of the box. Sit back with your hips until you are seated on the box, ensuring that you descend under control and don''t crash onto the surface.','Pause briefly, and explode off of the box, extending through the hips and knees.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/speed_box_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Speed_Box_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'speed_squats')::uuid, 'mfd', 'speed_squats', 'Speed Squats', array['Squat (Speed)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Speed Squats is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: light weight, as fast as possible on the way up.', array['This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.']::text[], array['Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Step away from the rack and position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).','Begin to lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knees should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to raise the bar as fast as possible without involving momentum as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position. Note: You should perform these exercises as fast as possible but without breaking perfect form and without involving momentum.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/speed_squats/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Speed_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_band', 'Squat (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Stand on the band and loop it over your shoulders or hold it at shoulder height.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_band/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Squats_-_With_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_barbell', 'Squat (Barbell)', array['back squat','barbell squat','bb squat']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Set the bar in a rack at about upper-chest height.','Step under it and rest it on your upper back (on the traps, not the neck), hands just outside your shoulders.','Stand up to lift it off, take two or three steps back, feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out slightly.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_bodyweight', 'Squat (Bodyweight)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width apart, arms out in front for balance.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_bodyweight/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_dumbbell', 'Squat (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width apart, a dumbbell in each hand at your sides or on your shoulders.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_machine', 'Squat (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Position yourself under the shoulder pads with feet shoulder-width on the platform.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_smith', 'Squat (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Set the bar in a rack at about upper-chest height.','Step under it and rest it on your upper back (on the traps, not the neck), hands just outside your shoulders.','Stand up to lift it off, take two or three steps back, feet shoulder-width apart, toes turned out slightly.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_smith/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_suspension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_suspension', 'Squat (Suspension)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Face the anchor holding the handles with arms extended.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_bosu')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_bosu', 'Squat on Bosu Ball', array['squat bosu ball','bosu squat']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Bending at the hips and knees to lower your body and standing back up. The foundation of lower-body strength.', array['Place the bosu flat side down and step onto the dome with feet hip- to shoulder-width apart.']::text[], array['Brace your core, then break at the hips and knees at the same time.','Sit down between your heels, knees tracking in line with your toes.','Go down until your hips are at least level with your knees, or as deep as you can with a neutral back.','Drive up through the whole foot until you are standing tall.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_with_bands', 'Squat with Bands', array['Squat (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Squat with Bands is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the adductors, calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: bands add load near the top.', array['Set up the bands on the sleeves, secured to either band pegs, the rack, or dumbbells so that there is appropriate tension.']::text[], array['Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the shoulders. Squeeze your shoulder blades together and rotate your elbows forward, attempting to bend the bar across your shoulders. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place your feet wide for more emphasis on the back, glutes, adductors, and hamstrings. Keep your head facing forward.','With your back, shoulders, and core tight, push your knees and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torso lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hip being in line with the top of the knee.','Keeping the weight on your heels and pushing your feet and knees out, drive upward as you lead the movement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the starting position.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Squat_with_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_with_chains')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_with_chains', 'Squat with Chains', array['Squat (Chains)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Squat with Chains is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the adductors, calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: chains add load near the top.', array['To set up the chains, begin by looping the leader chain over the sleeves of the bar. The heavy chain should be attached using a snap hook. Adjust the length of the lead chain so that a few links are still on the floor at the top of the movement.']::text[], array['Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the shoulders. Squeeze your shoulder blades together and rotate your elbows forward, attempting to bend the bar across your shoulders. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place your feet wide for more emphasis on the back, glutes, adductors, and hamstrings. Keep your head facing forward.','With your back, shoulders, and core tight, push your knees and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torso lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hip being in line with the top of the knee.','Keeping the weight on your heels and pushing your feet and knees out, drive upward as you lead the movement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the starting position.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_with_chains/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Squat_with_Chains/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_with_plate_movers')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_with_plate_movers', 'Squat with Plate Movers', array['Squat (Plate Movers)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Squat with Plate Movers is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abductors, adductors, calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the squat: a plate is moved with the feet between sets to build footwork.', array['To begin, first set the bar on a rack to just below shoulder level. Position a weight plate on the ground a couple feet back from the rack. Once the bar is loaded, step under it and place the back of your shoulders across it.']::text[], array['Hold on to the bar with both hands and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straighten your torso.','Step away from the rack and adopt a wide stance with the toes slightly pointed out, with one foot on the weight plate. Keep your head up at all times. This will be your starting position.','Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees and hips. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees.','Raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heels of your feet as you extend the hips and knees.','At the top of the movement, side step, bringing your feet together on the opposite side of the plate.','Using your inside foot, push the weight plate, sliding it across the floor to where you were just standing.','Place your inside foot on the weight plate, adopting a wide stance for the next repetition.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/squat_with_plate_movers/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Squat_with_Plate_Movers/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wide_stance_barbell_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wide_stance_barbell_squat', 'Wide Stance Barbell Squat', array['Squat (Wide Stance)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Wide Stance Barbell Squat is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back. A variation of the squat: feet wider, more hips and inner thighs.', array['This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.']::text[], array['Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Step away from the rack and position your legs using a wider-than-shoulder-width stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up at all times as looking down will get you off balance, and also maintain a straight back. This will be your starting position.','Begin to slowly lower the bar by bending the knees as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calves becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to the floor). Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the knees should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your knees are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the knee and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.','Begin to raise the bar as you exhale by pushing the floor with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Knees out in line with the toes','Chest up, back neutral','Whole foot on the floor, heels down','Stand up as fast as you can control']::text[], array['Knees caving inward','Heels lifting','Rounding the lower back at the bottom ("butt wink")','Hips rising faster than the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/wide_stance_barbell_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Wide_Stance_Barbell_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'squat_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'squat_row', 'Squat Row', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Holding a cable or strap handle at chest height, squatting down and rowing as you stand up.', array['Face a mid-height cable or suspension anchor holding the handles with straight arms.']::text[], array['Squat down with arms extended.','Stand up and row the handles to your ribs at the same time.','Extend the arms as you squat again.']::text[], array['Smooth, continuous movement']::text[], array['Leaning back instead of rowing']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_step_ups')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_step_ups', 'Barbell Step Ups', array['Step Up (Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Step Ups is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the step up: bar on the back.', array['Stand up straight while holding a barbell placed on the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) and stand upright behind an elevated platform (such as the one used for spotting behind a flat bench). This is your starting position.']::text[], array['Place the right foot on the elevated platform. Step on the platform by extending the hip and the knee of your right leg. Use the heel mainly to lift the rest of your body up and place the foot of the left leg on the platform as well. Breathe out as you execute the force required to come up.','Step down with the left leg by flexing the hip and knee of the right leg as you inhale. Return to the original standing position by placing the right foot of to next to the left foot on the initial position.','Repeat with the right leg for the recommended amount of repetitions and then perform with the left leg.']::text[], array['Push through the top leg, not the bottom foot','Stand fully tall on top']::text[], array['Pushing off the floor leg','Knee caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_step_ups/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Step_Ups/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'step_up_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'step_up_dumbbell', 'Dumbbell Step Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Stepping up onto a box or bench with one leg and standing tall on it.', array['Stand facing a box or bench at about knee height.']::text[], array['Place one whole foot on the box.','Push through that foot to stand up on the box.','Step down with control and repeat.']::text[], array['Push through the top leg, not the bottom foot','Stand fully tall on top']::text[], array['Pushing off the floor leg','Knee caving in']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/step_up_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Step_Ups/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'step_up_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'step_up_bodyweight', 'Step Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Stepping up onto a box or bench with one leg and standing tall on it.', array['Stand facing a box or bench at about knee height.']::text[], array['Place one whole foot on the box.','Push through that foot to stand up on the box.','Step down with control and repeat.']::text[], array['Push through the top leg, not the bottom foot','Stand fully tall on top']::text[], array['Pushing off the floor leg','Knee caving in']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'yoke_walk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'yoke_walk', 'Yoke Walk', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_distance', 'Yoke Walk is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, abductors, adductors, calves, glutes, hamstrings and lower back.', array['The yoke is usually done with a yoke apparatus, but is sometimes seen with refrigerators or other heavy objects.']::text[], array['Begin by racking the apparatus across the back of the shoulders. With your head looking forward and back arched, lift the yoke by driving through the heels.','Begin walking as quickly as possible using short, quick steps. You may hold the side posts of the yoke to help steady it and hold it in position. Continue for the given distance as fast as possible, usually 75-100 feet.']::text[], array['Brace before you lift and stay tall','Short, quick steps','Eyes ahead']::text[], array['Long strides that make the load swing','Leaning forward','Holding the breath for the whole distance']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/yoke_walk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Yoke_Walk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sandbag_load')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sandbag_load', 'Sandbag Load', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Sandbag Load is a beginner-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, biceps, calves, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, upper back and traps.', array['To load sandbags or other objects, begin with the implements placed a distance from the loading platform, typically 50 feet.']::text[], array['Begin by lifting the sandbag. Sandbags are extremely awkward, and the manner of lifting them can vary depending on the particular sandbag used. Reach as far around it as possible, extending through the hips and knees to pull it up high. Shouldering is usually not allowed.','Move as quickly as possible to the platform, and load it, extending through your hips, knees, and ankles to get it as high as possible. Place it onto the platform, ensuring it doesn''t fall off.','Return to the starting position to retrieve the next sandbag, and repeat until the event is completed.']::text[], array['Straddle the implement and wrap it tight to the body','Lap it first if needed, then drive the hips forward to load','Keep it close the whole way']::text[], array['Pulling with the arms','Letting it drift away from the body','Rounding with no brace']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sandbag_load/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sandbag_Load/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'plie_dumbbell_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'plie_dumbbell_squat', 'Plie Dumbbell Squat', array['Sumo Squat (Dumbbell (Plie))']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Plie Dumbbell Squat is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the abs & core, calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the sumo squat: wide stance, toes out, one dumbbell between the legs.', array['Hold a dumbbell at the base with both hands and stand straight up. Move your legs so that they are wider than shoulder width apart from each other with your knees slightly bent.']::text[], array['Your toes should be facing out. Note: Your arms should be stationary while performing the exercise. This is the starting position.','Slowly bend the knees and lower your legs until your thighs are parallel to the floor. Make sure to inhale as this is the eccentric part of the exercise.','Press mainly with the heel of the foot to bring the body back to the starting position while exhaling.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Knees follow the toes','Sit straight down']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Leaning forward']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/plie_dumbbell_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Plie_Dumbbell_Squat/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sumo_squat_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sumo_squat_bodyweight', 'Sumo Squat', array['plie squat']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A wide-stance squat with toes turned out, emphasising the inner thighs and glutes.', array['Stand with feet well wider than shoulders, toes turned out 30–45°.']::text[], array['Squat straight down, pushing the knees out over the toes.','Keep the torso upright.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Knees follow the toes','Sit straight down']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Leaning forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sumo_squat_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sumo_squat_barbell', 'Sumo Squat (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A wide-stance squat with toes turned out, emphasising the inner thighs and glutes.', array['Stand with feet well wider than shoulders, toes turned out 30–45°.']::text[], array['Squat straight down, pushing the knees out over the toes.','Keep the torso upright.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Knees follow the toes','Sit straight down']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Leaning forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sumo_squat_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sumo_squat_dumbbell', 'Sumo Squat (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A wide-stance squat with toes turned out, emphasising the inner thighs and glutes.', array['Stand with feet well wider than shoulders, toes turned out 30–45°.']::text[], array['Squat straight down, pushing the knees out over the toes.','Keep the torso upright.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Knees follow the toes','Sit straight down']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Leaning forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sumo_squat_kettlebell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sumo_squat_kettlebell', 'Sumo Squat (Kettlebell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A wide-stance squat with toes turned out, emphasising the inner thighs and glutes.', array['Stand with feet well wider than shoulders, toes turned out 30–45°.']::text[], array['Squat straight down, pushing the knees out over the toes.','Keep the torso upright.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Knees follow the toes','Sit straight down']::text[], array['Knees caving in','Leaning forward']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'thruster_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'thruster_barbell', 'Thruster (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A front squat that flows straight into an overhead press, using the drive from the legs.', array['Hold the weight in the front rack at your shoulders, feet shoulder-width.']::text[], array['Squat down with an upright torso.','Drive up hard and use the momentum to press the weight overhead.','Lower it to your shoulders as you go into the next squat.']::text[], array['One smooth movement','Elbows up in the squat']::text[], array['Pausing between squat and press','Pressing forward instead of up']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'thruster_kettlebell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'thruster_kettlebell', 'Thruster (Kettlebell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A front squat that flows straight into an overhead press, using the drive from the legs.', array['Hold the weight in the front rack at your shoulders, feet shoulder-width.']::text[], array['Squat down with an upright torso.','Drive up hard and use the momentum to press the weight overhead.','Lower it to your shoulders as you go into the next squat.']::text[], array['One smooth movement','Elbows up in the squat']::text[], array['Pausing between squat and press','Pressing forward instead of up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/thruster_kettlebell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Thruster/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'tire_flip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'tire_flip', 'Tire Flip', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Tire Flip is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, chest, forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, traps and triceps.', array['Begin by gripping the bottom of the tire on the tread, and position your feet back a bit. Your chest should be driving into the tire.']::text[], array['To lift the tire, extend through the hips, knees, and ankles, driving into the tire and up.','As the tire reaches a 45 degree angle, step forward and drive a knee into the tire. As you do so adjust your grip to the upper portion of the tire and push it forward as hard as possible to complete the turn. Repeat as necessary.']::text[], array['Squat down, chest against the tire, fingers under it','Drive forward and up with the legs','Push the tire over']::text[], array['Pulling with a rounded back','Curling it with the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/tire_flip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Tire_Flip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'walking_treadmill')::uuid, 'mfd', 'walking_treadmill', 'Walking, Treadmill', array['Treadmill (Walking)']::text[], 'cardio', 'distance_time', 'Walking, Treadmill is a beginner-level cardio exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the cardio, calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the treadmill: walking pace.', '{}'::text[], array['To begin, step onto the treadmill and select the desired option from the menu. Most treadmills have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and weight to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout.','Treadmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than walking outside. When walking, you should move at a moderate to fast pace, not a leisurely one. Being an activity of lower intensity, walking doesn''t burn as many calories as some other activities, but still provides great benefit. A 150 lb person will burn about 175 calories walking 4 miles per hour for 30 minutes, compared to 450 calories running twice as fast. Maintain proper posture as you walk, and only hold onto the handles when necessary, such as when dismounting or checking your heart rate.']::text[], array['Run tall with relaxed shoulders','Land under your hips, not far in front','Easy: you can hold a conversation']::text[], array['Holding the handrails while walking at an incline','Overstriding']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/walking_treadmill/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Walking_Treadmill/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_walking_lunge')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_walking_lunge', 'Barbell Walking Lunge', array['Walking Lunge (Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Walking Lunge is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the quadriceps, with help from the calves, glutes and hamstrings. A variation of the walking lunge: bar on the back.', array['Begin standing with your feet shoulder width apart and a barbell across your upper back.']::text[], array['Step forward with one leg, flexing the knees to drop your hips. Descend until your rear knee nearly touches the ground. Your posture should remain upright, and your front knee should stay above the front foot.','Drive through the heel of your lead foot and extend both knees to raise yourself back up.','Step forward with your rear foot, repeating the lunge on the opposite leg.']::text[], array['Long steps','Stay tall']::text[], array['Short choppy steps','Wobbling side to side']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_walking_lunge/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Walking_Lunge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'walking_lunge_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'walking_lunge_bodyweight', 'Walking Lunge', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Lunging forward continuously, stepping through with each rep to travel across the floor.', array['Stand tall with space in front of you.']::text[], array['Step forward into a lunge.','Push off and bring the back foot forward into the next lunge.','Continue for the set distance or reps.']::text[], array['Long steps','Stay tall']::text[], array['Short choppy steps','Wobbling side to side']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/walking_lunge_bodyweight/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Walking_Lunge/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'walking_lunge_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'walking_lunge_dumbbell', 'Walking Lunge (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_distance', 'Lunging forward continuously, stepping through with each rep to travel across the floor.', array['Stand tall with space in front of you.']::text[], array['Step forward into a lunge.','Push off and bring the back foot forward into the next lunge.','Continue for the set distance or reps.']::text[], array['Long steps','Stay tall']::text[], array['Short choppy steps','Wobbling side to side']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'walking_lunge_sandbag')::uuid, 'mfd', 'walking_lunge_sandbag', 'Walking Lunge (Sandbag)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_distance', 'Lunging forward continuously, stepping through with each rep to travel across the floor.', array['Stand tall with space in front of you.']::text[], array['Step forward into a lunge.','Push off and bring the back foot forward into the next lunge.','Continue for the set distance or reps.']::text[], array['Long steps','Stay tall']::text[], array['Short choppy steps','Wobbling side to side']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wall_ball')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wall_ball', 'Wall Ball', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Squatting with a medicine ball and throwing it up to a target on the wall as you stand.', array['Stand about an arm''s length from the wall holding a medicine ball at your chest.']::text[], array['Squat down below parallel.','Drive up and throw the ball to the target.','Catch it and go straight into the next squat.']::text[], array['Use the legs to throw','Catch high and absorb into the squat']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Shallow squats']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wall_sit')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wall_sit', 'Wall Sit', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Holding a seated position against a wall with the thighs parallel to the floor.', array['Stand with your back against a wall and feet about 60 cm in front of it.']::text[], array['Slide down until your knees are bent about 90°.','Hold for the target time.','Slide back up.']::text[], array['Knees over the ankles','Back flat against the wall']::text[], array['Hands pushing on the thighs']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'zercher_squat')::uuid, 'mfd', 'zercher_squat', 'Zercher Squat', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A squat with the bar held in the crook of your elbows, which heavily challenges the core and upper back.', array['Set the bar in a rack at about stomach height.','Hold it in the crease of your elbows, hands together, and stand up.']::text[], array['Squat down keeping the torso upright and the bar close.','Stand back up.']::text[], array['Elbows stay up','Upper back tight']::text[], array['Rounding forward','Letting the bar slide down the forearms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/zercher_squat/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Zercher_Squats/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'anti_gravity_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'anti_gravity_press', 'Anti-Gravity Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Anti-Gravity Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the upper back, traps and triceps.', array['Place a bar on the ground behind the head of an incline bench.']::text[], array['Lay on the bench face down. With a pronated grip, pick the barbell up from the floor. Flex the elbows, performing a reverse curl to bring the bar near your chest. This will be your starting position.','To begin, press the barbell out in front of your head by extending your elbows. Keep your arms parallel to the ground throughout the movement.','Return to the starting position and repeat to complete the set.']::text[], array['Lie face down on an incline bench','Press the bar forward and slightly up with straight arms','Keep the chest on the pad']::text[], array['Shrugging','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/anti_gravity_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Anti-Gravity_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_wrist_pull')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_wrist_pull', 'Side Wrist Pull', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Side Wrist Pull is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the forearms and lats.', '{}'::text[], array['This stretch works best standing. Cross your left arm over the midline of your body and hold the left wrist in your right hand down at the level of your hips. Start the stretch with a bent left arm.','Slowly straighten, pull, and lift it up to shoulder height, as pictured. Feel this stretch originate in your back, not your shoulders, and don''t pull too hard on the shoulders joint. Switch sides.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulder relaxed and down','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Pulling hard on the joint','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_wrist_pull/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_Wrist_Pull/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'arnold_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'arnold_press', 'Arnold Press (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A dumbbell shoulder press that starts with palms facing you and rotates to palms forward as you press.', array['Sit on an upright bench holding dumbbells in front of your shoulders, palms facing you, elbows in front.']::text[], array['As you press up, open your elbows out to the sides and rotate the palms to face forward.','Finish with arms straight overhead.','Reverse the rotation as you lower back to the start.']::text[], array['Smooth rotation through the whole press','Keep the ribs down']::text[], array['Rotating fully before pressing','Using weights too heavy to control the rotation']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/arnold_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Arnold_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_arnold_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_arnold_press', 'Kettlebell Arnold Press', array['Arnold Press (Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Arnold Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the arnold press: kettlebells instead of dumbbells.', array['Clean a kettlebell to your shoulder. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you raise the kettlebell towards your shoulder. The palm should be facing inward.']::text[], array['Looking straight ahead, press the kettlebell out and overhead, rotating your wrist so that your palm faces forward at the top of the motion.','Return the kettlebell to the starting position, with the palm facing in.']::text[], array['Smooth rotation through the whole press','Keep the ribs down']::text[], array['Rotating fully before pressing','Using weights too heavy to control the rotation']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_arnold_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Arnold_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'band_pull_apart')::uuid, 'mfd', 'band_pull_apart', 'Band Pullaparts', array['band pull apart']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Pulling a band apart in front of your chest. A simple warm-up and shoulder-health exercise.', array['Hold a light band in front of your chest with straight arms, hands shoulder-width apart.']::text[], array['Pull the band apart until it touches your chest.','Return slowly to the start.']::text[], array['Arms stay straight','Shoulders down']::text[], array['Shrugging','Bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/band_pull_apart/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Band_Pull_Apart/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bear_crawl')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bear_crawl', 'Bear Crawl', '{}'::text[], 'cardio', 'distance_time', 'Crawling on hands and feet with the knees hovering just above the floor.', array['Start on hands and knees, then lift the knees a few centimetres.']::text[], array['Move the opposite hand and foot forward together.','Keep crawling for the set distance.']::text[], array['Back flat, hips low','Small steps']::text[], array['Hips high in the air']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_rear_delt_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_rear_delt_row', 'Barbell Rear Delt Row', array['Bent Over Row (Rear Delt)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Rear Delt Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps, lats and upper back. A variation of the bent over row: wide grip, bar to the upper chest, elbows out, for the rear delts.', array['Stand up straight while holding a barbell using a wide (higher than shoulder width) and overhand (palms facing your body) grip.']::text[], array['Bend knees slightly and bend over as you keep the natural arch of your back. Let the arms hang in front of you as they hold the bar. Once your torso is parallel to the floor, flare the elbows out and away from your body. Tip: Your torso and your arms should resemble the letter "T". Now you are ready to begin the exercise.','While keeping the upper arms perpendicular to the torso, pull the barbell up towards your upper chest as you squeeze the rear delts and you breathe out. Tip: When performed correctly, this exercise should resemble a bench press in reverse. Also, refrain from using your biceps to do the work. Focus on targeting the rear delts; the arms should only act as hooks.','Slowly go back to the initial position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_rear_delt_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Rear_Delt_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'car_drivers')::uuid, 'mfd', 'car_drivers', 'Car Drivers', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Car Drivers is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the forearms.', array['While standing upright, hold a barbell plate in both hands at the 3 and 9 o''clock positions. Your palms should be facing each other and your arms should be extended straight out in front of you. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Initiate the movement by rotating the plate as far to one side as possible. Use the same type of movement you would use to turn a steering wheel to one side.','Reverse the motion, turning it all the way to the opposite side.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Hold a plate at arm''s length in front at shoulder height','Turn it like a steering wheel','Arms stay straight and still']::text[], array['Dropping the arms','Shrugging']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/car_drivers/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Car_Drivers/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chair_upper_body_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chair_upper_body_stretch', 'Chair Upper Body Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Chair Upper Body Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps and chest.', '{}'::text[], array['Sit on the edge of a chair, gripping the back of it.','Straighten your arms, keeping your back straight, and pull your upper body forward so you feel a stretch. Hold for 20-30 seconds.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chair_upper_body_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chair_Upper_Body_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'round_the_world_shoulder_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'round_the_world_shoulder_stretch', 'Round The World Shoulder Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Round The World Shoulder Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps and chest.', array['Stand up straight with your legs together, holding a bodybar or broomstick.']::text[], array['Hold the pole behind your hips with a wider than shoulder width grip. Your palms should be down and your thumbs facing out.','Slowly lift your arms up behind your head. Don''t force it if it gets hard to lift further.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/round_the_world_shoulder_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Round_The_World_Shoulder_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_front_deltoid')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_front_deltoid', 'Seated Front Deltoid', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Seated Front Deltoid is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest.', array['Sit upright on the floor with your legs bent, your partner standing behind you. Stick your arms straight out to your sides, with your palms facing the ground. Attempt to move them as far behind you as possible, as your assistant holds your wrists. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping your elbows straight, attempt to move your arms to the front, with your partner gently restraining you to prevent any actual movement for 10-20 seconds.','Now, relax your muscles and allow your partner to gently increase the stretch on the shoulders and chest. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_front_deltoid/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Front_Deltoid/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shoulder_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shoulder_stretch', 'Shoulder Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Shoulder Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders.', '{}'::text[], array['Reach your left arm across your body and hold it straight.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shoulder_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Shoulder_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'upward_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'upward_stretch', 'Upward Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Upward Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest and lats.', '{}'::text[], array['Extend both hands straight above your head, palms touching.','Slowly push your hands up and back, keeping your back straight.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulders down away from the ears','Keep the ribs down; do not arch the back to fake the range','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Shrugging','Arching the lower back','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/upward_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Upward_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'crucifix')::uuid, 'mfd', 'crucifix', 'Crucifix', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'time', 'Crucifix is a beginner-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the forearms.', '{}'::text[], array['In the crucifix, you statically hold weights out to the side for time. While the event can be practiced using dumbbells, it is best to practice with one of the various implements used, such as axes and hammers, as it feels different.','Begin standing, and raise your arms out to the side holding the implements. Your arms should be parallel to the ground. In competition, judges or sensors are used to let you know when you break parallel. Hold for as long as you can. Typically, the weights should be heavy enough that you fail in 30-60 seconds.']::text[], array['Arms straight out to the sides','Shoulders down, core braced','Hold for time']::text[], array['Bending the elbows','Leaning back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/crucifix/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Crucifix/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cuban_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cuban_press', 'Cuban Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cuban Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the traps.', array['Take a dumbbell in each hand with a pronated grip in a standing position. Raise your upper arms so that they are parallel to the floor, allowing your lower arms to hang in the "scarecrow" position. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['To initiate the movement, externally rotate the shoulders to move the upper arm 180 degrees. Keep the upper arms in place, rotating the upper arms until the wrists are directly above the elbows, the forearms perpendicular to the floor.','Now press the dumbbells by extending at the elbows, straightening your arms overhead.','Return to the starting position as you breathe in by reversing the steps.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upright row to elbows at shoulder height','Rotate the forearms up','Press overhead, then reverse the steps']::text[], array['Using too much weight','Elbows dropping before the rotation']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cuban_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cuban_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'arm_circles')::uuid, 'mfd', 'arm_circles', 'Arm Circles', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Arm Circles is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the traps.', array['Stand up and extend your arms straight out by the sides. The arms should be parallel to the floor and perpendicular (90-degree angle) to your torso. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Slowly start to make circles of about 1 foot in diameter with each outstretched arm. Breathe normally as you perform the movement.','Continue the circular motion of the outstretched arms for about ten seconds. Then reverse the movement, going the opposite direction.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/arm_circles/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Arm_Circles/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'elbow_circles')::uuid, 'mfd', 'elbow_circles', 'Elbow Circles', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Elbow Circles is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the traps.', array['Sit or stand with your feet slightly apart.']::text[], array['Place your hands on your shoulders with your elbows at shoulder level and pointing out.','Slowly make a circle with your elbows. Breathe out as you start the circle and breathe in as you complete the circle.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/elbow_circles/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Elbow_Circles/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shoulder_circles')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shoulder_circles', 'Shoulder Circles', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Shoulder Circles is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the traps.', '{}'::text[], array['With shoulders relaxed and arms resting loosely at your sides (or in your lap if you''re seated), gently roll your shoulders forward, up, back, and down.','Reverse direction. You can do this exercise alternating shoulders or both at the same time.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shoulder_circles/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Shoulder_Circles/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shoulder_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shoulder_raise', 'Shoulder Raise', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Shoulder Raise is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the lats.', '{}'::text[], array['Relax your arms to your sides and raise your shoulders up toward your ears, then back down.']::text[], array['Start small and slow, then grow the range','Smooth, controlled movement, no flinging','About 8–12 reps per side as a warm-up']::text[], array['Swinging into end range with momentum','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shoulder_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_rope_rear_delt_rows')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_rope_rear_delt_rows', 'Cable Rope Rear-Delt Rows', array['Face Pull (Seated Rope Row)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Rope Rear-Delt Rows is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the face pull: seated, rope pulled to the neck with the elbows high.', array['Sit in the same position on a low pulley row station as you would if you were doing seated cable rows for the back.']::text[], array['Attach a rope to the pulley and grasp it with an overhand grip. Your arms should be extended and parallel to the floor with the elbows flared out.','Keep your lower back upright and slide your hips back so that your knees are slightly bent. This will be your starting position.','Pull the cable attachment towards your upper chest, just below the neck, as you keep your elbows up and out to the sides. Continue this motion as you exhale until the elbows travel slightly behind the back. Tip: Keep your upper arms horizontal, perpendicular to the torso and parallel to the floor throughout the motion.','Go back to the initial position where the arms are extended and the shoulders are stretched forward. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows high and wide','Pull the ends apart','Finish like a "double biceps" pose']::text[], array['Leaning back to pull heavy weight','Letting the elbows drop']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_rope_rear_delt_rows/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Rope_Rear-Delt_Rows/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'face_pull')::uuid, 'mfd', 'face_pull', 'Face Pull', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pulling a rope toward your face with the elbows high. Trains the rear delts and rotator cuff and supports shoulder health.', array['Set a pulley at upper-chest to face height with a rope attachment.','Grip the rope with palms facing each other or down and step back.']::text[], array['Pull the rope toward your face, splitting the ends apart.','Finish with hands beside your ears and elbows high, rotating the forearms up.','Return slowly.']::text[], array['Elbows high and wide','Pull the ends apart','Finish like a "double biceps" pose']::text[], array['Leaning back to pull heavy weight','Letting the elbows drop']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/face_pull/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Face_Pull/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'low_pulley_row_to_neck')::uuid, 'mfd', 'low_pulley_row_to_neck', 'Low Pulley Row To Neck', array['Face Pull (Low Pulley to Neck)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Low Pulley Row To Neck is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps, upper back and traps. A variation of the face pull: seated at a low pulley, pulling to the neck with the elbows high.', array['Sit on a low pulley row machine with a rope attachment.']::text[], array['Grab the ends of the rope using a palms-down grip and sit with your back straight and your knees slightly bent. Tip: Keep your back almost completely vertical and your arms fully extended in front of you. This will be your starting position.','While keeping your torso stationary, lift your elbows and start bending them as you pull the rope towards your neck while exhaling. Throughout the movement your upper arms should remain parallel to the floor. Tip: Continue this motion until your hands are almost next to your ears (the forearms will not be parallel to the floor at the end of the movement as they will be angled a bit upwards) and your elbows are out away from your sides.','After holding for a second or so at the contracted position, come back slowly to the starting position as you inhale. Tip: Again, during no part of the movement should the torso move.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows high and wide','Pull the ends apart','Finish like a "double biceps" pose']::text[], array['Leaning back to pull heavy weight','Letting the elbows drop']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/low_pulley_row_to_neck/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Low_Pulley_Row_To_Neck/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_scaption')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_scaption', 'Dumbbell Scaption', array['Front Raise (Scaption)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Scaption is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the traps. A variation of the front raise: raised at 30 degrees out from the front, thumbs up, in the shoulder blade plane.', array['This corrective exercise strengthens the muscles that stabilize your shoulder blade. Hold a light weight in each hand, hanging at your sides. Your thumbs should pointing up.']::text[], array['Begin the movement raising your arms out in front of you, about 30 degrees off center. Your arms should be fully extended as you perform the movement.','Continue until your arms are parallel to the ground, and then return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_scaption/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Scaption/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_incline_dumbbell_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_incline_dumbbell_raise', 'Front Incline Dumbbell Raise', array['Front Raise (Incline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Front Incline Dumbbell Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the front raise: lying back on an incline bench, which starts the raise behind the body.', array['Sit down on an incline bench with the incline set anywhere between 30 to 60 degrees while holding a dumbbell on each hand. Tip: You can change the angle to hit the muscle a little differently each time.']::text[], array['Extend your arms straight in front of you and have your palms facing down with the dumbbells raised about 1 inch above your thighs. This will be your starting position.','Slowly raise the dumbbells straight up until they are slightly above your shoulders, while keeping your elbows locked. Squeeze at the top for a second and make sure you breathe out during this portion of the movement. Tip: Keep your head resting down against the bench and your legs on the floor at all times.','Lower the arms back to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_incline_dumbbell_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Incline_Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_raise_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_raise_band', 'Front Raise (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising a weight straight in front of you to shoulder height to target the front of the shoulders.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs.','Keep a small bend in the elbows.']::text[], array['Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height.','Pause briefly.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_raise_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_raise_barbell', 'Front Raise (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising a weight straight in front of you to shoulder height to target the front of the shoulders.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs.','Keep a small bend in the elbows.']::text[], array['Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height.','Pause briefly.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_raise_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_raise_cable', 'Front Raise (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising a weight straight in front of you to shoulder height to target the front of the shoulders.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs.','Keep a small bend in the elbows.']::text[], array['Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height.','Pause briefly.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_raise_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Cable_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_raise_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_raise_dumbbell', 'Front Raise (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising a weight straight in front of you to shoulder height to target the front of the shoulders.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs.','Keep a small bend in the elbows.']::text[], array['Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height.','Pause briefly.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_raise_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_raise_suspension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_raise_suspension', 'Front Raise (Suspension)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Raising a weight straight in front of you to shoulder height to target the front of the shoulders.', array['Face away from the anchor holding the handles at your hips, leaning forward.']::text[], array['Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height.','Pause briefly.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'front_raise_plate')::uuid, 'mfd', 'front_raise_plate', 'Plate Front Raise', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising a weight straight in front of you to shoulder height to target the front of the shoulders.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs.','Keep a small bend in the elbows.']::text[], array['Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height.','Pause briefly.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/front_raise_plate/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Front_Plate_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_dumbbell_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_dumbbell_raise', 'Single Dumbbell Raise', array['Front Raise (Single Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Single Dumbbell Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the forearms and traps. A variation of the front raise: one dumbbell held in both hands.', array['With a wide stance, hold a dumbell with both hands, grasping the head of the dumbbell instead of the handle. Your arms should be extended and hanging at the waist. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Raise the weight until it is above shoulder level, keeping your arms extended. Your torso and hips should remain stationary throughout the movement.','Return to the starting position and repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_dumbbell_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single_Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_dumbbell_straight_arm_front_delt_raise_above_head')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_dumbbell_straight_arm_front_delt_raise_above_head', 'Standing Dumbbell Straight-Arm Front Delt Raise Above Head', array['Front Raise (To Overhead)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Dumbbell Straight-Arm Front Delt Raise Above Head is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the front raise: raised all the way above the head.', array['Hold the dumbbells in front of your thighs, palms facing your thighs.']::text[], array['Keep your arms straight with a slight bend at the elbows but keep them locked. This will be your starting position.','Raise the dumbbells in a semicircular motion to arm''s length overhead as you exhale.','Slowly return to the starting position using the same path as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_dumbbell_straight_arm_front_delt_raise_above_head/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Straight-Arm_Front_Delt_Raise_Above_Head/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_front_barbell_raise_over_head')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_front_barbell_raise_over_head', 'Standing Front Barbell Raise Over Head', array['Front Raise (Barbell, To Overhead)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Front Barbell Raise Over Head is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the front raise: barbell raised all the way above the head.', array['To begin, stand straight with a barbell in your hands. You should grip the bar with palms facing down and a closer than shoulder width grip apart from each other.']::text[], array['Your feet should be shoulder width apart from each other. Your elbows should be slightly bent. This is the starting position.','Lift the barbell up until it is directly over your head while exhaling. Make sure to keep your elbows slightly bent when performing each repetition.','Once you feel the contraction, begin to lower the barbell back down to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Stop at shoulder height','Do not lean back']::text[], array['Swinging with the hips','Lifting well above head height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_front_barbell_raise_over_head/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Front_Barbell_Raise_Over_Head/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'handstand_hold')::uuid, 'mfd', 'handstand_hold', 'Handstand Hold', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'time', 'Holding a handstand, free-standing or against a wall, to build shoulder strength and balance.', array['Warm up your wrists.','Place your hands shoulder-width apart on the floor, about a hand-length from a wall if using one.']::text[], array['Kick up into a handstand.','Push the floor away and squeeze your legs together.','Hold for the target time, then come down with control.']::text[], array['Push tall through the shoulders','Ribs in, body in one line']::text[], array['Banana-shaped back','Letting the shoulders collapse']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'handstand_push_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'handstand_push_up', 'Handstand Push Up', array['hspu']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A vertical push up upside down, usually with your feet against a wall. It needs strong shoulders and good balance.', array['Kick up into a handstand facing a wall, hands about shoulder-width and 10–20 cm from the wall.','Body straight, core tight.']::text[], array['Lower your head slowly toward the floor until it lightly touches (use a pad).','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Make a tripod: head slightly in front of the hands','Keep the core tight so the back does not arch']::text[], array['Crashing onto the head','Over-arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/handstand_push_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Handstand_Push-Ups/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_incline_shoulder_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_incline_shoulder_raise', 'Barbell Incline Shoulder Raise', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Incline Shoulder Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest.', array['Lie back on an Incline Bench. Using a medium width grip (a grip that is slightly wider than shoulder width), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms straight. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['While keeping the arms straight, lift the bar by protracting your shoulder blades, raising the shoulders from the bench as you breathe out.','Bring back the bar to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Arms stay straight the whole time','Push the weight up by spreading the shoulder blades','Small, controlled range']::text[], array['Bending the elbows','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_incline_shoulder_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Incline_Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_incline_shoulder_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_incline_shoulder_raise', 'Dumbbell Incline Shoulder Raise', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Incline Shoulder Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps.', array['Sit on an Incline Bench while holding a dumbbell on each hand on top of your thighs.']::text[], array['Lift your legs up to kick the weights to your shoulders and lean back. Position the dumbbells above your shoulders with your arms extended. The arms should be perpendicular to the floor with your palms facing forward and knuckles pointing towards the ceiling. This will be your starting position.','While keeping the arms straight and locked, lift the dumbbells by raising the shoulders from the bench as you breathe out.','Bring back the dumbbells to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Arms stay straight the whole time','Push the weight up by spreading the shoulder blades','Small, controlled range']::text[], array['Bending the elbows','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_incline_shoulder_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Incline_Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_incline_shoulder_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_incline_shoulder_raise', 'Smith Incline Shoulder Raise', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Incline Shoulder Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest.', array['Place an incline bench underneath the smith machine. Place the barbell at a height that you can reach when lying down and your arms are almost fully extended. Once the weight you need is selected, lie down on the incline bench and make sure your shoulders are aligned right under the barbell.']::text[], array['Using a shoulder width pronated (palms forward) grip, lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with a slight bend at the elbows. This will be your starting position.','As you breathe out, lift the bar up until your arms are fully extended. Note: The contraction should be felt around the shoulders.','After a second pause, bring the bar back down to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.']::text[], array['Arms stay straight the whole time','Push the weight up by spreading the shoulder blades','Small, controlled range']::text[], array['Bending the elbows','Using too much weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_incline_shoulder_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Incline_Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'iron_cross')::uuid, 'mfd', 'iron_cross', 'Iron Cross', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Iron Cross is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, quadriceps and traps.', array['Stand with feet shoulder-width apart, holding a light dumbbell in each hand with arms straight out in front at shoulder height.']::text[], array['Keeping the arms straight out in front, sit down into a squat until your thighs are about parallel to the floor.','Drive back up to standing and, as you rise, sweep the arms out to the sides until they form a T at shoulder height.','Bring the arms back to the front and repeat, keeping the elbows soft and the shoulders down.']::text[], array['Arms stay straight at shoulder height','Squat with the dumbbells out in front','Stand and open the arms to the sides']::text[], array['Dropping the arms','Rounding the back in the squat']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/iron_cross/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Iron_Cross/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'two_arm_kettlebell_clean')::uuid, 'mfd', 'two_arm_kettlebell_clean', 'Two-Arm Kettlebell Clean', array['Kettlebell Clean (Two Arms)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Two-Arm Kettlebell Clean is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, glutes, hamstrings, lower back and traps. A variation of the kettlebell clean: one kettlebell held by both hands.', array['Place two kettlebells between your feet. To get in the starting position, push your butt back and look straight ahead.']::text[], array['Clean the kettlebells to your shoulders by extending through the legs and hips as you raise the kettlebells towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrists as you do so.','Lower the kettlebells back to the starting position and repeat.']::text[], array['Keep the bell close; zip up the jacket','Do not let it flip onto the forearm']::text[], array['Swinging it wide and letting it bang the wrist']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/two_arm_kettlebell_clean/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_halo')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_halo', 'Kettlebell Halo', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'weight_reps', 'Circling a kettlebell around your head. Warms up the shoulders and improves their range of motion.', array['Stand tall holding a kettlebell upside down by the horns at chest height.']::text[], array['Circle the kettlebell around your head, keeping it close.','Return to the front and reverse the direction.']::text[], array['Keep it close to your head and neck','Ribs down; do not arch']::text[], array['Moving the head instead of the bell','Using a bell that is too heavy']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_halo_with_overhead_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_halo_with_overhead_extension', 'Kettlebell Halo with Overhead Extension', array['Kettlebell Halo (With Overhead Press)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Halo with Overhead Extension is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders and triceps, with help from the traps, upper back and abs & core. A variation of the kettlebell halo: adds a press overhead after each circle.', array['Stand tall with your feet hip-width apart. Hold a kettlebell upside down by the horns, with the bell above your hands and close to your chest. Brace your abdominals and squeeze your glutes so your ribcage stays down. This is your starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping your elbows close to your head, move the kettlebell up past one ear and around until it sits behind your head. Pause here.','From this position, extend your elbows to press the kettlebell up and overhead until your arms are straight, keeping your upper arms alongside your head.','Bend your elbows to lower the kettlebell back to the pause position behind your head, under control.','Continue the circle past the opposite ear and back down to the starting position in front of your chest to complete one repetition.','Alternate the direction of the circle on each repetition. Keep your head, hips and lower back still throughout; if your lower back arches or you cannot reach the overhead position without leaning back, use a lighter weight or perform the halo and the extension as separate exercises.']::text[], array['Keep it close to your head and neck','Ribs down; do not arch']::text[], array['Moving the head instead of the bell','Using a bell that is too heavy']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'double_kettlebell_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'double_kettlebell_jerk', 'Double Kettlebell Jerk', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Double Kettlebell Jerk is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, quadriceps and triceps.', array['Hold a kettlebell by the handle in each hand.']::text[], array['Clean the kettlebells to your shoulders by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebells towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrists as you do so, so that the palms face forward. This will be your starting position.','Dip your body by bending the knees, keeping your torso upright.','Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum.','As you do so, press the kettlebells overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using your body''s momentum to move the weights.','Return your feet to the ground in a split fashion, with one foot forward and one foot back.','Keeping the weights overhead, return to a standing position, bringing your feet together. Lower the weights to perform the next repetition.']::text[], array['Short, quick dip with the torso upright','Drive the bell up with the legs, then drop under it','Lock the arm out before standing up']::text[], array['Pressing with the shoulder instead of using the legs','Leaning back','Bending the elbow at lockout']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/double_kettlebell_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_clean_and_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_clean_and_jerk', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Clean and Jerk', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Clean and Jerk is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders.', array['Hold a kettlebell by the handle.']::text[], array['Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulder. Rotate your wrist as you do so, so that the palm faces forward.','Dip your body by bending the knees, keeping your torso upright.','Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using your body''s momentum to move the weight.','Receive the weight overhead by returning to a squat position underneath the weight.','Keeping the weight overhead, return to a standing position. Lower the weight to the floor to perform the next repetition.']::text[], array['Short, quick dip with the torso upright','Drive the bell up with the legs, then drop under it','Lock the arm out before standing up']::text[], array['Pressing with the shoulder instead of using the legs','Leaning back','Bending the elbow at lockout']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_clean_and_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Clean_and_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_jerk', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Jerk', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Jerk is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, quadriceps and triceps.', array['Hold a kettlebell by the handle. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulder. Rotate your wrist as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Dip your body by bending the knees, keeping your torso upright.','Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using your body''s momentum to move the weight. Receive the weight overhead by returning to a squat position underneath the weight. Keeping the weight overhead, return to a standing position.','Lower the weight to perform the next repetition.']::text[], array['Short, quick dip with the torso upright','Drive the bell up with the legs, then drop under it','Lock the arm out before standing up']::text[], array['Pressing with the shoulder instead of using the legs','Leaning back','Bending the elbow at lockout']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_split_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_split_jerk', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Split Jerk', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Split Jerk is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the glutes, hamstrings, quadriceps and triceps.', array['Hold a kettlebell by the handle. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulder. Rotate your wrist as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Dip your body by bending the knees, keeping your torso upright.','Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using your body''s momentum to move the weight.','Receive the weight overhead by returning to a squat position underneath the weight, positioning one leg in front of you and one leg behind you.','Keeping the weight overhead, return to a standing position and bring your feet together. Lower the weight to perform the next repetition.']::text[], array['Short, quick dip with the torso upright','Drive the bell up with the legs, then drop under it','Lock the arm out before standing up']::text[], array['Pressing with the shoulder instead of using the legs','Leaning back','Bending the elbow at lockout']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_split_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Split_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'two_arm_kettlebell_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'two_arm_kettlebell_jerk', 'Two-Arm Kettlebell Jerk', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Two-Arm Kettlebell Jerk is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, quadriceps and triceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Clean two kettlebells to your shoulders. Clean the kettlebells to your shoulders by extending through the legs and hips as you swing the kettlebells towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrists as you do so, so that the palms face forward. Squat down a few inches and reverse the motion rapidly driving both kettlebells overhead. Immediately after the initial push, squat down again and get under the kettlebells. Once the kettlebells are locked out, stand upright to complete the exercise.']::text[], array['Short, quick dip with the torso upright','Drive the bell up with the legs, then drop under it','Lock the arm out before standing up']::text[], array['Pressing with the shoulder instead of using the legs','Leaning back','Bending the elbow at lockout']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/two_arm_kettlebell_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_pirate_ships')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_pirate_ships', 'Kettlebell Pirate Ships', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Pirate Ships is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the abs & core.', array['With a wide stance, hold a kettlebell with both hands. Allow it to hang at waist level with your arms extended. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Initiate the movement by turning to one side, swinging the kettlebell to head height. Briefly pause at the top of the motion.','Allow the bell to drop as you rotate to the opposite side, again raising the kettlebell to head height.','Repeat for the desired amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Kettlebell held by the horns at arm''s length','Swing it side to side in an arc overhead','Hips and legs stay still']::text[], array['Bending the arms','Twisting the hips']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_pirate_ships/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Pirate_Ships/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'double_kettlebell_snatch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'double_kettlebell_snatch', 'Double Kettlebell Snatch', array['Kettlebell Snatch (Double)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Double Kettlebell Snatch is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the glutes, hamstrings and quadriceps. A variation of the kettlebell snatch: two kettlebells.', array['Place two kettlebells behind your feet. Bend your knees and sit back to pick up the kettlebells.']::text[], array['Swing the kettlebells between your legs forcefully and reverse the direction.','Drive through with your hips and lock the ketttlebells overhead in one uninterrupted motion.']::text[], array['Punch through so the bell does not crash on the forearm']::text[], array['Letting the bell flip over']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/double_kettlebell_snatch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_split_snatch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_split_snatch', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Split Snatch', array['Kettlebell Snatch (Split)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Split Snatch is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the hamstrings and quadriceps. A variation of the kettlebell snatch: caught in a split stance.', array['Hold a kettlebell in one hand by the handle.']::text[], array['Squat towards the floor, and then reverse the motion, extending the hips, knees, and finally the ankles, to raise the kettlebell overhead.','After fully extending the body, descend into a lunge position to receive the weights overhead, one leg forward and one leg back. Ensure you drive through with your hips and lock the ketttlebells overhead in one uninterrupted motion.','Return to a standing position, holding the weight overhead, and bring the feet together. Lower the weight to return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Punch through so the bell does not crash on the forearm']::text[], array['Letting the bell flip over']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_split_snatch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Split_Snatch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'turkish_get_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'turkish_get_up', 'Kettlebell Turkish Get Up', array['turkish get up','tgu']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Getting up from lying to standing while holding a kettlebell straight overhead, then reversing the steps.', array['Lie on your back holding the kettlebell straight above your shoulder.','Bend the same-side knee with the foot flat.']::text[], array['Roll to the opposite elbow, then hand.','Lift the hips into a bridge and sweep the straight leg back under you to a kneel.','Stand up from the lunge.','Reverse every step back to lying.']::text[], array['Eyes on the bell','Arm stays vertical and locked']::text[], array['Rushing the transitions','Letting the arm drift']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/turkish_get_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Turkish_Get-Up_Squat_style/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternating_deltoid_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternating_deltoid_raise', 'Alternating Deltoid Raise', array['Lateral Raise (Front and Side)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating Deltoid Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the lateral raise: one arm raises to the front while the other raises to the side, then swap.', array['In a standing position, hold a pair of dumbbells at your side.']::text[], array['Keeping your elbows slightly bent, raise the weights directly in front of you to shoulder height, avoiding any swinging or cheating.','Return the weights to your side.','On the next repetition, raise the weights laterally, raising them out to your side to about shoulder height.','Return the weights to the starting position and continue alternating to the front and side.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternating_deltoid_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternating_Deltoid_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_seated_lateral_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_seated_lateral_raise', 'Cable Seated Lateral Raise', array['Lateral Raise (Cable, Seated)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Seated Lateral Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the upper back and traps. A variation of the lateral raise: seated beside a low pulley.', array['Stand in the middle of two low pulleys that are opposite to each other and place a flat bench right behind you (in perpendicular fashion to you; the narrow edge of the bench should be the one behind you). Select the weight to be used on each pulley.']::text[], array['Now sit at the edge of the flat bench behind you with your feet placed in front of your knees.','Bend forward while keeping your back flat and rest your torso on the thighs.','Have someone give you the single handles attached to the pulleys. Grasp the left pulley with the right hand and the right pulley with the left after you select your weight. The pulleys should run under your knees and your arms will be extended with palms facing each other and a slight bend at the elbows. This will be the starting position.','While keeping the arms stationary, raise the upper arms to the sides until they are parallel to the floor and at shoulder height. Exhale during the execution of this movement and hold the contraction for a second.','Slowly lower your arms to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions. Tip: Maintain upper arms perpendicular to torso and a fixed elbow position (10 degree to 30 degree angle) throughout exercise.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_seated_lateral_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Seated_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_raise', 'Dumbbell Raise', array['Lateral Raise (Palms Back)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps. A variation of the lateral raise: starts with the dumbbells beside the thighs and palms facing back.', array['Grab a dumbbell in each arm and stand up straight with your arms extended by your sides with a slight bend at the elbows and your back straight. This will be your starting position. Tip: The dumbbell should be next to your thighs with the palm of your hands facing back.']::text[], array['Use your side shoulders to lift the dumbbells as you exhale. The dumbbells should be to the side of the body as you move them up. Continue to lift it until the dumbbells are nearly in line with your chin. Tip: Your elbows should drive the motion. As you lift the dumbbell, your elbow should always be higher than your forearm. Also, keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.','Lower the dumbbells back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_raise_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_raise_band', 'Lateral Raise (Band)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms out to the sides to shoulder height. The key exercise for wider-looking shoulders.', array['Stand on the middle of the band and hold an end in each hand.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height.','Lead with the elbows, keeping the hands slightly lower than or level with the elbows.','Lower slowly back to your sides.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lateral_raise_band/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lateral_Raise_-_With_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_raise_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_raise_cable', 'Lateral Raise (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms out to the sides to shoulder height. The key exercise for wider-looking shoulders.', array['Set a pulley at the lowest position with a single handle.','Stand side-on and hold the handle with the far hand.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height.','Lead with the elbows, keeping the hands slightly lower than or level with the elbows.','Lower slowly back to your sides.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_raise_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_raise_dumbbell', 'Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', array['side raise','side lateral raise','db lateral raise']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms out to the sides to shoulder height. The key exercise for wider-looking shoulders.', array['Stand tall with the weights at your sides, palms facing in.','Bend the elbows slightly and lean forward a little.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height.','Lead with the elbows, keeping the hands slightly lower than or level with the elbows.','Lower slowly back to your sides.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lateral_raise_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_raise_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_raise_machine', 'Lateral Raise (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms out to the sides to shoulder height. The key exercise for wider-looking shoulders.', array['Adjust the seat so your shoulders line up with the machine pivot.','Place your arms against the pads.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height.','Lead with the elbows, keeping the hands slightly lower than or level with the elbows.','Lower slowly back to your sides.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_one_arm_lateral_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_one_arm_lateral_raise', 'Lying One-Arm Lateral Raise', array['Lateral Raise (Lying Side)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying One-Arm Lateral Raise is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the lateral raise: lying on your side on a bench; tension is highest at the bottom.', array['While holding a dumbbell in one hand, lay with your chest down on a flat bench. The other hand can be used to hold to the leg of the bench for stability.']::text[], array['Position the palm of the hand that is holding the dumbbell in a neutral manner (palms facing your torso) as you keep the arm extended with the elbow slightly bent. This will be your starting position.','Now raise the arm with the dumbbell to the side until your elbow is at shoulder height and your arm is roughly parallel to the floor as you exhale. Tip: Maintain your arm perpendicular to the torso while keeping your arm extended throughout the movement. Also, keep the contraction at the top for a second.','Slowly lower the dumbbell to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_one_arm_lateral_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_One-Arm_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_incline_lateral_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_incline_lateral_raise', 'One-Arm Incline Lateral Raise', array['Lateral Raise (Incline Side)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Incline Lateral Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the lateral raise: lying sideways on an incline bench.', array['Lie down sideways on an incline bench press with a dumbbell in the hand. Make sure the shoulder is pressing against the incline bench and the arm is lying across your body with the palm around your navel.']::text[], array['Hold a dumbbell in your uppermost arm while keeping it extended in front of you parallel to the floor. This is your starting position.','While keeping the dumbbell parallel to the floor at all times, perform a lateral raise. Your arm should travel straight up until it is pointing at the ceiling. Tip: Exhale as you perform this movement. Hold the dumbbell in the position and feel the contraction in the shoulders for a second.','While inhaling lower the weight across your body back into the starting position.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_incline_lateral_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Incline_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_side_laterals')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_side_laterals', 'One-Arm Side Laterals', array['Lateral Raise (Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Side Laterals is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the lateral raise: one arm at a time, holding a support with the other.', array['Pick a dumbbell and place it in one of your hands. Your non lifting hand should be used to grab something steady such as an incline bench press. Lean towards your lifting arm and away from the hand that is gripping the incline bench as this will allow you to keep your balance.']::text[], array['Stand with a straight torso and have the dumbbell by your side at arm''s length with the palm of the hand facing you. This will be your starting position.','While maintaining the torso stationary (no swinging), lift the dumbbell to your side with a slight bend on the elbow and your hand slightly tilted forward as if pouring water in a glass. Continue to go up until you arm is parallel to the floor. Exhale as you execute this movement and pause for a second at the top.','Lower the dumbbell back down slowly to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the exercise.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_side_laterals/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Side_Laterals/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'power_partials')::uuid, 'mfd', 'power_partials', 'Power Partials', array['Lateral Raise (Partials)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Power Partials is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the lateral raise: short, fast lateral raises from the bottom of the range.', array['Stand up with your torso upright and a dumbbell on each hand being held at arms length. The elbows should be close to the torso.']::text[], array['The palms of the hands should be facing your torso. Your feet should be about shoulder width apart. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your arms straight and the torso stationary, lift the weights out to your sides until they are about shoulder level height while exhaling.','Feel the contraction for a second and begin to lower the weights back down to the starting position while inhaling. Tip: Keep the palms facing down with the little finger slightly higher while lifting and lowering the weights as it will concentrate the stress on your shoulders mainly.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/power_partials/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Power_Partials/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_raise_seated_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_raise_seated_dumbbell', 'Seated Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms out to the sides to shoulder height. The key exercise for wider-looking shoulders.', array['Stand tall with the weights at your sides, palms facing in.','Bend the elbows slightly and lean forward a little.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height.','Lead with the elbows, keeping the hands slightly lower than or level with the elbows.','Lower slowly back to your sides.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lateral_raise_seated_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Side_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'side_laterals_to_front_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'side_laterals_to_front_raise', 'Side Laterals to Front Raise', array['Lateral Raise (Side to Front)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Side Laterals to Front Raise is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the traps. A variation of the lateral raise: raise to the side, bring the arms to the front at shoulder height, then lower.', array['In a standing position, hold a pair of dumbbells at your side. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping your elbows slightly bent, raise the weights directly in front of you to shoulder height, avoiding any swinging or cheating.','At the top of the exercise move the weights out in front of you, keeping your arms extended.','Lower the weights with a controlled motion.','On the next repetition, raise the weights in front of you to shoulder height before moving the weights laterally to your sides.','Lower the weights to the starting position.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/side_laterals_to_front_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Side_Laterals_to_Front_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lateral_raise_single_arm_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lateral_raise_single_arm_cable', 'Single Arm Lateral Raise (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms out to the sides to shoulder height. The key exercise for wider-looking shoulders.', array['Stand tall with the weights at your sides, palms facing in.','Bend the elbows slightly and lean forward a little.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height.','Lead with the elbows, keeping the hands slightly lower than or level with the elbows.','Lower slowly back to your sides.']::text[], array['Think "push the weight out", not up','Shoulders stay down, away from the ears','Slow on the way down']::text[], array['Swinging the body to lift the weight','Shrugging the traps up','Raising well above shoulder height']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lateral_raise_single_arm_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Low-Pulley_Deltoid_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'backward_medicine_ball_throw')::uuid, 'mfd', 'backward_medicine_ball_throw', 'Backward Medicine Ball Throw', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Backward Medicine Ball Throw is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the shoulders.', array['This exercise is best done with a partner. If you lack a partner, the ball can be thrown and retrieved or thrown against a wall.']::text[], array['Begin standing a few meters in front of your partner, both facing the same direction. Begin holding the ball between your legs.','Squat down and then forcefully reverse direction, coming to full extension and you toss the ball over your head to your partner.','Your partner can then roll the ball back to you. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/backward_medicine_ball_throw/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Backward_Medicine_Ball_Throw/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'medicine_ball_scoop_throw')::uuid, 'mfd', 'medicine_ball_scoop_throw', 'Medicine Ball Scoop Throw', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Medicine Ball Scoop Throw is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the abs & core, hamstrings and quadriceps.', array['Assume a semisquat stance with a medicine ball in your hands. Your arms should hang so the ball is near your feet.']::text[], array['Begin by thrusting the hips forward as you extend through the legs, jumping up.','As you do, swing your arms up and over your head, keeping them extended, releasing the ball at the peak of your movement. The goal is to throw the ball the greatest distance behind you.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/medicine_ball_scoop_throw/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Medicine_Ball_Scoop_Throw/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'return_push_from_stance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'return_push_from_stance', 'Return Push from Stance', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Return Push from Stance is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest and triceps.', array['You will need a partner for this drill.']::text[], array['Begin in an athletic 2 or 3 point stance.','At the signal, move into a position to receive the pass from your partner.','Catch the medicine ball with both hands and immediately throw it back to your partner.','You can modify this drill by running different routes.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/return_push_from_stance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Return_Push_from_Stance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_two_arm_overhead_throw')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_two_arm_overhead_throw', 'Standing Two-Arm Overhead Throw', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Two-Arm Overhead Throw is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest and lats.', array['Stand with your feet shoulder width apart holding a medicine ball in both hands. To begin, reach the medicine ball deep behind your head as you bend the knees slightly and lean back.']::text[], array['Violently throw the ball forward, flexing at the hip and using your whole body to complete the movement.','The medicine ball can be thrown to a partner or to a wall, receiving it as it bounces back.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_two_arm_overhead_throw/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Two-Arm_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_plate_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_plate_raise', 'Overhead Plate Raise', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A front raise that continues all the way overhead, holding a plate with both hands.', array['Stand tall holding a plate at the sides in front of your thighs.']::text[], array['Raise the plate in front of you with straight arms until it is overhead.','Lower slowly back to your thighs.']::text[], array['Ribs down at the top','Smooth and controlled']::text[], array['Arching the lower back to get overhead','Swinging']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternating_cable_shoulder_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternating_cable_shoulder_press', 'Alternating Cable Shoulder Press', array['Overhead Press (Cable, Alternating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating Cable Shoulder Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: two cable handles pressed one at a time.', array['Move the cables to the bottom of the tower and select an appropriate weight.']::text[], array['Grasp the cables and hold them at shoulder height, palms facing forward. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your head and chest up, extend through the elbow to press one side directly over head.','After pausing at the top, return to the starting position and repeat on the opposite side.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternating_cable_shoulder_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternating_Cable_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternating_kettlebell_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternating_kettlebell_press', 'Alternating Kettlebell Press', array['Overhead Press (Kettlebell, Alternating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating Kettlebell Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: two kettlebells pressed one at a time from the rack position.', array['Clean two kettlebells to your shoulders. Clean the kettlebells to your shoulders by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebells towards your shoulders. Rotate your wrists as you do so.']::text[], array['Press one directly overhead by extending through the elbow, turning it so the palm faces forward while holding the other kettlebell stationary .','Lower the pressed kettlebell to the starting position and immediately press with your other arm.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternating_kettlebell_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternating_Kettlebell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bradford_rocky_presses')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bradford_rocky_presses', 'Bradford/Rocky Presses', array['Overhead Press (Bradford)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bradford/Rocky Presses is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: bar passes over the head from front to back, never locking out.', array['Sit on a Military Press Bench with a bar at shoulder level with a pronated grip (palms facing forward). Tip: Your grip should be wider than shoulder width and it should create a 90-degree angle between the forearm and the upper arm as the barbell goes down. This is your starting position.']::text[], array['Once you pick up the barbell with the correct grip, lift the bar up over your head by locking your arms.','Now lower the bar down to the back of the head slowly as you inhale.','Lift the bar back up to the starting position as you exhale.','Lower the bar down to the starting position slowly as you inhale. This is one repetition.','Alternate in this manner until you complete the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bradford_rocky_presses/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bradford_Rocky_Presses/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_shoulder_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_shoulder_press', 'Cable Shoulder Press', array['Overhead Press (Cable)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Shoulder Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: two low cable handles pressed overhead.', array['Move the cables to the bottom of the towers and select an appropriate weight.']::text[], array['Stand directly in between the uprights. Grasp the cables and hold them at shoulder height, palms facing forward. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your head and chest up, extend through the elbow to press the handles directly over head.','After pausing at the top, return to the starting position and repeat.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_shoulder_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_one_arm_shoulder_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_one_arm_shoulder_press', 'Dumbbell One-Arm Shoulder Press', array['Overhead Press (Single Arm Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell One-Arm Shoulder Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: one dumbbell; the core resists leaning.', array['Grab a dumbbell and either sit on a military press bench or a utility bench that has a back support on it as you place the dumbbells upright on top of your thighs or stand up straight.']::text[], array['Clean the dumbbell up to bring it to shoulder height. The other hand can be kept fully extended to the side, by the waist or grabbing a fixed surface.','Rotate the wrist so that the palm of your hand is facing forward. This is your starting position.','As you exhale, push the dumbbell up until your arm is fully extended.','After a second pause, slowly come down back to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and then switch arms.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_one_arm_shoulder_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_One-Arm_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_seated_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_seated_press', 'Kettlebell Seated Press', array['Overhead Press (Kettlebell, Seated)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Seated Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: seated on the floor, which removes the leg drive.', array['Sit on the floor and spread your legs out comfortably.']::text[], array['Clean one kettlebell to your shoulder.','Press the kettlebell up and out until it is locked out overhead. Return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_seated_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Seated_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_seesaw_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_seesaw_press', 'Kettlebell Seesaw Press', array['Overhead Press (Kettlebell, Seesaw)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Seesaw Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: one arm lowers as the other presses.', array['Clean two kettlebells two your shoulders.']::text[], array['Press one kettlebell.','Lower the kettlebell and immediately press the other kettlebell. Make sure to do the same amount of reps on both sides.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kettlebell_seesaw_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Seesaw_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_kettlebell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_kettlebell', 'Kettlebell Shoulder Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Clean the kettlebell to the rack position: handle in your palm, bell resting on the outside of your forearm.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_kettlebell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Military_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_military_press_to_the_side')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_military_press_to_the_side', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Military Press To The Side', array['Overhead Press (Kettlebell, Single Arm Side)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Military Press To The Side is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: single kettlebell pressed with a slight lean away from it.', array['Clean a kettlebell to your shoulder. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulder. Rotate your wrist as you do so, so that the palm faces inward. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Look at the kettlebell and press it up and out until it is locked out overhead.','Lower the kettlebell back to your shoulder under control and repeat. Make sure to contract your lat, butt, and stomach forcefully for added stability and strength.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_military_press_to_the_side/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Military_Press_To_The_Side/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_para_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_para_press', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Para Press', array['Overhead Press (Kettlebell, Para Press)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Para Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: starts with the elbow out to the side at shoulder height.', array['Clean a kettlebell to your shoulder. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulder. Rotate your wrist as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Hold the kettlebell with the elbow out to the side, and press it up and out until it is locked out overhead.','Lower the kettlebell back to your shoulder under control and repeat. Make sure to contract your lat, butt, and stomach forcefully for added stability and strength.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_para_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Para_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_barbell', 'Overhead Press (Barbell)', array['ohp','shoulder press','press','barbell overhead press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart and the weight at shoulder height.','Grip just outside shoulder width with wrists straight and elbows slightly in front of the bar.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your stomach so your ribs stay down.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Military_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_dumbbell', 'Overhead Press (Dumbbell)', array['standing dumbbell press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart holding a dumbbell in each hand at shoulder height.','Palms forward or slightly inward, elbows slightly in front of your body.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your stomach so your ribs stay down.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_smith', 'Overhead Press (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart and the weight at shoulder height.','Grip just outside shoulder width with wrists straight and elbows slightly in front of the bar.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your stomach so your ribs stay down.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_smith/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Overhead_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_cable_shoulder_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_cable_shoulder_press', 'Seated Cable Shoulder Press', array['Overhead Press (Cable, Seated)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated Cable Shoulder Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: seated between two low cables.', array['Adjust the weight to an appropriate amount and be seated, grasping the handles. Your upper arms should be about 90 degrees to the body, with your head and chest up. The elbows should also be bent to about 90 degrees. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by extending through the elbow, pressing the handles together above your head.','After pausing at the top, return the handles to the starting position. Ensure that you maintain tension on the cables.','You can also execute this movement with your back off the pad and alternate hands.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_cable_shoulder_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Cable_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_seated_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_seated_barbell', 'Seated Overhead Press (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Sit on an upright bench, back against the pad, feet flat.','Unrack the bar at shoulder height with an overhand grip.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_seated_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_seated_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_seated_dumbbell', 'Seated Overhead Press (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Set a bench upright (about 80–90°) and sit with your back against it.','Kick the dumbbells up from your thighs to shoulder height.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_seated_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'see_saw_press_alternating_side_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'see_saw_press_alternating_side_press', 'See-Saw Press (Alternating Side Press)', array['Overhead Press (Dumbbell, Seesaw)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'See-Saw Press (Alternating Side Press) is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the abs & core and triceps. A variation of the overhead press: one arm lowers as the other presses, with a slight side lean.', array['Grab a dumbbell with each hand and stand up erect.']::text[], array['Clean (lift) the dumbbells to the chest/shoulder level and then rotate your wrists so that your palms are facing towards you as if you were getting ready to perform an Arnold Press. This will be your starting position.','Now start extending your left arm overhead as you rotate the wrist so that the palm of your hand faces forward as you go up. Your elbows should come out also as you lift the weight. Simultaneously, you will also be bending from your hip to your opposite side. Tip: If you perform the exercise correctly, is should look as if you are trying to reach for something overhead on the right hand side of your body, but with your left arm. Breathe out as you perform this movement.','Once you reach the top position breathe in. Then, with the weight fully extended overhead and you bent over to your right hand side, begin the movement to the left side.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/see_saw_press_alternating_side_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/See-Saw_Press_Alternating_Side_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_shoulder_press_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_shoulder_press_dumbbell', 'Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)', array['dumbbell shoulder press','db shoulder press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Sit on an upright bench (or stand) with a dumbbell in each hand at shoulder height.','Palms face forward, elbows slightly in front of your body.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_shoulder_press_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shoulder_press_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shoulder_press_with_bands', 'Shoulder Press - With Bands', array['Overhead Press (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Shoulder Press - With Bands is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: standing on a band; resistance rises toward the top.', array['To begin, stand on an exercise band so that tension begins at arm''s length. Grasp the handles and lift them so that the hands are at shoulder height at each side.']::text[], array['Rotate the wrists so that the palms of your hands are facing forward. Your elbows should be bent, with the upper arms and forearms in line to the torso. This is your starting position.','As you exhale, lift the handles up until your arms are fully extended overhead.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shoulder_press_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Shoulder_Press_-_With_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_alternating_dumbbell_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_alternating_dumbbell_press', 'Standing Alternating Dumbbell Press', array['Overhead Press (Dumbbell, Alternating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Alternating Dumbbell Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: dumbbells pressed one at a time.', array['Stand with a dumbbell in each hand. Raise the dumbbells to your shoulders with your palms facing forward and your elbows pointed out. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Extend one arm to press the dumbbell straight up, keeping your off hand in place. Do not lean or jerk the weight during the movement.','After a brief pause, return the weight to the starting position.','Repeat for the opposite side, continuing to alternate between arms.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_alternating_dumbbell_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Alternating_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_barbell_press_behind_neck')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_barbell_press_behind_neck', 'Standing Barbell Press Behind Neck', array['Overhead Press (Behind the Neck)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Barbell Press Behind Neck is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: bar lowered behind the head. Needs good shoulder mobility; use light weight.', array['This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for easier pick up of the bar. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your shoulders (slightly below the neck) across it.']::text[], array['Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with your legs and at the same time straightening your torso.','Step away from the rack and position your legs using a shoulder width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Your back should be kept straight while performing this exercise. This will be your starting position.','Elevate the barbell overhead by fully extending your arms while breathing out.','Hold the contraction for a second and lower the barbell back down to the starting position by inhaling.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_barbell_press_behind_neck/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Barbell_Press_Behind_Neck/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_bradford_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_bradford_press', 'Standing Bradford Press', array['Overhead Press (Bradford, Standing)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Bradford Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: bar passes over the head from front to back, never locking out.', array['Place a loaded bar at shoulder level in a rack. With a pronated grip at shoulder width, begin with the bar racked across the front of your shoulders. This is your starting position.']::text[], array['Initiate the lift by extending the elbows to press the bar overhead. Avoid locking out the elbow as you move the weight behind your head.','Lower the bar down to the back of the head until your elbow forms a right angle.','Lift the bar back over your head by extending the elbows','Lower the bar down to the starting position.','Alternate in this manner until you complete the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_bradford_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Bradford_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_press_military')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_press_military', 'Standing Military Press (Barbell)', array['military press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing a weight from your shoulders to straight arms overhead. The main strength exercise for the shoulders.', array['Stand with feet hip-width apart and the weight at shoulder height.','Grip just outside shoulder width with wrists straight and elbows slightly in front of the bar.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your stomach so your ribs stay down.']::text[], array['Press the weight straight up, moving your head back slightly to let it pass.','Once it passes your forehead, bring your head forward under the weight.','Finish with arms straight and the weight directly above your shoulders.','Lower under control back to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_press_military/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Military_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_palm_in_one_arm_dumbbell_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_palm_in_one_arm_dumbbell_press', 'Standing Palm-In One-Arm Dumbbell Press', array['Overhead Press (Single Arm, Palm In)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Palm-In One-Arm Dumbbell Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: one dumbbell, palm facing in.', array['Start by having a dumbbell in one hand with your arm fully extended to the side using a neutral grip. Use your other arm to hold on to an incline bench to keep your balance.']::text[], array['Your feet should be shoulder width apart from each other. Now slowly lift the dumbbell up until you create a 90 degree angle with your arm. Note: Your forearm should be perpendicular to the floor. Continue to maintain a neutral grip throughout the entire exercise.','Slowly lift the dumbbell up until your arm is fully extended. This the starting position.','While inhaling lower the weight down until your arm is at a 90 degree angle again.','Feel the contraction for a second and then lift the weight back up towards the starting position while exhaling. Remember to hold on to the incline bench and keep your feet positioned to keep balance during the exercise.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the exercise.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_palm_in_one_arm_dumbbell_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Palm-In_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_palms_in_dumbbell_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_palms_in_dumbbell_press', 'Standing Palms-In Dumbbell Press', array['Overhead Press (Dumbbell, Palms In)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Palms-In Dumbbell Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the triceps. A variation of the overhead press: palms face each other, easier on the shoulders.', array['Start by having a dumbbell in each hand with your arm fully extended to the side using a neutral grip. Your feet should be shoulder width apart from each other. Now slowly lift the dumbbells up until you create a 90 degree angle with your arms. Note: Your forearms should be perpendicular to the floor. This the starting position.']::text[], array['Continue to maintain a neutral grip throughout the entire exercise. Slowly lift the dumbbells up until your arms are fully extended.','While inhaling lower the weights down until your arm is at a 90 degree angle again.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Ribs down, glutes tight','Push your head through at the top','Finish with the weight stacked over your shoulders']::text[], array['Leaning back and turning it into an incline press','Pressing the weight out in front','Flaring the elbows wide at the start']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_palms_in_dumbbell_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Palms-In_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pike_push_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pike_push_up', 'Pike Pushup', array['pike push up']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A push up with your hips high so your body forms an upside-down V, shifting the work to the shoulders.', array['Start in a push-up position, then walk your feet in and lift your hips high.','Hands slightly wider than shoulders.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows and lower the top of your head toward the floor in front of your hands.','Push back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Head travels forward of the hands, forming a triangle','Hips stay high']::text[], array['Letting the hips drop into a normal push up','Elbows flaring straight out']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'press_under')::uuid, 'mfd', 'press_under', 'Press Under', array['snatch balance','sots press']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'A snatch drill: pushing yourself down under the bar into a squat while pressing it to locked arms.', array['Hold the bar behind your neck with a snatch grip, feet in the landing position.']::text[], array['Press against the bar to push yourself down into a deep squat.','Finish with arms locked and bar overhead.','Stand up.']::text[], array['Push yourself down, not the bar up']::text[], array['Pressing the bar up first']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'double_kettlebell_push_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'double_kettlebell_push_press', 'Double Kettlebell Push Press', array['Push Press (Double Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Double Kettlebell Push Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, quadriceps and triceps. A variation of the push press: two kettlebells from the rack position.', array['Clean two kettlebells to your shoulders.']::text[], array['Squat down a few inches and reverse the motion rapidly. Use the momentum from the legs to drive the kettlebells overhead.','Once the kettlebells are locked out, lower the kettlebells to your shoulders and repeat.']::text[], array['Short, straight-down dip','Legs then arms, in one smooth motion']::text[], array['Dipping too deep or letting the knees go forward','Pressing before the legs finish driving']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/double_kettlebell_push_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Push_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_push_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_push_press', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Push Press', array['Push Press (Single Arm Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Push Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, quadriceps and triceps. A variation of the push press: one kettlebell from the rack position.', array['Hold a kettlebell by the handle. Clean the kettlebell to your shoulder by extending through the legs and hips as you pull the kettlebell towards your shoulder. Rotate your wrist as you do so, so that the palm faces forward. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Dip your body by bending the knees, keeping your torso upright.','Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum. As you do so, press the kettlebell overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using your body''s momentum to move the weight. Lower the weight to perform the next repetition.']::text[], array['Short, straight-down dip','Legs then arms, in one smooth motion']::text[], array['Dipping too deep or letting the knees go forward','Pressing before the legs finish driving']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_push_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Push_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_press', 'Push Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'An overhead press driven by a short, explosive dip and drive of the legs. It lets you move more weight than a strict press.', array['Stand with the bar in the front rack, resting on your shoulders, grip just outside shoulder width.','Feet hip-width apart, core braced.']::text[], array['Dip a short distance by bending the knees, keeping the torso upright.','Drive up hard through the legs and use that momentum to press the bar overhead.','Lock out with arms straight and the bar over mid-foot.','Lower the bar back to your shoulders, absorbing it with the legs.']::text[], array['Short, straight-down dip','Legs then arms, in one smooth motion']::text[], array['Dipping too deep or letting the knees go forward','Pressing before the legs finish driving']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Push_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_press_behind_the_neck')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_press_behind_the_neck', 'Push Press - Behind the Neck', array['Push Press (Behind the Neck)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Push Press - Behind the Neck is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, quadriceps and triceps. A variation of the push press: bar starts behind the head. Needs good shoulder mobility.', array['Standing with the weight racked on the back of the shoulders, begin with the dip. With your feet directly under your hips, flex the knees without moving the hips backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, moving the bar in a vertical path.']::text[], array['Using the momentum generated, finish pressing the weight overhead be extending through the arms.','Return to the starting position, using your legs to absorb the impact.']::text[], array['Short, straight-down dip','Legs then arms, in one smooth motion']::text[], array['Dipping too deep or letting the knees go forward','Pressing before the legs finish driving']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/push_press_behind_the_neck/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Push_Press_-_Behind_the_Neck/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'back_flyes_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'back_flyes_with_bands', 'Back Flyes - With Bands', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Back Flyes - With Bands is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the upper back and triceps. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: pulling a band apart in front of the chest.', array['Run a band around a stationary post like that of a squat rack.']::text[], array['Grab the band by the handles and stand back so that the tension in the band rises.','Extend and lift the arms straight in front of you. Tip: Your arms should be straight and parallel to the floor while perpendicular to your torso. Your feet should be firmly planted on the floor spread at shoulder width. This will be your starting position.','As you exhale, move your arms to the sides and back. Keep your arms extended and parallel to the floor. Continue the movement until the arms are extended to your sides.','After a pause, go back to the original position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/back_flyes_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Back_Flyes_-_With_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_dumbbell_rear_delt_raise_with_head_on_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_dumbbell_rear_delt_raise_with_head_on_bench', 'Bent Over Dumbbell Rear Delt Raise With Head On Bench', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Head on Bench)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent Over Dumbbell Rear Delt Raise With Head On Bench is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: forehead rests on an incline bench to stop the body helping.', array['Stand up straight while holding a dumbbell in each hand and with an incline bench in front of you.']::text[], array['While keeping your back straight and maintaining the natural arch of your back, lean forward until your forehead touches the bench in front of you. Let the arms hang in front of you perpendicular to the ground. The palms of your hands should be facing each other and your torso should be parallel to the floor. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your torso forward and stationary, and the arms straight with a slight bend at the elbows, lift the dumbbells straight to the side until both arms are parallel to the floor. Exhale as you lift the weights. Caution: avoid swinging the torso or bringing the arms back as opposed to the side.','After a one second contraction at the top, slowly lower the dumbbells back to the starting position.','Repeat the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_dumbbell_rear_delt_raise_with_head_on_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Dumbbell_Rear_Delt_Raise_With_Head_On_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_low_pulley_side_lateral')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_low_pulley_side_lateral', 'Bent Over Low-Pulley Side Lateral', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Cable, Bent Over)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent Over Low-Pulley Side Lateral is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the lower back, upper back and traps. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: bent over beside a low pulley, one arm at a time.', array['Select a weight and hold the handle of the low pulley with your right hand.']::text[], array['Bend at the waist until your torso is nearly parallel to the floor. Your legs should be slightly bent with your left hand placed on your lower left thigh. Your right arm should be hanging from your shoulder in front of you and with a slight bend at the elbow. This will be your starting position.','Raise your right arm, elbow slightly bent, to the side until the arm is parallel to the floor and in line with your right ear. Breathe out as you perform this step.','Slowly lower the weight back to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and repeat the movement with the other arm.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_low_pulley_side_lateral/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Low-Pulley_Side_Lateral/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_fly_chest_supported')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_fly_chest_supported', 'Chest Supported Reverse Fly (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Opening the arms out to the sides while bent forward, to train the rear shoulders and upper back.', array['Lie face down on an incline bench set to about 30–45°.','Let the dumbbells hang straight down.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they are level with your body.','Pause, then lower slowly.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_fly_chest_supported/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Rear_Delt_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_lying_one_arm_rear_lateral_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_lying_one_arm_rear_lateral_raise', 'Dumbbell Lying One-Arm Rear Lateral Raise', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Single Arm, Lying)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Lying One-Arm Rear Lateral Raise is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the upper back. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: lying sideways on a bench, raising the top arm.', array['While holding a dumbbell in one hand, lay with your chest down on a slightly inclined (around 15 degrees when measured from the floor) adjustable bench. The other hand can be used to hold to the leg of the bench for stability.']::text[], array['Position the palm of the hand that is holding the dumbbell in a neutral manner (palms facing your torso) as you keep the arm extended with the elbow slightly bent. This will be your starting position.','Now raise the arm with the dumbbell to the side until your elbow is at shoulder height and your arm is roughly parallel to the floor as you exhale. Tip: Maintain your arm perpendicular to the torso while keeping your arm extended throughout the movement. Also, keep the contraction at the top for a second.','Slowly lower the dumbbell to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_lying_one_arm_rear_lateral_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_One-Arm_Rear_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_lying_rear_lateral_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_lying_rear_lateral_raise', 'Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Lying, Incline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: lying face down on an incline bench.', array['While holding a dumbbell in each hand, lay with your chest down on a slightly inclined (around 15 degrees when measured from the floor) adjustable bench.']::text[], array['Position the palms of the hands in a neutral manner (palms facing your torso) as you keep the arms extended with the elbows slightly bent. This will be your starting position.','Now raise the arms to the side until your elbows are at shoulder height and your arms are roughly parallel to the floor as you exhale. Tip: Maintain your arms perpendicular to the torso while keeping them extended throughout the movement. Also, keep the contraction at the top for a second.','Slowly lower the dumbbells to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and then switch to the other arm.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_lying_rear_lateral_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_Rear_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_fly_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_fly_cable', 'Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Opening the arms out to the sides while bent forward, to train the rear shoulders and upper back.', array['Set two pulleys at shoulder height and cross the cables, holding the left cable in your right hand and vice versa.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they are level with your body.','Pause, then lower slowly.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_fly_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Rear_Delt_Fly/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_fly_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_fly_dumbbell', 'Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Dumbbell)', array['reverse fly','rear delt fly','bent over lateral raise']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Opening the arms out to the sides while bent forward, to train the rear shoulders and upper back.', array['Hinge forward with a flat back until your torso is close to parallel, or use the support of the variation.','Let the weights hang below your chest with a slight elbow bend.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they are level with your body.','Pause, then lower slowly.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_fly_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Flyes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_fly_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_fly_machine', 'Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Machine)', array['reverse pec deck']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Opening the arms out to the sides while bent forward, to train the rear shoulders and upper back.', array['Sit facing the pec deck pad, handles at shoulder height.','Grip the handles with arms straight in front of you.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they are level with your body.','Pause, then lower slowly.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_fly_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Machine_Flyes/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_fly_single_arm_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_fly_single_arm_cable', 'Reverse Fly Single Arm (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Opening the arms out to the sides while bent forward, to train the rear shoulders and upper back.', array['Hinge forward with a flat back until your torso is close to parallel, or use the support of the variation.','Let the weights hang below your chest with a slight elbow bend.']::text[], array['Raise your arms out to the sides until they are level with your body.','Pause, then lower slowly.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_flyes_with_external_rotation')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_flyes_with_external_rotation', 'Reverse Flyes With External Rotation', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (With External Rotation)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Flyes With External Rotation is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: rotate the forearms up at the top to also work the rotator cuff.', array['To begin, lie down on an incline bench set at a 30-degree angle with the chest and stomach pressing against the incline.']::text[], array['Have the dumbbells in each hand with the palms facing down to the floor. Your arms should be in front of you so that they are perpendicular to the angle of the bench. Tip: Your elbows should have a slight bend. The legs should be stationary while applying pressure with the ball of your toes (your heels should not be touching the floor). This is the starting position.','Maintaining the slight bend of the elbows, move the weights out and away from each other in an arc motion while exhaling.','As you lift the weight, your wrist should externally rotate by 90-degrees so that you go from a palms down (pronated) grip to a palms facing each other (neutral) grip. Tip: Try to squeeze your shoulder blades together to get the best results from this exercise.','The arms should be elevated until they are level with the head.','Feel the contraction and slowly lower the weights back down to the starting position while inhaling.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_flyes_with_external_rotation/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Flyes_With_External_Rotation/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_bent_over_rear_delt_raise')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_bent_over_rear_delt_raise', 'Seated Bent-Over Rear Delt Raise', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Seated, Bent Over)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated Bent-Over Rear Delt Raise is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: seated on the end of a bench, chest toward the thighs.', array['Place a couple of dumbbells looking forward in front of a flat bench.']::text[], array['Sit on the end of the bench with your legs together and the dumbbells behind your calves.','Bend at the waist while keeping the back straight in order to pick up the dumbbells. The palms of your hands should be facing each other as you pick them. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your torso forward and stationary, and the arms slightly bent at the elbows, lift the dumbbells straight to the side until both arms are parallel to the floor. Exhale as you lift the weights. (Note: avoid swinging the torso or bringing the arms back as opposed to the side.)','After a one second contraction at the top, slowly lower the dumbbells back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_bent_over_rear_delt_raise/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_Rear_Delt_Raise/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sled_reverse_flye')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sled_reverse_flye', 'Sled Reverse Flye', array['Rear Delt Reverse Fly (Sled)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Sled Reverse Flye is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders. A variation of the rear delt reverse fly: walking backward pulling sled straps apart.', array['Attach dual handles to a sled connected by a rope or chain. Load the sled to a light weight.']::text[], array['Face the sled, backing up until there is some tension in the line. Take both handles at arms length at about waist level. Bend the knees slightly and keep your chest and head up. This will be your starting position.','Without flexing the elbow, pull the handles upward and apart, performing a reverse fly with some external rotation. Your palms should be facing forward as you do this.','Return to the starting position, taking a couple steps back to take the slack out of the line.']::text[], array['Lead with the back of the hands/elbows','Do not squeeze the shoulder blades hard; let the rear delts do it']::text[], array['Using momentum','Turning it into a row by bending the elbows']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sled_reverse_flye/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sled_Reverse_Flye/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'external_rotation')::uuid, 'mfd', 'external_rotation', 'External Rotation', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'External Rotation is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders.', array['Lie sideways on a flat bench with one arm holding a dumbbell and the other hand on top of the bench folded so that you can rest your head on it.']::text[], array['Bend the elbows of the arm holding the dumbbell so that it creates a 90-degree angle between the upper arm and the forearm. Tip: Keep the arm parallel to your torso.','Now bend the elbow while keeping the upper arm stationary. In this manner, the forearm will be parallel to the floor and perpendicular to your torso (Tip: So the forearm will be directly in front of you). The upper arm will be stationary by your torso and should be parallel to the floor (aligned with your torso at all times). This will be your starting position.','As you breathe out, externally rotate your forearm so that the dumbbell is lifted up in a semicircle motion as you maintain the 90 degree angle bend between the upper arms and the forearm. You will continue this external rotation until the forearm is perpendicular to the floor and the torso pointing towards the ceiling. At this point you will hold the contraction for a second.','As you breathe in, slowly go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and then switch to the other arm.']::text[], array['Elbow pinned to the side at 90 degrees (a rolled towel helps)','Rotate the forearm out, keeping the wrist straight','Light weight and slow, controlled reps']::text[], array['Elbow drifting away from the body','Using too much weight and twisting the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/external_rotation/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/External_Rotation/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'external_rotation_with_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'external_rotation_with_band', 'External Rotation with Band', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'External Rotation with Band is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders.', array['Choke the band around a post. The band should be at the same height as your elbow. Stand with your left side to the band a couple of feet away.']::text[], array['Grasp the end of the band with your right hand, and keep your elbow pressed firmly to your side. We recommend you hold a pad or foam roll in place with your elbow to keep it firmly in position.','With your upper arm in position, your elbow should be flexed to 90 degrees with your hand reaching across the front of your torso. This will be your starting position.','Execute the movement by rotating your arm in a backhand motion, keeping your elbow in place.','Continue as far as you are able, pause, and then return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Elbow pinned to the side at 90 degrees (a rolled towel helps)','Rotate the forearm out, keeping the wrist straight','Light weight and slow, controlled reps']::text[], array['Elbow drifting away from the body','Using too much weight and twisting the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/external_rotation_with_band/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/External_Rotation_with_Band/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'external_rotation_with_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'external_rotation_with_cable', 'External Rotation with Cable', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'External Rotation with Cable is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders.', array['Adjust the cable to the same height as your elbow. Stand with your left side to the band a couple of feet away.']::text[], array['Grasp the handle with your right hand, and keep your elbow pressed firmly to your side. We recommend you hold a pad or foam roll in place with your elbow to keep it firmly in position.','With your upper arm in position, your elbow should be flexed to 90 degrees with your hand reaching across the front of your torso. This will be your starting position.','Execute the movement by rotating your arm in a backhand motion, keeping your elbow in place.']::text[], array['Elbow pinned to the side at 90 degrees (a rolled towel helps)','Rotate the forearm out, keeping the wrist straight','Light weight and slow, controlled reps']::text[], array['Elbow drifting away from the body','Using too much weight and twisting the torso']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/external_rotation_with_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/External_Rotation_with_Cable/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_internal_rotation')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_internal_rotation', 'Cable Internal Rotation', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Internal Rotation is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders.', array['Sit next to a low pulley sideways (with legs stretched in front of you or crossed) and grasp the single hand cable attachment with the arm nearest to the cable. Tip: If you can adjust the pulley''s height, you can use a flat bench to sit on instead.']::text[], array['Position the elbow against your side with the elbow bent at 90° and the arm pointing towards the pulley. This will be your starting position.','Pull the single hand cable attachment toward your body by internally rotating your shoulder until your forearm is across your abs. You will be creating an imaginary semi-circle. Tip: The forearm should be perpendicular to your torso at all times.','Slowly go back to the initial position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and then repeat the movement with the next arm.']::text[], array['Elbow pinned to the side at 90 degrees','Rotate the forearm in across the stomach','Light, slow and controlled']::text[], array['Elbow drifting away from the body','Twisting the torso instead of the shoulder']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_internal_rotation/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Internal_Rotation/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'internal_rotation_with_band')::uuid, 'mfd', 'internal_rotation_with_band', 'Internal Rotation with Band', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Internal Rotation with Band is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders.', array['Choke the band around a post. The band should be at the same height as your elbow. Stand with your right side to the band a couple of feet away.']::text[], array['Grasp the end of the band with your right hand, and keep your elbow pressed firmly to your side. We recommend you hold a pad or foam roll in place with your elbow to keep it firmly in position.','With your upper arm in position, your elbow should be flexed to 90 degrees with your hand reaching away from your torso. This will be your starting position.','Execute the movement by rotating your arm in a forehand motion, keeping your elbow in place.','Continue as far as you are able, pause, and then return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Elbow pinned to the side at 90 degrees','Rotate the forearm in across the stomach','Light, slow and controlled']::text[], array['Elbow drifting away from the body','Twisting the torso instead of the shoulder']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/internal_rotation_with_band/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Internal_Rotation_with_Band/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shoulder_press_machine_seated')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shoulder_press_machine_seated', 'Seated Shoulder Press (Machine)', array['machine shoulder press']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated machine press. The guided path makes it a safe way to train the shoulders hard.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles start at about shoulder height.','Sit with your back against the pad and feet flat.']::text[], array['Press the handles up until your arms are almost straight.','Lower slowly until your hands are at shoulder height.']::text[], array['Back stays against the pad','Do not shrug at the top']::text[], array['Seat too low so the start is too deep','Arching away from the back pad']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shoulder_press_machine_seated/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Machine_Shoulder_Military_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shoulder_press_machine_plates')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shoulder_press_machine_plates', 'Shoulder Press (Machine Plates)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated machine press. The guided path makes it a safe way to train the shoulders hard.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles start at about shoulder height.','Sit with your back against the pad and feet flat.']::text[], array['Press the handles up until your arms are almost straight.','Lower slowly until your hands are at shoulder height.']::text[], array['Back stays against the pad','Do not shrug at the top']::text[], array['Seat too low so the start is too deep','Arching away from the back pad']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shoulder_press_machine_plates/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'landmine_linear_jammer')::uuid, 'mfd', 'landmine_linear_jammer', 'Landmine Linear Jammer', array['Single Arm Landmine Press (Linear Jammer)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Landmine Linear Jammer is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the abs & core, calves, chest, hamstrings, quadriceps and triceps. A variation of the single arm landmine press: both hands, driven explosively from a quarter squat.', array['Position a bar into landmine or, lacking one, securely anchor it in a corner. Load the bar to an appropriate weight and position the handle attachment on the bar.']::text[], array['Raise the bar from the floor, taking the handles to your shoulders. This will be your starting position.','In an athletic stance, squat by flexing your hips and setting your hips back, keeping your arms flexed.','Reverse the motion by powerfully extending through the hips, knees, and ankles, while also extending the elbows to straighten the arms. This movement should be done explosively, coming out of the squat to full extension as powerfully as possible.','Return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Ribs down, do not lean back','Reach at the top']::text[], array['Twisting the torso to push','Leaning away from the working arm']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/landmine_linear_jammer/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Landmine_Linear_Jammer/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'landmine_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'landmine_press', 'Single Arm Landmine Press (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pressing the end of a landmine bar up and forward with one arm. A shoulder-friendly alternative to overhead pressing.', array['Stand or kneel facing the end of a landmine bar.','Hold the bar end in one hand at shoulder height, elbow tucked.']::text[], array['Press the bar up and forward until your arm is straight.','Let your shoulder blade reach forward at the top.','Lower under control back to your shoulder.']::text[], array['Ribs down, do not lean back','Reach at the top']::text[], array['Twisting the torso to push','Leaning away from the working arm']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'single_arm_linear_jammer')::uuid, 'mfd', 'single_arm_linear_jammer', 'Single-Arm Linear Jammer', array['Single Arm Landmine Press (Single Arm Jammer)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Single-Arm Linear Jammer is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the chest and triceps. A variation of the single arm landmine press: one hand, driven explosively from a quarter squat.', array['Position a bar into a landmine or securely anchor it in a corner. Load the bar to an appropriate weight.']::text[], array['Raise the bar from the floor, taking it to your shoulders with one or both hands. Adopt a wide stance. This will be your starting position.','Perform the movement by extending the elbow, pressing the weight up. Move explosively, extending the hips and knees fully to produce maximal force.','Return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Ribs down, do not lean back','Reach at the top']::text[], array['Twisting the torso to push','Leaning away from the working arm']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/single_arm_linear_jammer/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Single-Arm_Linear_Jammer/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sled_overhead_backward_walk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sled_overhead_backward_walk', 'Sled Overhead Backward Walk', array['Sled Pull (Overhead Backward Walk)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Sled Overhead Backward Walk is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the calves, upper back and quadriceps. A variation of the sled pull: straps held overhead, walking backward.', array['Attach dual handles to a sled connected by a rope or chain. Load the sled to a light weight.']::text[], array['Face the sled, backing up until there is some tension in the line. Hold your hands directly above your head with your elbows extended. This will be your starting position.','Walk backwards, keeping your arms raised above your head. Avoid jerky movements.']::text[], array['Stay low and drive through the legs']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sled_overhead_backward_walk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sled_Overhead_Backward_Walk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'jerk_balance')::uuid, 'mfd', 'jerk_balance', 'Jerk Balance', array['Split Jerk (Jerk Balance (Drill))']::text[], 'olympic', 'time', 'Jerk Balance is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the glutes, hamstrings, quadriceps and triceps. A variation of the split jerk: drill: step into the split while pressing under the bar.', array['This drill helps you learn to drive yourself low enough during the jerk and corrects those who move backward during the movement. Begin with the bar racked in the jerk position, with the shoulders forward, torso upright, and the feet split slightly apart.']::text[], array['Initiate the movement as you would a normal jerk, dipping at the knees while keeping your torso vertical, and driving back up forcefully, using momentum and not your arms to elevate the weight.','Keep the rear foot in place, using it to drive your body forward into a full split as you jerk the weight. Recover by standing up with the weight overhead.']::text[], array['Vertical dip','Punch under the bar']::text[], array['Dipping forward','Soft elbows in the catch']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/jerk_balance/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Jerk_Balance/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rack_delivery')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rack_delivery', 'Rack Delivery', array['Split Jerk (Rack Delivery (Drill))']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Rack Delivery is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the forearms and traps. A variation of the split jerk: drill: practise catching the bar in the front rack.', array['This drill teaches the delivery of the barbell to the rack position on the shoulders. Begin holding a bar in the scarecrow position, with the upper arms parallel to the floor, and the forearms hanging down. Use a hook grip, with your fingers wrapped over your thumbs.']::text[], array['Begin by rotating the elbows around the bar, delivering the bar to the shoulders. As your elbows come forward, relax your grip. The shoulders should be protracted, providing a shelf for the bar, which should lightly contact the throat.','It is important that the bar stay close to the body at all times, as with a heavier load any distance will result in an unwanted collision. As the movement becomes smoother, speed and load can be increased before progressing further.']::text[], array['Vertical dip','Punch under the bar']::text[], array['Dipping forward','Soft elbows in the catch']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rack_delivery/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rack_Delivery/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'split_jerk')::uuid, 'mfd', 'split_jerk', 'Split Jerk', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Driving the bar up from the shoulders with the legs and dropping under it into a split stance with locked arms.', array['Hold the bar in the front rack, feet hip-width.']::text[], array['Dip a short distance straight down.','Drive up explosively and push yourself under the bar.','Land in a split stance with arms locked overhead.','Step the front foot back, then the back foot forward to finish.']::text[], array['Vertical dip','Punch under the bar']::text[], array['Dipping forward','Soft elbows in the catch']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/split_jerk/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Split_Jerk/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kneeling_arm_drill')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kneeling_arm_drill', 'Kneeling Arm Drill', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'reps', 'Kneeling Arm Drill is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the abs & core.', array['This drill helps increase arm efficiency during the run. Begin kneeling, left foot in front, right knee down. Apply pressure through the front heel to keep your glutes and hamstrings activated.']::text[], array['Begin by blocking the arms in long, pendulum like swings. Close the arm angle, blocking with the arms as you would when jogging, progressing to a run and finally a sprint.','As soon as your hands pass the hip, accelerate them forward during the sprinting motion to move them as quickly as possible.','Switch knees and repeat.']::text[], array['Drive the knee up and the foot down under the hips','Arms swing from the shoulder, elbows about 90 degrees','Stay tall with a slight forward lean']::text[], array['Reaching out with the foot in front of the body','Arms crossing the body','Running the drill tired; quality comes first']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kneeling_arm_drill/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kneeling_Arm_Drill/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'circus_bell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'circus_bell', 'Circus Bell', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Circus Bell is an advanced-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the forearms, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, traps and triceps.', array['The circus bell is an oversized dumbbell with a thick handle. Begin with the dumbbell between your feet, and grip the handle with both hands.']::text[], array['Clean the dumbbell by extending through your hips and knees to deliver the implement to the desired shoulder, letting go with the extra hand.','Ensure that you get one of the dumbbell heads behind the shoulder to keep from being thrown off balance. To raise it overhead, dip by flexing the knees, and the drive upwards as you extend the dumbbell overhead, leaning slightly away from it as you do so.','Carefully guide the bell back to the floor, keeping it under control as much as possible. It is best to perform this event on a thick rubber mat to prevent damage to the floor.']::text[], array['Clean the implement to the chest or shoulder first','Dip and drive with the legs, then press','Lock out with the implement over the mid-foot']::text[], array['Pressing without leg drive','Leaning back excessively','Losing the brace during the clean']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/circus_bell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Circus_Bell/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'log_lift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'log_lift', 'Log Lift', '{}'::text[], 'strongman', 'weight_reps', 'Log Lift is an intermediate-level strongman exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the abs & core, chest, glutes, hamstrings, lower back, upper back, quadriceps, traps and triceps.', array['Begin standing with the log in front of you. Grasp the handles, and begin to clean the log. As you are bent over to start the clean, attempt to get the log as high as possible, pulling it into your chest. Extend through the hips and knees to bring it up to complete the clean.']::text[], array['Push your head back and look up, creating a shelf on your chest to rest the log. Begin the press by dipping, flexing slightly through the knees and reversing the motion. This push press will generate momentum to start the log moving vertically. Continue by extending through the elbows to press the log above your head. There are no strict rules on form, so use whatever techniques you are most efficient with. As the log is pressed, ensure that you push your head through on each repetition, looking forward.','Repeat as many times as possible. Attempt to control the descent of the log as it is returned to the ground.']::text[], array['Clean the implement to the chest or shoulder first','Dip and drive with the legs, then press','Lock out with the implement over the mid-foot']::text[], array['Pressing without leg drive','Leaning back excessively','Losing the brace during the clean']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/log_lift/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Log_Lift/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_one_arm_upright_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_one_arm_upright_row', 'Dumbbell One-Arm Upright Row', array['Upright Row (Single Arm Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell One-Arm Upright Row is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps and traps. A variation of the upright row: one dumbbell, other hand on the hip.', array['Grab a dumbbell and stand up straight with your arm extended in front of you with a slight bend at the elbows and your back straight. This will be your starting position. Tip: The dumbbell should be resting on top of your thigh with the palm of your hands facing your thighs.']::text[], array['Keep the other hand can be kept fully extended to the side, by the waist or grabbing a fixed surface. This will be your starting position.','Use your side shoulders to lift the dumbbell as you exhale. The dumbbell should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until the dumbbell is nearly in line with your chin. Tip: Your elbows should drive the motion. As you lift the dumbbell, your elbow should always be higher than your forearm. Also, keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.','Lower the dumbbell back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and switch arms.']::text[], array['Elbows above the hands','Stop at shoulder height']::text[], array['Narrow grip and pulling too high, which can pinch the shoulders','Swinging the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_one_arm_upright_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_One-Arm_Upright_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_one_arm_upright_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_one_arm_upright_row', 'Smith Machine One-Arm Upright Row', array['Upright Row (Smith, Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine One-Arm Upright Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the biceps and traps. A variation of the upright row: one hand in the middle of a Smith bar.', array['With the bar at thigh level, load an appropriate weight.']::text[], array['Take a wide grip on the bar and unhook the weight, removing your off hand from the bar. Your arm should be extended as you stand up straight with your head and chest up. This will be your starting position.','Begin the movement by flexing the elbow, raising the upper arm with the elbow pointed out. Continue until your upper arm is parallel to the floor.','After a brief pause, return the weight to the starting position.','Repeat for the desired number of repetitions before engaging the hooks to rack the weight.']::text[], array['Elbows above the hands','Stop at shoulder height']::text[], array['Narrow grip and pulling too high, which can pinch the shoulders','Swinging the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_one_arm_upright_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_One-Arm_Upright_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'upright_row_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'upright_row_barbell', 'Upright Row (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pulling a weight from your thighs up along your body to chest height, leading with the elbows.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs with an overhand grip about shoulder-width or wider.']::text[], array['Pull the weight straight up, leading with the elbows, until your upper arms are about level with your shoulders.','Keep the weight close to your body.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Elbows above the hands','Stop at shoulder height']::text[], array['Narrow grip and pulling too high, which can pinch the shoulders','Swinging the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/upright_row_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Upright_Barbell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'upright_row_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'upright_row_cable', 'Upright Row (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pulling a weight from your thighs up along your body to chest height, leading with the elbows.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs with an overhand grip about shoulder-width or wider.']::text[], array['Pull the weight straight up, leading with the elbows, until your upper arms are about level with your shoulders.','Keep the weight close to your body.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Elbows above the hands','Stop at shoulder height']::text[], array['Narrow grip and pulling too high, which can pinch the shoulders','Swinging the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/upright_row_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Upright_Cable_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'upright_row_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'upright_row_dumbbell', 'Upright Row (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pulling a weight from your thighs up along your body to chest height, leading with the elbows.', array['Stand tall holding the weight in front of your thighs with an overhand grip about shoulder-width or wider.']::text[], array['Pull the weight straight up, leading with the elbows, until your upper arms are about level with your shoulders.','Keep the weight close to your body.','Lower slowly.']::text[], array['Elbows above the hands','Stop at shoulder height']::text[], array['Narrow grip and pulling too high, which can pinch the shoulders','Swinging the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/upright_row_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Upright_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'straight_raises_on_incline_bench')::uuid, 'mfd', 'straight_raises_on_incline_bench', 'Straight Raises on Incline Bench', array['Y Raise (Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straight Raises on Incline Bench is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the shoulders, with help from the traps. A variation of the y raise: lying face down on an incline bench, raise a light bar straight out in front.', array['Place a bar on the ground behind the head of an incline bench.']::text[], array['Lay on the bench face down. With a pronated grip, pick the barbell up from the floor, keeping your arms straight. Allow the bar to hang straight down. This will be your starting position.','To begin, raise the barbell out in front of your head while keeping your arms extended.','Return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Thumbs point up','Shoulders down, away from the ears']::text[], array['Shrugging','Using weights too heavy']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/straight_raises_on_incline_bench/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Straight_Raises_on_Incline_Bench/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'clean_shrug')::uuid, 'mfd', 'clean_shrug', 'Clean Shrug', array['Clean Pull (Clean Shrug)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Clean Shrug is a beginner-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the traps, with help from the forearms. A variation of the clean pull: from the hang, extend and shrug, no arm pull.', '{}'::text[], array['Begin with a shoulder width, double overhand or hook grip, with the bar hanging at the mid thigh position. Your back should be straight and inclined slightly forward.','Shrug your shoulders towards your ears. While this exercise can usually by loaded with heavier weight than a clean, avoid overloading to the point that the execution slows down.']::text[], array['Full extension of hips, knees and ankles','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Bending the arms early','Leaning back excessively']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/clean_shrug/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Clean_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'snatch_shrug')::uuid, 'mfd', 'snatch_shrug', 'Snatch Shrug', array['Clean Pull (Snatch Shrug)']::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'Snatch Shrug is an intermediate-level Olympic-lifting exercise that mainly targets the traps, with help from the forearms. A variation of the clean pull: from the hang with a snatch grip, extend and shrug.', '{}'::text[], array['Begin with a wide grip, with the bar hanging at the mid thigh position. You can use a hook or overhand grip. Your back should be straight and inclined slightly forward.','Shrug your shoulders towards your ears. While this exercise can usually by loaded with heavier weight than a snatch, avoid overloading to the point that the execution slows down.']::text[], array['Full extension of hips, knees and ankles','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Bending the arms early','Leaning back excessively']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/snatch_shrug/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Snatch_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'high_pull_deadlift')::uuid, 'mfd', 'high_pull_deadlift', 'Deadlift High Pull', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'An explosive pull from the floor that brings the weight up to chest height with the elbows high.', array['Set up as for a deadlift with the bar over mid-foot and a flat back.']::text[], array['Lift and extend explosively through the hips.','Pull the weight up to chest height, elbows high and out.','Lower under control.']::text[], array['Hips drive the pull, the arms finish it']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'high_pull_kettlebell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'high_pull_kettlebell', 'Kettlebell High Pull', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'An explosive pull from the floor that brings the weight up to chest height with the elbows high.', array['Stand with the kettlebell on the floor between your feet.','Hinge with a flat back and grip it with one hand.']::text[], array['Lift and extend explosively through the hips.','Pull the weight up to chest height, elbows high and out.','Lower under control.']::text[], array['Hips drive the pull, the arms finish it']::text[], array['Pulling only with the arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/high_pull_kettlebell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kettlebell_Sumo_High_Pull/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'jump_shrug')::uuid, 'mfd', 'jump_shrug', 'Jump Shrug', '{}'::text[], 'olympic', 'weight_reps', 'From the hang, an explosive jump with the bar finishing in a strong shrug. Teaches full extension for Olympic lifts.', array['Hold the bar at mid-thigh with straight arms, slight hinge.']::text[], array['Jump explosively, extending hips, knees and ankles.','Shrug hard at the top, arms straight.','Land softly and reset.']::text[], array['Arms stay long','Drive through the floor']::text[], array['Bending the arms']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'barbell_shrug_behind_the_back')::uuid, 'mfd', 'barbell_shrug_behind_the_back', 'Barbell Shrug Behind The Back', array['Shrug (Barbell Behind Back)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Barbell Shrug Behind The Back is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the traps, with help from the forearms and upper back. A variation of the shrug: bar held behind the thighs, which hits the middle traps more.', array['Stand up straight with your feet at shoulder width as you hold a barbell with both hands behind your back using a pronated grip (palms facing back). Tip: Your hands should be a little wider than shoulder width apart. You can use wrist wraps for this exercise for better grip. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Raise your shoulders up as far as you can go as you breathe out and hold the contraction for a second. Tip: Refrain from trying to lift the barbell by using your biceps. The arms should remain stretched out at all times.','Slowly return to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/barbell_shrug_behind_the_back/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Shrug_Behind_The_Back/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'calf_machine_shoulder_shrug')::uuid, 'mfd', 'calf_machine_shoulder_shrug', 'Calf-Machine Shoulder Shrug', array['Shrug (Calf Machine)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Calf-Machine Shoulder Shrug is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the traps. A variation of the shrug: using the shoulder pads of a standing calf machine.', array['Position yourself on the calf machine so that the shoulder pads are above your shoulders. Your torso should be straight with the arms extended normally by your side. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Raise your shoulders up towards your ears as you exhale and hold the contraction for a full second.','Slowly return to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/calf_machine_shoulder_shrug/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Calf-Machine_Shoulder_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shrug_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shrug_barbell', 'Shrug (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the shoulders straight up toward the ears to train the upper traps.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with straight arms at your sides or in front of your thighs.']::text[], array['Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears.','Hold for a second at the top.','Lower slowly to a full stretch.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shrug_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Barbell_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shrug_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shrug_cable', 'Shrug (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the shoulders straight up toward the ears to train the upper traps.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with straight arms at your sides or in front of your thighs.']::text[], array['Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears.','Hold for a second at the top.','Lower slowly to a full stretch.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shrug_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Shrugs/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shrug_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shrug_dumbbell', 'Shrug (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the shoulders straight up toward the ears to train the upper traps.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with straight arms at your sides or in front of your thighs.']::text[], array['Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears.','Hold for a second at the top.','Lower slowly to a full stretch.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shrug_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shrug_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shrug_machine', 'Shrug (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the shoulders straight up toward the ears to train the upper traps.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with straight arms at your sides or in front of your thighs.']::text[], array['Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears.','Hold for a second at the top.','Lower slowly to a full stretch.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/shrug_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Leverage_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'shrug_smith')::uuid, 'mfd', 'shrug_smith', 'Shrug (Smith Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lifting the shoulders straight up toward the ears to train the upper traps.', array['Stand tall holding the weight with straight arms at your sides or in front of your thighs.']::text[], array['Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears.','Hold for a second at the top.','Lower slowly to a full stretch.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_behind_the_back_shrug')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_behind_the_back_shrug', 'Smith Machine Behind the Back Shrug', array['Shrug (Smith, Behind Back)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine Behind the Back Shrug is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the traps. A variation of the shrug: smith bar held behind the thighs.', array['With the bar at thigh level, load an appropriate weight.']::text[], array['Stand with the bar behind you, taking a shoulder-width, pronated grip on the bar and unhook the weight. You should be standing up straight with your head and chest up and your arms extended. This will be your starting position.','Initiate the movement by shrugging your shoulders straight up. Do not flex the arms or wrist during the movement.','After a brief pause return the weight to the starting position.','Repeat for the desired number of repetitions before engaging the hooks to rack the weight.']::text[], array['Straight up and down; do not roll the shoulders','Arms stay straight']::text[], array['Rolling the shoulders in circles','Bending the elbows','Bouncing with heavy weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_behind_the_back_shrug/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Behind_the_Back_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_upright_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_upright_row', 'Smith Machine Upright Row', array['Upright Row (Smith)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine Upright Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the traps, with help from the biceps and upper back. A variation of the upright row: smith machine bar.', array['To begin, set the bar on the smith machine to a height that is around the middle of your thighs. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, grasp the bar using a pronated (palms forward) grip that is shoulder width apart. You may need some wrist wraps if using a significant amount of weight.']::text[], array['Lift the barbell up and fully extend your arms with your back straight. There should be a slight bend at the elbows. This is the starting position.','Use your side shoulders to lift the bar as you exhale. The bar should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until it nearly touches your chin. Tip: Your elbows should drive the motion. As you lift the bar, your elbows should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.','Lower the bar back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows above the hands','Stop at shoulder height']::text[], array['Narrow grip and pulling too high, which can pinch the shoulders','Swinging the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_upright_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Upright_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'upright_row_with_bands')::uuid, 'mfd', 'upright_row_with_bands', 'Upright Row - With Bands', array['Upright Row (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Upright Row - With Bands is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the traps. A variation of the upright row: standing on a band.', array['To begin, stand on an exercise band so that tension begins at arm''s length. Grasp the handles using a pronated (palms facing your thighs) grip that is slightly less than shoulder width. The handles should be resting on top of your thighs. Your arms should be extended with a slight bend at the elbows and your back should be straight. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Use your side shoulders to lift the handles as you exhale. The handles should be close to the body as you move them up. Continue to lift the handles until they nearly touches your chin. Tip: Your elbows should drive the motion. As you lift the handles, your elbows should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torso stationary and pause for a second at the top of the movement.','Lower the handles back down slowly to the starting position. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows above the hands','Stop at shoulder height']::text[], array['Narrow grip and pulling too high, which can pinch the shoulders','Swinging the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/upright_row_with_bands/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Upright_Row_-_With_Bands/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps', 'Overhead Triceps', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Overhead Triceps is an advanced-level stretch that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the lats.', array['Sit upright on the floor with your partner behind you. Raise one arm straight up, and flex the elbow, attempting to touch your hand to your back. Your parner should hold your elbow and wrist. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Attempt to extend the arm straight into the air as your partner prevents you from doing actually doing so.','After 10-20 seconds, relax the arm and allow your partner to further stretch the tricep by applying gentle pressure to the wrist. Hold for 10-20 seconds, and then switch sides.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulder relaxed and down','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Pulling hard on the joint','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_triceps/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Overhead_Triceps/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'tricep_side_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'tricep_side_stretch', 'Tricep Side Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Tricep Side Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the triceps.', '{}'::text[], array['Bring right arm across your body and over your left shoulder, holding your elbow with your left hand, until you feel a stretch in your tricep. Then repeat for your other arm.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulder relaxed and down','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Pulling hard on the joint','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/tricep_side_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Tricep_Side_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_stretch', 'Triceps Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Triceps Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the lats.', '{}'::text[], array['Reach your hand behind your head, grasp your elbow and gently pull. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds, then switch sides.']::text[], array['Keep the shoulder relaxed and down','Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension, never pain','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Pulling hard on the joint','Bouncing to go deeper','Forcing the stretch until it hurts','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Triceps_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_dip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_dip', 'Bench Dip', array['chair dip']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Dips with your hands on a bench behind you and feet on the floor.', array['Sit on the edge of a bench, hands beside your hips, fingers forward.','Slide your hips off the bench, feet on the floor in front.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower your hips toward the floor.','Stop when your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Press back up.']::text[], array['Keep your back close to the bench','Elbows point straight back']::text[], array['Dropping too low and straining the shoulders','Elbows flaring out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_dip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bench_Dips/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'weighted_bench_dip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'weighted_bench_dip', 'Weighted Bench Dip', array['Bench Dip (Weighted)']::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'Weighted Bench Dip is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the bench dip: a plate on the thighs.', array['For this exercise you will need to place a bench behind your back and another one in front of you. With the benches perpendicular to your body, hold on to one bench on its edge with the hands close to your body, separated at shoulder width. Your arms should be fully extended.']::text[], array['The legs will be extended forward on top of the other bench. Your legs should be parallel to the floor while your torso is to be perpendicular to the floor. Have your partner place the dumbbell on your lap. Note: This exercise is best performed with a partner as placing the weight on your lap can be challenging and cause injury without assistance. This will be your starting position.','Slowly lower your body as you inhale by bending at the elbows until you lower yourself far enough to where there is an angle slightly smaller than 90 degrees between the upper arm and the forearm. Tip: Keep the elbows as close as possible throughout the movement. Forearms should always be pointing down.','Using your triceps to bring your torso up again, lift yourself back to the starting position while exhaling.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep your back close to the bench','Elbows point straight back']::text[], array['Dropping too low and straining the shoulders','Elbows flaring out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/weighted_bench_dip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Weighted_Bench_Dip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_close_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_close_grip', 'Bench Press - Close Grip (Barbell)', array['close grip bench','cgbp']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A bench press with hands about shoulder-width apart, which shifts more of the work to the triceps.', array['Lie on the bench with your eyes under the bar (or the handles/weights level with your chest).','Plant your feet flat on the floor, slightly wider than your hips.','Pull your shoulder blades back and down and keep them pinned to the bench; allow a small natural arch in your lower back.','Grip slightly wider than shoulder width with wrists stacked straight over your forearms.']::text[], array['Unrack or lift the weight to straight arms over your shoulders.','Lower it under control to your lower chest, elbows about 45–70° from your torso.','Touch the chest lightly without bouncing.','Press back up and slightly toward your face so the weight finishes over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders','Elbows tucked close to the ribs']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_press_close_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bench_press_with_chains')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bench_press_with_chains', 'Bench Press with Chains', array['Bench Press (Chains)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bench Press with Chains is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest and lats. A variation of the bench press: chains add load as the bar rises, so the top of the press is heaviest.', array['Adjust the leader chain, shortening it to the desired length. Place the chains on the sleeves of the bar.']::text[], array['Lying on the bench, get your head beyond the bar if possible. Tuck your feet underneath you and arch your back. Using the bar to help support your weight, lift your shoulder off the bench and retract them, squeezing the shoulder blades together. Use your feet to drive your traps into the bench. Maintain this tight body position throughout the movement. However wide your grip, it should cover the ring on the bar.','Pull the bar out of the rack without protracting your shoulders. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart. Lower the bar to your lower chest or upper stomach. The bar, wrist, and elbow should stay in line at all times.','Pause when the barbell touches your torso, and then drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The elbows should be tucked in until lockout.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bench_press_with_chains/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bench_Press_with_Chains/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'board_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'board_press', 'Board Press', array['Bench Press (Board Press)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Board Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest, forearms and lats. A variation of the bench press: boards on the chest stop the bar short to overload the top half.', array['Begin by lying on the bench, getting your head beyond the bar if possible. One to five boards, made out of 2x6''s, can be screwed together and held in place by a training partner, bands, or just tucked under your shirt.']::text[], array['Tuck your feet underneath you and arch your back. Using the bar to help support your weight, lift your shoulder off the bench and retract them, squeezing the shoulder blades together. Use your feet to drive your traps into the bench. Maintain this tight body position throughout the movement.','You can take a standard bench grip, or shoulder width to focus on the triceps. Pull the bar out of the rack without protracting your shoulders. The bar, wrist, and elbow should stay in line at all times. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart.','Lower the bar to the boards, and then drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The elbows should be tucked in until lockout.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/board_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Board_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'close_grip_dumbbell_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'close_grip_dumbbell_press', 'Close-Grip Dumbbell Press', array['Bench Press (Close Grip Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Close-Grip Dumbbell Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the bench press: dumbbells pressed touching each other, which shifts work to the triceps.', array['Place a dumbbell standing up on a flat bench.']::text[], array['Ensuring that the dumbbell stays securely placed at the top of the bench, lie perpendicular to the bench with only your shoulders lying on the surface. Hips should be below the bench and your legs bent with your feet firmly on the floor.','Grasp the dumbbell with both hands and hold it straight over your chest at arm''s length. Both palms should be pressing against the underside of the sides of the dumbbell. This will be your starting position.','Initiate the movement by lowering the dumbbell to your chest.','Return to the starting position by extending the elbows.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/close_grip_dumbbell_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'close_grip_ez_bar_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'close_grip_ez_bar_press', 'Close-Grip EZ-Bar Press', array['Bench Press (Close Grip EZ Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Close-Grip EZ-Bar Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the bench press: eZ bar with a narrow grip, which shifts work to the triceps.', array['Lie on a flat bench with an EZ bar loaded to an appropriate weight.']::text[], array['Using a narrow grip lift the bar and hold it straight over your torso with your elbows in. The arms should be perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position.','Now lower the bar down to your lower chest as you breathe in. Keep the elbows in as you perform this movement.','Using the triceps to push the bar back up, press it back to the starting position by extending the elbows as you exhale.','Repeat.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/close_grip_ez_bar_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Close-Grip_EZ-Bar_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'pin_presses')::uuid, 'mfd', 'pin_presses', 'Pin Presses', array['Bench Press (Pin Press)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pin Presses is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest, forearms, lats and upper back. A variation of the bench press: pressing from safety pins set just above the chest, starting from a dead stop.', array['Pin presses remove the eccentric phase of the bench press, developing starting strength. They also allow you to train a desired range of motion.']::text[], array['The bench should be set up in a power rack. Set the pins to the desired point in your range of motion, whether it just be lockout or an inch off of your chest. The bar should be moved to the pins and prepared for lifting.','Begin by lying on the bench, with the bar directly above the contact point during your regular bench. Tuck your feet underneath you and arch your back. Using the bar to help support your weight, lift your shoulder off the bench and retract them, squeezing the shoulder blades together. Use your feet to drive your traps into the bench. Maintain this tight body position throughout the movement.','You can take a standard bench grip, or shoulder width to focus on the triceps. The bar, wrist, and elbow should stay in line at all times. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart.','Drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The elbows should be tucked in until lockout.','Return the bar to the pins, pausing before beginning the next repetition.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/pin_presses/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Pin_Presses/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_band_bench_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_band_bench_press', 'Reverse Band Bench Press', array['Bench Press (Reverse Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Band Bench Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest, forearms, lats and upper back. A variation of the bench press: bands from the top of the rack help most at the chest and less at lockout.', array['Position a bench inside a power rack, with the bar set to the correct height. Begin by anchoring bands either to band pegs or to the top of the rack. Ensure that you will be position properly under the bands. Attach the other end to the barbell.']::text[], array['Lie on the bench, tuck your feet underneath you and arch your back. Using the bar to help support your weight, lift your shoulder off the bench and retract them, squeezing the shoulder blades together. Use your feet to drive your traps into the bench. Maintain this tight body position throughout the movement. However wide your grip, it should cover the ring on the bar.','Pull the bar out of the rack without protracting your shoulders. Focus on squeezing the bar and trying to pull it apart. Lower the bar to your lower chest or upper stomach. The bar, wrist, and elbow should stay in line at all times.','Pause when the barbell touches your torso, and then drive the bar up with as much force as possible. The elbows should be tucked in until lockout.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_band_bench_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Band_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_triceps_bench_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_triceps_bench_press', 'Reverse Triceps Bench Press', array['Bench Press (Reverse Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Triceps Bench Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the bench press: underhand grip; works the triceps and upper chest. Use a spotter.', array['Lie back on a flat bench. Using a close, supinated grip (around shoulder width), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms locked extended in front of you and perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['As you breathe in, come down slowly until you feel the bar on your middle chest. Tip: Make sure that as opposed to a regular bench press, you keep the elbows close to the torso at all times in order to maximize triceps involvement.','After a second pause, bring the bar back to the starting position as you breathe out and push the bar using your triceps muscles. Lock your arms in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly again. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_triceps_bench_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Triceps_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'smith_machine_close_grip_bench_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'smith_machine_close_grip_bench_press', 'Smith Machine Close-Grip Bench Press', array['Bench Press (Smith, Close Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Smith Machine Close-Grip Bench Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the bench press: smith machine with a narrow grip, for the triceps.', array['Place a flat bench underneath the smith machine. Place the barbell at a height that you can reach when lying down and your arms are almost fully extended. Once the weight you need is selected, lie down on the flat bench. Using a close and pronated grip (palms facing forward) that is around shoulder width, unlock the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms locked. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['As you breathe in, come down slowly until you feel the bar on your middle chest. Tip: Make sure that as opposed to a regular bench press, you keep the elbows close to the torso at all times in order to maximize triceps involvement.','After a second pause, bring the bar back to the starting position as you breathe out and push the bar using your triceps muscles. Lock your arms in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down slowly again. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','When you are done, lock the bar back in the rack.']::text[], array['Shoulder blades stay pinched the whole set','Forearms vertical at the bottom','Push your feet into the floor','Weight travels from lower chest to over the shoulders']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows to 90°, which stresses the shoulders','Bouncing the weight off the chest','Lifting the hips off the bench','Letting the wrists bend back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/smith_machine_close_grip_bench_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Close-Grip_Bench_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'body_tricep_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'body_tricep_press', 'Body Tricep Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Body Tricep Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps.', array['Position a bar in a rack at chest height.']::text[], array['Standing, take a shoulder width grip on the bar and step a yard or two back, feet together and arms extended so that you are leaning on the bar. This will be your starting position.','Begin by flexing the elbow, lowering yourself towards the bar.','Pause, and then reverse the motion by extending the elbows.','Progress from bodyweight by adding chains over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Body in one straight line like a plank','Only the elbows move','Lower until the forearms touch, then press back up']::text[], array['Hips sagging','Pushing with the shoulders']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/body_tricep_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Body_Tricep_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'body_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'body_up', 'Body-Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Body-Up is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the abs & core and forearms.', array['Assume a plank position on the ground. You should be supporting your bodyweight on your toes and forearms, keeping your torso straight. Your forearms should be shoulder-width apart. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Pressing your palms firmly into the ground, extend through the elbows to raise your body from the ground. Keep your torso rigid as you perform the movement.','Slowly lower your forearms back to the ground by allowing the elbows to flex.','Repeat.']::text[], array['Body in one straight line like a plank','Only the elbows move','Lower until the forearms touch, then press back up']::text[], array['Hips sagging','Pushing with the shoulders']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/body_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Body-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'floor_press_with_chains')::uuid, 'mfd', 'floor_press_with_chains', 'Floor Press with Chains', array['Floor Press (Chains)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Floor Press with Chains is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the floor press: chains add load near lockout.', array['Adjust the j-hooks so they are at the appropriate height to rack the bar. For this exercise, drape the chains directly over the end of the bar, trying to keep the ends away from the plates.']::text[], array['Begin lying on the floor with your head near the end of a power rack. Keeping your shoulder blades pulled together, pull the bar off of the hooks.','Lower the bar towards the bottom of your chest or upper stomach, squeezing the bar and attempting to pull it apart as you do so. Ensure that you tuck your elbows throughout the movement. Lower the bar until your upper arm contacts the ground and pause, preventing any slamming or bouncing of the weight.','Press the bar back up as fast as you can, keeping the bar, your wrists, and elbows in line as you do so.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/floor_press_with_chains/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Floor_Press_with_Chains/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_floor_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_floor_press', 'One Arm Floor Press', array['Floor Press (Single Arm Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One Arm Floor Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the floor press: one hand in the middle of the bar; needs control to keep it level.', array['Lie down on a flat surface with your back pressing against the floor or an exercise mat. Make sure your knees are bent.']::text[], array['Have a partner hand you the bar on one hand. When starting, your arm should be just about fully extended, similar to the starting position of a barbell bench press. However, this time your grip will be neutral (palms facing your torso).','Make sure the hand you are not using to lift the weight is placed by your side.','Begin the exercise by lowering the barbell until your elbow touches the ground. Make sure to breathe in as this is the eccentric (lowering part of the exercise).','Then start lifting the barbell back up to the original starting position. Remember to breathe out during the concentric (lifting part of the exercise).','Repeat until you have performed your recommended repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Elbows about 45° from your body','Pause on the floor, do not bounce']::text[], array['Slamming the elbows into the floor','Flaring elbows straight out']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_floor_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Arm_Floor_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'floor_triceps_dip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'floor_triceps_dip', 'Floor Triceps Dip', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A small triceps dip sitting on the floor with hands behind you, lifting your hips by straightening your arms.', array['Sit on the floor, knees bent, hands on the floor behind you with fingers forward.','Lift your hips slightly.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower toward the floor.','Straighten them to push back up.']::text[], array['Elbows point back','Keep the hips lifted']::text[], array['Shrugging the shoulders']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'jm_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'jm_press', 'JM Press (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A hybrid of a close-grip bench press and a skullcrusher that lets you load the triceps heavily.', array['Lie on a bench with a shoulder-width grip on the bar, arms straight over your shoulders.']::text[], array['Lower the bar toward your chin/upper chest by bending the elbows and letting them travel slightly forward.','Stop when the forearms meet the upper arms.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Elbows stay tucked','Bar path to the upper chest/chin']::text[], array['Flaring the elbows','Going too heavy before learning the path']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/jm_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/JM_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'supine_chest_throw')::uuid, 'mfd', 'supine_chest_throw', 'Supine Chest Throw', '{}'::text[], 'plyometrics', 'weight_reps', 'Supine Chest Throw is a beginner-level plyometric exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest.', array['This drill is great for chest passes when you lack a partner or a wall of sufficient strength. Lay on the ground on your back with your knees bent.']::text[], array['Begin with the ball on your chest, held with both hands on the bottom.','Explode up, extending through the elbow to throw the ball directly above you as high as possible.','Catch the ball with both hands as it comes down.']::text[], array['Use the legs and hips first, the arms last','Throw as hard as you can; every rep is maximal','Use a light ball (2–5 kg) you can move fast','Reset fully between throws']::text[], array['Throwing with the arms only','Using a ball too heavy to move quickly','Rounding the back when picking up or catching']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/supine_chest_throw/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Supine_Chest_Throw/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kettlebell_overhead_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kettlebell_overhead_triceps_extension', 'Kettlebell Overhead Triceps Extension', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kettlebell Overhead Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the abs & core. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: one kettlebell held by the horns.', array['Stand with your feet hip-width apart, holding a kettlebell by the horns with both hands. Press it overhead until your arms are extended, with the bell hanging behind your hands.']::text[], array['Brace your abdominals and keep your upper arms vertical and close to your head. This is your starting position.','Bend at the elbows to lower the kettlebell behind your head, going as far as your shoulder mobility allows without your elbows flaring outward.','Extend your elbows to press the kettlebell back to the starting position, keeping your upper arms still throughout.','Keep your ribcage down and avoid arching your lower back as you extend.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'kneeling_cable_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'kneeling_cable_triceps_extension', 'Kneeling Cable Triceps Extension', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Cable, Kneeling)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Kneeling Cable Triceps Extension is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: kneeling with the upper arms on a bench, facing away from a high pulley.', array['Place a bench sideways in front of a high pulley machine.']::text[], array['Hold a straight bar attachment above your head with your hands about 6 inches apart with your palms facing down.','Face away from the machine and kneel.','Place your head and the back of your upper arms on the bench. Your elbows should be bent with the forearms pointing towards the high pulley. This will be your starting position.','While keeping your upper arms close to your head at all times with the elbows in, press the bar out in a semicircular motion until the elbows are locked and your arms are parallel to the floor. Contract the triceps hard and keep this position for a second. Exhale as you perform this movement.','Slowly return to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/kneeling_cable_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Kneeling_Cable_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'low_cable_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'low_cable_triceps_extension', 'Low Cable Triceps Extension', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Cable, Low Pulley)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Low Cable Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: facing away from a low pulley.', array['Select the desired weight and lay down face up on the bench of a seated row machine that has a rope attached to it. Your head should be pointing towards the attachment.']::text[], array['Grab the outside of the rope ends with your palms facing each other (neutral grip).','Position your elbows so that they are bent at a 90 degree angle and your upper arms are perpendicular (90 degree angle) to your torso. Tip: Keep the elbows in and make sure that the upper arms point to the ceiling while your forearms point towards the pulley above your head. This will be your starting position.','As you breathe out, extend your lower arms until they are straight and vertical. The upper arms and elbows remain stationary throughout the movement. Only the forearms should move. Contract the triceps hard for a second.','As you breathe in slowly return to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/low_cable_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Low_Cable_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps_extension_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps_extension_cable', 'Overhead Triceps Extension (Cable)', array['overhead extension','french press','cable overhead extension']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straightening the arms overhead. With the arms up, the long head of the triceps is stretched and works hard.', array['Attach a rope to a low or mid pulley.','Face away from the stack, step forward and hold the rope behind your head.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower the weight behind your head.','Go as low as is comfortable to feel a stretch in the triceps.','Straighten your arms back overhead.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_triceps_extension_cable/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Rope_Overhead_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_triceps_press_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_triceps_press_dumbbell', 'Seated Triceps Press', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Seated Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated Triceps Press is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: one dumbbell in both hands, seated.', array['Sit down on a bench with back support and grasp a dumbbell with both hands and hold it overhead at arm''s length. Tip: a better way is to have somebody hand it to you especially if it is very heavy. The resistance should be resting in the palms of your hands with your thumbs around it. The palm of the hand should be facing inward. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping your upper arms close to your head (elbows in) and perpendicular to the floor, lower the resistance in a semi-circular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Tip: The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Breathe in as you perform this step.','Go back to the starting position by using the triceps to raise the dumbbell. Breathe out as you perform this step.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_triceps_press_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Triceps_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps_extension_single_arm_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps_extension_single_arm_dumbbell', 'Single Arm Tricep Extension (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straightening the arms overhead. With the arms up, the long head of the triceps is stretched and works hard.', array['Hold the weight overhead with arms straight and elbows pointing forward.','Brace your core so your lower back does not arch.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower the weight behind your head.','Go as low as is comfortable to feel a stretch in the triceps.','Straighten your arms back overhead.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_triceps_extension_single_arm_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sled_overhead_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sled_overhead_triceps_extension', 'Sled Overhead Triceps Extension', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Sled)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Sled Overhead Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: facing away from a sled, extending overhead and walking it back.', array['Attach dual handles to a sled using a chain or rope. Load the sled to an appropriate load.']::text[], array['Facing away from the sled, step away until there is tension in the line. Raise your hands above your head, keeping them together, palms facing each other. Your elbows should be pointed upward with the elbows flexed. This will be your starting position.','Extend through the elbow to straighten the arm. Ensure that your upper arm stays in position to isolate the triceps.','Upon full extension, step forward to take the slack out of the line. You may keep your feet staggered for more stability.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sled_overhead_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sled_Overhead_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'speed_band_overhead_triceps')::uuid, 'mfd', 'speed_band_overhead_triceps', 'Speed Band Overhead Triceps', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Band, Speed)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Speed Band Overhead Triceps is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: band anchored behind, fast reps.', array['For this exercise anchor a band to the ground. We used an incline bench and anchored the band to the base, standing over the bench. Alternatively, this could be performed standing on the band.']::text[], array['To begin, pull the band behind your head, holding it with a pronated grip and your elbows up. This will be your starting position.','To perform the movement, extend through the elbow to to straighten your arms, ensuring that you keep your upper arm in place.','Pause, and then return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/speed_band_overhead_triceps/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Speed_Band_Overhead_Triceps/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_low_pulley_one_arm_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_low_pulley_one_arm_triceps_extension', 'Standing Low-Pulley One-Arm Triceps Extension', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Cable, Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Low-Pulley One-Arm Triceps Extension is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: one arm, facing away from a low pulley.', array['Grab a single handle with your left arm next to the low pulley machine. Turn away from the machine keeping the handle to the side of your body with your arm fully extended. Now use both hands to elevate the single handle directly above the head with the palm facing forward. Keep your upper arm completely vertical (perpendicular to the floor) and put your right hand on your left elbow to help keep it steady. This is the starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping your upper arms close to your head (elbows in) and perpendicular to the floor, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Tip: The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Breathe in as you perform this step.','Go back to the starting position by using the triceps to raise the single handle. Breathe out as you perform this step.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the exercise.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_low_pulley_one_arm_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Low-Pulley_One-Arm_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_towel_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_towel_triceps_extension', 'Standing Towel Triceps Extension', array['Overhead Triceps Extension (Towel, Partner)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Standing Towel Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the overhead triceps extension: a partner resists a towel held behind the head.', array['To begin, stand up with both arms fully extended above the head holding one end of a towel with both hands. Your elbows should be in and the arms perpendicular to the floor with the palms facing each other while your feet should be shoulder width apart from each other. This is the starting position.']::text[], array['Now communicate with your partner so that he/she can grip the other side of the towel to apply resistance. Keeping your upper arms close to your head (elbows in) and perpendicular to the floor, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Tip: The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Breathe in as you perform this step.','Go back to the starting position by using the triceps to raise the towel. Breathe out as you perform this step.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_towel_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Towel_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps_extension_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps_extension_barbell', 'Triceps Extension (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straightening the arms overhead. With the arms up, the long head of the triceps is stretched and works hard.', array['Sit on an upright bench holding an EZ bar or barbell overhead with a narrow overhand grip.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower the weight behind your head.','Go as low as is comfortable to feel a stretch in the triceps.','Straighten your arms back overhead.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_triceps_extension_barbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Overhead_Barbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps_extension_cable_generic')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps_extension_cable_generic', 'Triceps Extension (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straightening the arms overhead. With the arms up, the long head of the triceps is stretched and works hard.', array['Hold the weight overhead with arms straight and elbows pointing forward.','Brace your core so your lower back does not arch.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower the weight behind your head.','Go as low as is comfortable to feel a stretch in the triceps.','Straighten your arms back overhead.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps_extension_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps_extension_dumbbell', 'Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straightening the arms overhead. With the arms up, the long head of the triceps is stretched and works hard.', array['Sit or stand holding one dumbbell overhead with both hands cupped under the top plate.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower the weight behind your head.','Go as low as is comfortable to feel a stretch in the triceps.','Straighten your arms back overhead.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_triceps_extension_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps_extension_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps_extension_machine', 'Triceps Extension (Machine)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated machine triceps extension; depending on the machine the arms are in front of you or overhead.', array['Adjust the seat so your elbows line up with the machine pivot.','Rest your upper arms on the pad and grip the handles.']::text[], array['Straighten your arms against the resistance.','Squeeze the triceps.','Bend the elbows slowly back to the start.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/overhead_triceps_extension_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Machine_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'overhead_triceps_extension_suspension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'overhead_triceps_extension_suspension', 'Triceps Extension (Suspension)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Straightening the arms overhead. With the arms up, the long head of the triceps is stretched and works hard.', array['Face away from the anchor holding the handles in front of your forehead, leaning forward.']::text[], array['Bend the elbows so your head moves toward the handles.','Straighten your arms to push back to the start.']::text[], array['Elbows point forward, not out','Upper arms stay still','Ribs down']::text[], array['Elbows flaring wide','Arching the lower back']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'close_grip_push_up_off_of_a_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'close_grip_push_up_off_of_a_dumbbell', 'Close-Grip Push-Up off of a Dumbbell', array['Push Up (Close Grip on Dumbbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Close-Grip Push-Up off of a Dumbbell is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the abs & core and chest. A variation of the push up: both hands on one dumbbell, for the triceps.', array['Lie on the floor and place your hands on an upright dumbbell. Supporting your weight on your toes and hands, keep your torso rigid and your elbows in with your arms straight. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Lower your body, allowing the elbows to flex while you inhale. Keep your body straight, not allowing your hips to rise or sag.','Press yourself back up to the starting position by extending the elbows. Breathe out as you perform this step.','After a pause at the contracted position, repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/close_grip_push_up_off_of_a_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Push-Up_off_of_a_Dumbbell/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'push_up_diamond')::uuid, 'mfd', 'push_up_diamond', 'Diamond Push Up', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'The classic bodyweight press. It trains the chest, shoulders and triceps while the core holds the body straight.', array['Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than shoulder width, under or just outside your shoulders.','Step your feet back so your body forms a straight line from head to heels.','Squeeze your glutes and brace your core.']::text[], array['Lower your body as one unit until your chest is a few centimetres from the floor.','Keep your elbows about 45° from your body.','Push the floor away until your arms are straight.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_push_up_close_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_push_up_close_grip', 'Incline Push-Up Close-Grip', array['Push Up (Incline, Close Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Incline Push-Up Close-Grip is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the push up: hands on a raised surface, close together.', array['Stand facing a Smith machine bar or sturdy elevated platform at an appropriate height.']::text[], array['Place your hands next to one another on the bar.','Position your feet back from the bar with arms and body straight. This will be your starting position.','Keeping your body straight, lower your chest to the bar by bending the arms.','Return to the starting position by extending the elbows, pressing yourself back up.']::text[], array['Body stays one straight plank','Elbows point back, not out','Push the floor away at the top']::text[], array['Hips sagging or piking up','Head dropping forward','Doing half reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_push_up_close_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Push-Up_Close-Grip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_dip_machine')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_dip_machine', 'Seated Dip Machine', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated machine that copies the dip movement, pushing handles down beside your body.', array['Adjust the seat so the handles are at about chest height beside you.','Sit tall and grip the handles.']::text[], array['Push the handles down until your arms are straight.','Return slowly until your elbows are bent about 90°.']::text[], array['Elbows point back','Shoulders down']::text[], array['Leaning forward','Letting the stack slam']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_dip_machine/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dip_Machine/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_triceps_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_triceps_press', 'Seated Triceps Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A machine triceps extension done seated, pressing pads or handles by straightening the elbows.', array['Adjust the seat so your elbows line up with the machine pivot.','Rest your upper arms on the pad.']::text[], array['Straighten your arms against the resistance.','Return slowly.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay on the pad']::text[], array['Using the shoulders to push']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'band_skull_crusher')::uuid, 'mfd', 'band_skull_crusher', 'Band Skull Crusher', array['Skullcrusher (Band)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Band Skull Crusher is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: lying on a band anchored behind the head.', array['Secure a band to the base of a rack or the bench. Lay on the bench so that the band is lined up with your head.']::text[], array['Take hold of the band, raising your elbows so that the upper arm is perpendicular to the floor. With the elbow flexed, the band should be above your head. This will be your starting position.','Extend through the elbow to straighten your arm, keeping your upper arm in place. Pause at the top of the motion, and return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/band_skull_crusher/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Band_Skull_Crusher/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_incline_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_incline_triceps_extension', 'Cable Incline Triceps Extension', array['Skullcrusher (Cable, Incline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Incline Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: lying on an incline bench facing away from a low pulley.', array['Lie on incline an bench facing away from a high pulley machine that has a straight bar attachment on it.']::text[], array['Grasp the straight bar attachment overhead with a pronated (overhand; palms down) narrow grip (less than shoulder width) and keep your elbows tucked in to your sides. Your upper arms should create around a 25 degree angle when measured from the floor.','Keeping the upper arms stationary, extend the arms as you flex the triceps. Breathe out during this portion of the movement and hold the contraction for a second.','Slowly go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_incline_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Incline_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_lying_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_lying_triceps_extension', 'Cable Lying Triceps Extension', array['Skullcrusher (Cable)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable Lying Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: lying on a bench with the head toward a low pulley.', array['Lie on a flat bench and grasp the straight bar attachment of a low pulley with a narrow overhand grip. Tip: The easiest way to do this is to have someone hand you the bar as you lay down.']::text[], array['With your arms extended, position the bar over your torso. Your arms and your torso should create a 90-degree angle. This will be your starting position.','Lower the bar by bending at the elbow while keeping the upper arms stationary and elbows in. Go down until the bar lightly touches your forehead. Breathe in as you perform this portion of the movement.','Flex the triceps as you lift the bar back to its starting position. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement.','Hold for a second at the contracted position and repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_lying_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_Lying_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chain_handle_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chain_handle_extension', 'Chain Handle Extension', array['Skullcrusher (Chain Handles)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Chain Handle Extension is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: chains clipped to handles; extend from elbows pointing up.', array['You will need two cable handle attachments and a flat bench, as well as chains, for this exercise. Clip the middle of the chains to the handles, and position yourself on the flat bench. Your elbows should be pointing straight up.']::text[], array['Begin by extending through the elbow, keeping your upper arm still, with your wrists pronated.','Pause at the lockout, and reverse the motion to return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chain_handle_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Chain_Handle_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'decline_close_grip_bench_to_skull_crusher')::uuid, 'mfd', 'decline_close_grip_bench_to_skull_crusher', 'Decline Close-Grip Bench To Skull Crusher', array['Skullcrusher (Decline Press Combo)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Decline Close-Grip Bench To Skull Crusher is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest. A variation of the skullcrusher: alternates close-grip presses and skull crushers on a decline bench.', array['Secure your legs at the end of the decline bench and slowly lay down on the bench.']::text[], array['Using a close grip (a grip that is slightly less than shoulder width), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms locked and elbows in. The arms should be perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position. Tip: In order to protect your rotator cuff, it is best if you have a spotter help you lift the barbell off the rack.','Now lower the bar down to your lower chest as you breathe in. Keep the elbows in as you perform this movement.','Using the triceps to push the bar back up, press it back to the starting position as you exhale.','As you breathe in and you keep the upper arms stationary, bring the bar down slowly by moving your forearms in a semicircular motion towards you until you feel the bar slightly touch your forehead. Breathe in as you perform this portion of the movement.','Lift the bar back to the starting position by contracting the triceps and exhaling.','Repeat steps 3-6 until the recommended amount of repetitions is performed.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/decline_close_grip_bench_to_skull_crusher/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Decline_Close-Grip_Bench_To_Skull_Crusher/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'decline_dumbbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'decline_dumbbell_triceps_extension', 'Decline Dumbbell Triceps Extension', array['Skullcrusher (Dumbbell, Decline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Decline Dumbbell Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: dumbbells on a decline bench.', array['Secure your legs at the end of the decline bench and lie down with a dumbbell on each hand on top of your thighs. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.']::text[], array['Once you are laying down, move the dumbbells in front of you at shoulder width. The palms of the hands should be facing each other and the arms should be perpendicular to the floor and fully extended. This will be your starting position.','As you breathe in and you keep the upper arms stationary (and elbows in), bring the dumbbells down slowly by moving your forearms in a semicircular motion towards you until your thumbs are next to your ears. Breathe in as you perform this portion of the movement.','Lift the dumbbells back to the starting position by contracting the triceps and exhaling.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/decline_dumbbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Decline_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'decline_ez_bar_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'decline_ez_bar_triceps_extension', 'Decline EZ Bar Triceps Extension', array['Skullcrusher (EZ Bar, Decline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Decline EZ Bar Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: eZ bar on a decline bench.', array['Secure your legs at the end of the decline bench and slowly lay down on the bench.']::text[], array['Using a close grip (a grip that is slightly less than shoulder width), lift the EZ bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with your arms locked and elbows in. The arms should be perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position. Tip: In order to protect your rotator cuff, it is best if you have a spotter help you lift the barbell off the rack.','As you breathe in and you keep the upper arms stationary, bring the bar down slowly by moving your forearms in a semicircular motion towards you until you feel the bar slightly touch your forehead. Breathe in as you perform this portion of the movement.','Lift the bar back to the starting position by contracting the triceps and exhaling.','Repeat until the recommended amount of repetitions is performed.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/decline_ez_bar_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Decline_EZ_Bar_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'dumbbell_tricep_extension_pronated_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'dumbbell_tricep_extension_pronated_grip', 'Dumbbell Tricep Extension -Pronated Grip', array['Skullcrusher (Dumbbell, Palms Down)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Dumbbell Tricep Extension -Pronated Grip is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: dumbbells with palms facing down.', array['Lie down on a flat bench holding two dumbbells directly above your shoulders. Your arms should be fully extended and form a 90 degree angle from your torso and the floor.']::text[], array['The palms of your hands should be facing forward, and your elbows should be tucked in. This will be your starting position.','Now, inhale and slowly lower the dumbbells until they are near your ears. Be sure to keep your upper arms stationary and your elbows tucked in.','Then, exhale and use your triceps to return the weight to the starting position.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/dumbbell_tricep_extension_pronated_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Tricep_Extension_-Pronated_Grip/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'ez_bar_skullcrusher')::uuid, 'mfd', 'ez_bar_skullcrusher', 'EZ-Bar Skullcrusher', array['Skullcrusher (EZ Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'EZ-Bar Skullcrusher is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the forearms. A variation of the skullcrusher: eZ bar.', array['Using a close grip, lift the EZ bar and hold it with your elbows in as you lie on the bench. Your arms should be perpendicular to the floor. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping the upper arms stationary, lower the bar by allowing the elbows to flex. Inhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Pause once the bar is directly above the forehead.','Lift the bar back to the starting position by extending the elbow and exhaling.','Repeat.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/ez_bar_skullcrusher/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/EZ-Bar_Skullcrusher/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_barbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_barbell_triceps_extension', 'Incline Barbell Triceps Extension', array['Skullcrusher (Incline)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Incline Barbell Triceps Extension is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the forearms. A variation of the skullcrusher: on an incline bench, bar lowered behind the head.', array['Hold a barbell with an overhand grip (palms down) that is a little closer together than shoulder width.']::text[], array['Lie back on an incline bench set at any angle between 45-75-degrees.','Bring the bar overhead with your arms extended and elbows in. The arms should be in line with the torso above the head. This will be your starting position.','Now lower the bar in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Inhale as you perform this movement. Tip: Keep your upper arms stationary and close to your head at all times. Only the forearms should move.','Return to the starting position as you breathe out and you contract the triceps. Hold the contraction for a second.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_barbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Barbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_close_grip_barbell_triceps_extension_behind_the_head')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_close_grip_barbell_triceps_extension_behind_the_head', 'Lying Close-Grip Barbell Triceps Extension Behind The Head', array['Skullcrusher (Behind the Head)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying Close-Grip Barbell Triceps Extension Behind The Head is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: bar lowered behind the head for a bigger stretch.', array['While holding a barbell or EZ Curl bar with a pronated grip (palms facing forward), lie on your back on a flat bench with your head close to the end of the bench. Tip: If you are holding a barbell grab it using a shoulder-width grip and if you are using an E-Z Bar grab it on the inner handles.']::text[], array['Extend your arms in front of you and slowly bring the bar back in a semi circular motion (while keeping the arms extended) to a position over your head. At the end of this step your arms should be overhead and parallel to the floor. This will be your starting position. Tip: Keep your elbows in at all times.','As you inhale, lower the bar by bending at the elbows and while keeping the upper arm stationary. Keep lowering the bar until your forearms are perpendicular to the floor.','As you exhale bring the bar back up to the starting position by pushing the bar up in a semi-circular motion until the lower arms are also parallel to the floor. Contract the triceps hard at the top of the movement for a second. Tip: Again, only the forearms should move. The upper arms should remain stationary at all times.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_close_grip_barbell_triceps_extension_behind_the_head/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Close-Grip_Barbell_Triceps_Extension_Behind_The_Head/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_close_grip_barbell_triceps_press_to_chin')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_close_grip_barbell_triceps_press_to_chin', 'Lying Close-Grip Barbell Triceps Press To Chin', array['Skullcrusher (Press to Chin)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying Close-Grip Barbell Triceps Press To Chin is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: eZ bar lowered toward the chin.', array['While holding a barbell or EZ Curl bar with a pronated grip (palms facing forward), lie on your back on a flat bench with your head off the end of the bench. Tip: If you are holding a barbell grab it using a shoulder-width grip and if you are using an E-Z Bar grab it on the inner handles.']::text[], array['Extend your arms in front of you as you hold the barbell over your chest. The arms should be perpendicular to your torso (90-degree angle). This will be your starting position.','As you inhale, lower the bar in a semi-circular motion by bending at the elbows and while keeping the upper arm stationary and elbows in. Keep lowering the bar until it lightly touches your chin.','As you exhale bring the bar back up to the starting position by pushing the bar up in a semi-circular motion. Contract the triceps hard at the top of the movement for a second. Tip: Again, only the forearms should move. The upper arms should remain stationary at all times.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_close_grip_barbell_triceps_press_to_chin/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Close-Grip_Barbell_Triceps_Press_To_Chin/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_triceps_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_triceps_press', 'Lying Triceps Press', array['Skullcrusher (Lying Triceps Press)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying Triceps Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: eZ bar lowered to the forehead.', array['Lie on a flat bench with either an e-z bar (my preference) or a straight bar placed on the floor behind your head and your feet on the floor.']::text[], array['Grab the bar behind you, using a medium overhand (pronated) grip, and raise the bar in front of you at arms length. Tip: The arms should be perpendicular to the torso and the floor. The elbows should be tucked in. This is the starting position.','As you breathe in, slowly lower the weight until the bar lightly touches your forehead while keeping the upper arms and elbows stationary.','At that point, use the triceps to bring the weight back up to the starting position as you breathe out.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_triceps_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Triceps_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_pronated_dumbbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_pronated_dumbbell_triceps_extension', 'One Arm Pronated Dumbbell Triceps Extension', array['Skullcrusher (Single Arm, Palm Down)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One Arm Pronated Dumbbell Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: one dumbbell, lowered across the body.', array['Lie flat on a bench while holding a dumbbell at arms length. Your arm should be perpendicular to your body. The palm of your hand should be facing towards your feet as a pronated grip is required to perform this exercise.']::text[], array['Place your non lifting hand on your bicep for support.','Slowly begin to lower the dumbbell down as you breathe in.','Then, begin lifting the dumbbell upward as you contract the triceps. Remember to breathe out during the concentric (lifting part of the exercise).','Repeat until you have performed your set repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_pronated_dumbbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Arm_Pronated_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_supinated_dumbbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_supinated_dumbbell_triceps_extension', 'One Arm Supinated Dumbbell Triceps Extension', array['Skullcrusher (Single Arm, Palm Up)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One Arm Supinated Dumbbell Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the skullcrusher: one dumbbell, palm facing the head.', array['Lie flat on a bench while holding a dumbbell at arms length. Your arm should be perpendicular to your body. The palm of your hand should be facing towards your face as a supinated grip is required to perform this exercise.']::text[], array['Place your non lifting hand on your bicep for support.','Slowly begin to lower the dumbbell down as you breathe in.','Then, begin lifting the dumbbell upward as you contract the triceps. Remember to breathe out during the concentric (lifting part of the exercise).','Repeat until you have performed your set repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the movement.','Switch arms again and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_supinated_dumbbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Arm_Supinated_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'skullcrusher_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'skullcrusher_barbell', 'Skullcrusher (Barbell)', array['lying triceps extension']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying on a bench and lowering a weight toward your forehead by bending only the elbows.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding the weight above your chest with straight arms.','Tilt the arms slightly back toward your head.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower the weight toward your forehead or just behind your head.','Straighten your arms back to the start.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'skullcrusher_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'skullcrusher_dumbbell', 'Skullcrusher (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying on a bench and lowering a weight toward your forehead by bending only the elbows.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding the weight above your chest with straight arms.','Tilt the arms slightly back toward your head.']::text[], array['Bend your elbows to lower the weight toward your forehead or just behind your head.','Straighten your arms back to the start.']::text[], array['Upper arms stay still, tilted slightly back','Elbows point to the ceiling, not out']::text[], array['Elbows flaring','Turning it into a press by moving the upper arms']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/skullcrusher_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Dumbbell_Tricep_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'tate_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'tate_press', 'Tate Press', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Tate Press is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps, with help from the chest.', array['Lie down on a flat bench with a dumbbell in each hand on top of your thighs. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.']::text[], array['By using your thighs to help you get the dumbbells up, clean the dumbbells one arm at a time so that you can hold them in front of you at shoulder width. Note: when holding the dumbbells in front of you, make sure your arms are wider than shoulder width apart from each other using a pronated (palms forward) grip. Allow your elbows to point out. This is your starting position.','Keeping the upper arms stationary, slowly move the dumbbells in and down in a semi circular motion until they touch the upper chest while inhaling. Keep full control of the dumbbells at all times and do not move the upper arms nor rest the dumbbells on the chest.','As you breathe out, move the dumbbells up using your triceps and the same semi-circular motion but in reverse. Attempt to keep the dumbbells together as they move up. Lock your arms in the contracted position, hold for a second and then start coming down again slowly again. Tip: It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.']::text[], array['Dumbbells touch over the chest, elbows out','Lower the dumbbells to the chest by bending the elbows outward','Press back up']::text[], array['Using too much weight','Letting the dumbbells roll away']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/tate_press/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Tate_Press/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_dip_bodyweight')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_dip_bodyweight', 'Triceps Dip', array['dip']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'A dip on parallel bars with an upright torso, which puts most of the work on the triceps.', array['Support yourself on parallel bars with straight arms.','Keep your torso upright and legs under you.']::text[], array['Lower yourself by bending the elbows, keeping them pointing back.','Stop when your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Torso stays upright','Elbows point straight back']::text[], array['Leaning forward (turns it into a chest dip)','Dropping too deep']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_dip_bodyweight/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dips_-_Triceps_Version/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_dip_assisted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_dip_assisted', 'Triceps Dip (Assisted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'assisted_bodyweight', 'A dip on parallel bars with an upright torso, which puts most of the work on the triceps.', array['Support yourself on parallel bars with straight arms.','Keep your torso upright and legs under you.']::text[], array['Lower yourself by bending the elbows, keeping them pointing back.','Stop when your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Torso stays upright','Elbows point straight back']::text[], array['Leaning forward (turns it into a chest dip)','Dropping too deep']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_dip_weighted')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_dip_weighted', 'Triceps Dip (Weighted)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weighted_bodyweight', 'A dip on parallel bars with an upright torso, which puts most of the work on the triceps.', array['Support yourself on parallel bars with straight arms.','Keep your torso upright and legs under you.']::text[], array['Lower yourself by bending the elbows, keeping them pointing back.','Stop when your upper arms are about parallel to the floor.','Press back up to straight arms.']::text[], array['Torso stays upright','Elbows point straight back']::text[], array['Leaning forward (turns it into a chest dip)','Dropping too deep']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_dip_weighted/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dips_-_Triceps_Version/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_bent_over_one_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_bent_over_one_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension', 'Seated Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', array['Triceps Kickback (Seated, Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the triceps kickback: seated and bent over, one arm.', array['Sit down at the end of a flat bench with a dumbbell in one arm using a neutral grip (palms of the hand facing you).']::text[], array['Bend your knees slightly and bring your torso forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to the floor. Make sure that you keep the head up.','The upper arm with the dumbbell should be close to the torso and aligned with it (lifted up until it is parallel to the floor while the forearms are pointing towards the floor as the hands hold the weights). Tip: There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearms and the upper arm. This is your starting position.','Keeping the upper arm stationary, use the triceps to lift the weight as you exhale until the forearm is parallel to the floor and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.','After a second contraction at the top, slowly lower the dumbbell back to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the exercise.']::text[], array['Upper arm stays parallel to the floor','Only the forearm moves']::text[], array['Letting the elbow drop','Swinging the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_bent_over_one_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_bent_over_two_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_bent_over_two_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension', 'Seated Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', array['Triceps Kickback (Seated, Two Arms)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Seated Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the triceps kickback: seated and bent over, both arms.', array['Sit down at the end of a flat bench with a dumbbell in both arms using a neutral grip (palms of the hand facing you).']::text[], array['Bend your knees slightly and bring your torso forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to the floor. Make sure that you keep the head up.','The upper arms with the dumbbells should be close to the torso and aligned with it (lifted up until they are parallel to the floor while the forearms are pointing towards the floor as the hands hold the weights). Tip: There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearms and the upper arm. This is your starting position.','Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the weight as you exhale until the forearms are parallel to the floor and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.','After a second contraction at the top, slowly lower the dumbbells back to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arm stays parallel to the floor','Only the forearm moves']::text[], array['Letting the elbow drop','Swinging the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/seated_bent_over_two_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_bent_over_one_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_bent_over_one_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension', 'Standing Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', array['Triceps Kickback (Standing, Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the triceps kickback: one arm, other hand on the knee.', array['With a dumbbell in one hand and the palm facing your torso, bend your knees slightly and bring your torso forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to the floor. Make sure that you keep the head up.']::text[], array['The upper arm should be close to the torso and parallel to the floor while the forearm is pointing towards the floor as the hand holds the weight. Tip: There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearm and the upper arm. This is your starting position.','Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the weights as you exhale until the forearms are parallel to the floor and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.','After a second contraction at the top, slowly lower the dumbbell back to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the exercise.']::text[], array['Upper arm stays parallel to the floor','Only the forearm moves']::text[], array['Letting the elbow drop','Swinging the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_bent_over_one_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Bent-Over_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'standing_bent_over_two_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'standing_bent_over_two_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension', 'Standing Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', array['Triceps Kickback (Standing, Two Arms)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Standing Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the triceps kickback: both arms together.', array['With a dumbbell in each hand and the palms facing your torso, bend your knees slightly and bring your torso forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to the floor. Make sure that you keep the head up. The upper arms should be close to the torso and parallel to the floor while the forearms are pointing towards the floor as the hands hold the weights. Tip: There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearms and the upper arm. This is your starting position.']::text[], array['Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the weights as you exhale until the forearms are parallel to the floor and the whole arms are extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.','After a second contraction at the top, slowly lower the dumbbells back to their starting position as you inhale.','Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Upper arm stays parallel to the floor','Only the forearm moves']::text[], array['Letting the elbow drop','Swinging the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/standing_bent_over_two_arm_dumbbell_triceps_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Standing_Bent-Over_Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_kickback_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_kickback_cable', 'Triceps Kickback (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent forward with the upper arm held parallel to the floor, you straighten the elbow to "kick" the weight back.', array['Hinge forward (or support yourself on a bench) with a flat back.','Raise your upper arm so it is parallel to the floor, elbow bent 90°.']::text[], array['Straighten your arm back until it is fully extended.','Squeeze the triceps.','Bend back to 90° slowly.']::text[], array['Upper arm stays parallel to the floor','Only the forearm moves']::text[], array['Letting the elbow drop','Swinging the weight']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_kickback_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_kickback_dumbbell', 'Triceps Kickback (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent forward with the upper arm held parallel to the floor, you straighten the elbow to "kick" the weight back.', array['Hinge forward (or support yourself on a bench) with a flat back.','Raise your upper arm so it is parallel to the floor, elbow bent 90°.']::text[], array['Straighten your arm back until it is fully extended.','Squeeze the triceps.','Bend back to 90° slowly.']::text[], array['Upper arm stays parallel to the floor','Only the forearm moves']::text[], array['Letting the elbow drop','Swinging the weight']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_kickback_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Tricep_Dumbbell_Kickback/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'cable_one_arm_tricep_extension')::uuid, 'mfd', 'cable_one_arm_tricep_extension', 'Cable One Arm Tricep Extension', array['Triceps Pushdown (Single Arm, Underhand)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Cable One Arm Tricep Extension is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the triceps pushdown: one handle, palm up.', array['With your right hand, grasp a single handle attached to the high-cable pulley using a supinated (underhand; palms facing up) grip. You should be standing directly in front of the weight stack.']::text[], array['Now pull the handle down so that your upper arm and elbow are locked in to the side of your body. Your upper arm and forearm should form an acute angle (less than 90-degrees). You can keep the other arm by the waist and you can have one leg in front of you and the other one back for better balance. This will be your starting position.','As you contract the triceps, move the single handle attachment down to your side until your arm is straight. Breathe out as you perform this movement. Tip: Only the forearms should move. Your upper arms should remain stationary at all times.','Squeeze the triceps and hold for a second in this contracted position.','Slowly return the handle to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and then perform the same movement with the other arm.']::text[], array['Elbows stay pinned to your sides','Only the forearms move']::text[], array['Elbows flaring and moving forward','Leaning over the weight and pushing with the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/cable_one_arm_tricep_extension/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Cable_One_Arm_Tricep_Extension/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_pushdown_reverse_grip')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_pushdown_reverse_grip', 'Reverse Grip Triceps Pushdown', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a cable handle down by straightening the elbows. The most common triceps exercise.', array['Attach a bar or rope to a high pulley.','Stand close, grip the attachment, elbows bent and tucked to your sides.']::text[], array['Push the handle down until your arms are straight.','Squeeze the triceps.','Let the handle rise until your forearms are just above parallel.']::text[], array['Elbows stay pinned to your sides','Only the forearms move']::text[], array['Elbows flaring and moving forward','Leaning over the weight and pushing with the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_pushdown_reverse_grip/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Grip_Triceps_Pushdown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_pushdown_single_arm')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_pushdown_single_arm', 'Single Arm Triceps Pushdown (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a cable handle down by straightening the elbows. The most common triceps exercise.', array['Attach a bar or rope to a high pulley.','Stand close, grip the attachment, elbows bent and tucked to your sides.']::text[], array['Push the handle down until your arms are straight.','Squeeze the triceps.','Let the handle rise until your forearms are just above parallel.']::text[], array['Elbows stay pinned to your sides','Only the forearms move']::text[], array['Elbows flaring and moving forward','Leaning over the weight and pushing with the body']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_pushdown_pressdown')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_pushdown_pressdown', 'Triceps Pressdown', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a cable handle down by straightening the elbows. The most common triceps exercise.', array['Attach a bar or rope to a high pulley.','Stand close, grip the attachment, elbows bent and tucked to your sides.']::text[], array['Push the handle down until your arms are straight.','Squeeze the triceps.','Let the handle rise until your forearms are just above parallel.']::text[], array['Elbows stay pinned to your sides','Only the forearms move']::text[], array['Elbows flaring and moving forward','Leaning over the weight and pushing with the body']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_pushdown')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_pushdown', 'Triceps Pushdown', array['tricep pushdown','cable pushdown','straight bar pushdown']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a cable handle down by straightening the elbows. The most common triceps exercise.', array['Attach a bar or rope to a high pulley.','Stand close, grip the attachment, elbows bent and tucked to your sides.']::text[], array['Push the handle down until your arms are straight.','Squeeze the triceps.','Let the handle rise until your forearms are just above parallel.']::text[], array['Elbows stay pinned to your sides','Only the forearms move']::text[], array['Elbows flaring and moving forward','Leaning over the weight and pushing with the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_pushdown/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_pushdown_v_bar_attachment')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_pushdown_v_bar_attachment', 'Triceps Pushdown - V-Bar Attachment', array['Triceps Pushdown (V-Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Triceps Pushdown - V-Bar Attachment is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the triceps. A variation of the triceps pushdown: v-bar attachment.', array['Attach a V-Bar to a high pulley and grab with an overhand grip (palms facing down) at shoulder width.']::text[], array['Standing upright with the torso straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to your body and perpendicular to the floor. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the bar. The thumbs should be higher than the small finger. This is your starting position.','Using the triceps, bring the bar down until it touches the front of your thighs and the arms are fully extended perpendicular to the floor. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torso and only the forearms should move. Exhale as you perform this movement.','After a second hold at the contracted position, bring the V-Bar slowly up to the starting point. Breathe in as you perform this step.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Elbows stay pinned to your sides','Only the forearms move']::text[], array['Elbows flaring and moving forward','Leaning over the weight and pushing with the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_pushdown_v_bar_attachment/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_V-Bar_Attachment/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'triceps_pushdown_rope')::uuid, 'mfd', 'triceps_pushdown_rope', 'Triceps Rope Pushdown', array['rope pushdown']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Pushing a cable handle down by straightening the elbows. The most common triceps exercise.', array['Attach a bar or rope to a high pulley.','Stand close, grip the attachment, elbows bent and tucked to your sides.']::text[], array['Push the handle down until your arms are straight.','Squeeze the triceps.','Let the handle rise until your forearms are just above parallel.']::text[], array['Elbows stay pinned to your sides','Only the forearms move']::text[], array['Elbows flaring and moving forward','Leaning over the weight and pushing with the body']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/triceps_pushdown_rope/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_Rope_Attachment/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'wide_elbow_triceps_press')::uuid, 'mfd', 'wide_elbow_triceps_press', 'Wide-Elbow Triceps Press (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying with dumbbells over the chest, elbows flared out, lowering the dumbbells toward the chest and pressing them up with the triceps.', array['Lie on a flat bench holding dumbbells over your chest, palms facing your feet.']::text[], array['Bend the elbows out to the sides, lowering the dumbbells to your chest.','Straighten the arms to press them back up.']::text[], array['Keep the upper arms still','Control the lowering']::text[], array['Turning it into a chest press','Bouncing the dumbbells off the chest']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'middle_back_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'middle_back_stretch', 'Middle Back Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Middle Back Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the abs & core, lats and lower back.', '{}'::text[], array['Stand so your feet are shoulder width apart and your hands are on your hips.','Twist at your waist until you feel a stretch. Hold for 10 to 15 seconds, then twist to the other side.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/middle_back_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Middle_Back_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'spinal_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'spinal_stretch', 'Spinal Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Spinal Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the lats, lower back, neck and traps.', array['Sit in a chair so your back is straight and your feet planted on the floor.']::text[], array['Interlace your fingers behind your head, elbows out and your chin down.','Twist your upper body to one side about 3 times as far as you can. Then lean forward and twist your torso to reach your elbow to the floor on the inside of your knee.','Return to upright position and then repeat for your other side.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/spinal_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Spinal_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'upper_back_stretch')::uuid, 'mfd', 'upper_back_stretch', 'Upper Back Stretch', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Upper Back Stretch is a beginner-level stretch that mainly targets the upper back.', '{}'::text[], array['Clasp fingers together with your thumbs pointing down, round your shoulders as you reach your hands forward.']::text[], array['Move slowly through the spine, one segment at a time','Stay in a comfortable range; this should feel easy','Hold 20–30 seconds, then repeat on the other side','Keep the rest of the body relaxed']::text[], array['Forcing the twist or bend','Moving fast','Holding the breath']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/upper_back_stretch/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Upper_Back_Stretch/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternating_kettlebell_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternating_kettlebell_row', 'Alternating Kettlebell Row', array['Bent Over Row (Kettlebell, Alternating)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating Kettlebell Row is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the bent over row: two kettlebells rowed one at a time.', array['Place two kettlebells in front of your feet. Bend your knees slightly and push your butt out as much as possible. As you bend over to get into the starting position grab both kettlebells by the handles.']::text[], array['Pull one kettlebell off of the floor while holding on to the other kettlebell. Retract the shoulder blade of the working side, as you flex the elbow, drawing the kettlebell towards your stomach or rib cage.','Lower the kettlebell in the working arm and repeat with your other arm.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternating_kettlebell_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternating_Kettlebell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_two_dumbbell_row_with_palms_in')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_two_dumbbell_row_with_palms_in', 'Bent Over Two-Dumbbell Row With Palms In', array['Bent Over Row (Dumbbell, Palms In)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent Over Two-Dumbbell Row With Palms In is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the bent over row: palms face each other.', array['With a dumbbell in each hand (palms facing each other), bend your knees slightly and bring your torso forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to the floor. Tip: Make sure that you keep the head up. The weights should hang directly in front of you as your arms hang perpendicular to the floor and your torso. This is your starting position.']::text[], array['While keeping the torso stationary, lift the dumbbells to your side as you breathe out, squeezing your shoulder blades together. On the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and hold for a second.','Slowly lower the weight again to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_two_dumbbell_row_with_palms_in/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Two-Dumbbell_Row_With_Palms_In/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'reverse_grip_bent_over_rows')::uuid, 'mfd', 'reverse_grip_bent_over_rows', 'Reverse Grip Bent-Over Rows', array['Bent Over Row (Reverse Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Reverse Grip Bent-Over Rows is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the bent over row: underhand grip; more lats and biceps.', array['Stand erect while holding a barbell with a supinated grip (palms facing up).']::text[], array['Bend your knees slightly and bring your torso forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to the floor. Tip: Make sure that you keep the head up. The barbell should hang directly in front of you as your arms hang perpendicular to the floor and your torso. This is your starting position.','While keeping the torso stationary, lift the barbell as you breathe out, keeping the elbows close to the body and not doing any force with the forearm other than holding the weights. On the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and hold for a second.','Slowly lower the weight again to the starting position as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/reverse_grip_bent_over_rows/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Reverse_Grip_Bent-Over_Rows/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'straight_bar_bench_mid_rows')::uuid, 'mfd', 'straight_bar_bench_mid_rows', 'Straight Bar Bench Mid Rows', array['Bent Over Row (Bench Mid Row)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Straight Bar Bench Mid Rows is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the bent over row: standing on a bench behind a bar resting on its end.', array['Place a loaded barbell on the end of a bench. Standing on the bench behind the bar, take a medium, pronated grip. Stand with your hips back and chest up, maintaining a neutral spine. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Row the bar to your torso by retracting the shoulder blades and flexing the elbows. Use a controlled movement with no jerking.','After a brief pause, slowly return the bar to the starting position, ensuring to go all the way down.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/straight_bar_bench_mid_rows/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Straight_Bar_Bench_Mid_Rows/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'two_arm_kettlebell_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'two_arm_kettlebell_row', 'Two-Arm Kettlebell Row', array['Bent Over Row (Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Two-Arm Kettlebell Row is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the bent over row: two kettlebells.', '{}'::text[], array['Place two kettlebells in front of your feet. Bend your knees slightly and then push your butt out as much as possible as you bend over to get in the starting position.','Grab both kettlebells and pull them to your stomach, retracting your shoulder blades and flexing the elbows. Keep your back straight. Lower and repeat.']::text[], array['Pull with the elbows, not the hands','Keep the back flat and the torso angle fixed','Chest proud']::text[], array['Standing up as you pull, turning it into a shrug','Rounding the lower back','Jerking the weight with momentum']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/two_arm_kettlebell_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_supported_row_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_supported_row_dumbbell', 'Chest Supported Incline Row (Dumbbell)', array['incline row']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A row with your chest resting on a support, which takes the lower back out of the exercise.', array['Set an incline bench to about 30–45° and lie face down with your chest on the pad.','Let your arms hang straight down holding the weight.']::text[], array['Row the weight up until your elbows pass your torso.','Squeeze the shoulder blades together.','Lower slowly to straight arms.']::text[], array['Chest stays on the pad','Lead with the elbows']::text[], array['Lifting the chest off the pad to cheat','Shrugging toward the ears']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_supported_row_dumbbell/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Incline_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'chest_supported_row_t_bar')::uuid, 'mfd', 'chest_supported_row_t_bar', 'Chest Supported T Bar Row', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A row with your chest resting on a support, which takes the lower back out of the exercise.', array['Set an incline bench to about 30–45° and lie face down with your chest on the pad.','Let your arms hang straight down holding the weight.']::text[], array['Row the weight up until your elbows pass your torso.','Squeeze the shoulder blades together.','Lower slowly to straight arms.']::text[], array['Chest stays on the pad','Lead with the elbows']::text[], array['Lifting the chest off the pad to cheat','Shrugging toward the ears']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/chest_supported_row_t_bar/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_T-Bar_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'incline_bench_pull')::uuid, 'mfd', 'incline_bench_pull', 'Incline Bench Pull', array['Chest Supported Row (Barbell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Incline Bench Pull is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the lats. A variation of the chest supported row: lying face down on an incline bench, rowing a barbell.', array['Grab a dumbbell in each hand and lie face down on an incline bench that is set to an incline that is approximately 30 degrees.']::text[], array['Let the arms hang to your sides fully extended as they point to the floor.','Turn the wrists until your hands have a pronated (palms down) grip.','Now flare the elbows out. This will be your starting position.','As you breathe out, start to pull the dumbbells up as if you are doing a reverse bench press. You will do this by bending at the elbows and bringing the upper arms up as you let the forearms hang. Continue this motion until the upper arms are at the same level as your back. Tip: The elbows will come out to the side and your upper arms and torso should make the letter "T" at the top of the movement. Hold the contraction at the top for a second.','Slowly go back down to the starting position as you breathe in.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Chest stays on the pad','Lead with the elbows']::text[], array['Lifting the chest off the pad to cheat','Shrugging toward the ears']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/incline_bench_pull/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Incline_Bench_Pull/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_chin_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_chin_up', 'One Arm Chin-Up', array['Chin Up (Single Arm)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'One Arm Chin-Up is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps, forearms and lats. A variation of the chin up: one hand on the bar; the other may hold the wrist for help. Very advanced.', array['For this exercise, start out by placing a towel around a chin up bar.']::text[], array['Grab the chin-up bar with your palm facing you. One hand will be grabbing the chin-up bar and the other will be grabbing the towel.','Bring your torso back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your chest out. This is your starting position.v','Pull your torso up until the bar touches your upper chest by drawing the shoulders and the upper arms down and back. Exhale as you perform this portion of the movement. Tip: Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torso should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.','After a second on the contracted position, start to inhale and slowly lower your torso back to the starting position when your arms are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.','Repeat this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.','Switch arms and repeat the movement.']::text[], array['Chest to the bar','Elbows close in front of the body','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Swinging','Stopping short of a full hang']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_chin_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One_Arm_Chin-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_kettlebell_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_kettlebell_row', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Row', array['Dumbbell Row (Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Kettlebell Row is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the dumbbell row: kettlebell instead of a dumbbell.', '{}'::text[], array['Place a kettlebell in front of your feet. Bend your knees slightly and then push your butt out as much as possible as you bend over to get in the starting position. Grab the kettlebell and pull it to your stomach, retracting your shoulder blade and flexing the elbow. Keep your back straight. Lower and repeat.']::text[], array['Pull toward the hip, not the shoulder','Keep the shoulders square to the floor']::text[], array['Twisting the torso to lift the weight','Shrugging the shoulder up to the ear','Cutting the stretch short']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_kettlebell_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Kettlebell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'rhomboids_smr')::uuid, 'mfd', 'rhomboids_smr', 'Rhomboids-SMR', '{}'::text[], 'mobility', 'time', 'Rhomboids-SMR is an intermediate-level self-massage (foam rolling) exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the traps.', '{}'::text[], array['Lay down with your back on the floor. Place a foam roll underneath your upper back, and cross your arms in front of you, protracting your shoulders. This will be your starting position.','Raise your hips off of the ground, placing your weight onto the foam roll. Shift your weight to one side at a time, rolling over your middle and upper back. Pause at points of tension for 10-30 seconds.']::text[], array['Roll slowly, about 2–3 cm per second','Pause 20–30 seconds on tender spots','Support your weight with hands and feet to control the pressure','30–90 seconds per area']::text[], array['Rolling fast back and forth','Rolling directly over joints or bones','Pressing so hard you tense up']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/rhomboids_smr/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Rhomboids-SMR/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bodyweight_mid_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bodyweight_mid_row', 'Bodyweight Mid Row', array['Inverted Row (Mid Row)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Bodyweight Mid Row is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the inverted row: rowing the body up to a bar or handles.', array['Begin by taking a medium to wide grip on a pull-up apparatus with your palms facing away from you. From a hanging position, tuck your knees to your chest, leaning back and getting your legs over your side of the pull-up apparatus. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Beginning with your arms straight, flex the elbows and retract the shoulder blades to raise your body up until your legs contact the pull-up apparatus.','After a brief pause, return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Body stays a straight plank','Lead with the chest']::text[], array['Hips sagging','Reaching with the chin instead of the chest']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bodyweight_mid_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Mid_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'suspended_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'suspended_row', 'Suspended Row', array['Low Row (Suspension) (Straps)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Suspended Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the low row (suspension): suspension straps.', array['Suspend your straps at around chest height. Take a handle in each hand and lean back. Keep your body erect and your head and chest up. Your arms should be fully extended. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Begin by flexing the elbow to initiate the movement. Protract your shoulder blades as you do so.','At the completion of the motion pause, and then return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Body stays rigid','Squeeze the shoulder blades at the top']::text[], array['Hips dropping','Letting the shoulders shrug']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/suspended_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Suspended_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_one_arm_long_bar_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_one_arm_long_bar_row', 'Bent Over One-Arm Long Bar Row', array['Meadows Row (Long Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent Over One-Arm Long Bar Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps, lats, lower back and traps. A variation of the meadows row: one hand on the end of a barbell anchored in a corner.', array['Put weight on one of the ends of an Olympic barbell. Make sure that you either place the other end of the barbell in the corner of two walls; or put a heavy object on the ground so the barbell cannot slide backward.']::text[], array['Bend forward until your torso is as close to parallel with the floor as you can and keep your knees slightly bent.','Now grab the bar with one arm just behind the plates on the side where the weight was placed and put your other hand on your knee. This will be your starting position.','Pull the bar straight up with your elbow in (to maximize back stimulation) until the plates touch your lower chest. Squeeze the back muscles as you lift the weight up and hold for a second at the top of the movement. Breathe out as you lift the weight. Tip: Do not allow for any swinging of the torso. Only the arm should move.','Slowly lower the bar to the starting position getting a nice stretch on the lats. Tip: Do not let the plates touch the floor. To ensure the best range of motion, I recommend using small plates (25-lb ones) as opposed to larger plates (like 35-45lb ones).','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions and switch arms.']::text[], array['Elbow travels high and back','Keep the hips square']::text[], array['Twisting the torso','Shortening the range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_one_arm_long_bar_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent_Over_One-Arm_Long_Bar_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'one_arm_long_bar_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'one_arm_long_bar_row', 'One-Arm Long Bar Row', array['Meadows Row (Long Bar, Staggered)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'One-Arm Long Bar Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the meadows row: one hand on the end of a barbell anchored in a corner.', array['Position a bar into a landmine or in a corner to keep it from moving. Load an appropriate weight onto your end.']::text[], array['Stand next to the bar, and take a grip with one hand close to the collar. Using your hips and legs, rise to a standing position.','Assume a bent-knee stance with your hips back and your chest up. Your arm should be extended. This will be your starting position.','Pull the weight to your side by retracting the shoulder and flexing the elbow. Do not jerk the weight or cheat during the movement.','After a brief pause, return to the starting position.']::text[], array['Elbow travels high and back','Keep the hips square']::text[], array['Twisting the torso','Shortening the range']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/one_arm_long_bar_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/One-Arm_Long_Bar_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'middle_back_shrug')::uuid, 'mfd', 'middle_back_shrug', 'Middle Back Shrug', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Middle Back Shrug is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back.', array['Lie facedown on an incline bench while holding a dumbbell in each hand. Your arms should be fully extended hanging down and pointing towards the floor. The palms of your hands should be facing each other. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['As you exhale, squeeze your shoulder blades together and hold the contraction for a full second. Tip: This movement is just like the reverse action of a hug, or trying to perform rear laterals as if you had no arms.','As you inhale go back to the starting position.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Lie face down on an incline bench','Squeeze the shoulder blades together, arms straight','Hold 1 second, lower slowly']::text[], array['Bending the elbows','Shrugging toward the ears']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/middle_back_shrug/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Middle_Back_Shrug/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'mixed_grip_chin')::uuid, 'mfd', 'mixed_grip_chin', 'Mixed Grip Chin', array['Pull Up (Mixed Grip)']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Mixed Grip Chin is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the pull up: one palm toward you, one away.', array['Using a spacing that is just about 1 inch wider than shoulder width, grab a pull-up bar with the palms of one hand facing forward and the palms of the other hand facing towards you. This will be your starting position.']::text[], array['Now start to pull yourself up as you exhale. Tip: With the arm that has the palms facing up concentrate on using the back muscles in order to perform the movement. The elbow of that arm should remain close to the torso. With the other arm that has the palms facing forward, the elbows will be away but in line with the torso. You will concentrate on using the lats to pull your body up.','After a second contraction at the top, start to slowly come down as you inhale.','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','On the following set, switch grips; so if you had the right hand with the palms facing you and the left one with the palms facing forward, on the next set you will have the palms facing forward for the right hand and facing you for the left.']::text[], array['Elbows drive down to your ribs','Body stays still; no swinging','Full hang at the bottom']::text[], array['Kicking or swinging to get up','Half reps without a full hang','Craning the neck to reach the bar']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/mixed_grip_chin/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Mixed_Grip_Chin/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'alternating_renegade_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'alternating_renegade_row', 'Alternating Renegade Row', array['Renegade Row (Kettlebell)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Alternating Renegade Row is an advanced-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the abs & core, biceps, chest, lats and triceps. A variation of the renegade row: kettlebells instead of dumbbells.', array['Place two kettlebells on the floor about shoulder width apart. Position yourself on your toes and your hands as though you were doing a pushup, with the body straight and extended. Use the handles of the kettlebells to support your upper body. You may need to position your feet wide for support.']::text[], array['Push one kettlebell into the floor and row the other kettlebell, retracting the shoulder blade of the working side as you flex the elbow, pulling it to your side.','Then lower the kettlebell to the floor and begin the kettlebell in the opposite hand. Repeat for several reps.']::text[], array['Hips stay square to the floor','Brace like a plank']::text[], array['Twisting the hips up as you row','Sagging the hips']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/alternating_renegade_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Alternating_Renegade_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'scapular_pull_up')::uuid, 'mfd', 'scapular_pull_up', 'Scapular Pull Ups', array['scap pull up']::text[], 'strength', 'reps', 'Small pull ups where only the shoulder blades move. They teach the first part of a pull up and strengthen the shoulders.', array['Hang from a bar with straight arms and an overhand grip.']::text[], array['Without bending your elbows, pull your shoulder blades down and together so your body rises a few centimetres.','Hold for a second.','Let your shoulders rise back to a relaxed hang.']::text[], array['Arms stay straight','Think "shoulders away from ears"']::text[], array['Bending the elbows','Rushing the reps']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/scapular_pull_up/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Scapular_Pull-Up/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'lying_cambered_barbell_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'lying_cambered_barbell_row', 'Lying Cambered Barbell Row', array['Seal Row (Cambered Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Lying Cambered Barbell Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps, lats and traps. A variation of the seal row: a cambered bar lets the hands travel past the bench.', array['Place a cambered bar underneath an exercise bench.']::text[], array['Lie face down on the exercise bench and grab the bar using a palms down (pronated grip) that is wider than shoulder width. This will be your starting position.','As you exhale row the bar up as you keep the elbows close to your body to either your chest, in order to target the upper mid back, or to your stomach if targeting the lats is your goal.','After a second hold at the top, lower back down to the starting position slowly as you inhale.']::text[], array['Chest and hips stay on the bench','Squeeze the shoulder blades at the top']::text[], array['Lifting the head and chest','Bouncing at the bottom']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/lying_cambered_barbell_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Lying_Cambered_Barbell_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seal_row_barbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seal_row_barbell', 'Seal Row (Barbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A strict row lying face down on a raised flat bench, so no body movement can help the lift.', array['Lie face down on a high flat bench (on boxes) so your arms can hang straight.','Hold the weight below the bench with straight arms.']::text[], array['Row the weight up until it touches the underside of the bench.','Lower slowly to straight arms.']::text[], array['Chest and hips stay on the bench','Squeeze the shoulder blades at the top']::text[], array['Lifting the head and chest','Bouncing at the bottom']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seal_row_dumbbell')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seal_row_dumbbell', 'Seal Row (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A strict row lying face down on a raised flat bench, so no body movement can help the lift.', array['Lie face down on a high flat bench (on boxes) so your arms can hang straight.','Hold the weight below the bench with straight arms.']::text[], array['Row the weight up until it touches the underside of the bench.','Lower slowly to straight arms.']::text[], array['Chest and hips stay on the bench','Squeeze the shoulder blades at the top']::text[], array['Lifting the head and chest','Bouncing at the bottom']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'seated_cable_row_wide')::uuid, 'mfd', 'seated_cable_row_wide', 'Seated Cable Row - Bar Wide Grip', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'A seated row on a low cable station. A controlled way to train the mid back and lats with constant tension.', array['Sit on the bench with feet on the footplate and knees slightly bent.','Grab the handle and sit upright with your arms straight in front of you.']::text[], array['Pull the handle toward your lower ribs while keeping your torso upright.','Squeeze the shoulder blades together.','Let the arms extend forward slowly until you feel a stretch between the shoulder blades.']::text[], array['Sit tall; small forward lean at the stretch is fine','Elbows drive back past the body','Shoulders down, not shrugged']::text[], array['Rocking the torso back and forth','Rounding the back at the front','Pulling with the arms only']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'sled_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'sled_row', 'Sled Row', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Sled Row is a beginner-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats.', array['Attach dual handles to a sled connected by a rope or chain. Load the sled to an appropriate weight. Face the sled, backing up until there is some tension in the line.']::text[], array['With a handle in each hand, bend the knees slightly, keep your head and chest up, and begin with your arms extended.','To initiate the movement, flex the elbow as you retract your shoulder blades, pulling the sled towards you.','Take a step or two back to get tension in the line and repeat.']::text[], array['Walk back until the line is tight','Row the handles to the ribs','Step back to reset tension']::text[], array['Leaning back to pull','Slack in the line']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/sled_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Sled_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'bent_over_two_arm_long_bar_row')::uuid, 'mfd', 'bent_over_two_arm_long_bar_row', 'Bent Over Two-Arm Long Bar Row', array['T Bar Row (Long Bar)']::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Bent Over Two-Arm Long Bar Row is an intermediate-level strength exercise that mainly targets the upper back, with help from the biceps and lats. A variation of the t bar row: barbell anchored in a corner, both hands behind the plates.', array['Put weight on one of the ends of an Olympic barbell. Make sure that you either place the other end of the barbell in the corner of two walls; or put a heavy object on the ground so the barbell cannot slide backward.']::text[], array['Bend forward until your torso is as close to parallel with the floor as you can and keep your knees slightly bent.','Now grab the bar with both arms just behind the plates on the side where the weight was placed and put your other hand on your knee. This will be your starting position.','Pull the bar straight up with your elbows in (to maximize back stimulation) until the plates touch your lower chest. Squeeze the back muscles as you lift the weight up and hold for a second at the top of the movement. Breathe out as you lift the weight. Tip: Use a stirrup or double handle cable attachment by hooking it under the end of the bar.','Slowly lower the bar to the starting position getting a nice stretch on the lats. Tip: Do not let the plates touch the floor. To ensure the best range of motion, I recommend using small plates (25-lb ones) as opposed to larger plates (like 35-45lb ones).','Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.']::text[], array['Keep the chest up and back flat','Drive the elbows back past the body']::text[], array['Rounding the back','Standing up taller each rep']::text[], '/catalogue/app_media/images/bent_over_two_arm_long_bar_row/start.webp', 'https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/blob/main/exercises/Bent_Over_Two-Arm_Long_Bar_Row/0.jpg', 'Unlicense (public domain)'),
(md5('mfd:' || 'y_raise_chest_supported')::uuid, 'mfd', 'y_raise_chest_supported', 'Chest Supported Y Raise (Dumbbell)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms up and out into a Y shape. Strengthens the lower traps and helps shoulder health.', array['Lie face down on an incline bench with arms hanging down, thumbs up.']::text[], array['Raise your arms up and out at about 30° from your head, forming a Y.','Pause at the top, then lower slowly.']::text[], array['Thumbs point up','Shoulders down, away from the ears']::text[], array['Shrugging','Using weights too heavy']::text[], null, null, null),
(md5('mfd:' || 'y_raise_cable')::uuid, 'mfd', 'y_raise_cable', 'Standing Y Raise (Cable)', '{}'::text[], 'strength', 'weight_reps', 'Raising the arms up and out into a Y shape. Strengthens the lower traps and helps shoulder health.', array['Set two low pulleys and cross the cables in front of you.']::text[], array['Raise your arms up and out at about 30° from your head, forming a Y.','Pause at the top, then lower slowly.']::text[], array['Thumbs point up','Shoulders down, away from the ears']::text[], array['Shrugging','Using weights too heavy']::text[], null, null, null)
